window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4301,"title":"Chapter 4301: Chapter 4300: Anomaly! IV","paragraphs":["The name was unique, a sound that seemed to carry the weight of a thousand forgotten philosophies!","Anaximander bowed, a gesture of polite, scholarly respect.","\"I apologize for intruding on your experiment,\" he said. \"I just appeared here after testing something of my own.\"","He then continued, his eyes, which held a light of pure, unadulterated curiosity, fixed on Noah. \"But, are you truly trying to learn about The Ways of Existence too? I have also embarked on this journey and made some progress!\"","...!","Noah replied to Anaximander, his voice a calm, even current in the frigid air of the First Folds.","\"Yes, I am learning about The Way of Existence, but...\"","He did not finish his words. His gaze swept over Anaximander, from the simple, archaic cut of his robes to the brilliant, almost naive, curiosity in his eyes.","This being had introduced himself, had given a name, but he remained an anomaly, a variable in an equation that did not compute! In a realm where power was the very air one breathed, where Complexity and Purity were the fundamental metrics of being, this man claimed to have none.","Yet he stood here, in a place that should have unmade him in a nanosecond, as if he were taking a leisurely stroll through a park.","The temperatures seemed to sway around him as if...they weren’t supposed to touch him!","Beside him, the crimson-blue holographic figure of RUIN/EDEN materialized, her form a stark, beautiful contrast to the pristine white of the snow. Her voice was a cold, clinical whisper in the quiet of his mind.","|I did not sense him appear in my previous scans, Master. He had to have just arrived here moments ago, but even then, even I could not detect his arrival. He is a ghost Existence, a blind spot in reality itself.|","HUUM!","At her silent, communicated words and Noah’s own heavy silence, Anaximander blinked.","A brilliant light of pure, unadulterated intellect flashed in his eyes. \"Ah,\" he said, a warm, almost apologetic smile spreading across his face. \"Let me introduce myself properly. You must have some reservations on seeing me here...\"","He gestured to himself, a simple, disarming motion. \"I have come across many unique beings since I began this journey, and many of them have seemed just as confused and distrustful as you currently are. From their perspective, they were seeing someone who did not have an ounce of power... appearing before them in places where they shouldn’t be.\"","He began to pace, his steps leaving no prints in the sparkling snow.","\"I have met colossal, sentient mountains that have tried to crush me for the audacity of my presence. I have conversed with beings of pure, chaotic energy who have tried to devour me for the novelty of it. Most, however, either attacked me on sight or fled in terror. It seems a being with no discernible authority is a profound anomaly, and anomalies tend to make the powerful... uncomfortable. I have found that a clear and honest introduction can sometimes mitigate the... misunderstandings.\"","He stopped, his gaze open and sincere. \"So, please, treat me like a harmless explorer, because that is who I am. Just someone seeking to understand Existence. As for your other questions, yes, my existence does not contain any authority...which seems to be the biggest issue for many of those I have met. But I simply do not need authority. That is... my Way. My nature... or what I have discovered of it so far. I am still doing my best to learn and understand. Because not too long ago, I was introduced to all of this by entities I have been searching for since they appeared before me... THE Weavers.\"","...!","THE Weavers!","Noah’s eyes became exceedingly grave. The name was a detonation in the silent chambers of his mind. THE.","A distinction of the highest, most terrifying order.","This Fold Dweller, this seemingly powerless anomaly, had been in contact with a Level One Scale existence? Or multiple? And they had guided him?","THE Weavers...who the fuck were they?!","WAA!","This entire situation had just transitioned from a curious anomaly to a potentially catastrophic variable. His Early Atlas of the Folds buzzed, a silent, ready hum, the pathway for an emergency Temporal Traversal already primed!","His careful, assessing gaze was observed by Anaximander.","\"Oh,\" he said, his own eyes lighting up with a new, excited curiosity. \"Based on your reaction, do you know something of them? I haven’t gotten a chance to talk to many knowledgeable beings about them. In fact, part of the reason why I appeared here... I closed my eyes and told my very being... to send me somewhere where I could potentially gain answers or satisfy my scientific curiosity even more, and I appeared here!\"","...!","His words were heavy, each one adding another layer of mystery to his already impossible presence. Noah looked at him closely, his gaze a scalpel dissecting every word.","\"You say THE Weavers introduced all of this to you? Your Way of Existence? What did they say?\"","At such words, the eyes of Anaximander brightened up. \"Yes! This may be able to help you as well. When it comes to the Way, I will try to do it similarly to how they did it with me. Haha, I haven’t been able to get this far with anyone to replicate it, so let’s see!\"","He took a step back, his posture shifting, becoming less a fellow explorer and more a guide, a teacher.","His voice took on a new, profound weight, a resonant, multi-tonal quality that was an eerie echo of voices!","\"They asked me,\" Anaximander began, his eyes looking past Noah, as if seeing a memory playing out in the swirling snow, \"’Every night you reach out to the stars. Why do you not simply take a step and see them with your own two eyes?’\"","He paused, a faint, almost nostalgic smile on his lips. \"Of course, I explained the scientific impossibilities. The vacuum. The radiation. The cold. All the reasons why such an act would be suicide. And they listened, with a patience that was both a comfort and a profound, unnerving thing. And then they asked, ’Have you ever tried? How do you know you cannot, if you don’t try?’\""]},{"number":4302,"title":"Chapter 4302: Chapter 4301: Anomaly! V","paragraphs":["He looked at Noah, his eyes now holding a deep, philosophical light. \"I told them that science, that nature, that the very Way the world works told me what would happen. And then they said the words that changed everything for me.\"","Anaximander’s voice dropped to a whisper, a carrier of a terrible, beautiful truth. \"They told me that all of that... is simply what others decided what nature is. That I was different. That my Way of Existence was special, unique compared to others. That what is known as a fact of reality may not be a fact for me. That I could bend it and change it.\"","He took a step closer, his eyes burning with the fervor of a convert sharing his gospel. \"They told me I could take a step and truly appear all the way in outer space. That I could decide that nature is wrong. That I could simply decide that my Way, my nature, was to survive. And then they said...\" His voice was a final, compelling call to action.","\"So... just take the step forward. Ignore what nature is, and simply decide what your nature is. What your Way is. Come on, give it a try.\"","...!","Anaximander was expectant. He looked at Noah, at this being of impossible power, and he urged him, with a genuine, almost childlike, enthusiasm.","Noah listened to all of these words, his own eyes flashing sharply. He decides what existence is? Ignore nature? Ignore existence?","A brilliant, tyrannical light flashed in his eyes. He looked at the expectant Fold Dweller, and he spoke, his voice a calm, even, and utterly absolute declaration.","\"Existence deems that I have the power of a few hundred Quadrillion Purity... but I actually have tens of thousands of Quadrillions of Purity.\"","...!","\"...\"","He said the words. He chose that nature. And... nothing happened.","\"...\"","He blinked. He looked towards Anaximander with bright, questioning eyes.","Anaximander frowned, a look of profound, intellectual concentration on his face. \"Try again?\" he suggested, his tone now that of a fellow scientist troubleshooting a failed experiment.","\"But really believe it. That with surety, your existence will be that way.\"","Noah stared at this Fold Dweller up and down. Just who was this crook?","He shook his head, but he played along. His voice, this time, was not just a declaration, but a roar of pure, unadulterated, tyrannical will.","\"I have actually attained the distinction of THE.\"","...!","He said it. He believed it. And once more... nothing happened.","\"Huh...\"","Anaximander stood in thought, his brow furrowed in deep, analytical contemplation. A moment later, his eyes shone with the light of a new, dawning comprehension. He looked at Noah, and a slow, almost apologetic smile spread across his face.","\"I may have to thank you, friend,\" he said, his voice a mixture of gratitude and a faint, academic disappointment. \"This experiment here may confirm the possibility thst was staring at me in the face but I did not wish to see... that what happened was unique to me. Something unique to my Code of Existence. This whole time, I may have been thinking that maybe I was not...alone in this. Oh well! But this is a bummer... how can I help you find your Way if mine is so different and solely related to me?\"","...!","Noah looked at the brilliant Fold Dweller before him, at Anaximander, who was now gazing at him with an expression of profound disappointment.","He shook his head, a faint, almost imperceptible smile touching his lips.","\"It’s okay,\" he said, \"I will find my own Way. But you said... others have attacked you before? How did you survive with no authority or mana?\"","The question was a sharp, analytical probe- seeking the heart of the mystery that was Anaximander!","How could a being of no discernible power stand in a place that could unmake Quadrillions, and speak of being attacked as if it were a mere inconvenience?","Anaximander’s expression shifted, the disappointment giving way to a bright, almost childlike, enthusiasm.","\"Ah, yes! That is the most fascinating part of my journey so far!\" he exclaimed, his voice filled with the pure, unadulterated joy of a scientist who has just stumbled upon a new, beautiful law of nature.","He began to pace, his feet leaving no prints in the sparkling snow, his movements a graceful, almost weightless dance.","\"After my... impromptu trip to the stars, and my subsequent realization that my existence did not have to adhere to the standard operational parameters of this universe, I knew I had to establish some new parameters of my own. A set of personal, existential guidelines, if you will.\"","He stopped, his eyes, which held a light of pure, unadulterated curiosity, fixed on Noah. \"I have an internal journal,\" he said, a note of pride in his voice.","\"In it, I have meticulously detailed every encounter, every observation, every new guideline I have forged for my own being. It is a work in progress, of course, but the core tenets are quite robust.\"","He raised a finger, as if beginning a lecture. \"Guideline #1: I exist. A simple, but necessary, starting point. Guideline #2: I will continue to exist. A statement of intent. But Guideline #3... that is the one that has proven most useful in my travels.\"","He smiled, a brilliant, almost blinding, expression of pure, intellectual delight.","\"Guideline #3: My existence cannot be unwillingly altered or ended by the will or authority of another. Any hostile action or intent directed at me will be treated not as an attack, but as an interesting, but ultimately irrelevant, external phenomenon for me to study and understand.\"","WAA!","The words were a quiet detonation in the silent, frozen air!","Noah stared at him, his own vast, analytical mind struggling to process the sheer, audacious simplicity of it.","\"And it... works?\" Noah asked, the question a whisper of genuine, profound curiosity.","Anaximander’s smile widened. \"So far, the data is promising. I have been struck by a living mountain. I have been bathed in the conceptual fire of a sentient star. I have been... shouted at by a very angry, very large lizard. And in every instance, the result was the same. Their authority, their power, their very intent to harm... it simply did not apply to me. It was like they were speaking a language my existence no longer understood, or really, chose not to.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes blazed with a tyrannical fervor.","\"How about...\" he began, his voice a low, dangerous murmur, \"I try to attack you? For research purposes, of course.\"","Anaximander laughed, a sound of pure, unadulterated delight. \"But of course! I would be honored! Your authority feels... different. Denser. More complex. The data would be invaluable!\"","He stood there, his arms open in a gesture of willing, enthusiastic acceptance. \"So go ahead. Give it your best sho-\"","BOOM!","Before the words could even finish leaving his mouth, Noah acted!","He did not move a muscle. He did not raise a hand. He simply... wove.","From the Crucible of Quintessence, he drew forth a river of his own, terrifying power!","He wove a spell of pure, analytical dread, a concept he named, in that very instant, [Existential Scrutiny].","It was not a blast of fire or a blade of force. It was a wave of pure, absolute judgment, a question asked of Anaximander’s very right to exist.","It shot forth, a beam of incandescent, white-gold light that was so pure, so potent, that it seemed to be the only real thing in this frozen, illusory world!","It was a thing of terrible, beautiful power, an attack that did not seek to break, but to dissect, to unravel, to understand its target to death.","And...","HUUM!","Ridiculously, it passed right through him.","\"...\"","Anaximander stood, bathed in the glorious, terrible light of the attack, and he was... untouched.","The Weave of pure, conceptual power washed over him, around him, through him, like a gentle breeze.","He blinked, a slow, curious movement, and then he looked down at his own, unharmed body, a faint, almost puzzled, smile on his face.","\"Interesting, isn’t it?\" he said, his voice filled with a genuine, almost childlike, wonder. \"No matter how many times it happens, even I cannot quite believe it.\"","...!"]},{"number":4303,"title":"Chapter 4303: Chapter 4302: This is MY Way! I","paragraphs":["Noah stared with bright eyes!","The Weave had not been repelled. It had not been negated. It had been... ignored. His attack, a thing of Quadrillions in power, had been treated as an irrelevant piece of data, a null value in the equation of Anaximander’s existence!","He felt the necklace on his chest grow warm.","The Aegis of the Architect, his symbiotic armor, was responding to his own, unspoken will.","\"Let’s try something else,\" Noah murmured.","In the next instant, he was no longer a man. The Aegis materialized around him, a silent, perfect symphony of interlocking white and gold plates!","HUUM!","The golden visor flared to life, a sun in the growing twilight of the mountain. His entire being was now a conduit for a singular, terrible purpose: absolute Purity.","The armor blazed with a white-gold light so intense it seemed to burn the very concept of color from the air.","He raised his hand, and from his palm, a beam of pure, conceptual certainty shot forth, a torrent of over 500 Quadrillion in pure, unadulterated Purity!","BOOM!","It was a wave of absolute, unyielding truth...and it passed right through him.","...!","Anaximander stood, bathed in a new, even more glorious light, a look of profound, academic fascination on his face.","He even reached out, his hand moving through the beam of annihilating power as if it were nothing more than a curious, harmless hologram.","Noah stopped.","The armor, with a soft, almost disappointed hiss, receded, returning to its dormant, necklace form!","He stood in the swirling, snowy winds, a profound, almost frustrating, silence settling between him and this impossible being.","|Master, I have been analyzing the subject, Anaximander.|","|Conclusion: He is a unique, one-of-a-kind anomaly. I have cross-referenced his existential signature with all known data, and there is... nothing that fits. He is not immune to your attacks; he is simply not a valid target for them. To him, your authority is a language he does not speak, a force that has no context in his self-defined reality.|","|Recommendation: Further study is... essential. This being is a living, breathing loophole in the very fabric of existence. Understanding him may provide us with a new, unprecedented path to power.|","...!","Noah looked at Anaximander, who was now gazing at the dormant Aegis with a blinding light of pure curiosity.","\"Wow,\" he breathed, his voice filled with a genuine, almost reverent, awe. \"What is a suit of armor like that made of? Your existence feels much heavier with it, and if you can do all of this... ah, what a conundrum this is. Oh, just who are you, Friend?\"","Who was he? The question, once so simple, was now a complex, multifaceted thing.","He had given his name freely to many. But to this... this beautiful, terrible, and utterly baffling anomaly?","Anaximander blinked, and a warm, understanding smile spread across his face.","\"You do not have to worry. I didn’t tell you any names of others I met before, right? Well, except THE Weavers it seems... but yes, I keep my interactions and research to myself mostly!\"","He smiled, a genuine expression. Noah looked at him, and in that moment, he called out.","\"Osmont,\" he said, his voice a quiet, resonant note in the frozen silence. \"Noah Osmont. And yes, don’t mention that to anyone. And frankly, be... cautious and careful of THE Weavers you met.\"","...!","His words, a simple warning, seemed to surprise Anaximander. \"What do you mean?\" he asked, a flicker of confusion in his bright, intelligent eyes.","\"They guided me to be where I am now. They did not wish harm as far as I can tell...\"","Noah shook his head in a slow, deliberate motion.","\"In existence,\" he began, his voice a low murmur that seemed to carry the weight of eons, \"especially for those who hold the distinction of THE... nothing is done without purpose. The guidance they gave you, the path they set you on... it was for their purpose, not for yours. In existence, rarely do any beings at the very peak of power do anything for the good of others. All they do... all they will ever do... is something to serve themselves. Theur Way. So, question everything.\"","WAA!","His words were heavy, each one a seed of doubt planted in the fertile soil of Anaximander’s scientific mind!","The Fold Dweller went quiet, his gaze turning inward, as if he were re-examining the very foundations of his own, impossible journey.","\"What...\" he finally asked, his voice a low, hesitant whisper, \"can you tell me about THE Weavers? There are others like them?\"","...!","Noah stood before Anaximander, his simple, white-gold wrappings a stark contrast to the swirling, snowy landscape, and he began to speak.","\"THE Weavers, based on what you have described,\" he said, his voice a quiet, informative current, \"are existences of an entirely different Scale of Existence from me and you. The ones I know of are THE Creature...\"","He began to explain, his voice a calm, steady narration in the heart of the storm. He spoke of the Scales of Existence, of the vast chasm that separated the beings of Level Zero from the architects of Level One!","He spoke of THE Creature, of THE Living Existences, and of grand while he continued to...analyze Anaximander.","And Anaximander, the brilliant, naive, and impossibly powerful Fold Dweller, listened, his eyes wide, his mind a wonder of terrible comprehension!","—","Aethelgard.","In the quiet, profound stillness of the central hall, three hooded figures sat, their silence a weight that seemed to bend the very light of the room.","Before them, Gilgamesh, The First Leader, floated, his golden eyes a storm of contained, imperial power!","\"The war was a precursor,\" the unison voice of THE Weavers echoed, a calm, prophetic statement in the charged silence. \"A test. A demonstration. You have shown your strength. Now, you will be approached.\"","Gilgamesh’s gaze was a thing of cold, analytical fire. \"By whom?\"","\"THE Living Emotive,\" they replied, their voices a single, harmonious chord. \"They will come to you with an offer. A sanctuary. A place of peace and shared purpose in the face of the coming storm. They will offer you...a Civilization.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4304,"title":"Chapter 4304: Chapter 4303: This is MY Way! II","paragraphs":["The King of Aethelgard laughed, a short, sharp, and utterly contemptuous sound.","\"I do not need to be given a Civilization. And I have no desire to be entangled in the emotional, chaotic weavings of THE Living Emotive.\"","...!","THE Weavers remained still, their faceless hoods a void of unreadable intent. \"In this case,\" their unison voice was a gentle, yet absolute, counter-argument, \"you have to. It will benefit your Way of Existence... and your budding Civilization.\"","Gilgamesh was silent for a long, heavy moment. He looked at these three mysterious beings, at their quiet, unshakeable certainty, and he gave a single, almost imperceptible, nod of assent.","And then, it happened.","WUU!","The three hooded figures, who had been a single, unified presence, suddenly stopped. Their forms, which had been perfectly still, flickered!","A silent, internal conversation, a wave of pure, conceptual data, passed between them.","\"Something is wrong,\" one of them, the one with the high, melodic voice, whispered, the word a fragile, uncertain thing!","\"An interference with a budding Weaving of Existence we have set in place...\"","The one with the dry, academic voice replied, its tone now sharp with a new, analytical coldness. \"I cannot sense who... could THE Creature have noticed something? But they are occupied right now...\"","HUUM!","The three of them rose as one. The calm, prophetic certainty they had projected was gone, replaced by a new, more profound, and utterly terrifying, silence.","They looked at each other, their faceless hoods a void of shared, unspoken concern.","\"We will proceed carefully,\" their unison voice was now a low, dangerous whisper. \"We will see what interference occurred, and where.\"","With those final, ominous words, they turned to Gilgamesh, a silent dismissal in their posture.","He looked at them, a new, cautious light in his golden eyes, and with a final, lingering glance, he vanished, leaving them alone in their silent, shadowed hall, with a new, unforeseen, and very, very dangerous variable in their grand equation!","—","It was cold, and yet a sense of terrifying warmth of knowledge and power was present in the center of a glacial expanse in the Earliest Folds...in a small corner of these vast Folds!","​Two figures sat upon glacial blue stones that seemed to be carved from frozen time itself.","One, a man exuding a quiet, analytical brilliance, held a simple stick, idly drawing intricate diagrams and cryptic words on the frozen ground.","He sighed, the sound a small, human thing in this ancient, terrible place.","​\"THE Creature...THE Living Paradox...THE Living Emotive...Stories of the Earliest Folds....Ay, so convoluted...\" Anaximander muttered, shaking his head.","​In the last hour, Noah had cracked open his understanding of existence, revealing the complex, glittering, and dangerous structures within!","The Stories of the Earliest Folds Noah had shared, the concepts of Scales of Existence...it was a universe of data that made his own explorations feel like a child’s first steps.","​Sitting opposite him, Noah’s gaze was calm, his vast power held in perfect, effortless check.","He had, in turn, been analyzing this impossible being, this Anaximander, and had found nothing!","His existence was a perfect, smooth wall, a blank page that refused to be read.","​|He is an anomaly through and through, Master. His self-defined ’Way’ is something we have never encountered. There seems to be a reason why the so-called THE Weavers approached him. Anything that can require the attention of entities like that is not simple.|","​Beside Noah, the holographic, crimson-blue figure of RUIN/EDEN frowned with a profound, analytical contemplation, her gaze fixed on Anaximander as if he were the most complex, unsolvable equation she had ever encountered.","​At this moment, Noah leaned forward.","​\"Hey, say...\" he began, \"If you knew there was an apocalyptic problem, a grand, existential threat where the complete cessation of existence was coming... a Fallout of sorts, as some might call it. How would you avoid it? Prevent it? Escape it?\"","​...!","​Anaximander looked up, his bright, intelligent eyes blinking in surprise. The stick in his hand paused mid-diagram. He gazed at Noah, his mind a brilliant engine of logic!","​\"What an exquisitely terrifying hypothesis,\" he breathed, a flicker of genuine, scientific excitement in his eyes.","He stood, his simple robes fluttering in a wind that wasn’t there, and began to pace.","​\"Well,\" he began, his voice taking on the rhythmic cadence of a lecturer dissecting a grand problem, \"the first step, in any logical framework, would be to identify the source. The catalyst. Causality is not just a suggestion; it is the spine of Existence. If a collapse is coming, something caused it. I would dedicate all my resources to finding that First Domino. If one could find the source, the trigger... could one not, theoretically, stop it? Alter it? Convince it not to have been triggered at all? It is the most direct, and likely the most impossible, solution.\"","​\"But,\" he continued, holding up a finger, \"let us assume the catalyst is unstoppable. That it is a force of nature, like a hurricane that has already made landfall. What then? Then, the logical recourse is not to fight the storm, but to build a shelter.\"","​He gestured to the vast, swirling sky above them. \"Not a simple shelter of stone and metal, but a conceptual one. A fortress built outside the very rules of the storm. A sanctuary forged from a different kind of reality, a place so fundamentally separate from the collapsing Folds that this...what did you call it...Fallout, could not find its purchase. An isolated, perfect bunker.\"","WAA!","Noah couldn’t help but smile at all the answers this being gave as they were...the same ones powerful entities came up with!","​\"A beautiful theory,\" Anaximander mused, \"but one that relies on the existence of such a place, or the means to build it. So, if the storm cannot be stopped, and a shelter cannot be built, what remains?\"","​He smiled, a bright, intellectual spark. \"A third path. You do not fight the storm, and you do not hide from it. You find a place the storm simply cannot reach. You go... elsewhere. A hidden garden, a forgotten pocket of existence. You find a new civilization, a new place to plant your seeds, and you simply... wait for the storm to pass, hoping it does not find you.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4305,"title":"Chapter 4305: Chapter 4304: This is MY Way! III","paragraphs":["​Anaximander’s logic was a chilling, perfect echo of the very paths Noah had been forced to consider.","The Fold Dweller stopped pacing and looked at Noah, his expression now one of profound, philosophical contemplation.","​\"And if all else fails,\" he said, his voice dropping to a low, almost reverent whisper, \"if the cause cannot be stopped, if no shelter can be built, and if there is nowhere left to hide... there is only one, final, and most arrogant solution left.\"","​He met Noah’s gaze, and in his eyes, there was a brilliant, almost manic, light.","​\"You must become the storm. You must cease to be the thing that is in the storm, and become the thing that is the storm. You would have to elevate your own existence to a Scale where the Fallout is no longer an apocalypse, but simply... weather. You would have to become a being for whom the cessation of existence is not an ending, but simply...a Monday.\"","​BOOM!","​Noah stared, his expression unreadable.","This powerless, manaless Fold Dweller had, in the span of a few minutes, perfectly and independently deduced four impossible, desperate paths to survival that he thought of and others acted on.","​Anaximander, seeing Noah’s heavy silence, seemed to mistake it for disappointment.","He sighed, the brilliant energy fading from him, replaced by a humble, almost apologetic, shrug.","​\"But those are just grand, impossible theories, of course,\" he said, sitting back down on his glacial stone. \"Just the ramblings of a man who has seen too much and understands too little. It seems existence is more complicated the more you scratch the surface and peel the layers. I am sorry that I was not able to be of much help to you.\"","​He poked at the diagrams on the ground with his stick. \"But if I can say one last thing... it is about your Way. If I am to be considered an anomaly, it is because my Way is related to what makes me an anomaly. That I can ignore the rules that bind others. What is it about you that is anomalous? Your Way would be easiest to open up and guide your existence from there.\"","​...!","​Noah smiled, a genuine, almost warm expression. What made him an anomaly? He knew the answer to that. It was the very first truth of his existence!","​It was the foundation upon which his Heart, his Atlas, his Principles, his very Tyranny was built.","Anaximander’s words were not a new revelation, but a profound, timely reminder.","​\"Thank you for the words, Anaximander,\" Noah said. \"You helped by expanding my point of view somewhat. More than you know.\"","​At his words, Anaximander brightened. He stood, brushing the sparkling frost from his simple robes, his task here seemingly complete.","He smiled, a genuine expression of a scholar who has just had a truly fascinating exchange of ideas.","​\"Existence is a laboratory, friend Osmont,\" he said, his voice filled with a new, vibrant energy.","\"We are all just experiments, running our own hypothesis against the unyielding wall of reality. Some of us choose to build a Civilization, a grand, collective experiment. It is a noble path. They seek to find the answers together, to build a tower of shared knowledge tall enough to see over the next horizon.\"","​He gestured to the vast, empty, and beautiful expanse around them.","​\"But I... I am a field researcher. I must walk, I must see, I must ask. The best data is not found in the lab, but in the wild, untamed wilderness of the unknown. A civilization is a beautiful, warm, and comfortable place... but it is also a cage, a bubble that limits one’s perception to only what is inside.\"","​He bowed, a final, respectful gesture from one anomaly to another.","​\"I will add another Guideline to my existence,\" he declared, his voice ringing with the light of a new, forged law. \"If ever I hear an existence I deem... a friend call out the words, ’Anaximander, come!’, then I will be able to sense wherever you are. And so long as I am not busy being dissected by a curious star or something of the sort, I will come. As for now...I like to get answers directly. I must continue exploring existence!\"","​...!","​Noah nodded, a silent acknowledgment of the offer.","He watched, his gaze sharp and analytical, as Anaximander, the brilliant, impossible Fold Dweller, turned.","​He took a single step.","​And disappeared!","HUUM!","​He was gone, leaving Noah alone in the vast, silent, and glittering expanse of the frozen First Folds, with a head full of new, terrible, and glorious possibilities.","​Existence, as Noah had already come to understand it, was a brutal and relentless series of escalations.","​One achieved a new, unimaginable height of power, only to look up and see a mountain range of beings whose casual footsteps were the very power he had just attained!","​He had felt it multiple times before.","​And now, as he stood in the First Folds and gazed at the distant ideas of existences with the distinctions of THE, he felt it again, but on a scale that made all previous escalations seem like minor, introductory Chapters!","What he had to do amidst these series of escalations of existence...was forge something that even those who had already forged their grand civilization would be envious of!","Noah stood in the field of endless snow and cold as he breathed out.","These last few hours, after taking on the form of different life forms to observe and carry out their Way of existence, after learning and observing the Way of existence of a terrifying anomaly that had no mana or any authority in his body... after all of these experiences, he was now ready to take a heavy and irreversible step forward.","What his Way of Existence could be was never a question!","From the words of the brilliant Fold Dweller that had just left, what made him an anomaly? If everything about him was stripped away, what did he have? And where did everything begin?","If he said that his Way of existence was Quintessence, he would not be wrong, but he would not be entirely correct.","If he said his Way of existence was Tyranny, it would once more be correct, but he would also be wrong!","He could say the same for the Ways of Existence of Cheats, Infinity, Apocalypse, Ruination, Veritarch, Kuklos, Megalos... you could list countless Ways of Existence that would fit him, but they wouldn’t entirely encapsulate and get to the root cause of who, and what he was!","Before Tyranny, what did he have?","Because in the beginning, he did not have Tyranny, nor did he have Quintessence or Cheats.","What did he have in the very beginning?!"]},{"number":4306,"title":"Chapter 4306: Chapter 4305: This is MY Way! IV","paragraphs":["When he asked such a question, he had to decide for himself what was his beginning!","His beginning.","At this thought, a billowing storm of snow picked up around Noah.","And in the snow, an illusory image of a dilapidated apartment began to form in front of him as it displayed a scene from years ago!","It displayed the scene of him Looking at a glistening skill book that stated...[Fireball].","Yes. This was his beginning!","The moment that he awakened was his beginning.","When he did so, he had not yet formed his Tyranny and Quintessence and Cheats and all these other glamorous and glorious parts of him.","All he had was...","\"Mana.\"","HUUM!","As he said these words, the illusory image of his younger self touched the skill book that disappeared into light into his body.","It acted as an initiator, as if something was turning a light bulb on. The illusory body of his younger self was then filled with boundless, intricate lines of Mana.","Mana!","\"Oh, Mana!\"","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes shone with a glorious light as the storm around him picked up even more, his eyes radiating tendrils of blue mana at this moment!","Did he invent Mana, or did he simply discover it?","The answer was clear. Like Principles... Mana had always been there, whether he knew it or not. He found it and became it.","In the very beginning, before he had built anything else, all he had was Mana.","So for his Way of existence, for the System of Existence that he wanted to forge... the path was undoubtedly and explicitly Mana!","Within it...the idea of Infinity was held. The idea of Quintessence was held. The idea of Tyranny burned!","He smiled brilliantly as he turned towards the holographic, crimson-blue figure of RUIN/EDEN, who had been observing him with her usual, analytical calm.","\"We should be ready to finalize the new system of existence,\" he said, his voice a low, resonant hum that seemed to make the very snowflakes around them vibrate with purpose.","\"One that integrates the many systems of power that we have come across, and even the ones that we have forged ourselves. Take these ideas in my mind and actualize them for me, will you?\"","RUIN/EDEN’s illusory form, that perfect, beautiful fusion of Ruination’s tragic grace and a system’s cold logic, smiled.","She bowed deeply, a gesture of profound, absolute loyalty.","\"Yes, Master.\"","An instant later, Noah’s body, standing at the center of the frozen, primordial expanse, became a beacon!","A beam of incandescent blue brilliance, the very color of his infinite, boundless Mana, shot out from him. It did not strike the ground or the sky, but seemed to pierce the very fabric of reality itself, crawling upwards towards the endless, chaotic heavens of the Earliest Folds!","Waves and tendrils of this same blue mana began to snake around his figure, a glorious, swirling storm of pure potential.","He closed his eyes, his entire being focused on this singular, monumental act of creation. He was not just building a system; he was a blind man grasping towards and sensing a new Way!","As he did so, prompts, rendered in that new, vivid crimson-blue, bloomed before his eyes.","|You have begun to consciously walk your chosen Way of Existence.|","|This is a heavy and irreversible step. By choosing this path, all other potential ’Ways’ become secondary, tributaries to this one, great river.|","|You are embarking on the Way of Mana.|","|To truly and completely embody this Way, to achieve the distinction of ’THE,’ is a journey that may require eons. You are still a long, long way off.|","|But the first step has been taken. The first course of action toward this grand design is being enacted.|","|The boons for embarking on this Way will be determined and granted after you have taken your first course of action towards it...|","HUUM!","After he had taken his first course of action?","After he had forged his system of existence, is that right?","Noah smiled at such a thought.","At this moment, the holographic, crimson-blue figure of RUIN/EDEN burned brightly before him, stepping gracefully out of the swirling azure storm as if she were its master.","She looked at him, at the raw, untamed power he was unleashing, and her smile was a thing of sublime, analytical beauty.","Her voice echoed in his mind, a symphony of logic and ruin. As she spoke, her hands, elegant and ethereal, began to move, weaving the very air into holographic displays that bloomed around them in the swirling snow and mana.","\"Based on all known data, your core authorities, the principles of [Perpetual Harvest] and [The Cheating Architect], and your stated goal of creating a scalable, universal methodology for your burgeoning Civilization, I have finalized the schematic.\"","Her voice formed words and not purely a prompt!","She raised a hand, and the swirling blue mana around them seemed to part, revealing a grand, floating title composed of pure, informational light.","\"I present to you...\"","|THE WAY OF THE MANA ARCHITECT|","|CORE PHILOSOPHY:|","|All power, all authority, all existence, stems from a single, fundamental source: Mana.|","|Glyphs, Haki, Armaments, Arcana... these are not separate, competing systems. They are merely different expressions, different languages, for the one true grammar of existence. This grammar is Mana.|","|This System of Existence, [The Way of the Mana Architect], is a unified methodology that integrates all known forms of power under a single, cohesive framework. It is a path of progression open to any existence, from the weakest manaless being to a Primordial creature.|","...!","Oh!","The Way of the Mana Architect! This was the proposed name of the new System of Existence!","\"You are not just a wielder of these disparate forces, Master,\" RUIN/EDEN explained, as her hand conjured an illusion.","A single, brilliant blue thread of Mana shot out, then split, weaving itself into the distinct forms of a Glyph, an aura of Haki, a shimmering suit of Armor, and a glowing Arcana card.","\"You are the source from which all these expressions flow. This system simply gives that flow... structure.\"","Noah watched, his eyes shining with a cold, tyrannical light. He nodded, a silent command to continue.","\"The system itself,\" she continued, \"is built upon the one authority that allows for such a unification.\"","|THE SKELETON: THE CHEATING ARCHITECT|","|This entire System is built upon the foundation of your [Principle of the Cheating Architect]. It is the operating system, the underlying code.|","|Primary Function: The Principle allows this System to ’cheat’ the established rules of existence. It creates loopholes, bypasses limitations, and finds the most efficient, often paradoxical, path to power.|","|Civilization Boon: As the creator, you are the Architect. You can alter, update, and deploy ’patches’ to this System as your understanding grows. You can create unique ’exploits’ or ’backdoors’ for your most trusted followers.|","...!"]},{"number":4307,"title":"Chapter 4307: Chapter 4306: This is MY Way! V","paragraphs":["Her hand gestured, and the illusion shifted.","A vast, intricate blueprint of the system appeared, with the fractured, multicolored infinity symbol of [The Cheating Architect] at its very center, its tendrils connected to every other component.","\"And the engine that drives this impossible machine,\" RUIN/EDEN said, her voice filled with a note of profound respect, \"is twofold.\"","|THE FUEL: INFINITE MANA & PERPETUAL HARVEST|","|For you, Master, the fuel for every action within this System is your [Infinite Mana]. The cost is irrelevant; your reservoir is boundless. This makes you the absolute, unchallengeable master of this Way.|","|For all other beings who walk this path, Mana is a finite resource they must cultivate through the initial stages of progression. This creates a natural, unbreachable hierarchy. They are practitioners; you are the source.|","|Furthermore, your [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] is woven into the very code of this System. All effort exerted within this path, be it cultivation, forging, or combat- is recognized as ’Effort’ and will yield a ’Harvest,’ accelerating the progression of all who follow it.|","A new illusion formed: a vast, raging, azure ocean, Noah’s Mana, flowed endlessly, while beside it, a tiny, crystal cup slowly filled, drop by drop...that of a normal practitioner.","Noah’s smile widened. He saw it. A system of perfect, absolute tyranny, disguised as a path of universal opportunity.","\"And this,\" RUIN/EDEN said, her voice now taking on the cadence of a grand lecturer, \"is the path itself. The Edicts of Progression.\"","|THE EDICTS OF PROGRESSION|","|This is the linear, nine-stage journey of advancement within the Way of the Mana Architect. Each Edict represents a new level of mastery over Mana, unlocking a new expression of power.|","Her hands moved, and with each Edict she named, a new, beautiful, and terrifying illustration bloomed in the frozen air.","|EDICT 0: THE UNINITIATED|","| - State: A being with no Mana, a ’manaless’ existence.|","| - Potential: All beings possess the latent potential to awaken. This System provides the key.|","| - The Spark: Through a ritual of initiation (a direct bestowment of Mana from an existing practitioner, or through finding a ’Spark’ cultivated by you), an Uninitiated can awaken.|","She showed an image of a simple, manaless being, dark and formless, being touched by a single spark of blue light.","|EDICT 1: THE SPARK|","| - Awakening: The being’s existence is rewritten. A [Mana Locus] is formed at the core of their being.|","| - The Mana Locus: A nascent, internal core that can now passively absorb ambient Mana from existence (or be directly filled by you). It needs to be filled and expanded to a vast sea before it can be deemed a reservoir.|","| - Boon: The being is no longer Manaless. They can begin the slow, arduous process of cultivation.|","| - (Note: For you, Master, you began with an Infinite Locus. A slight advantage.)|","...!","The illusion shifted. The dark figure now held a tiny, glowing blue star in its chest: the [Mana Locus].","It was a glorious thing to see!","|EDICT 2: THE RESERVOIR|","| - Objective: To fill the [Mana Locus] to its absolute capacity.|","| - Process: Through meditation, consumption of Mana-rich materials, devouring lifeforms rich in Mana, or direct endowment, the being expands their Locus. This is the foundation of all future power. Reservoir Foundation can become World Sized Mana Reservoir or exceed this.|","| - Boon: A larger reservoir allows for grander, more sustained expressions of power.|","| - (Note: Your reservoir is... well, you know.)|","The blue star pulsed on the illusory being she displayed grew brighter and larger, becoming a stable, humming [Reservoir].","|EDICT 3: THE WEAVE|","| - Objective: To learn to express Mana externally.|","| - Process: The practitioner learns to draw Mana from their Locus and ’weave’ it into a desired effect. This is the foundation of all spells, techniques, and abilities.|","| - Example Weaves: [Weave of Fireball], [Weave of Minor Fortification], [Weave of Quickened Thought].|","| - Boon: The ability to directly influence reality through Mana.|","Azure threads now pulled from the Reservoir, coalescing in the figure’s hand into the shimmering, unstable form of a [Weave of Fireball].","It was a fantastical sight to see!","|EDICT 4: THE GLYPH|","| - Objective: To internalize and perfect a Weave.|","| - Process: By casting a single Weave (e.g., [Weave of Fireball]) ten thousand times, a practitioner can achieve ’Conceptual Resonance.’ This allows them to forge the Weave into a permanent [Mana Glyph] upon their existence.|","| - Integration: This is the integration of the Glyph System. These [Mana Glyphs] are permanent, passive or active enhancements, identical in function to the Glyphs you have forged, but their power scales directly with the wielder’s total Mana.|","| - Boon: The ability is now innate, requiring no complex casting, only an act of will.|","...!","Oh!","What a glorious change!","Cast an ability, a Weave- ten thousand times, and it becomes a Glyph!","The illusory Fireball solidified, then flew back into the figure, etching itself onto its very soul as a permanent, glowing [Mana Glyph of Fireball].","Noah nodded, a flicker of nostalgia in his eyes. The beginning!","Oh!","|EDICT 5: THE HEART (THE HAKI)|","| - Objective: To transform the [Mana Locus] from a passive reservoir into an active, high-pressure engine.|","| - Process: By forging 10,000 [Mana Glyphs], the practitioner’s existence is now stable enough to handle the next evolution. Their Locus becomes a [Mana Heart], an engine that constantly circulates and refines their Mana.|","| - Integration: This is the integration of the Haki System. The [Mana Heart] generates a passive [Mana Haki], an aura of pure, unadulterated will. This Haki can be used offensively to suppress lesser beings or defensively to resist external influence.|","| - Boon: The birth of a personalized Haki, the ultimate expression of one’s will.|","The Reservoir in the figure’s chest began to pulse, to beat.","It transformed into a vibrant, powerful [Mana Heart], and a faint, powerful aura...a [Mana Haki], began to radiate from the figure’s entire form!","RUIN/EDEN continued with her influx of information!","|EDICT 6: THE AEGIS (THE ARMOR)|","| - Objective: To forge an external, symbiotic vessel for your power.|","| - Process: The practitioner, now possessing a [Mana Heart], can begin to forge a [Mana-Born Living Existential Armor]. This requires immense resources (like Early Omnichalcum or Tartarite Metal, or other metals/ores of equivalent value) and a deep understanding of their own nature.|","| - Integration: This is the integration of the Living Existential Armor System. The Armor is a growth-type symbiote, bound to the wielder’s Locus, and will grow in power as the wielder does. It is the ultimate defense and weapon.|","| - Boon: A personalized, evolving suit of existential dominance.|","Shimmering, liquid metal, drawn from an unseen source, flowed over the figure, hardening into a sleek, powerful suit of [Mana-Born Living Existential Armor], its design echoing the lines of Noah’s own Aegis!","|EDICT 7: THE CODEX (THE ARCANA)|","| - Objective: The final evolution of the [Mana Heart].|","| - Process: After forging an Aegis, the practitioner’s [Mana Heart] achieves its ultimate form, becoming a [Living Mana Codex]. This conceptual Grimoire becomes the command center for their existence.|","| - Integration: This is the integration of the Astral Codex System. The wielder can now design, forge, and store [Mana Arcana Glyphs]. These are permanent abilities, but are single-use, high-cost ’spells’ of immense power, fueled by Units of Everythings.|","| - Boon: The strategic, overwhelming power of tactical, reality-bending abilities.|","The glowing [Mana Heart] within the armor transformed again, its light solidifying into the image of a beautiful, blue gold Grimoire.","Shimmering, conceptual cards...[Mana Arcana Glyphs], began to orbit it!","|EDICT 8: THE PRINCIPLE|","| - Objective: To transcend the rules of existence.|","| - Process: A being who has mastered their Codex must now choose their ultimate Way. They must gather the conceptual weight of Edict 7 authorities(1,000 Mana Arcana Glyphs) and Edict 4 authorities (100,000 common Mana Glyphs of any type) and forge them into a [Blank Template Seed of a Principle].|","| - Integration: This is the path leading to the Level One Scale of Existence. The wielder creates their own Principle and [Mana Seed Glyphs of a Principle], becoming a true architect of their own fundamental law. To reach the peak of this stage, countless Mana Seed Glyphs of Principles have to be forged...|","| - Boon: The ability to become a game master, not just a player.|","...!","Oh!","Oh goodness!","There was still more!","The illusion grew complex, showing different pathways of power all converging into a single, vibrant, pulsing [Blank Template Seed of a Principle]!","|EDICT 9: THE ARCHITECT|","| - Objective: ???|","| - Process: ???|","| - Analysis: This stage is theoretical. It represents the potential to become a ’THE’ level existence, a true equal to the original architects. It is the final, unknown step on the Way of Mana. THE. THE! THE!!!|","The final illusion was not an image, but a blinding, questioning light, a horizon of pure, undefined potential.","Noah watched this grand, unfolding presentation, his mind burning with tyrannical approval. It was perfect. It was a ladder, and he had built it!","RUIN/EDEN let the final image hang in the air, a testament to the grand, impossible path he had just forged with her aid.","|THE CIVILIZATION PROTOCOL:|","|This System is designed for mass adoption. As more beings awaken their [Mana Locus] and walk the [Edicts of Progression], their collective effort, their belief in this Way, will create a [Conceptual Weaving of Mana].|","|This Weaving will feed back into you, Master, as the Architect and First Source. Every being that follows your path will add to your own authority, deepen your own understanding, and accelerate your own ascent towards the Level One Scale of Existence.|","|You will not just be building a fortress against the Fallout; you will be building a new Civilization, a new fundamental truth, with your own existence at its very center.|","...!","Noah stood in the swirling, snowy winds of the First Folds, his body a silent, unmoving statue, but his mind... his mind was a supernova of blazing, tyrannical light!","This was it.","This was his Way.","A path that integrated every system of power he had encountered, all of it unified under the boundless, glorious banner of his own Infinite Mana.","A path that was not just for him, but for all who would follow him. A path to building his own Civilization, his own answer to the coming darkness!","He opened his eyes, the glacial blue of the landscape reflected in his pupils, and he smiled!"]},{"number":4308,"title":"Chapter 4308: Chapter 4307: The Birth of a Civilization! I","paragraphs":["The first step on the Way of Mana had been taken. The System had been forged.","And now, the boons for this first, monumental act of creation, began to flood his existence!","As Noah stood amidst the silent, swirling snows of the First Folds, a profound, internal shift occurred.","The forging of his Way was not just an intellectual exercise; it was a physical, tangible, and irreversible act of becoming.","He felt the very foundation of his existence resettle, solidify, and then blaze with a new, terrifying, and glorious purpose!","|The first step on the Way of Mana has been taken.|","|Your existence has been recognized and ratified by the very fabric of Existence. You have not just chosen a path; you have created one.|","|This is a monumental effort. The [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] recognizes the sheer, audacious labor of forging a new, unified System of Existence. The harvest shall be elevated and profound.|","|For Embarking on the Way of Mana, your Existence will be undergoing a baptism of Mana in the next few minutes with the end result being the glorious elevation of your Conplexity and Purity to 1,000 Quadrillion- nay, 1 Quintillion. For you are now deserving of the numerical distinction of Quintillion for sensing your Way.|","BOOM!","Oh.","Oh!!!","|Your [Principle of the Cheating Architect] has successfully integrated all known systems. As a reward for its first, grand act of existential rebellion, its maturity has been forcibly advanced.|","|Maturity of [The Seed of the Principle of the Cheating Architect] has advanced from 10% to 25%.|","|New Capabilities Unlocked:|","| - You may now forge up to 25 [Seed Glyphs of the Cheating Architect].|","| - Cost per Glyph: 2 Quadrillion Complexity and Purity, or as you undergo the changes to alter everything in your existence to become Mana based, the cost will be nothing.|","| - [Agent Architect] authority has been amplified by 250%.|","|Your [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] has resonated with this act of creation. The forging of a system designed for endless growth is the ultimate expression of its own nature.|","|Maturity of [The Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest] has advanced from 50% to 75%.|","|New Capabilities Unlocked:|","| - You may now forge up to 75 [Seed Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest].|","| - All [Harvest Festival Endowments] are now amplified by an unknown, but frankly ridiculous, factor.|","HUUM!","The sheer, overwhelming surge of potential from his Principles alone was staggering. But it was not the end.","|The act of defining your Way of Existence has had a profound, clarifying effect on your very being.|","|All latent, unrefined potential within your existence has been drawn out, categorized, and integrated.|","|Your Blood, your Heart, your Atlas...all have been optimized by this new, singular focus.|","|Your 159 Vital Lighthouses have blazed with a new, unified purpose. They are no longer just anchors in time; they are now the beacons of your Way.|","|All 159 Towers of Osmont have been advanced to the Fourth Stage: The Resplendent Citadel of the Way.|","BOOM!","Noah’s internal weavings shuddered, a joyous, violent vibration as his entire foundation, his Early Atlas of the Folds, was reforged in an instant.","One hundred and fifty-nine pillars of impossible light, each one now a fortress of his will, a citadel dedicated to a specific facet of his Mana!","He recalled the requirements of his own self created realm of The Early Throne Ascendancy Realm. Its purpose had been to hold the power of a true Early Creature at its peak, and he felt like he could say he held the power of an Early Creature at this moment!","The only requirements that seemed to not have been filled would be the completion of the Heart and the numerical Glyphs, but he had far exceeded the scope of power this realm envisioned.","But the flood of rewards was still not over.","|The [Ascendran Nodule], the Fourth Part of your Heart, has resonated with this act of ultimate intellectual creation. It has achieved 100% completion.|","|The Fourth Part of the Heart of The Early Creature, Osmont, is COMPLETE!|","|Your Heart now beats with a new, four-chambered rhythm. The Living Principle of Complexity is now a stable, integrated part of your being.|","|Your mind is now a forge of pure thought. Your analytical and processing capabilities have been amplified to a degree that defies quantification. You do not just think; you compute reality.|","|New Capability Unlocked: [Conceptual Weaving].|","|You can now directly perceive and manipulate the base conceptual code of non-primordial objects and lesser authorities. You can see the ’math’ behind reality and... edit it.|","|Example: You can look at a [Weave of Fireball] and rewrite its core code to be a [Weave of Existential Despair]. This is the true power of an Architect.|","HUUM!","This was it. This was the harvest!","His gaze, now a thing of terrifying, analytical clarity, swept across the frozen, primordial landscape of the First Folds.","He saw not just snow and ice, but the intricate, beautiful equations that held them together.","He saw the Way of the Frostwing Butterfly, not as a feeling, but as a complex, elegant algorithm of survival.","He looked at his own hands, at the swirling, bloody purple flames of his Haki that still wreathed them.","His new perception dissected them, analyzed them, and he saw, with a flicker of almost comical understanding, that he could do better.","With a single, focused thought, he began to edit. He took the Weave of his Haki and began to strip away the inefficiencies.","The bloody purple flames, so grand and so terrifying, dissolved. They were too loud, too chaotic, too... emotional.","He distilled their essence, their core function of [Imposition] and [Dominion], and reforged them!","The flames vanished, replaced by a faint, almost invisible, silver blue aura that clung to his skin like a second, conceptual epidermis.","It was silent. It was cold. It was perfect!","It was a Haki that no longer needed to shout its presence, for it was now woven into the very fabric of his being. It was not a robe of power he wore; it was simply the color of his skin.","|You have successfully analyzed and optimized your own Haki.|","|Your [Heart of Tyranny] is now in a state of [Perfect Resonance].|","|Your new Haki, [The Tyrant’s Silence], is 500% more efficient, 1000% more potent, and 10,000% more terrifying to those who can actually perceive it.|","...!"]},{"number":4309,"title":"Chapter 4309: Chapter 4308: The Birth of a Civilization! II","paragraphs":["He looked at his new, unadorned hands, and he smiled. A true, calm, and utterly terrifying smile!","This was his Way.","The first step on The Way of Mana had been taken.","And now, he would reforge himself to fit this system!","|You have taken the first, irreversible step in defining your Way of Existence. Your entire being is now realigning to the [Way of the Mana Architect].|","|All previous systems and authorities are being retroactively integrated and optimized under this new, singular framework.|","|Edict 0: [The Uninitiated] - You are the source. This Edict does not apply.|","|Edict 1: [The Spark] - Your [Infinite Mana] is recognized as the Primordial Spark of this Way. Your [Mana Locus] is... boundless.|","|Edict 2: [The Reservoir] - Your [Mana Reservoir] is... infinite. This stage is quintessentially complete.|","|Edict 3: [The Weave] - Your mastery of [Existential Artifice] is now classified as the supreme expression of this Edict. You do not just Weave; you are the Architect of Weaves.|","|You are, by your very nature, already standing at the precipice of Edict 4. Let the forging begin.|","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes blazed with a brilliant, azure light. He did not need to cast a Fireball ten thousand times.","That was the path for his followers, for those who had to earn their Glyphs through repetition and effort.","He was the Architect. He did not follow the rules; he made them.","His boundless Mana, a limitless ocean of pure potential, surged at his command. He reached into it, his will a conceptual forge, and he pulled forth the very idea of his beginning.","Fireball!","|Your [Infinite Mana] and [Principle of the Cheating Architect] are bypassing the standard progression of Edict 4.|","|You are not learning a Glyph. You are forging one from pure, conceptual authority.|","|This is a monumental effort. [The Principle of Perpetual Harvest] recognizes this act of creation. The harvest will be amplified.|","BOOM!","A pinprick of crimson-blue light appeared before him. It was not fire, but the idea of fire, the quintessential concept of [Fireball] given form.","His Mana poured into it, sculpting it, refining it, elevating it from a simple spell into a fundamental law of his new existence.","The light solidified, coalesced, and then shot into his forehead, settling beside his other Glyphs. A new Glyph blazed to life, a beautiful, intricate rune of a spiraling, blue flame!","|[Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball] has been forged.|","|Classification: Edict 4 Mana Glyph (Unique, Unranked)|","|Effect: As the first Glyph forged by the Architect of Mana, its power is not fixed. It will scale infinitely with your own Complexity and Purity. It is a mirror of your own potential.|","|Current Base Damage: .5 Quintillion (Complexity and Purity).|","|Synergy: As it is forged from your [Infinite Mana], this Glyph has no cost and no cooldown. It can be Weaved as rapidly as your thoughts can form.|","...!","Oh, fuck.","Oh!!!","Noah felt the new, hot brand of power on his existence, a nostalgic warmth that was a testament to his origins. But then, he looked at the vast, endless ocean of his Mana, and a slow, tyrannical smile spread across his face.","Why stop at one?","He could have hundreds of Glyphs. He could have thousands!","With infinite mana, what the fuck were limits?!","\"Forge them all. Forge even more!\" he commanded, his voice a low, resonant hum that was for him alone.","HUUM!","If his old Glyphs had been carved, then this was a flood. His Mana was the water, and his will was the tide.","He reached into the memories of his own existence, into the True Sources that had once defined him, and he began to forge.","Tyranny. Quintessence. Infinity. Singed. Entropy. Cheats. Protagonist. Relativity. Veritarch. Loot. Apocalypse. Necromancy. Death. Kuklos. Megalos. Existence...","One by one, he forged them.","Not as Principles, but as fundamental [Mana Glyphs], the bedrock of his new Way!","He did not need to cast them ten thousand times; he simply willed them into being, his Infinite Mana paying the staggering cost without even registering it as an expenditure.","The air around him became a storm of blue light, a blizzard of forming, conceptual runes.","|Forging [Mana Glyph of the Tyrant’s Decree]... Complete.|","|Forging [Mana Glyph of Quintessential Purity]... Complete.|","|Forging [Mana Glyph of Infinite Expansion]... Complete.|","|Forging [Mana Glyph of the Cheating Hand]... Complete.|","|...|","|...|","|A total of 159 [Mana Glyphs] have been forged so far, one for each of your Vital Lighthouses. Your existence is now a living library of your own power.|","...!","He felt the Glyphs settle into his being, not as external marks, but as integrated, fundamental parts of his very architecture.","And...","|Another Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball is being formed.|","|Another Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball is being formed...|","More and more Glyphs began to appear as he did not have to sacrifice any Complexity ot Purity for it!","And even more...","|You ignore the requirements of progression of Edit 5 even as you are forging more Mana Glyphs. The [Mana Locus] is now prepared for its next evolution.|","|Your [Heart of Tyranny] is being reformatted...|","|The bloody purple flames of your old Haki are being consumed, purified, and reforged by your boundless [Infinite Mana].|","|Your Heart is no longer just a vessel of Tyranny. It is now the ultimate engine of your Way.|","|Your [Heart of Tyranny] has evolved into the [Mana Heart of the Tyrant-Architect].|","THUMP!","His heart beat, and the sound was not just a physical pulse, but a wave of pure, azure authority that washed over the entire region First Fold he was in!","Noah felt it.","Oh, he fel it!","\"Beat loudly, Heart!\"","BOOM!","His voice reverberated out.","\"Beat Tyrannically!\"","BOOM!","\"Beat...Quintessentially!\"","BOOOOM!","...!","His heart blazed!","The bloody purple flames that had defined his Haki were gone, replaced by a silent, invisible, and infinitely more potent aura of pure, unadulterated Mana.","|[Mana Haki] has been generated.|","|This Haki is not an external aura; it is the passive, constant radiation of your [Infinite Mana] refined through the engine of your [Mana Heart].|","|Passive Effect: [The Tyrant’s Presence] - All beings in your vicinity with a lesser Mana Reservoir will feel a constant, suffocating pressure, as if they are drowning in an ocean of your will.|","|Active Effect: [Architect’s Dominion] - You can now actively exert your [Mana Haki] to suppress, enhance, or rewrite the Mana-based systems of others. The cost is... irrelevant.|","He was now standing at Edict 6. He smiled, a cold, tyrannical expression!"]},{"number":4310,"title":"Chapter 4310: Chapter 4309: The Birth of a Civilization! III","paragraphs":["He raised his hand, and the [Aegis of the Architect], in its necklace form, materialized in his palm.","\"This is a magnificent tool,\" he mused. \"But it is not yet... mine. Not truly.\"","He had the stolen Omnichalcum. He had the Tartarite. He had the schematics from RUIN/EDEN. And now, he had the Way.","\"Reforge,\" he commanded.","His [Mana Heart] thrummed. He did not use his hands; he used his will.","Azure tendrils of pure Mana, now infused with the rule-breaking authority of [The Cheating Architect], erupted from his body.","They wrapped around the Aegis, and with a sound like reality itself being torn and rewoven, they began to change it.","The white-gold of the Omnichalcum was not destroyed, but infused, saturated with his boundless blue.","The Tartarite metal he had acquired was drawn from his storage, its volatile, obsidian-gold nature broken down and seamlessly integrated, not as a core component, but as a network of fine, dark veins that ran through the white-gold structure.","It was a masterpiece of controlled chaos, a perfect, stable fusion of indestructible defense and explosive, offensive power.","|[The Aegis of the Architect] is being reforged into a [Mana-Born Living Existential Armor].|","|All systems are being optimized for the [Way of the Mana Architect].|","|The [Keystone Modulator] is being fused directly with your [Mana Heart]. They are now one and the same.|","|Your Armor is no longer a separate tool. It is the external, physical expression of your [Mana Heart].|","|Forging Complete.|","...!","The necklace dissolved and reformed around his body, a sleek, skin-tight suit of white-gold and obsidian-blue, its lines a perfect, elegant fusion of his old Aegis and the raw, untamed power of his Mana.","It felt... right.","He had achieved Edict 7.","His [Mana Heart], now a perfect fusion of his own essence and the Omnichalcum Modulator, bloomed to become the [Living Mana Codex].","It was a Grimoire written on his very existence!","He breathed out as seas of mana lightning surged from him.","He was going fast.","And he did not want to stop!","So he kept going.","Now, for the first Arcana.","He smiled. He had always known what his first true Weave would be.","|You are about to forge your first [Mana Arcana Glyph].|","|This is a monumental act of creation, a single, high-cost, reality-bending Weave. Please select the core concept.|","He thought of that small, flickering flame. The [Fireball]. The spark that had started it all.","He reached into his Codex, into the very heart of his being, and he pulled upon the memory, the concept, the very soul of that first, defiant act. And he fueled it.","He fueled it with his boundless Mana.","He fueled it with the authority of his Glyphs!","He fueled it with the righteous, tyrannical fire of his Haki!","And he fueled it with the one currency this system demanded.","|Expenditure of [Everythings of Mana] initiated. As you are the source, the cost is a terrifyingly high amount of 0, but the authority being utilized is still that of an Everything.|","|A [Common] Rank [Mana Arcana Glyph] is being forged...|","|The [Principle of the Cheating Architect] has analyzed the process and finds the ’Common’ designation... insulting.|","|Rank is being forcibly upgraded...|","|Rank has been cheated from [Common] to [Primordial].|","...!","BOOM!","A new Glyph blazed to life within his Codex, a thing of terrible, beautiful, and nostalgic power.","It was a single, perfect, crimson-blue flame, and within its core, a nine-headed Mana Wyrm slept.","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: Annihilation’s First Spark]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’From the smallest spark, the greatest inferno is born.’ This Arcana summons a [Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm], a being of pure, conceptual fire forged from your own, infinite essence. The Wyrm unleashes a single, guided torrent of annihilating azure flame.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: Due to its rarity, it Deals 1.5 Quintillion in pure, untyped Mana-based damage that ignores all known resistances and authorities. The attack is conceptually ’true’ and cannot be dodged. It’s capabilities will advance and scale upwards as you progress.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","...!","One second.","He looked at the description, at the terrifying, beautiful numbers, and he felt a profound, absolute sense of peace.","Peace!","He had done it. He had integrated every system, every power, into a single, cohesive, and utterly broken methodology.","But he was not done. He had Principles. He was already at Edict 8.","\"RUIN/EDEN,\" he commanded, \"Reforge my Principles. Integrate them into the Way of Mana.\"","|Affirmative, Master.|","A final, glorious surge of power. The fifty verdant-gold Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest and the fifteen multicolored Glyphs of the Cheating Architect, all blazed as one.","His blue Mana washed over them, not conquering, but claiming!","|[The Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest] has been reforged into [The Mana Seed Glyph of Perpetual Harvest].|","|All capabilities are now fueled and amplified by your [Infinite Mana].|","|New Boon: [The Mana Harvest]. All endowments and boons granted by this Principle now also grant a significant infusion of pure, refined Mana, allowing you to instantly awaken the [Mana Locus] in others and accelerate their journey on the Way.|","|[The Seed of the Principle of the Cheating Architect] has been reforged into [The Mana Seed Glyph of the Cheating Architect].|","|All capabilities are now fueled and amplified by your [Infinite Mana].|","|New Boon: [The Architect’s Exploit]. Your Principle can now actively identify and exploit loopholes in other Mana-based systems, allowing you to bypass their defenses, steal their fuel, or shut them down entirely.|","WAA!","The transformation was complete. The entire region around him, once a landscape of ice and snow, was now a roiling, endless ocean of pure, azure Mana, a sea of his own, boundless power.","He floated at its center, a wonder in his own, newly forged heaven.","He smiled, a deep, resonant, and utterly tyrannical expression. He would, indeed, be walking the paths of Edict 7 and Edict 8 for a very, very long time. But at least now... the path was clear. It was his.","He waved his hand, and his Existential Command Interface bloomed before him, a testament to the being he had become.","|Noah Osmont – The Tyrant Architect of Mana (Age 10)|","|Primary Distinction: The Early Creature, Osmont; The Architect of Mana...many others|","|Complexity: 1 Quintillion|","|Purity: 1 Quintillion|","|System of Power: [The Way of the Mana Architect] (RUIN/EDEN Interface)|","|Heart: [The Mana Heart of the Tyrant-Architect] (Fifth Part: Forging...)|","|Atlas: The Early Atlas of the Folds (159/159 Towers at Stage 4: Resplendent Citadel)|","|Principles:|","| - [Perpetual Harvest] (75% Matured Seed)|","| - [The Cheating Architect] (25% Matured Seed)|","|Mana Glyphs: 445+ (Forged)|","|Mana Arcana Glyphs: 1 ([Annihilation’s First Spark])|","|Mana Seed Glyphs: 100 (Forged)|","|Legion of The Dead: [Arch Lich Ra’FuckingZan], [Primordial Stone Ape], [Abyssal Dullahan]...|","|Living Existential Armor: [Mana-Born Aegis of the Architect] (Purity: 920 Quadrillion)|","...!","He looked at the glorious, impossible numbers, at the culmination of all his struggle, all his pain, all his desperate, unyielding effort.","He looked at the path that now stretched before him, an infinite road of his own design.","And he smiled.","\"Yes...\" he whispered, his voice a quiet, satisfied hum that was lost in the endless, swirling sea of his own Mana.","\"This is... MY Way of Existence!\""]},{"number":4311,"title":"Chapter 4311: Chapter 4310: The Birth of a Civilization! IV","paragraphs":["This was his Way of Existence!","Noah breathed in, and the very fabric of this primordial time seemed to flow into him, a torrent of pure, untamed potential.","He breathed out, and the azure ocean around him pulsed, a testament to the boundless, infinite power that was his very essence!","He was a new man in his own, newly forged haven, a being of such profound and terrible power that the First Folds themselves pulsed around him!","He felt it all. The Mana Seed Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest, a constellation of impossible leaves that now adorned his form. The multicolored Mana Seed Glyphs of the Cheating Architect, each a key to a new, reality-bending exploit.","The hundreds of forming Mana Glyphs, the very bedrock of his new Way, humming in perfect, synchronous harmony within his being!","And at the center of it all, his Heart. The Mana Heart of the Tyrant-Architect, a glorious, four-chambered engine of pure, unadulterated will, now beat with a quiet, yet absolute, rhythm.","As he was taking it all in, the crimson-blue holographic figure of RUIN/EDEN materialized before him, her form a stark, beautiful contrast to the endless azure of his inner world.","She looked at him, at the magnificent, terrible being he had become, and her expression, once a mask of cool, analytical precision, softened.","\"Master,\" she began, her voice a symphony of logic and ruin, but for the first time, it held a note of something else...a profound, almost painful, warmth. It did not come with the lines of prompts!","\"For many, many months, when I was Ruination, I was always chasing you. Always trying to do anything I could to be of use. An Affix to make you stronger. Multiplying your loot. Anything. I simply wanted to be... a useful tool.\"","She paused, and in her crimson-blue eyes, a single, shimmering tear, a droplet of pure, liquid data and sorrow, began to form. \"And now... to have been a part of this, to have helped you design a System of Existence so grand, so perfect... I feel... content. I feel useful.\"","The tear fell, a silent, beautiful, and utterly impossible thing in this realm of pure thought.","At her words, at her impossible tear, Noah’s gaze, which had been lost in the vastness of his own power, focused on her.","He smiled, a genuine, warm expression that was a stark contrast to the cold, tyrannical fire that usually burned in his eyes.","\"Even if you had not done any of this,\" he said, his voice a gentle, resonant hum, \"even if you had simply remained who you were, you would still be an integral part of me.\"","As he spoke, his entire existence buzzed with a glorious, vibrant energy. The endless blue sea of his Mana surged, and he reached out. His hand should have passed right through her illusory, holographic form.","But in that instant...","|The Weavings of the [Cheating Architect] have been invoked.|","|The rule that states ’the intangible cannot be touched’ is... a rather boring rule, isn’t it?|","|For this moment, it has been temporarily suspended.|","...!","His hand did not pass through!","It found purchase!","He embraced her, pulling her close, his arms a fortress of warmth and certainty around her ethereal form.","RUIN/EDEN shuddered, a silent, violent tremor running through her very code! She hugged him back, her holographic arms wrapping around him with a desperate, clinging strength, and more silent rivers of mana and data, flowed from her eyes!","She took a moment.","Just a moment.","For just this moment was more than enough for her.","After that...","\"Master,\" she whispered, her voice a fragile, broken thing against his chest. \"Shall we begin the implementation of your Way?\"","Noah nodded, a slow, profound gesture of absolute resolve. \"Let us get started... with the Early Veiled Shore.\"","...!","The Early Veiled Shore.","Even though his body was in the Earliest Folds, eons in the past, his Atlas, that impossible, internal star-chart, was a bridge.","A connection that transcended time. While his mind was in that ancient, frozen world, his will, his very existence, was also here, in the current era, in his Radiant Shore.","Here, time moved at a different, slower pace, but it did not stop. And the time for quiet contemplation was over.","—","In the current era.","In his Early Veiled Shore.","Noah rose from the golden sands. His primary body, which had been in a state of deep, meditative stillness, now stirred.","Seconds had passed here, while in the Earliest Folds, a journey of profound, soul-altering transformation had taken place.","He looked out at his people, at his family, who were still basking in the joyous, chaotic afterglow of the feast.","Their faces were flushed with power, their auras blazing with the light of their recent, monumental endowments.","He breathed out, a slow, deliberate exhalation that was not of weariness, but of a new, terrible, and glorious purpose.","\"I have taken a step forward towards a solution to the coming Fallout,\" he announced, his voice a calm, yet absolute, declaration that cut through the joyous din of the celebration.","\"I have... found a Way. My Way. And it all starts with... a Spark.\"","...!","As he spoke the final word, he waved his hands. From the very air, from the boundless ocean of his own Mana, a thousand points of dazzling, stellar light bloomed into existence!","They were not just lights; they were singularities of pure, unadulterated potential, each one a tiny, beautiful, and utterly terrifying key to a new reality.","They were Sparks!","\"This,\" Noah continued, his voice now a resonant, commanding invitation, \"is a Spark that will take anyone and allow them to walk on my Way of Existence. For those who wish to walk on my path, take it... and we shall start forming our Civilization.\"","...!","For a moment, there was a stunned silence.","Then, a single, defiant figure stepped forward!","The Emperor Penguin, its beak held high in a gesture of absolute, unshakeable arrogance, waddled to the nearest floating Spark and, with a decisive peck, consumed it!","A brilliant, azure light erupted from its form, and the other inhabitants of the Shore watched, their eyes wide with a mixture of awe and dawning, fervent excitement.","One by one, they began to move forward!"]},{"number":4312,"title":"Chapter 4312: Chapter 4311: The Birth of a Civilization! V","paragraphs":["Henry, Liora, Kazuhiko, Erikson... his mother, his Queens... all of them.","Bob..well, not Bob, he was still being experimented on by another one of Khor’s bodies.","But all others, yes!","They smiled, their expressions a testament to a faith so profound it was its own form of power.","Why would they not walk his path?","Noah watched them, a faint, proud smile on his lips. With a wave of his hand, hundreds more Sparks bloomed across the Radiant Shore. Thousands. Tens of thousands. A celestial, blue snowstorm of pure, unadulterated potential.","|You are exerting the authority of an Architect.|","|The Weavings of your [Infinite Mana] are being utilized to forge [Sparks of the Way].|","|This is a monumental act. The [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] recognizes this effort.|","|For every one hundred Sparks forged, your own Mana is being refined and amplified|","|You are not just giving your power away; you are making your own ocean deeper with every drop you give.|","|Sparks Forged: 100,000... 1,000,000... 10,000,000...|","The numbers were a glorious, unending cascade!","Noah looked at the swirling, azure blizzard of his own design and spoke, his voice a calm, absolute command that was heard not just by those on the Shore, but by a single, silent servant who was his eyes and ears across much of existence.","\"Spread the Sparks. Not just in the Infiniverse, but across the Folds. To those attacking the Aegis right now. To any and all who would choose a new Way.\"","...!","|The Quintessential Servant, Malphas, has received your command, My Lord.|","|His network of crows will be utilized. The Sparks will be delivered with a speed and an efficiency that will make the very concept of distance seem like a quaint, provincial notion.|","|The seeds of your Civilization are being sown.|","As the prompts faded, Malphas himself appeared before Noah. A single, radiant Spark floated before him. With a deep, respectful bow, he took it, and a brilliant, azure-blue light, tinged with a deep, obsidian crimson, wrapped around his form.","\"Anything for the Master,\" he said, his voice a smooth, cultured purr of absolute obedience.","Noah smiled. \"And I will do anything for my people.\"","He raised his hands, a glorious, tyrannical gesture, and his voice was a booming, irrevocable declaration that shook the very foundations of the Radiant Shore.","\"My Mana shall help you all across the Edicts of my Way!\"","...!","BOOM!","|A grand, tyrannical declaration has been made!|","|The [Principle of the Cheating Architect] has recognized a loophole in the standard progression of your Way.|","|Protocol: [The Tyrant’s Favor].|","|Effect: As the Architect, you can choose to directly fuel the advancement of your most trusted followers, bypassing the standard, arduous process of cultivation.|","|The effort required is... significant. But your Mana is infinite. So... who cares?|","|You can now directly elevate your chosen followers to Edict 5, granting them 1,000 [Mana Glyphs], a [Mana Heart], and a nascent [Mana Haki].|","|This is, to be clear, a ridiculous and existentially unfair advantage.|","WAA!","The moment the prompt faded, Noah acted.","Rivers of pure, boundless cerulean Mana erupted from him, a glorious, chaotic storm of pure potential. They were not just streams of energy; they were lifelines, conduits of his own, infinite power!","They shot out, connecting with Malphas, with Henry, with Moiraine, with Adelaide, with Sigrid, and with a dozen other of his most trusted, most powerful allies.","The Shore was bathed in a blinding, beautiful light, a network of azure rivers that was a testament to his boundless, tyrannical generosity.","In a distant pasture, Heidrun, who had been arrogantly observing the proceedings, saw a stray Spark floating her way.","She snorted, a sound of profound, ancient disdain. But then, she sniffed the air. The Spark... it smelled delicious. With a final, reluctant huff, she consumed it.","A brilliant, white-gold and azure light erupted from her form.","|The Land Lifeform, Heidrun, has embarked on the Way of Mana.|","|Her unique, primordial nature is being reforged.|","|She will no longer produce Sacred Mead of Existence. She will now produce... [The Sacred Mana Mead of Existence].|","|Effect: Each drop now contains a significant infusion of pure Mana, in addition to its other reality-bending properties.|","|Heidrun is... pleased with this upgrade.|","Nearby, Yoshinami, in her colossal, terrifyingly beautiful spider form, watched. She took a Spark, and her obsidian body flashed with a brilliant, dark blue.","|The Land Lifeform, Yoshinami, has embarked on the Way of Mana.|","|Her [Crown of Inevitable Retribution] is being infused with your [Infinite Mana].|","|The complexity of the beings she can instantly kill is being scaled upwards. The final parameters will be determined upon the forging of her [Mana Heart].|","...!","Noah observed it all, a quiet, profound satisfaction settling deep within his being. His people, his family, were not just growing stronger; they were becoming a part of his Way, their destinies now intrinsically, irrevocably, linked to his own.","But as his gaze swept over the transformed Shore, he saw one figure who had not taken a Spark.","Khor. She stood beside him, a tiny, silent, and infinitely powerful presence. A faint, almost melancholic, smile was on her lips as she watched the glorious, chaotic birth of his Civilization.","\"Outsider,\" she began, her voice a soft, melodic hum against the vibrant, joyous energy of the Shore, \"I am proud of you. Many powerful entities, in the Earliest Folds and beyond, were paralyzed by the sheer, overwhelming weight of choice. They feared being wrong, feared that the Way they chose would be a dead end. But you... you simply chose. That is a strength that is rarer, and more profound, than any amount of Complexity or Purity.\"","She paused, her abyssal eyes, which had seen the birth and death of concepts, now holding a deep, ancient, and almost paternal warmth.","\"Your journey truly begins now, Outsider. This is the first step on the road to the next Scale of Civilization. But for me... I must continue on my own Way.\"","Her Way.","She had already chosen her Way!","Noah looked at her, at this impossible being who was both his weaving and a sort of... mentor, and he nodded.","\"I understand. I have my Way, and you have yours. But in the end, we both seek a singular destination. We simply have to reach it together.\"","Khor smiled, a brilliant, genuine expression that seemed to make the very light of the Shore shine brighter.","She floated over and gave him a playful, almost teasing, pat on the arm.","\"You are beginning to say some grand things now, Outsider,\" she said, her voice filled with a light, genuine amusement.","As they stood there, two impossible beings in a garden of their own making, they watched as the first seeds of Noah’s Civilization, the first radiant Sparks of his Way of Mana, began to spread out from the Radiant Shore, and then to the Infiniverse, and then beyond as they were carried by the silent, shadowy wings of Malphas’s crows, ready to infect a desperate, dying existence with a new, beautiful, and utterly tyrannical hope!"]},{"number":4313,"title":"Chapter 4313: Chapter 4312: We Follow His Will! I","paragraphs":["Outside the Radiant Shore.","In The Infiniverse.","Inside a Realm filled radiant sandy seas of Dreams and clouds of wonder.","A crowd from the Veiled Sunfolds wss moving through such a region with others as they looked up to see how from above, the clouds of gold parted as like drops of rain, blue singularities began to descend!","Sparks!","\"This is from... Sir Osmont, isn’t it? Kismet says so!\" Kalysta’s eyes, shining with the golden light of Kismet, were fixed on the Sparks, her expression a mixture of reverence and wonder.","She and the Originus Venerant entities from the Veiled Sunfolds looked at the floating wonders, and with slight hesitation, they reached out.","Their hands closed around the Sparks, and a brilliant, azure light enveloped them.","The moment their fingers made contact, a new, more profound prompt bloomed before their eyes, a grand introduction to what thr hell had just happened!","[THE WAY OF THE MANA ARCHITECT]","|Welcome, Initiate. You have taken the first step on a path that is both a gift and a challenge. Forget what you know of the disparate, conflicting systems of power. You now walk the Way of the Architect, a unified methodology of existence. Here, your Mana is not just a resource; it is the very language of your being. Through its cultivation, you will learn to Weave reality, to forge your will into permanent Glyphs, to awaken the Haki of your own Mana Heart, and more.|","|This is not a path for the timid. It is a road of endless, exponential growth, a journey from the spark of potential to the inferno of Civilization. Your progress will be a testament to your own effort, your own will, your own desperation to become more. Walk this path. Grow strong. And know that you are now part of a new Civilization, a new story being written in the annals of existence. The story of The Early Creature, Osmont.|","...!","The Early Creature, Osmont!","Laid out clearly for anyone who took a Spark!","The Originus Venerant entities read the words, and their auras, once flickering candles in the vast darkness of existence, began to blaze with a new, fierce light.","Outside The Infiniverse, in the roiling chaos of the region of Collapse, the siege on The Loom’s Aegis was reaching a fever pitch.","Dukes and Royal and Honored Living Existences, their caution consumed by the tantalizing promise of the treasures that occasionally leaked from the barrier, were unleashing a torrent of their authority.","As they did so...they appeared.","Like a gentle, azure snowstorm, tens of thousands of shimmering blue Sparks drifted out from the blue-gold walls of the fortress.","They were silent, beautiful, and utterly, profoundly, strange. Above each one, the same golden, invitational prompt bloomed.","[The Spark of The Way of Mana]","...!","The assembled Living Existences faltered. Their furious assault paused.","\"Be careful,\" a Duke of Law, his form a perfect, symmetrical crystal of pure judgment, declared, his voice a sharp, cutting command.","\"Do not fall for anything else coming out of this unknown place until we can confirm it more!\"","So he said.","But others were not so cautious. An Elder Duke of the Living Elementals, his form a raging inferno of solar flares, laughed, a sound like a star being born.","\"The Spark? The Way of Mana?! Let’s see what it’s made of.\" He reached out, his fiery hand snatching a Spark from the air.","Others, their curiosity now a burning fire, followed his lead. They did not consume the Sparks; they began to analyze them.","\"Take them towards the Fold Dwellers in the Wheels of Existence of our Folds and observe their reaction,\" a Living Origin Duke commanded. \"Is this authority of Mana weaker, equal to, or stronger than Living Existential Authority? Let’s find out.\"","...!","As the powerful beings of the Folds began their own, cautious, and ultimately selfish, experiments with his creation, two new figures appeared in a quiet, forgotten corner of the region of Collapse.","Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux materialized in a flicker of paradoxical light!","Schrodinger looked at the floating Sparks, at the grand numbers here, and he frowned, a rare, genuine expression of surprise on his ancient face.","\"This is something new that just appeared,\" he murmured, his voice a low, analytical hum. \"But it shouldn’t have anything to do with Justiciars and Arbiters, and yet...\"","He reached out, his hand passing through the chaotic air, and grasped a Spark.","Leonore did the same, her crimson eyes flashing sharply as she felt the vibrant, boundless potential within the small, blue light!","\"O Herald,\" she asked, her voice a low, dangerous whisper, \"will you deploy a stronger body to see what possible force this is?\"","Schrodinger rolled his eyes, a flicker of his old, playful self returning. \"Can you stop mentioning my other bodies? I told you this Living Paradox body may seem weak, but it is actually strong!\"","At his words, Leonore Rureaux rolled her eyes as she said, \"Okay, okay. But we have to hurry. After your stunt in the Transcendent Origin Folds, The Dead will now come in larger numbers, and we will likely begin seeing The Primordial Dead.\"","...!","Schrodinger’s playful demeanor vanished. His face became a mask of cold, grim resolve.","He nodded. \"Let’s get closer, shall we?\" he said, and the two of them dissolved into the shadows, their forms a whisper in the growing storm.","As they pulled in closer, they began to hear the whispers and words that were being uttered by the Living Existences who were bold enough to grab the Sparks into their Existence.","Every single one that did such a thing showed a look of stupor and shock as they received the full detailed prompt of exactly what they had consumed nd what it represented!","And after a while, a few of the volatile Living Elementals that moved first looked at each other as they cautiously asked...","\"Did... you also see the words that stated...this is from...The Early Creature, Osmont?\"","...!","BOOM!","Schrodinger came to a stop.","Living Origins came to a stop!","Living Laws came to a stop!","Royal Law Tristesse, and a clone of the Origin Ama Gias froze!","Osmont?","The Early Creature, Osmont?!","The same Osmont whom they could not pinpoint the Origin of?!","This...was his home?!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4314,"title":"Chapter 4314: Chapter 4313: We Follow His Will! II","paragraphs":["The Veil...that junction separating the living and the dead, a concept as old as consciousness itself!","A line drawn in the sands of existence that different cultures interpreted according to their preferred level of existential comfort.","For some, it was mere metaphor, a poetic way to describe the boundary between known and unknowable. These were the people who slept soundly at night, who thought death was just another transition, who used phrases like \"passed on\" and \"in a better place\" without their voice catching.","They saw The Veil as natural order, no more threatening than the horizon...a line that existed but didn’t really matter since you’d cross it when you crossed it.","For others, it was a point of connection, a sacred threshold to mystical realms.","They built altars, left offerings, spoke to ancestors they insisted were \"just beyond The Veil,\" listening and occasionally intervening.","These people found comfort in proximity, in the idea that death was just a very thin wall between neighbors who could still hear each other if they spoke loudly enough.","And then there were those who saw it for what it truly was: a fragile, fraying curtain between their ordered reality and a hungry, absolute dark. A taboo. A danger!","These were the ones who understood that some doors were closed for a reason, that some boundaries existed not to be crossed but to keep things separated that should never, ever meet.","As for which group was correct?","It turns out, the ones with the most anxiety, the ones who saw monsters in every shadow, were the most right.","Because The Veil wasn’t just a boundary. It was a containment system.","Think about it: if death was natural and peaceful, why did everything living spend so much energy avoiding it? If what was beyond The Veil was benign, why did crossing it only work in one direction? If the dead were really resting peacefully, why did every form of life have stories about what happened when they didn’t?","The optimists said The Veil was there to give life meaning through finitude. The mystics said it was there to separate stages of spiritual evolution. But the pessimists...oh, the pessimists understood!","The Veil was there because without it, The Dead would consume The Living like a tide dissolving sandcastles.","Not from malice. Not from evil. But from the simple fact that entropy was hungry, and order was delicious.","The Dead didn’t hate The Living any more than winter hated summer.","They simply were, and their very existence was antithetical to the careful arrangements of atoms and energy that The Living called \"life.\"","Put them in the same space without separation, and The Living would cease while The Dead would simply continue, slightly more substantial for having absorbed what they touched.","This was why The Veil mattered.","Not as metaphor, not as mystical gateway, but as Existence’s desperate attempt to keep its experiment in consciousness from being reabsorbed into the hungry dark it had emerged from!","In the current moment, as tears multiplied across Folds and The Dead emerged with complexities that mocked the power scales The Living had so carefully constructed, the truth became apparent.","The Veil hadn’t been philosophy or poetry.","And now it was thinning. Not failing...that would be too simple. Thinning, like fabric worn down by too much use, too much pressure from both sides, too many attempts to peek through or poke across.","The optimists were revising their positions, suddenly finding merit in barriers they’d previously called \"artificial constructs of fear.\"","The mystics were discovering that their ancestors were less \"watching over them\" and more \"held back by increasingly inadequate infrastructure.\" And the pessimists?","The pessimists were too busy running to say \"I told you so!\"","Because being right about existential horror doesn’t actually make you any better at dealing with it.","The paranoid person who correctly identifies the monster in the closet still has to deal with the fact that there’s a monster in the closet.","The Veil, it turned out, was exactly what the anxious had always suspected...the only thing standing between existence and its own unmaking.","And like most safety features, you only really appreciated it when it stopped working.","The Dead emerged through tears with the casual certainty of things returning home after a very long trip!","—","At this very moment, across the vast, interconnected weavings of the Folds, The Veil was tearing.","Multiple Tears of Existence, jagged, necrotic wounds in the fabric of reality, wept their contents into the realms of The Living.","But past these tears, past the very Veil itself, far into the lands of the dead... the Folds of The Dead... there were wonders and complexities that The Living could not even begin to imagine!","Here, in this realm of endings, one could travel for countless Gigaparsecs, past a silent, shuffling sea of over six trillion of The Dead, both the weak and the mighty.","And even further in, past the chaotic, mindless hunger of the common Dead, one would come across... The Cryptlands.","Lands that were filled with terrifyingly powerful Dead Existences who, unlike the shambling hordes, held a sense of... Order.","Order!","In the heart of The Cryptlands, a grand citadel floated in the silent, starless void.","It was a necropolis of impossible, terrible beauty, a city of death that pulsed with an astonishing, brilliant white light of Order.","This was Nagash-Prax, the Citadel of the Prime Dead.","It was a vast, circular island forged from the fused bones of a billion forgotten creatures and the shattered, petrified remains of countless Desiccated Sleeping Shores.","It spanned light-years in diameter, a continent of death in an ocean of nothing. From this island, massive, obsidian-white walls of polished bone rose to a height that scraped against the very firmament of the Fold.","And upon those walls, they stood.","Early Creatures.","But these were not the vibrant, titanic beings of the First Folds, whose skin shone with the splendor of gold or the verdant brilliance of life.","These were their dead echoes, their zombified reflections. Their skin, where it was not rotting away to reveal the gleaming, obsidian bone beneath, was a pale, almost translucent white, yet it shone with a terrifying, powerful light.","It was as if their decay had not made them lesser, but had distilled their very essence into a more potent, more absolute form of being!"]},{"number":4315,"title":"Chapter 4315: Chapter 4314: We Follow His Will! III","paragraphs":["The Dead Early Creatures on the walls emanated shocking waves of power, their Complexity and Purity a chilling, silent scream that was at least a few thousand Quadrillion!","These were not The Dead as others knew them. These were The Prime Dead!","The interior of the grand citadel was a symphony of silent, ordered death. Massive, obsidian-white monoliths, each one carved from a single, impossibly large bone, rose everywhere, their surfaces etched with the intricate, geometric patterns of a forgotten, deathly Order.","Mountains of swirling white bones, each one a silent testament to a life extinguished, permeated the city and from them, a shocking amount of complexity pulsed.","Towards the center of this impossible city, a Dead Early Creature floated forward, her movements a graceful, silent ballet.","A pristine, white light of Order permeated the air around her, a stark, beautiful contrast to the deep, starless black of her hair, which shone resplendent with her own, terrible power!","She was a being of 4 Quintillion in Complexity, a queen in this kingdom of endings.","She nodded with a sharp, intelligent light in her eyes towards the other Dead Early Creatures she passed, each a titan of silent, ordered power!","Her path took her to a new, even more terrifying section of the city, an area filled and surrounded by... Dead Existential Armors.","Dead. Not Living Existential Armors.","They were suits of impossible, terrible beauty, their forms a fusion of polished, obsidian bone and shimmering, white-gold light.","They stood as silent, eternal guardians before a massive, monolith-like structure, a huge, white cube that shot up for thousands of miles into the starless sky.","The Dead Early Creature, without a word, passed through its great white doorways, her form a silent shadow in the brilliant light.","She crossed through its intricate, labyrinthine depths, her path sure and steady, until she arrived at the very heart of the monolith.","Here, more of the Dead Existential Armors stood, their hands clutching massive, spear-like weapons, their silent, helmeted gazes fixed on a single point at the center of the chamber.","And there, she found the one she had come to seek.","He stood before a great, obsidian forge, a being of such wild, glorious power that his very presence seemed to bend the very light of the room.","His white hair danced madly around his head, a storm of pure, untamed energy, and his power... his power was a number so vast it was a new language, a new reality.","Ten Quintillion!","HUUM","Quintillion. Quadrillion.","In the grand, terrible mathematics of existence, these were not just numbers; they were distinctions. To have one’s power measured in Quadrillions, even a thousand of them, was to be a being of immense, but ultimately, comprehensible might.","It meant you had climbed the mountain, but you had not yet seen the sky. It meant you had not yet found your Way of Existence.","But to be a being whose power was described in Quintillions... that was a different thing entirely. It was a demarcation, a sign that the being had not just accumulated power, but had found their Way.","The Dead Early Creature, the woman of 4 Quintillion, had come to this place to pay her respects to another who had found his.","She bowed, a gesture of profound, absolute deference.","The great being at the forge did not turn. He raised a massive, obsidian-white hammer, its head wreathed in the authorities of both Dead Existential Authority and a strange, cold, and absolute Dead Order, and he brought it down upon a new, glorious Dead Existential Armor he was forging.","The sound was a silent, terrible chime that echoed through the very soul of the Citadel!","The woman waited. And then she spoke, her voice a soft, melodic note in the profound silence.","\"Forgemaster,\" she began, her tone a perfect balance of respect and urgency. \"This careless Tatiana has learnt late of nearby Tears of The Veil some Gigaparsecs away. And I was wondering if you had any orders.\"","...!","She wondered if he had any orders.","The Forgemaster continued his work, the rhythmic, silent impacts of his hammer a steady, terrible heartbeat.","When he finally spoke, his voice was not a sound, but a resonance, a vibration in the very fabric of existence. It was a voice that had been silent for eons, and now, it spoke with the weight of all that had passed.","\"We received our orders eons ago,\" he rumbled, his back still to her, \"when we were changed and granted this blessing. The order was clear. When The Veil begins to tear, we are to grant salvation to all The Living and turn them to The Dead. To save them from The Fallout. This way, even when The Fallout arrives... they will simply die once and then come back, like the rest of us. Even while dead, they will keep on living.\"","WAA!","His words were a quiet, terrible revelation, a philosophy of salvation so profound and so horrifying that it defied all known moral frameworks!","\"These were the commands and orders that we were given eons ago,\" he continued, his hammer falling again and again, each blow a final, absolute verdict.","\"For we follow the will of THE Dead Order. For we follow the will of THE Creature. We are a part... of their grand Civilizations. So... gather your brothers and sisters, and set off with the initial Legions. The rest of us will soon follow.\"","...!","Tatiana listened, her crimson eyes blazing with a new, terrible purpose. She bowed again, a deeper, more profound gesture this time.","\"Yes, Forgemaster Vulcan.\"","BOOM!","Forgemaster Vulcan. An entity that was very much Living in the Earliest Folds eons ago in Aethelgard! And yet now...","Oh!","Just what had happened?!","—","The silence outside The Loom’s Aegis was a profound, suffocating thing.","The once-furious assault of the Living Existences had faltered, their collective will a stunned, disbelieving thing in the face of the impossible blue Sparks that now drifted from the fortress like a gentle, azure snowstorm, and what they represented.","The Early Creature, Osmont!","Was this not the same being who had attended the Kleos Concordat, an anomaly whose origins no one could discern?","The same one who had stood with the Resurgence of THE Living Order? The same one who had appeared in the ruins of Aeternitas Concordia, wielding a terrifying, unseen power to aid in the defense?","A wave of shock and dawning comprehension rippled through the assembled forces.","Among the Living Origins, the clone of Origin Ama Gias stared at the floating Sparks, and her face, a mask of sublime, ancient beauty, looked as if she had just swallowed a particularly large, particularly foul piece of shit.","And it was that type of shit that did not even have a single consistency, but different vile types in a single clump!"]},{"number":4316,"title":"Chapter 4316: Chapter 4315: Resplendent Citadels! I","paragraphs":["A Royal Living Origin, his form a shimmering, white-gold beacon of pure genesis, floated beside her.","\"Origin Ama,\" he whispered, his voice a mixture of awe and dawning horror, \"is... The Early Creature, Osmont, the same Osmont you had an... interaction with at the Kleos Concordat?\"","Gias’s pure white eyes, which held the light of a billion nascent stars, turned to him.","She did not speak, but her glare was a physical force, a silent, furious question that screamed, Why are you asking such stupid fucking questions?","The Royal Living Origin flinched, his own brilliant aura dimming under the weight of her unspoken rage.","A sour, bitter mood settled over the entire contingent of Living Origins. They all remembered. They all remembered the quiet, confident words of Duke Whisker.","He had warned them. He had told them to treat Osmont with a caution that bordered on reverence, to not assume they understood his origins. And Origin Ama Gias, in her pride, in her absolute certainty of her own authority, had not listened.","This dumb bitch.","And now, that same entity, that anomaly they had sought to command, was the very being who held one of their most precious, most powerful assets: The Young Miss, Sigrid. The Resurgence of THE Living Order!","They gazed at the massive, blue-gold fortress, at the impossible, beautiful structure that had risen from the ashes of a forgotten Fold, and for the first time in eons, they felt... helpless.","Regret. It is a poison for which there is no antidote, a wound that never truly heals. It is the ghost of a choice not made, a path not taken.","And it is a weight that even beings of immense, immeasurable power cannot escape. For Origin Ama Gias and the Living Origins, it was the bitter, undeniable truth that their own arrogance, their own pride, had led them to this moment of profound, helpless uncertainty!","But regret, as always, amounted to absolutely nothing.","In another section of the void, among the shimmering, silver-white forms of the Living Laws, Royal Law Tristesse’s face was ashen. She floated towards the more powerful Dukes, her usual bright, confident smile gone, replaced by a mask of cold, dawning dread.","\"Osmont,\" she whispered, her voice a low, urgent hiss that was for them alone, \"is the... friend of Alexander Asmodeus. Both stemmed from the same Folds that used to be in this region of Collapse. You don’t think... Asmodeus is also an Early Creature, right? He is with Seraphina right now, obtaining the Inheritance of THE Living Law!\"","...!","The Dukes of Law exchanged glances, their minds, flawless engines of logic and precedent, racing through the terrible, beautiful implications.","They looked at the fortress, at the Sparks, and then at each other. Their conclusion was a silent, unanimous verdict.","\"We must cease the assault,\" Duke Justinius declared, his voice a calm, absolute command. \"And ensure that no one else is foolish enough to continue. For now... we need to start a dialogue.\"","They wanted to communicate. And they were not the only ones.","In a quiet, forgotten corner of the region of Collapse, the figures of Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux were in a flicker of paradoxical light, their presence so potent, yet so perfectly contained, that they were invisible to all but the most focused observers.","Schrodinger’s gaze was fixed on the blue-gold fortress, a profound, almost analytical, interest in his ancient eyes.","\"I tested Osmont. I checked to make sure I wasn’t dealing with an Early Creature as the result was negative, even though I continued to be doubtful...\"","At such words, Leonore’s eyes flashed.","\"Then Herald, It seems for that one moment you were wrong. Though it is not possible for you to be wrong, because no Early Creature, a Living one anyways, should be on this side. All Early Creatures are either in THE Loom, or we are about to meet many of them when they walk past The Veil to begin decimating The Living. Since he cannot possibly come from THE Loom, is he a Dead Early Creature? A Prime Dead Early Creature?\"","BOOM!","...!","The possibilities she pointed out are terrifying to think of as at this moment, the eyes of Schrodinger flashed with a sense of power and certainty as he uttered out...","\"We can only be straightforward and check then. It’s about time that I have a sit down with Osmont again. Though this time, we can make our identities....clear.\"","WAA!","Schrodinger’s playful demeanor vanished. His face became a mask of cold, grim resolve. He nodded.","He began to float forward, and as he did, his figure began to burn with a new, terrible power. The beggar’s rags seemed to melt away, replaced by an aura of pure, unadulterated Haki that made the very space around him tremble!","The other Living Existences, who had been lost in their own, shocked contemplations, now turned their gazes to him.","He moved to the forefront of the assembled forces, a lone, terrifying figure against the backdrop of the blue-gold fortress, and he called out, his voice a calm, clear, and utterly audacious invitation.","\"The Early Creature, Osmont, might you be free for a discussion?\"","...!","His words were a quiet, polite inquiry, yet they echoed through the void with the force of a thunderclap, a stunning, straightforward move in a game of shadows and secrets!","—","Meanwhile, inside The Infiniverse itself, Noah stood upon the golden sands of his Radiant Shore. Tendrils of pure, azure mana surged from him, a glorious, chaotic storm of pure potential, connecting him to every being in his domain.","His people, his family, were all now on the path of the Mana Architect, their own powers blossoming under the gentle, tyrannical rain of his boundless authority.","He smiled as he focused his gaze inward, towards the new, magnificent architecture of his own existence.","His 159 Towers of Osmont, once simple Vital Lighthouses, were now Resplendent Citadels, glorious monuments to his new Way!","They were now cities of power, their forms a breathtaking fusion of advanced, almost futuristic, design and the archaic, primal grandeur of the First Folds.","They shone with a serene, cerulean brilliance, and at their very peaks, the unique colors of their individual authorities...the purple of Tyranny, the colorless light of Quintessence, the deep blue of Infinity...burned like radiant flames.","As Noah gazed upon these wonders, he gave a quiet command. \"RUIN/EDEN. Give me a breakdown.\"","HUUM!","The crimson-blue holographic figure of his System appeared in his internal weavings, her smile a perfect, analytical curve. She bowed.","\"Of course, Master,\" her voice was a symphony of logic and ruin. \"The advancement of all 159 of your Towers to the Fourth Stage, the Resplendent Citadel of the Way, has been a monumental leap in your existential framework.\"","Prompts, clear and concise, bloomed before him.","|Resplendent Citadels – Analysis.|","|Primary Boon: Each of your 159 Citadels now contributes a staggering 2.5 Quadrillion to your base Complexity and Purity. This has already been integrated into your current totals.|","|Secondary Boon (Atlas Enhancement): Your Vital Lighthouses have now become a true navigation system. Your traversal into the First Folds is no longer a blind leap into a random coordinate. You can now select a specific region, or even a specific event, to travel to. The duration of your stay has been extended to one month.|","|Tertiary Boon (Civilization Engines): The Resplendent Citadels are the very engines of your burgeoning Civilization. They can now be forged not just in your Radiant Shore, but across the entirety of The Infiniverse. Each one will act as a nexus of your Way.|","RUIN/EDEN’s voice continued, her hands conjuring illusory diagrams of impossible, beautiful architecture. \"I have based their new functions on theoretical models based on what we know regarding the Vakochev Scale of Existence\"","|Resplendent Citadel – Civilization Protocols.|","|Energy Dominion : A single Citadel can now harness the entire energy output of an entire Minor Fold within your Infiniverse. It can absorb the light of its Wheels, stellar bodies, the gravity of its structures, and the very heat of its creation. The energy is then refined into pure, usable Mana for your Civilization.|","|Existential Weaving: A network of 9 Citadels can now engage in large-scale Existential manipulation. They can replicate and multiply primordial materials like Omnichalcum, seek to forge new material like it, construct new Wheels of Existence, and even forge new, stable Minor Folds. They are the forges of your new reality.|","|Existential Engineering: A network of 18 or more Citadels can create a [Domain of Accelerated Evolution]. Within this domain, you can influence the very developmental path of a Existences, guiding them along your Way of Mana, accelerating their progression from Edict 0 to Edict 7 in a fraction of the normal time.|","|Civilization Network: Once forged across The Infiniverse, all 159 of your Citadels are now a single, unified, super-intelligent network. They share data, coordinate defenses, and can, in a moment of absolute crisis, focus their entire, collective power into a single, reality-breaking point as they can defend your Civilization from attacks 3x the capacity of your current Complexity and Purity|","BOOM!","She smiled, a final, triumphant flourish. \"You are no longer just a king of your own small Shore, Master. You are the architect of a new, boundless, and utterly tyrannical Civilization.\"","...!"]},{"number":4317,"title":"Chapter 4317: Chapter 4316: Resplendent Citadels! II","paragraphs":["The Early Veiled Shore was a continent of impossible, vibrant life- a sanctuary forged in the heart of Existence that was, for the most part, a cold and unforgiving thing.","Noah stood upon the golden sands, a silent, unmoving pillar in the midst of a symphony of glory!","From his very being, from the boundless blue ocean of his Infinite Mana, a thousand delicate, surgical tendrils of pure, liquid energy surged!","At this moment.","His gaze was turned inward.","An appreciative observation of the new, magnificent architecture of his own existence.","He looked at his Early Atlas of the Folds, and then at the grand Resplendent Citadels that now rose on it!","Their features were so grand that they had to be implemented right away!","\"The first order of business,\" his voice was a low, resonant hum that was for him and him alone, \"is to lay the foundation.\"","HUUM!","His will was the command.","Across the vast, impossible expanse of his domain, his one hundred and fifty-nine Resplendent Citadels, the very engines of his burgeoning Civilization, roared to life.","In the Radiant Shore, eighteen of the white-gold and obsidian Sacred Totems, which had stood as silent sentinels for a short period of time, began to change.","It was not a slow, grinding transformation. It was a bloom of a ridiculously violent, beautiful genesis.","A Magisterial genesis!","The very substance of the Totems, a fusion of his own authority and the Shore’s primordial essence, was rewritten.","They stretched upward, their forms elongating, their structures becoming more complex, more... intentional.","Great, swirling rings of pure, cerulean mana materialized around each one, spinning with a silent, hypnotic grace.","They were like the rings of a gas giant, a celestial halo that declared these were not mere towers, but nexuses of a new, cosmic power.","Citadels!","Oh, glorious Citadels!","The Citadels themselves were masterpieces of a new, impossible architectural style. They were not the brutalist, functional designs of the Justiciars or the archaic, primal grandeur of Aethelgard.","They were sleek, elegant spires of a shimmering, blue-white material that seemed to be woven from solidified light and pure, unadulterated Mana.","At their very peaks, the unique colors of their individual authorities... the deep purple of Tyranny, the colorless, absolute light of Quintessence, the bottomless blue of Infinity... burned like watchful stars.","As the eighteen Citadels in the Shore solidified, their transformation complete, the remaining one hundred and forty-one followed suit.","Across the boundless, internal expanse of the Infiniverse, in some forming Fold across Frequencies, on some designated Wheel of Existence brought in...a Resplendent Citadel rose, a silent, beautiful testament to his will!","|One Hundred and Fifty-Nine [Resplendent Citadels] are being forged across your budding Civilization.|","|Your Civilization now has its foundational engines. The Way of the Mana Architect is no longer a theory; it is a reality.|","Noah stood amidst the eighteen newly forged Citadels on his Shore, their collective presence a low, powerful hum that resonated in his very bones. And then, he gave his next command!","\"Activate the Domain of Accelerated Evolution.\"","HUUM!","The eighteen Citadels answered as one. Their spinning, cerulean rings of mana flared with a brilliant, blinding light.","Beams of pure, conceptual energy shot from their peaks, not outward, but inward, converging on a single point high above the Radiant Shore.","There, in the luminous, featureless sky, a new, impossible structure began to form. It was an intricate outline of an expanding sphere!","A great, looping structure of shimmering, cerulean plates, each one the size of a continent, began to spin and weave around a central, non-existent point, forming a hollow, celestial sphere that now encapsulated the entire Early Veiled Shore.","It was a breathtaking, terrifying, and beautiful cage of pure, conceptual power.","Through the gaps in the swirling plates, one could see the Shore within, now bathed in a soft, blue light, a jewel in the heart of an existential engine!","|The [Domain of Accelerated Evolution] is being established.|","|Primary Function: This Domain is a temporal-existential accelerator. It draws upon the collective power of the eighteen networked Citadels to create a localized field of hyper-accelerated growth.|","|Boon of the Architect: All beings within this Domain will find their journey on the [Way of the Mana Architect]... expedited. The progression from Edict 0 to Edict 7 will now occur at a rate one thousand times faster than the standard progression.|","|Secondary Boon: The Domain is a font of pure, refined Mana. A constant, gentle rain of conceptual energy will now fall upon the Shore, providing a passive, continuous source of nourishment for all inhabitants.|","...!","Oh!","The moment the prompts faded, the effect began.","Sigrid, Moiraine, and the others, who had been watching in silent awe, gasped as a new, profound wave of power washed over them.","From the swirling, cerulean sphere above, a gentle, shimmering rain of pure, liquid Mana began to fall.","It was a soft, beautiful, and utterly glorious downpour!","They felt the Mana seep into their very beings, their own, newly-formed Mana Loci drinking it in with a ravenous, joyful thirst.","In a quiet corner of the Shore, a tiny, almost imperceptible figure floated.","Khor.","The First Hunger","She had been observing the grand display with a faint, almost nostalgic smile. As if she was seeing the beginning of...THE.","THE!","But as the rain of Mana began to fall, her expression changed. A new, more profound, and utterly ravenous light entered her abyssal eyes.","\"Outsider,\" she said, her voice a low, melodic hum that was filled with a primal, ancient hunger. \"The authority you are exuding is... quite delicious. It would be extremely beneficial for me to break my seals and return to my old power. Since there seems to be so much... I will see if I can feed my Hunger.\"","Noah smiled, a grand, tyrannical expression.","\"Go ahead.\"","...!","Khor’s smile was a thing of terrible, beautiful hunger. She opened her mouth.","WAP!","She closed it.","And in that single, infinitesimal instant, the Existence changed!","Oh, existence changed!"]},{"number":4318,"title":"Chapter 4318: Chapter 4317: Resplendent Citadels! III","paragraphs":["The glorious, torrential rain of Mana, the very atmosphere of the Shore which had been thick with a power so dense it was almost liquid...vanished.","90% of it, gone. Devoured!","|The First Hunger has... partaken.|","|90% of the ambient Mana within the [Domain of Accelerated Evolution] has been consumed.|","|Analysis: That was the equivalent of the total energy output of an entire Fold. Consumed. In an instant.|","|The Engines of your Civilization are responding...|","The eighteen Resplendent Citadels, which had been humming with a quiet, steady power, now roared to life.","Their cerulean rings spun faster, a blur of pure, conceptual energy.","The Citadels pulsed, a single, unified heartbeat, and...","HUUM!","The Mana returned. Instantly!","The rain began to fall again, the air grew thick with power, as if the last few seconds had never happened.","|Energy reserves have been replenished. The Engines of your Civilization burn strong.|","Khor blinked, a look of genuine, profound surprise on her ancient, youthful face. She looked at Noah, then at the Citadels, then back at Noah.","\"Outsider,\" she said, her voice filled with a new, deeper level of awe, \"that was the energy of an entire Fold I swallowed just now... and your towers here can fill it up again just like that?\"","Noah’s smile was a slow, cold, and utterly tyrannical thing. \"I have said it before, didn’t I? A Civilization... is a garden. And my garden is very, very fertile!\"","WAA!","Khor stared at him for a long, silent moment.","Then she laughed, a sound of pure, unadulterated delight.","She opened her mouth again, and this time, she did not just take a bite.","She drank. A river of pure, azure Mana flowed from the very air and into her, a willing, endless tribute to her primordial hunger!","Her endlessly dark eyes, for the first time, began to be filled with a faint, almost imperceptible, blue light.","Noah watched her, then turned his gaze away.","The Existential Engineering was a success.","Now, for the Existential Weaving.","\"RUIN/EDEN,\" he commanded. \"Let us begin.\"","|Understood, Master. Please, follow me.|","The holographic figure of his System appeared, a silent, graceful guide in this realm of his own making.","She led him to the base of one of the eighteen Resplendent Citadels. The doors, a seamless expanse of the azure-white material, opened with a silent, willing hum.","They stepped inside. The interior was a vast, cathedral-like space, its walls a shimmering, ever-shifting display of pure, informational light.","At its very center, a new, more profound structure hummed. It was a nexus of nine colossal, metallic blue rings, each one spinning in a different, impossible direction, their orbits intersecting in a way that should have been chaotic, but was instead a perfect, harmonious dance.","At the very heart of this dance, a single point of pure, creative energy pulsed. This was the forge!","\"This, Master,\" RUIN/EDEN said, her voice a quiet, reverent whisper, \"is where you can engage in Existential Weaving. What would you like to do? Replicate a known material, or forge a new one?\"","Noah’s gaze was fixed on the swirling, creative heart of the forge. His voice was a low, dangerous, and utterly tyrannical command.","\"Forge a new one. Based entirely on Mana.\"","...!","HUUM!","The nine rings spun faster. Beams of pure, cerulean brilliance converged from all around, striking the central point.","A new, terrible, and glorious process began.","THUMP!","It felt...like a booming beating heart as the concentrated beans of blue light smashed onto each other at tbe very center.","As if dense atomic particles were smashing onto each other at high speeds!","THUMP!","Arcs of light emerged with every passing second as in a short period of time...","In the heart of that creative storm, RUIN/EDEN reached in.","\"...\"","Noah looked over with sharp eyes.","She pulled forth a single, perfect ingot of a new metal.","It was a beautiful, terrible thing, its surface a swirling, liquid azure that seemed to contain the light of a billion nascent wheels.","It was not just a metal; it was a concept, a law, a new fundamental truth of his existence.","\"I call it... [Tyrannical Mana-Born Adamant],\" RUIN/EDEN declared, her voice a proud, triumphant proclamation.","\"It is not just a material, Master; it is an extension of your own will. It is conceptually ’true,’ meaning it cannot be broken, bent, or unmade by any authority that is not your own. It is the perfect material for a Tyrant. It is the best metal.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Form even more,\" he commanded. \"It shall be used to reforge and enhance my Mana-Born Living Existential Armor.\"","|Understood, Master.|","He stood, watching as the forge roared to life again, his eyes luminous with a new, profound understanding.","He was doing a great deal, and he was doing it rapidly. But... would it be enough? Would it be enough to tip the scales of what was coming?","Because he was getting powerful, but he knew that even the Early Creatures that were currently living in the era of the Earliest Folds that his other body was in... even they did not remain stationary.","He considered himself an anomaly that exponentially advanced across the stages of power, but other existences had eons!","From all the way to the Earliest Folds until now, entities like Forgemaster Vulcan or others who had thousands of Quadrillions of Purity and Complexity... such power could be doubled or tripled if not more.","Nobody remained stationary. He was not the only one that advanced!","So he had to keep moving forward as it wss better to overestimate than to underestimate!","As he thought this, RUIN/EDEN’s voice was a soft, almost casual, interruption.","\"Oh, by the way, Master. That Schrodinger is looking to meet with you. He is currently hanging around the Infiniverse with that Leonore Rureaux. Your distinction as The Early Creature has begun to spread due to your Sparks.\"","Noah’s gaze sharpened.","\"Oh?\" he said, his voice a quiet, dangerous note in the humming silence of the forge.","He thought of the Schrodinger from the past, the defeated, apathetic Living Concept. And he thought of the one from his present, the chaotic, deceptive Living Paradox.","A being of many secrets. It would be no issue to meet with him again.","To obtain more information!"]},{"number":4319,"title":"Chapter 4319: Chapter 4318: Entry! I","paragraphs":["Outside the Infiniverse.","The assembled forces of the Living Existences, a congregation of beings who could unmake Wheels with a thought, were staring.","Their gazes, filled with a mixture of awe, dread, and a profound, galling sense of irrelevance as they stared ahead.","This was right after Schrodinger had called out that he wanted to communicate with The Early Creature, Osmont!","Whispers, not of sound but of pure, conceptual data, rippled through the ranks.","Many of the older Dukes, their forms ancient and terrible, recognized the woman beside the beggar-paradox. Leonore Rureaux. A name that was a ghost, a legend whispered in the darkest corners of their history.","A being who had supposedly fallen in a blaze of glory eons ago, a martyr for the cause of Paradox. And yet, here she stood, frail but undeniably present.","The Living Origins were quieter as if they knew some sort of secret.","As if to add another layer of impossibility to the scene, more Living Paradoxes were arriving.","They flickered into existence, their forms shimmering with a contained, restless energy, and their gazes, when they fell upon Schrodinger and Leonore, held a deep veneration.","Schrodinger had simply spoken, his voice a calm, audacious invitation across the void, a request for a discussion with The Early Creature, Osmont.","The other Living Existences, whose hatred for the Paradoxes was a thing as old and as fundamental as their own authorities, watched this with a distaste so profound it was a physical presence.","Among a cluster of Living Temporals, their bodies surrounded by the dilapidated, ancient aura of time itself, the whispers turned to venom.","\"Who does that Schrodinger think he is?\" one of them, a Duke whose form was a swirling vortex of clocks and rivers, hissed.","\"That he would voice out that he wants an audience with a supposed Early Creature, and he would simply be granted that meeting? The sheer, unmitigated arrogance!\"","WAA!","Another, a being whose very presence seemed to slow the moments around her, nodded in agreement. \"It is a performance. A show. This ’Osmont’ is likely just another of their tricks, another layer of their endless, infuriating games. Could he truly even be...an Early Creature?\"","...!","But at this time, their bitter, self-assured pronouncements were cut short.","A region of the massive, blue-gold Aegis of the Infiniverse pulsed.","It was a soft, gentle thrum, a quiet note in the silent chaos. Then, a bubble of pure, blue-gold brilliance began to emerge from the larger structure.","It was a perfect, world-sized sphere, a floating island of impossible beauty covered by the same, impenetrable barrier.","In the next moment, a small doorway formed in the side of this new, isolated domain, a silent, waiting invitation. And from it, a figure emerged.","Malphas!","Oh!","He was a masterpiece of silent, terrible grandeur. His obsidian butler’s attire, once a simple, elegant uniform, was now etched with invisible lines of brilliant blue, the very authority of his Master’s Mana woven into its fabric.","His eyes, no longer just crimson, now danced with a dangerous, captivating glow of crimson-blue. The power that emanated from him was not a wave, but a suffocating, absolute pressure.","It was enough to stifle the very thoughts of nearly all who were present!","His cold gaze swept over the assembled forces of the Living Existences, a silent, dismissive assessment. It lingered for a moment on the fuming Temporals, then the shocked Origins, and finally, it came to rest on Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux.","His voice, when he spoke, was a calm, cold, and utterly absolute command. \"The Master will see you now.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words were a quiet detonation in the stunned silence. The Living Temporals, who had just been dismissing Schrodinger’s chances, now had faces of pure, ashen disbelief.","They gritted their teeth, their own authority feeling fragile and insignificant in the face of this new, impossible power.","Schrodinger and the woman beside him simply nodded. They floated calmly towards the isolated, blue-gold sphere, their movements unhurried, their acceptance of this impossible invitation a silent testament to their own, terrible confidence.","As Schrodinger passed by Malphas, he frowned, his ancient eyes sweeping over the butler’s form, a quick, analytical up-and-down glance. He seemed to be reassessing, recalculating.","He shook his head, a gesture of profound, almost frustrated, thought, and then passed through the opened doorway.","Malphas turned, and the doorway sealed behind them, a silent, final click in the lock of reality. An immense, heavy silence descended once more.","In that silence, the Temporal Duke who had been so vocal in his disdain, his pride now a raw, burning wound, floated forward.","He looked at the sealed sphere, at the silent, beautiful fortress, and he bellowed, his voice a desperate, arrogant echo of Schrodinger’s own call.","\"I, Duke Chronokolos of the Living Temporals, also wish to have an audience with The Early Creature, Osmont!\"","...!","A grand proclamation!","But...","A heavy and embarrassing silence followed. Seconds trickled by, each one a small, cruel eternity. There was no answer. Not a glow of brilliance, not another bubble of blue-gold light... nothing.","The void was a silent, mocking testament to his own, profound insignificance.","Other Dukes of the Temporals floated over, their forms shimmering with a mixture of embarrassment and pity, and began to pull their shamed colleague back into their ranks!","Status.","It is a concept that has driven more beings to madness than any curse, a hunger more insatiable than any Inevitability!","In the grand, chaotic weavings of existence, there are countless actors who believe themselves to be the lead, who strut and fret upon the stage, their lines loud and their gestures grand, utterly oblivious to the fact that they are, and always will be, mere extras.","They are the footnotes in a story that is not about them. The statistical noise in a symphony they cannot hear. And the cruelest joke of all is that they will never know.","For to truly understand one’s own status, one must first possess the humility to ask the question: What is my role in this play?","And most beings are far too in love with the sound of their own voice to ever listen for the answer.","The Duke of the Temporals, his face now a mask of pure, unadulterated humiliation, was pulled back.","Among the Living Origins, Origin Ama Gias watched this pathetic, comical display, but her mind was elsewhere.","She thought of her own, failed attempt at a dialogue. And then she thought of the one, fragile thread of connection she still held.","The Young Miss. Sigrid.","’If I use our connection,’ she thought, her mind a whirlwind of desperate, strategic calculation, ’can we not clear the table? Can we not forge a new, more... respectful relationship with this Osmont?’","After all, she had her clone here. And...","\"Oh, isn’t a body of Osmont... err, The Early Creature, Osmont, on the vessel that went to the Wandering Territories? Who has a body there close by?!\"","...!","The voice, a piercing, far-too-happy note from a Living Emotive, echoed out and reminded everyone of this crucial fact.","Origin Ama Gias turned towards the being, a flicker of pure, unadulterated distaste in her eyes. It was exactly what she had just been thinking.","Her other body, her primary existence, was even now on that impossible Barge, crossing the dangerous Wandering Territories with Elysia Firmhand.","And on that very vessel was another body of Osmont, and with him, The Young Miss.","It was a chance. Perhaps their best, and last, chance to reach out, to mend the bridges that her own pride had burned.","Origin Ama Gias clenched her fist, a gesture of profound, bitter resolve. She had caused herself and the Living Origins to eat a lot of shit. Now, she had to see if she could wash it down, wipe their chins, and clear their plate.","An Early Creature... was not someone to offend!"]},{"number":4320,"title":"Chapter 4320: Chapter 4319: Entry! II","paragraphs":["On the other side of The Veil.","A massive, oval, white-obsidian vessel floated through the silent, starless void.","It was The Ashen Ark of Judgment, its surface as smooth and as cold as a polished tombstone.","Upon its vast, flat deck, a legion of The Dead stood in perfect, silent formation. There was no chaotic aura, no mindless rage. There was only a profound, chilling sense of Order.","At the forefront stood Tatiana, her dark hair a stark, beautiful contrast to the pale, deathly perfection of her skin.","Around her, other Dead Early Creatures stood as silent sentinels, and behind them, in hundreds of perfect rows, were Dead Existential Armors, their obsidian-black forms radiating a silent, contained power!","The air was thick with a regality that was both beautiful and utterly terrifying.","The Ashen Ark approached a Tear of The Veil, a jagged, weeping wound in the fabric of their reality.","The Early Creatures around Tatiana watched it with calm, ancient eyes, their expressions unreadable masks of power and purpose.","Tatiana stepped forward, her voice echoing out across the silent deck as they began to cross the threshold.","\"We are asked to have a purpose,\" she began, her tone a perfect, commanding cadence that brooked no dissent.","\"We are asked to have a singular focus, a driving will that defines our every action. For many, that purpose is a scattered, chaotic thing, a collection of selfish desires and fleeting ambitions. But for us... for us, there is only one purpose. One Order. Our Way is the Way of THE Dead Order.\"","HUUM!","Her voice grew stronger, more resonant, a creed spoken into the void!","\"We adhere to the Doctrines. The First Doctrine: Order is Salvation. All chaos, all the messy, unpredictable weavings of life, are a sickness. We are the cure. The Second Doctrine: All Endings Are Beginnings. We do not bring death; we offer a new, more perfect, more ordered form of existence. The Third Doctrine: The Will of THE Creature is Absolute. All that we do is in service of a design so grand, so profound, that lesser beings cannot even begin to comprehend it.\"","She paused, letting the weight of her words settle upon her silent, loyal legion. \"Existence has unfolded in the way it has as The Fallout is coming. Our purpose is to establish Order before it does, and afterwards. We are to transform the countless Lifeforms in Existence from The Living... to The Dead. Not kill. Transform. Anyone who kills a single lifeform without a transformation occurring will answer directly to me and the other Commanders.\"","...!","The Ark was now halfway through the Tear, the chaotic, vibrant light of the living Folds bleeding into their silent, monochrome world.","\"We are simply an advanced party, sent to get things started. The Forgemaster and the other Lords of the Cryptlands will soon join us to ensure Order as The Veil continues to thin. There will be those who stand in opposition to what we seek to do, as they do not understand. The protocol for such beings is to transform them first and have them understand later. Understood?\"","A single, unified roar, a sound that was both a shout and a silent, psychic affirmation, erupted from the legion behind her. \"UNDERSTOOD, MA’AM!\"","The Ashen Ark of Judgment crossed fully into the new Fold. An Early Creature, his form regal in a pristine white robe, half of his face a bare, gleaming skeletal structure, floated over to Tatiana.","He whistled, a low, appreciative sound. \"Nice speech there, Tatiana. I told you the role of a leader was always meant for you.\"","Tatiana merely scoffed, her gaze remaining cold and fixed on the new reality before them.","\"Remain focused, Valerius.\"","They had arrived. The air here was thick, vibrant, and alive. They were in the Transcendent Elemental Folds, in a region surrounded by bronze, flowing rivers of earthen elements and sands that shone with a stellar brilliance. It was a world of pure, untamed life.","And that life had just noticed them.","In the distance, a group of Living Elementals, their forms blazing with the bronze light of their authority, froze.","They stared at the Ashen Ark, at the few hundred Dead Early Creatures, at the legions of Dead Existential Armors.","A wave of pure, oppressive Haki, the silent, collective will of the arriving legion, washed over them. And in an instant, their lights were snuffed out. They fell from the sky like extinguished stars, their consciousnesses collapsing under a weight they could not even begin to comprehend.","...!","Tatiana gave a light, almost imperceptible nod. Behind her, a Dead Early Creature, his skin a grotesque, beautiful mosaic of decaying flesh and vibrant, living power, flew out.","He moved towards the unconscious Elementals... a paltry force of three Honored and nine Prime Living Existences, their combined complexity a mere whisper against the storm that had just arrived.","The Early Creature came to a stop before the first of the fallen Elementals. He raised a hand, his fingers long and skeletal, and plunged it into the creature’s chest. His hand sank in as if through butter.","He did so rapidly in the span of a nanosecond for all the Living Elementals here!","And then, the shocking phenomenon of... The Change began.","On the first Elemental.","A brilliant, obsidian-white light erupted from the point of contact. It was not a destructive light, but a transformative one. It spread across the Elemental’s body like a fast-moving frost, its bronze skin turning an ashen, obsidian white. It looked lifeless, and yet, impossibly, the complexity of its existence began to rise!","The process was a terrible, beautiful thing to witness. The vibrant, chaotic energy of the Living Elemental was being... ordered. Refined. Distilled into a new, more potent form of being. The light faded, and the Elemental, now a being of ashen, dead perfection, opened its eyes.","It woke from its state of unconsciousness, and its eyes, once a simple, bronze glow, now shone with a new, grander power and a profound, chilling intelligence. It radiated a power of over one hundred trillion in both Complexity and Purity. A Duke. From a mere Honored, it had become a Duke!","The newly changed Elemental looked at the Dead Early Creature who had transformed it, and it bowed. \"Thank you,\" its voice was a new, resonant thing. \"How can I be of service?\"","The Dead Early Creature nodded. \"Return to your homes,\" it commanded, its voice a low, rumbling echo. \"And grant this Change to others. Do it silently. Make the spread as vast as possible before any conflicts arise.\"","...!","The new Duke, and the twelve others who had been similarly transformed in a silent, terrifyingly efficient process, bowed as one.","They turned and flew back towards their home, towards... The Heart of Elementals.","...!","Back on the Ark, Tatiana watched this scene with a calm, almost detached, expression. The vessel had now fully entered the Transcendent Elemental Folds.","But in the next second, she frowned. She sniffed the air. Her eyes, which had been as cold and as still as a frozen lake, now showed a flicker of surprise. She sniffed again.","\"Can you all smell that?\" she asked, her voice a low, puzzled murmur.","...!","The Early Creatures behind her stirred, their own ancient senses reaching out. A collective, silent gasp rippled through their ranks. They could smell it too!","Tatiana’s eyes turned sharp, a dangerous, inquisitive light burning in their depths. \"I can smell Order,\" she said, her voice a low, dangerous whisper. \"But... Living Order. How could there be Living Order on this side of The Veil?!\"","WAA!","They all knew Order was dead. Dead, but still gloriously present, as could be seen through them. But this... this was different. This was a vibrant, living echo of a power that should have been an impossibility.","Tatiana’s gaze was a thing of pure, unadulterated focus. She turned to her legion. \"You three,\" she commanded, her voice a sharp, cutting command, \"report this back to Forgemaster Vulcan. The rest of you... let us follow the light of Order and see why it is emanating on this side of The Veil... and whether it is true Order, or False Order!\"","...!"]},{"number":4321,"title":"Chapter 4321: Chapter 4320: An Exchange! I","paragraphs":["Inside the small, world-sized isolated bubble that Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux were invited in.","They walked upon a radiant stellar blue pathway, a bridge of solidified light that cut through an expanse of breathtaking, cosmic beauty. All around them was the allure of a starlit environment, as if this entire isolated domain was a captured piece of the night sky, a private galaxy where the only destination was a single, glowing point of life at its center: a round garden, pulsing with a gentle, welcoming light.","Leonore Rureaux, her form still frail but her crimson eyes now burning with a cold, clear, and rejuvenated light, gazed at the impossible architecture with a flicker of analytical interest. \"Before I even meet him,\" she said, her voice a low, melodic thing that held the sharp edge of a razor, \"I am going to bet ten thousand Everythings of Paradox that he is an Early Creature. Would you take that bet, O Herald?\"","Schrodinger smiled, a genuine, almost wistful expression. He shook his head, his bearing a stark, absurd contrast to the celestial grandeur around them. \"I will agree with you that he is an Early Creature,\" he said, his voice a quiet, philosophical murmur. \"Though none of that would make sense, but existence is filled with impossibilities. Maybe he is simply another impossibility.\"","With such a conversation taking place, they arrived at the edge of the garden. In the next moment, a figure appeared before them, a silent, graceful materialization at the garden’s entrance. It was Malphas. His obsidian butler’s attire seemed to drink the starlight, but woven within its fabric were invisible lines of brilliant blue that pulsed with a quiet, contained power. His eyes, no longer just crimson, now danced with a dangerous, captivating glow of crimson-blue, and the authority he emanated was enough to stifle the very air.","His cold gaze swept over them, a silent, dismissive assessment, before it came to rest on Schrodinger. \"Please,\" he said, his voice a smooth, cultured baritone that was both a polite invitation and an absolute command, \"this way.\"","The garden was a masterpiece of impossible, beautiful life. Radiant sacred herbs, their leaves shimmering with the light of a thousand different authorities, grew in perfect, geometric patterns. Trees, their bark the color of polished moonlight, bore fruits that glowed with a gentle, internal fire. And at the very center, arranged in a perfect circle, were elevated cushions of a shimmering blue-gold material. They surrounded a low table, upon which sat pristine, white-gold plates and cups.","Malphas appeared at the table, and with a graceful wave of his hand, he revealed a somewhat crude-looking bucket. It was forged from the heated sands of the Early Veiled Shore, now cooled into a swirling, opalescent glass. But from this humble vessel, he began to pour... the Sacred Mead of Existence.","Schrodinger and Leonore’s eyes widened. They could feel it, the terrifying complexity and potency of the white-gold milky liquid as it filled the cups, its very presence a wave of pure, unadulterated life force that made their own ancient existences hum with a forgotten, primal hunger. As for the plates, Malphas waved his hands again, and they were filled with radiant, boiling sacred waters, in which floated perfect, bite-sized pieces of celestial marine life.","After he finished, he rose like a gloriously efficient butler. \"The Master will be here soon,\" he said. \"Please, help yourselves.\"","With those words, he stepped to the side, his posture one of cold, calm, and absolute stillness. Schrodinger couldn’t help but stare, his curiosity a palpable, analytical force. \"Who are you?\" he asked, his voice a low, intrigued murmur. \"You should not be a mere Living Existence or Fold Dweller. And you don’t seem like an Early Creature, as I have not seen an Early Creature serve anyone. And yet, I cannot shake the immensity that you are giving off...\"","Malphas turned his head, his crimson-blue eyes fixing on Schrodinger with a cold, dismissive light. \"I am merely a servant of The Master. Even my name is inconsequential. Again, enjoy the refreshments. The Master will be here soon.\"","The words made Schrodinger even more intrigued. But beside him, Leonore Rureaux had already picked up a glass. She drank the Sacred Mead of Existence, and her eyes lit up, her entire being buzzing with a unique, vibrant radiance.","And then, he arrived.","A figure manifested just outside the garden, a silent, instantaneous appearance that was not a traversal, but a simple declaration of presence. He floated to one of the radiant, elevated cushions and sat. He was adorned in a simple, blue-gold emperor’s robe, his hair now a cascade of extremely radiant blue-gold, as if a thousand oceans of Mana were warring for dominance against the light of a captured sun. His fair, white skin was scintillating, shining as if it were crystalline, and it held within it an unfathomable ocean of power. He was an impossible weapon, an emperor in his prime, yet young, and also ancient with a power that defied all comprehension.","The moment he appeared... Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux both frowned. They felt it.","Suppression!","The two of them, beings of such profound and terrible power, actually felt a sense of suppression in his presence. Noah looked back at them, and beside him, unseen by either of them, the crimson-blue holographic form of RUIN/EDEN materialized.","|Master, the existential signatures of the two subjects have been ascertained.|","|The subject, Schrodinger, is currently radiating a power of 0.5 Quintillion in both Complexity and Purity.|","|The subject, Leonore Rureaux, is at 0.8 Quintillion. My analysis indicates that this is a degraded state; her potential maximum is likely in excess of 2 Quintillion. It seems her previous imprisonment has left her... gravely injured.|","0.5 Quintillion and 0.8 Quintillion. Noah processed the numbers, a cold, tyrannical calm settling over him. The usage of Quintillion meant these entities had already embarked on, or at least sensed, their Way of Existence. This was the Schrodinger he knew, the Living Paradox. But the other one, the defeated, apathetic Living Concept he had seen in the Early Laboratories... if that being was one and the same, then now was the time to learn, to understand.","He sat, his gaze sweeping over the two of them. He nodded once, a gesture of a king granting an audience. \"You were looking for me.\"","...!"]},{"number":4322,"title":"Chapter 4322: Chapter 4321: An Exchange! II","paragraphs":["The silence was a taut, humming thing. Schrodinger looked at Noah, and a brilliant, almost dazzling, smile spread across his face. \"I’m going to go out on a limb,\" he said, his voice filled with a genuine, almost joyous, wonder, \"and simply affirm that you are, in fact, an Early Creature. Which begs me to question... How did a piece of the weapon of THE Living Law not work against you?\"","Noah looked at him, and his expression was a perfect, unreadable mask.","He appreciated the nature of a being like this who did not beat around the bush too much!","His voice, when he spoke, was not loud, but it was absolute. It was the voice of a man who did not need to raise his tone to command a room, for the room already belonged to him. \"As far as I know, the weapon of THE Living Law works against Early Creatures. I am not an Early Creature. I am The Early Creature, Osmont.\"","...!","BOOM!","Simply.","Impossibly.","A very straightforward answer was given.","Schrodinger and Leonore’s eyes sharpened, a new, more profound level of calculation entering their gazes. Noah calmly picked up his own glass of Mead and took a sip, his eyes, burning with a quiet, tyrannical fire, still fixed on Schrodinger.","\"Now you...\" he began, his voice a low, dangerous hum. \"You have been a question in my mind for a little while now. I’ve asked myself again and again, what could that Schrodinger be up to? What’s he doing purposefully accelerating Tears of The Veil? What’s he doing with a corpse of an Early Creature? But now, in the grand scale of things, it doesn’t matter too much. What does matter is my curiosity. As I want to ask... do you remember anything regarding the Early Laboratories? Elderborns?\"","BOOM!","The Early Laboratories and Elderborns!","Noah asked such a question simply to see exactly what reaction would bloom from Schrodinger, and he saw it. A flicker of sharp, analytical light in both his eyes and the crimson depths of Leonore’s. It was not him who replied, but the woman who was currently more powerful than him.","\"With every word you say,\" Leonore began, her voice a low, resonant note that cut through the starlit quiet of the garden, \"you make it clear to us that you know a whole lot more than you are letting on. We can skip any back and forth and get right to business then-\"","\"Oh, Elderborns! That takes me back!\"","Schrodinger interjected, his voice a bright, almost nostalgic, chime that shattered her serious tone. Leonore turned to him, her expression a mask of pure, unadulterated annoyance.","He simply smiled, a mischievous, almost childlike, glint in his ancient eyes, and gently tapped her thigh as if to say, let me handle this.","He kept his gaze fixed on Noah. \"I know a thing or two about Elderborns,\" he said, his voice now a conspiratorial whisper. \"Do you know their true origins? Let me tell you a story...\"","Leonore rolled her eyes, a gesture of profound, weary exasperation. \"Really? Right now?\"","Yet, Schrodinger’s gaze did not waver from Noah.","Noah, for his part, simply took another slow, deliberate sip of the Sacred Mead of Existence, his expression a calm, unreadable mask. He was a mountain, and their words were but wind.","\"Many believed,\" Schrodinger began, his voice taking on the cadence of a master storyteller, \"that the Elderborns were simply a glorious accident of existence. Beings blessed with a heavily concentrated measure of THE Creature’s Everythings. The First Leader, Gilgamesh, a being of such unyielding ambition that he sought to unite all Early Creatures under a single banner. Tatiana, a weaver of dreams whose power could shape the very fabric of reality. Each a titan in their own right, their power a testament to a glorious, cosmic lottery.\"","He paused, letting the weight of the legend settle. Then, his smile turned sharp, dangerous. \"But that... is not the case. The Elderborns did not form naturally. They were not an accident. They were a guided emergence from the hands of THE Living Existences. They were... purposeful designs. Which begs you to wonder, why did THE Living Existences seek to cluster the concentrated Everythings of THE Creature onto a few, specific beings?\"","...!","Why?","The air in the garden, once so serene, turned heavy and cold. Noah studied Schrodinger and Leonore, his eyes shining with a brilliant, analytical light. \"Elderborns were always seen around THE Living Existences, carrying out their whims,\" he said, his voice not a question, but a statement of fact, a piece of a puzzle he was now assembling aloud. \"Are you going to tell me that THE Living Existences were grooming them as tools or weapons? For their fun? Or against THE Creature?\"","BOOM!","At his words, Schrodinger smiled. \"That is a great question. Who can say for sure? One can only be certain if they can track what every Elderborn has done across the Earliest Folds. Well, before they and countless other Early Creatures disappeared, which brings us to the next point... the disappearance of Early Creatures and the implausibility of you being here. I’m going to assume you already know a lot about The Fallout?\"","...!","Schrodinger spoke the words with a grand, theatrical flourish. Noah calmly raised his glass of Sacred Mead of Existence and drained the last of the shimmering, white-gold liquid. The cup was empty. In the next instant, Malphas appeared beside him, a silent, graceful specter of perfect servitude, the crude, beautiful bucket in his hand as he refilled the glass without a word.","Noah gave a single, almost imperceptible nod of acknowledgment. \"I know a little bit about The Fallout.\"","Schrodinger’s smile widened, a flash of genuine, almost manic, delight in his eyes.","As if he sought to one-up him, to always hold the final, most devastating card, he leaned forward, his voice a low, triumphant whisper. \"We... know where the entrance to a Shelter that can withstand the Fallout is.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4323,"title":"Chapter 4323: Chapter 4322: Do Not Idolize! I","paragraphs":["Schrodinger stated that he knew where the entrance to a Shelter that could survive The Fallout was!","At such words, Noah’s gaze, which had been a calm, almost leisurely thing, sharpened into a point of absolute, tyrannical focus.","The air in the small, world-sized bubble grew heavy, the starlit environment seeming to hold its breath. Beside him, unseen by the two ancient Paradoxes, the crimson-blue holographic figure of RUIN/EDEN materialized, her voice a cool, clinical whisper in his mind.","|Based on my analysis of his existential signature, Master, the subject ’Schrodinger’ genuinely believes his words to be true. He is not bluffing or engaging in theatrical misdirection. Whether the information itself is accurate... is a variable that remains unknown.|","Noah looked at Schrodinger, his expression remained a perfect, unreadable mask.","His voice, when he spoke, was a low, resonant, and utterly imposing thing. \"To clarify,\" he began, each word a carefully placed piece on a board of vast scale, \"you know the entrance into THE Loom?\"","...!","At his words, Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux looked at each other once more. Schrodinger then smiled, a brilliant, almost dazzling expression of pure, unadulterated amusement. \"Well now,\" he said, his voice a playful, conspiratorial hum, \"I am going to continue with my assumption that you already know a whole lot, similar to us, so I’ll keep talking. If ever you are lost, just let me know. So... no. I do not have knowledge of the entry to THE Loom. That is an impossibility. THE Loom will never be open, or even have the possibility of opening... until after The Fallout has taken place. Nothing can go in or out. What I have knowledge of is a subsidiary of THE Loom. A small portion of it where those who designed THE Loom... kept their toys.\"","BOOM!","Their toys.","\"You should have met them already,\" Schrodinger continued, his smile never wavering. \"The Justiciars. The Arbiters.\"","...!","His expression then shifted. The smile vanished, replaced by a look of cold, callous rage so profound it seemed to make the very starlight around them curdle.","\"For the designers of THE Loom,\" he hissed, his voice a venomous whisper, \"it wasn’t enough that countless existences would collapse. One designer in particular wanted to continue harvesting from its Way of Existence. Its Way of Emotive. That despicable, shitty, bum clusterfuck of an existence, Emotive, placed behind a protocol where as The Fallout approached, its tools would appear to begin reaping and rousing even more emotions.\"","...!","\"To let all remaining existences know they would perish, and as a form of mercy, some would be collapsed even before The Fallout came, the whole thing displayed until the day of The Fallout. What just happened with Aeternitas Glacies was exactly that. To induce fear. To rouse emotions. Because The Fallout itself is not enough... but for their Way of Existence... they will milk it for even more.\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes flashed with a chilling light. Beside him, Malphas’s arms trembled slightly, not with fear, but with a deep, resonant fury. He glared towards Schrodinger. \"THE Living Emotive experienced negative and positive emotions differently,\" he stated, his voice a cold, hard blade.","\"Their Way of Existence would be even more boundless when it fed on positive emotions. Such a thing would not be put in place by THE Living Emotive. They are not like this!\"","Malphas had spoken out, his loyalty a shield against the accusation.","Schrodinger’s eyes turned sharp, squinting as he analyzed the butler. \"How would you know THE Living Emotive’s nature so well?\"","...!","Malphas did not reply. He stared at Schrodinger coldly, then turned to Noah and bowed, his form a perfect expression of regret. \"I apologize for my outburst, My Lord.\"","Noah nodded towards him, a silent acknowledgment. \"It’s okay.\"","His head turned, his gaze sweeping over the vibrant, beautiful garden around them. He sighed.","The Way of Existence.","He thought of the Ways of Emotive and the other Living Existences. He even wondered about the Way of THE Creature. Did all of them treat the countless lifeforms across Existence as their Civilizations? Was this the reason for the endless, teeming life that permeated the Folds?","\"Living Paradoxes and how they live day in and day out... feed The Way of Paradox. The Civilization of Paradox,\" he mused aloud, his voice a low, contemplative rumble.","\"Origin feeds the Way of Origin, Law feeds The Way of Law... and so on and so forth.\" He turned back to Schrodinger, his gaze a sharp, analytical probe. \"Where in this does THE Creature come in? Do you know of The Way of THE Creature?\"","...!","At his words, Schrodinger shook his head. \"That is inconsequential. His Way does not matter. Because THE Creature abandoned us. He went silent. With his nature, he wouldn’t have allowed THE Loom to come to fruition, and yet it did. Why is that? Why did he leave us? Why did he abandon us? WHY?!\"","Towards the end of his words, Schrodinger’s voice rose to a furious, almost desperate, roar. Leonore Rureaux placed a hand on his shoulder, her touch a calm, steadying anchor in his storm of rage.","\"THE Creature did not abandon us,\" she said, her voice firm, unwavering. \"I and others always believed that something happened. Something we do not know. Maybe THE Living Existences did something. There is a lot about history we do not know. There is the Curse overflowing across The Dead that we know THE Creature was involved in. The Veil that THE Creature was involved in. We may be misunderstanding many things here...\"","...!","Schrodinger looked at her, his expression weary, his rage giving way to a deep, ancient bitterness. He shook his head.","\"The dangers of idolizing a common existence as if any of them were different...\" he began, his voice now a low drum.","\"Idolizing someone can lead to de-existentialization, where we project a fictional image of perfection onto them, denying their own, flawed existence. When they inevitably fail to live up to this image, it leads to intense disappointment and even bitterness. Heavy, heavy bitterness. It can lead to defending inexcusable actions or ignoring evidence of wrongdoing that are blatantly there.\"","...!"]},{"number":4324,"title":"Chapter 4324: Chapter 4323: Do Not Idolize! II","paragraphs":["\"THE Creature was born. THE Creature will die, or is already dead. THE Living Existences can be killed just like you and I. Just look at THE Living Order. Deader than Dead. All of them...They eat. They shit. They hate. They fear. They may be higher on the Scale of Existence than us... but they are still that. Existences. I will never fucking idolize them. Not ever again.\"","...!","His words were heavy, each one a stone dropped into the silent, contemplative pool of the garden.","Malphas looked down, his own thoughts a swirling vortex of loyalty and doubt.","Noah’s eyes, however, shone with a bright, tyrannical light. \"THE Creature had his Way of Existence, and we have our own,\" he declared, his voice a calm, absolute verdict. \"Yes, we are no different. Regardless of what happened in the past that we do not know, it is the present and future that matter the most. So... this Shelter. Where is it, and how can the vast lifeforms of all Folds be relocated in it to survive The Fallout?\"","...!","At his critical question, Schrodinger fell silent. He picked up his drink, downing the entire cup of Sacred Mead of Existence in a single, decisive gulp. His eyes shone with a new, sharp light as he looked at Noah. \"When a Justiciar appears again,\" he said, his voice a low, conspiratorial whisper, \"just follow it back to where it came from. Track it. Let it lead you to its base, and it will be a Shelter connected to THE Loom. A tiny little subsidiary. A Garden of Hope. A line of salvation. Reach it, and one may just survive The Fallout.\"","...!","A heavy silence settled over the garden.","|Master, the new information has been analyzed.|","|The subject ’Schrodinger’ is proposing a high-risk, high-reward infiltration mission. The ’Garden of Hope’ is likely a forward operating base or a manufacturing facility holding the Justiciars and Arbiters.|","|Feasibility: If such a location exists, and if it is indeed a ’subsidiary’ of THE Loom, it may possess a degree of the same protective qualities. It is a viable, if exceedingly dangerous, path. There is no harm in seeing if this is actually true.|","Noah looked at Schrodinger calmly, the two of them locked in a silent, analytical gaze. Finally, Schrodinger spoke again.","\"That is one of my goals, anyway. Even if my methods are questioned. Even if some lives are lost. All life will be extinguished in the near future if this solution, or another, is not attained. Since you seem to have enacted your own Way, you have your own drive to survive, and you might even have the mindset of wanting to save those in your Way of Existence. If your existence can cause this body of mine here to feel a sense of suppression, your power could tip the scales if need be. I partly came here to say this, to make sure that you would not be a force of interference in my plans. If we are all going towards the same thing, even better. There is no harm in having an Early Creature with unknown origins bearing the grunt of the weight of Existence. After all... why should I be alone in suffering?\"","...!","Why should he be alone in suffering? The words were a quiet, terrible confession, a glimpse into the profound, ancient loneliness of the being before him.","Schrodinger believed himself to be carrying the weight of existence on his shoulders, a self-appointed, and perhaps, self-deluded, savior.","Noah shook his head internally. In existence, one could believe they were a chosen one, a herald, a bringer of apocalypse. But what mattered in the end... was power. Power would ultimately decide what role one played.","He had come across many who thought themselves saviors, and yet they had the highest body count of those they killed.","He did not even have to look far as when he looked at himself...oh!","As Noah was thinking this, his gaze, and the gazes of Schrodinger and Leonore, snapped outwards. Their perception pierced through the blue-gold barrier of their isolated domain, to the chaos beyond.","Behind the teeming, anxious crowds of Living Existences, a massive, flat vessel had appeared, a silent, obsidian white omen in the swirling void.","And on it... were entities so terrifying that their mere Haki caused the nearby Prime, Honored, and Royal Living Existences to lose consciousness, their forms slumping in the void like puppets with their strings cut.","Oh!","Noah’s eyes focused, his perception, now a thing of wonder, dissecting the new arrivals.","He saw...Early Creatures!","Dead ones!","And at the forefront, one who shone with tremendous radiance.","He saw... Tatiana, a queen of ordered death, her complexity a staggering 4 Quintillion. He saw the regal, half-skeletal Valerius, his power a calm, terrible 3.5 Quintillion. He saw the others, a legion of The Prime Dead, their power a silent, crushing wave!","|Alert: High-threat entities have arrived.|","|Source: The Folds of The Dead.|","|Primary Signatures:|","| - [Tatiana – The Ashen Dreaming Queen] – 4.1 Quintillion Complexity.|","| - [Valerius – The Silent Regent] – 3.5 Quintillion Complexity.|","| - [Legion of the Prime Dead] – Average Complexity: 2.5 Quintillion.|","...!","Oh!","Beside him, Leonore’s voice was a low, dangerous hiss towards Schrodinger.","\"Now might be a good time for you to awaken a stronger body. Otherwise, we all may just be fucked.\"","The Prime Dead had arrived. But as Noah watched, a final, chilling detail registered in his perception, a detail that was confirmed by a final, terrible prompt from RUIN/EDEN.","The gazes of the newly arrived legion, their collective, silent will, was not focused on the assembled forces of the Living, nor on the curious Paradoxes, nor on the enraged Origins. Their attention was fixed, with a profound, almost religious, focus, on the blue-gold fortress of the Infiniverse.","And their bodies, their very auras, were surrounded by a brilliant, pristine, and utterly familiar white light.","|Analysis of The Prime Dead legion is complete. A significant and unexpected anomaly has been detected.|","|Their authority is not just that of The Dead. It is... intertwined with the authority of Order.|","...!","Order.","Oh, Order!"]},{"number":4325,"title":"Chapter 4325: Chapter 4324: Sheer Depravity! I","paragraphs":["The area surrounding The Infiniverse became unfathomably silent. Over ninety percent of The Living Existences that had gathered, beings who could command the very fabric of reality, slumped down listlessly.","Their consciousnesses were entirely turned off, snuffed out like candle flames in a hurricane by the mere proximity of the terrifying existences that had arrived!","And yet, like a grand and terrifying sea, these waves of power and suppression that were culminating in Haki actually stopped short, parting like water before a sacred mountain as they neared the blue-gold Aegis of The Infiniverse.","Inside the small, world-sized isolated bubble, Noah stood, his gaze turning from the chaotic, beautiful garden to the scene outside. His eyes were cold, calculating, and utterly, profoundly, calm.","|Master, I am detecting a subtle, yet significant, anomaly in the existential signatures of the newly arrived Prime Dead.|","|Analysis: They are exhibiting... hesitation.|","...!","Hesitation?","Why would such powerful beings hesitate? Their gazes were fixed on his home with an intensity that was almost religious, and their very existence swam with a potent, undeniable allure of Order. Noah could put two and two together. The reason for their hesitation... he did not like the direction his thoughts were taking him.","\"The appearance of the Prime Dead is much faster than anticipated,\" Schrodinger’s voice was a low, analytical murmur beside him. \"Reinforcements will arrive here soon, but for the most part, all existences here are on their own.\"","At his words, Noah’s eyes flashed brightly. His gaze focused on the figure of the Dead Early Creature, Tatiana. She was floating from the vessel, her hand raised in a gesture that was both a command and a reassurance to her legion. She was moving, shockingly, towards The Infiniverse.","She paid no attention to the dazed, terrified Living Existences. Her focus was singular. She drew closer, and the blue-gold glow of the Aegis reflected on her pale, beautiful, and utterly dead features. And then, she stopped.","Noah watched this being, this queen of a dead empire, and his thoughts were a silent, rapid-fire exchange with his new System. ’RUIN/EDEN. The network of Resplendent Citadels is active, yes?’","|Confirmed, Master. The Civilization Network is online and operating at peak efficiency. All 159 Citadels are linked, their collective power forming a defensive matrix capable of withstanding an attack three times the capacity of your own current Complexity and Purity.|","|Analysis: Sufficient for a protracted defensive engagement against the current threat, but a direct, focused assault from their combined might would be... problematic.|","It may be enough, but the situation was still perilous. And yet, the Prime Dead did not attack. As Noah watched, Tatiana... opened her mouth to speak.","Her voice was a thing of impossible, terrible beauty. It was not a shout, but a clear, resonant pronouncement that carried across the void with the weight of an unshakeable, absolute truth.","\"I am Tatiana, the Ashen Dream Queen, First Blade of the Cryptlands of Nagash-Prax. I, and all those you see before you, are followers of THE Creature. We are followers of Order. We revere Order, and we live by its Doctrines. We had altered our course to come here directly because we sensed an allure, a beacon of Order so pure, so potent, that it could not be ignored. And now, having come close, I can affirm that what emanates from within this sanctuary... it is the truest type of Order. Living Order. It is for this reason, and this reason alone, that I show the respect that I currently am.\"","...!","In the Early Veiled Shore, Noah’s other body gently touched Sigrid’s shoulder. She came out of her deep, power-infusing cultivation, her form now pulsing with waves of pure, white-gold mana and Order.","She blinked, and as Noah directed her gaze to the scene unfolding outside the Infiniverse, her eyes widened.","Outside, Tatiana continued, her voice a calm, commanding current. \"I realize how our appearance here, especially our current state of existence, may seem threatening. It may even cause misconceptions. I wish to clear that up first, before anything else. I know that within this isolated, protective domain, lies a budding Living Order. And it is to you that I speak now, and to nobody else.\"","...!","Her gaze was fixed on the Aegis, but her words were a spear, aimed at a single heart within. \"I wish to ease the mind of the young Living Order and let them know that the reason for our being is none other than.. The Fallout.\"","HUUM!","As she spoke the final word, her expression, which had been a mask of regal calm, turned cold.","It was a subtle shift, a tightening around her eyes, a clenching of her jaw, a deep, chilling frost that seemed to settle over her features. She was reining in a storm of pure, incandescent rage.","\"The Fallout,\" she began again, her voice now a low, dangerous murmur, \"was a betrayal. A betrayal of all the ideals of existence, of Order, of what THE Creature stood for. The Fallout was a conspiracy, a grand, terrible design forged by multiple of THE Living Existences who turned their backs on THE Creature... and built something for their own sakes, for their own Civilizations. They built THE Loom... and I talk about THE Loom as I mention The Fallout because... these two are one and the same. THE Loom is The Fallout. THE Loom is the weapon of destruction that will extinguish every single Way of Existence and Civilization that lies outside of it, all for the sake of those within it.\"","BOOM!","Oh!","The words were a quiet, terrible detonation in the silent void. \"THE Loom is a shelter for those inside of it, and a weapon, a tool of mass destruction for those outside of it. Any of those that remain within have the blood of countless on their hands, as the destruction of the budding Civilizations and Ways of Existence of countless existences will all be collapsed and devoured by THE Loom. All of it will be harvested by THE Living Existences within it, the Early Creatures under them, and the Fold Dwellers who managed to gain entry into that abomination. For many of us, me included, and many others back in our lands... we consciously made the choice to not enter THE Loom when it was offered to us, because we knew the sheer depravity that would be required for its very existence.\"","...!"]},{"number":4326,"title":"Chapter 4326: Chapter 4325: Sheer Depravity! II","paragraphs":["\"We chose to stand with THE Creature and find another way. What you see before you is that way. I, and all those behind me, and countless others on the other side of The Veil, all chose to fight against the abomination that is THE Loom.\"","\"The reason for our coming through at this very moment was to lay out the path of survival for the countless masses, as THE Loom prepares to unleash its horrors upon all of existence. I had wished to tell you all of this because we also follow Order... on the other side of The Veil. Order helped us establish who we are today and fight against the tyranny of THE Living Existences against THE Creature. For there to be a piece of THE Living Order in this domain... is not by chance.\"","...!","Her words were heavy!","So, so heavy!","\"And so, after explaining all of this, I hereby invite THE Living Order within to come back with me to the other side of The Veil. Your mere existence... may very well change a tremendous amount of things. With you and the radiant Order that is on the other side of The Veil, the possibilities for existence and its survival against the abomination that is THE Loom... are tremendously altered. Once more... I hereby invite the Young Living Order to come with me to the other side of The Veil.\"","BOOM!","The invitation was a thing of impossible, terrible weight.","Noah’s eyes shone with a terrifying, brilliant light. Schrodinger and Leonore, in their isolated bubble, turned to him, their gazes stern and questioning.","|Master, the information provided by the subject ’Tatiana’ is a paradigm-shifting event.|","|Primary Revelations:|","| - [The Fallout] is not a natural event, but a man-made (or rather, Existence-made) one.|","| - [THE Loom] is not a passive sanctuary, but an active, predatory weapon.|","| - A significant faction, aligned with [THE Creature], exists on the other side of The Veil. Their objective is to oppose THE Loom.|","|Strategic Re-evaluation:|","| - The solution of [Halting the Catalyst] is now... significantly more complex. The catalyst is not a single entity, but a coalition of Level One Scale existences.|","| - The solution of [Breaching THE Loom] is now re-contextualized.|","| - The solution of [The First Farmer] remains a viable, if now more urgent, path for a potential third faction and alliance.|","Noah processed the information, his mind a silent storm of calculation. He opened his mouth, and his voice, a calm, resonant, and utterly absolute thing, boomed out from the isolated domain, reaching Tatiana and all those in the surrounding void.","\"You have mentioned Order multiple times on the other side of The Veil... just who is embodying Order on the other side of The Veil?\"","His voice echoed out.","Tatiana frowned. She did not like that someone other than the Living Order had replied to her. But she answered, her voice as calm and as cold as a tombstone. \"On the other side of The Veil, the only Order that has been present and aiding THE Creature has been THE Dead Order.\"","BOOM!","The Dead Order. One of THE Living Existences... on the side of The Dead.","In the Early Veiled Shore, Sigrid fell to her knees, the revelation a physical blow. But Noah remained calm. His voice boomed out again. \"You mentioned THE Living Order from here coming with you to the other side of The Veil... THE Living Order on this side is merely a resurgence, unable to make any grand changes in existence. How exactly would their crossing over change anything in the vast weavings of what is unfolding?\"","Tatiana’s frown deepened. \"I would very much like to be discussing all of this with THE Living Order, and not a bystander.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed with a cold light. \"Whether you stand to have any discussion with THE Living Order or not is dependent on whether you answer this question. What exactly would THE Living Order be doing if she crosses to the other side of The Veil?\"","The air grew cold. A silent, terrible wave of power pulsed from Tatiana.","But she held it in check. \"Out of respect to the Order that we follow, I will answer. THE Living Order coming to the other side of The Veil would mean that THE Dead Order and THE Living Order can come and join together in a profound and unfathomable union that may just be the grandest answer to THE Loom and the abomination of actions that were taken to enact it.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed coldly.","|Master, the probability of a true ’union’ is 0.01%. The probability of a complete and total assimilation of the lesser, resurgent Order by the established, primordial Dead Order is 99.99%. She is asking for a sacrifice.|","In the deafening silence that followed, only one reply came. Two simple words from Noah, ringing with a glorious, tyrannical clarity.","\"Fuck off.\"","BOOM!","Tatiana’s eyes flashed with lividity.","\"Due to the immense respect and decorum that I have for Order, I am holding myself back right now from this very clear disrespect. I ask once more, do not speak on behalf of THE Living Order. I wish to have this dialogue with nobody else other than THE Living Order.\"","She waited. The silence stretched. And then, again, the same two words, in the same grand, glorious, tyrannical voice.","\"Fuck off.\"","BOOM!","Oh!","Oh!","Tatiana had reached the end of her patience. \"We are a solution to the abomination that is THE Loom,\" she stated, her voice now a cold, flat pronouncement.","\"That solution is to grant all living existences on this side of The Veil the blessing of becoming like us. This was a mercy designed by THE Creature and THE Dead Order, and we will now proceed in carrying it out.\"","\"Alongside this will be the procurement and safe obtainment of THE Living Order, who seems to have been taken captive by an entity with intentions that do not align with THE Creature or with Order itself. With respect to the Order that we continue to hold in high regard... we will now begin our operation to rescue you from the clutches of this entity.\"","...!"]},{"number":4327,"title":"Chapter 4327: Chapter 4326: A Glorious Protocol! I","paragraphs":["A terrifying progression.","In existence, there are good enemies, and there are horrid enemies. A good enemy is a straightforward thing.","They want your land, your resources, your head on a spike. They make their intentions clear, and they attack you. You fight, you win or you lose. It is a clean, honest, and brutal transaction.","But a horrid enemy... a horrid enemy is a different beast entirely. They are the ones who attack you while telling you they are doing it for your own good. To save you. To make sure you do not harm yourself.","They are the ones who will burn your house to the ground and then explain, with a sad, paternalistic smile, that they were simply trying to keep you warm. These types of enemies... they are absolutely the worst.","In the Early Veiled Shore.","A profound stillness had settled over the Radiant Shore. The joyous, chaotic energy of progression had given way to a quiet, focused solemnity.","Across the golden sands, Noah’s people had emerged from their states of rapid, endowment-fueled cultivation.","Sigrid rose, her form a beacon of pure white Order against the azure backdrop of the Shore. Noah turned to her, a faint, almost teasing smile on his lips. \"Are you my captive?\"","She looked at him, and her eyes, which held the serene, unyielding light of a fundamental law, flashed with a flicker of something almost like... annoyance. \"It doesn’t seem like I am,\" she said, her voice a calm, even current.","\"But these existences...\" Her gaze drifted to the screens, to the silent, orderly legions of The Prime Dead, and a shadow of concern crossed her perfect features.","Noah saw it, that flicker of worry, and his smile softened. \"They are merely Prime Dead,\" he said, his voice a quiet, reassuring anchor in the sea of her unspoken fears. \"Nothing too crazy.\"","In the next moment, a new presence made itself known.","Khor floated towards him, her diminutive form a stark, beautiful contrast to the vast, open expanse of the Shore, her abyssal eyes pulsing with a contained, ancient power. She turned and looked across the Shore, her gaze settling on the far corner where a second, identical body of herself was calmly overseeing the separation of Bob from the Mutated In Abitability, with Liora standing nearby, her face a mask of anxious, hopeful anticipation.","Khor looked at all of this, then turned back to Noah. \"I need to let loose, Outsider,\" she said, her voice a low, dangerous purr. \"I am holding a little anger inside of me, and it would be good to express it. With how much I have been eating... I could likely keep that Tatiana busy. Though she is not a simple one, as she appears. You would have to find a way to deal with the other ones.\"","...!","Noah smiled at her words. Yes, out of all the impossible, terrible weapons in his arsenal, Khor was undoubtedly one of the strongest. With his power, her power, and the overwhelming might of the Resplendent Citadels, they might just be able to hold back this terrifying new force.","But...","Noah shook his head.","He stared at Khor, at his people, at the magnificent, terrible army he had built, and his smile widened into a grand, tyrannical expression. \"You all have gotten a glimpse of My Way. My Civilization. I now wish to give you... a full look at it.\"","BOOM!","A full look!","Khor was astonished. She looked at him, at the quiet, unshakeable confidence in his eyes, and she realized, with a shock that was a profound, almost delightful thing, that against an enemy that was three, perhaps four times more powerful than him, he was denying her help. Why? Could his Way of Existence be that terrifying?","His Complexity and Purity was only at approximately one Quintillion, while Tatiana alone exceeded four Quintillion, and there were others behind her at three Quintillion and two Quintillion.","Nearly all those he stood against were more powerful than him.","\"Are you sure, Outsider?\" she asked, her voice a mixture of genuine concern and a deep, ancient curiosity.","Noah smiled and nodded. \"Yes. Watch My Way of Existence. Watch My Way of the Mana Architect. Watch My Civilization... and try to hold on strong to your Hunger.\"","...!","He spoke the words with a grand, almost playful, authority. Khor shook her head with a look of pure, unadulterated incredulity. \"You are insane, Outsider.\"","At that moment, Noah smiled. He closed his eyes and sent his will to RUIN/EDEN.","’Are the Mana Arcana Glyphs I told you to design ready?’","...!","Yes. Mana Arcana Glyphs!","In the Earliest Folds, he had only forged the Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball that dealt half a Quintillion in damage and the Mana Arcana Glyph: Annihilation’s First Spark that dealt 1.5 Quintillion damage.","But his body had still remained in the Earliest Folds this whole time, and in the hours that had passed there, it had been very, very productive.","Endless Mana had been used to forge an arsenal of the most powerful Mana Arcana Glyphs he could imagine, Glyphs that would allow him to truly express just how terrifying his Way of Existence was!","Because his strength and the strength of his System, at the end of the day, lay in Mana. Infinite Mana.","And for something others did not have, how could he use it best? The answer was terrifyingly clear!","Otherd had limitations of Everythings and much more, but he...did not!","\"Show me.\"","His existence buzzed as he gave the command to RUIN/EDEN, and in the quiet, internal sanctum of his mind, a glorious, terrible presentation began.","|Project: [One Man Army] is complete, Master. Multiple new Mana Arcana Glyphs have been added to your Codex. Allow me to begin the demonstration.|","In his mind’s eye, the radiant, card-like structure of the Annihilation’s First Spark bloomed into existence.","On its surface, a magnificent, nine-headed Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm slept, its azure scales shimmering with a contained, apocalyptic power!"]},{"number":4328,"title":"Chapter 4328: Chapter 4327: A Glorious Protocol! II","paragraphs":["The first one displayed in his mind was what he had already forged before, but it was still a critical piece of his Codex!","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: Annihilation’s First Spark]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’From the smallest spark, the greatest inferno is born.’ This Arcana summons a [Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm], a being of pure, conceptual fire forged from your own, infinite essence. The Wyrm unleashes a single, guided torrent of annihilating azure flame.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: Due to its rarity, it deals 1.5 Quintillion in pure, untyped Mana-based damage that ignores all known resistances and authorities. The attack is conceptually ’true’ and cannot be dodged. Its capabilities will advance and scale upwards as you progress.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","The illusory image of the first card moved to the side, and a new one floated into view.","On its surface was a glorious, azure-furred beast, a Mellivora benfieldi, an ancient honey badger, its eyes blazing with a defiant, almost comical, indifference.","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Indomitable Will]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’Existence is a relentless, brutal assault. This Arcana simply... does not care.’ Summons the conceptual form of an Ancient Honey Badger, a being whose very nature is a defiant rejection of all external influence. The Badger floats above the caster, a silent, furry guardian of pure, unadulterated stubbornness.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: For one minute, you are protected by a [Badger’s Barrier of Mana], a shield capable of absorbing up to 1.5 Quintillion in damage from any source. As they say... a honey badger does not give a damn.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","Noah’s mind buzzed as he looked at its full details. He nodded once. \"Let’s see the next ones.\"","The presentation continued, a pageant of impossible, beautiful, and utterly broken tools of war.","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Unshakeable Mountain]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’The storm rages, the winds howl, but the mountain remains.’ This Arcana summons not a creature, but a concept: a spectral, azure mountain range that surrounds the caster, a fortress of pure, unyielding stability.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: Grants the [Mountain’s Heart] aura for one minute. All incoming attacks are reduced by 1 Quintillion in power. This is a flat reduction, not a percentage. Small attacks are simply... negated.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Tyrant’s Maw]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’The ocean is not just water; it is a mouth.’ Summons the conceptual ghost of a Megalodon, its form a shimmering, azure vortex of pure, predatory hunger.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: For one minute, all of your attacks deal 50% more damage. This is a conceptual amplification; your very intent to harm is made more potent.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Saber’s Edge]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’There is no defense against a perfect cut.’ Summons the ephemeral spirit of a Smilodon, its azure fangs long, sharp, and impossibly, conceptually, true.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: For one minute, all of your attacks gain a base damage of 1 Quintillion. This damage is applied before all other multipliers and ignores all resistances.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Unbreakable Shell]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’The best offense is an impenetrable defense.’ Summons the spectral carapace of an ancient Ankylosaurus, a living fortress of azure, crystalline plates.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: For one minute, all incoming damage is reduced by 25%.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","|[Mana Arcana Glyph: The Unbound Moment]|","|School: Mana (Primordial)|","|Rarity: Primordial|","|Description: ’Time is a river. This Arcana is a dam.’ Summons a glorious, spectral Wheel of Existence, its azure form spinning with the light of a billion frozen moments.|","|Cost: 1 Unit of [Everythings of Mana].|","|Requirements to Cast: Must be the Architect of Mana.|","|Effect: For one minute, all of your abilities, including your Mana Arcana Glyphs, have no cooldown.|","|Cooldown: 1 Second.|","..!","Noah looked at the glorious, terrible arsenal that had been laid out before him in the quiet of his own mind. A one-second cooldown. He could, theoretically, have them all active at once. He could become a walking, talking, and utterly unbreakable apocalypse!","And he even went further to give a big middle finger to cooldowns with another terrifying Arcana!","Oh!","\"Okay,\" he said, his voice a quiet, satisfied hum. \"The Codex is coming along nicely. Let us go and show others what the Way of Mana truly means, okay?\"","—","Being overpowered.","Many...misunderstand the very idea of this concept itself!","It’s like the difference between imagining being rich (yacht parties and endless vacation) versus actually being rich (mostly tax documents and people asking for money).","Most believe being overpowered means winning every fight, solving every problem with a gesture, having Existence bend to your whims. They imagine it as freedom from consequence, the ultimate power fantasy where you’re basically playing life with cheat codes enabled.","This...was a fundamental misunderstanding of the burden of being overpowered!","Some say that truly overpowered beings understand something the power-seekers don’t: strength isn’t freedom- it’s prison. The stronger you become, the smaller your world gets. Every increase in power is a decrease in things that can matter to you.","This is why truly overpowered beings often become either utterly detached or desperately attached to tiny, trivial things. THE Creature playing with Early Creatures and Fold Dwellers like pets. THE Living Paradox obsessing over THE Creature!","Some overpowered beings cling to whatever can still provide meaning in an existence that has become tissue paper to their touch.","What it truly means to be overpowered is to be disconnected from the very fabric of existence you sought to master.","It was winning so thoroughly that there’s no game left to play. It’s being so strong that strength itself...becomes meaningless.","Some believe that those who are genuinely overpowered don’t seek more power. They seek limitations, weaknesses, something...anything, that can make them feel connected to existence again.","The goal of becoming overpowered is to never have to struggle again.","But struggle...is what gives existence meaning.","So when someone says they want to be overpowered, what they really mean is they want to be just powerful enough to overcome their current problems. Actually being overpowered? Well...this was hard to conceptualize!"]},{"number":4329,"title":"Chapter 4329: Chapter 4328: A Glorious Protocol! III","paragraphs":["In the isolated bubble where Noah, Schrodinger, and Leonore Rureaux were meeting.","POP!","The small, world-sized isolated domain popped like a soap bubble, its blue-gold light scattering into the chaotic void of Collapse.","Noah began to float up, his figure a slow, deliberate ascent into the heart of the storm. His presence immediately came under the gazes of Tatiana and the Prime Dead, who had been waiting with a profound, terrible patience. Their collective authority, a silent, crushing weight, began to buzz with a new, focused power.","From the small garden he had just left, Schrodinger frowned, his usual playful demeanor gone, replaced by a mask of genuine concern.","\"What exactly could you be doing, friend?\" he shouted, his voice a sharp, cutting blade of disbelief. \"I did not take you for someone on a suicide mission...\"","...!","Noah ignored the words. He continued his ascent, a silent, tyrannical king rising to meet a challenge.","He came to a stop at the same level as Tatiana, the two of them now facing each other across a chasm of silent, simmering hostility.","It was a glorious, terrible standoff. And in the periphery of this cosmic duel, a quiet, almost comical, exodus was underway.","The Living Existences who had remained conscious, beings who could command the very fabric of reality, were now engaged in a desperate, silent retreat.","They pulled along their unconscious comrades, their movements a frantic, chaotic scramble to get as far away from this impending cataclysm as possible.","They did not run; they scurried, their usual regal dignity replaced by the primal, undeniable urge to simply... not be here!","Tatiana’s gaze, cold and sharp as a shard of obsidian, swept over Noah, a slow, dismissive up-and-down assessment. \"Are you the one,\" she asked, her voice the sound of a tombstone cracking, \"who has been disrespectfully replying on behalf of THE Living Order and holding her captive?\"","Noah gazed back at her, at the legion of Prime Dead Early Creatures that were beginning to rise on the vessel behind her, at the hundreds of obsidian-white Dead Existential Armors that were now lighting up, their dead eyes glowing with a cold, malevolent light.","\"I’m the one who has been telling you to fuck off,\" he replied, his voice not a shout, but a low, resonant, and utterly absolute pronouncement. \"But you cannot seem to get the message.\"","...!","His words were a physical weight in the dead air. Tatiana’s eyes pulsed with a dangerous, crimson light. But Noah was not done.","\"Are you the same Tatiana who held a concentrated Everything of THE Creature?\" he asked, his tone now a blade of pure, condescending curiosity. \"You seem a bit weak compared to others of your stature, like Gilgamesh... is this a lesser body of yours, or did you simply not live up to the potential you were born with? You were not defective... right?\"","BOOM!","The words were a calculated, tyrannical cruelty, a series of precise, surgical strikes aimed at the very heart of her pride. And in response, Tatiana smiled.","\"Okay.\"","A single word. She didn’t curse. She didn’t bellow in rage. She simply said, \"Okay,\" and the very fabric of the collapsed space trembled.","A brilliant, pristine white light of Order began to pulse around her, and woven within it, a deep, obsidian grandeur, the unmistakable signature of a Principle, began to bloom.","The moment that terrifying display of aura began, Noah’s eyes flashed with a cold, almost bored, light. \"Activate the One Man Army Protocol.\"","...!","One Man Army. He named it this because other entities, even the great and terrible beings of the Earliest Folds, had their limits.","They had to expend their Everythings, a finite, precious resource, to unleash their most terrifying capabilities. This limitation... his existence did not even register it.","He had Infinite Mana. And his most terrifying capabilities, his Mana Arcana Glyphs... all ran on Mana.","In the next instant, a glorious, swirling storm of stellar blue brilliance erupted around him. The first Mana Arcana Glyph was cast.","|[The Indomitable Will] has been activated.|","A wave of pure, boundless Mana, an ocean of it, surged from his small figure. It coalesced above him, forming a creature of impossible, glorious defiance.","It was a Mellivora benfieldi, an ancient honey badger, its form now a shimmering, spectral azure. Its eyes were two cold, arrogant stars, and they gazed out at Tatiana and her legion with a look of profound, absolute indifference.","|The conceptual form of an Ancient Honey Badger has been summoned. It is a being whose very nature is a defiant rejection of all external influence. For one minute, you are protected by a [Badger’s Barrier of Mana], a shield capable of absorbing up to 1.5 Quintillion in damage. As they say... a honey badger does not give a damn.|","A shimmering, azure barrier, its surface a swirling, chaotic vortex of pure, unyielding will, formed around Noah. But the symphony of his power had only just begun.","|Master, the other Mana Arcana Glyphs under the [One Man Army Protocol] are being activated.|","|[The Unbound Moment] has been cast.|","|[The Tyrant’s Maw] has been cast.|","|[The Unbreakable Shell] has been cast.|","|[The Saber’s Edge] has been cast.|","|[The Unshakeable Mountain] has been cast.|","Above him, the azure badger was joined by a pantheon of impossible, beautiful, and utterly terrifying manifestations.","A glorious, spectral Wheel of Existence, its azure form spinning with the light of a billion frozen moments, appeared, its presence a declaration that time itself was now his to command.","The conceptual ghost of a Megalodon, its form a shimmering, azure vortex of pure, predatory hunger, materialized, its silent roar a promise of a feast to come!","A spectral carapace of an ancient Ankylosaurus, a living fortress of azure, crystalline plates, formed a second, denser layer of defense around him!","HUUM!","The ephemeral spirit of a Smilodon, its azure fangs long, sharp, and impossibly, conceptually, true, materialized, its silent roar a promise of a perfect, unavoidable cut.","And finally, a vast, spectral mountain range, a fortress of pure, unyielding stability, rose behind him, its peaks scraping against the very firmament of the Fold.","He was a glorious, terrible sight. The entire region around him was now a roiling sea of his Mana, and from its depths, these six colossal, illusory manifestations glared out at his enemies, a council of primordial titans ready to dispense judgment!","OOOOH!","|Finalizing Protocol...|","|All buffs are now active.|","| - [The Unbound Moment]: For one minute, all of your abilities, including your Mana Arcana Glyphs, have no cooldown.|","| - [The Tyrant’s Maw]: For one minute, all of your attacks deal 50% more damage.|","| - [The Unbreakable Shell]: For one minute, all incoming damage is reduced by 25%.|","| - [The Saber’s Edge]: For one minute, all of your attacks gain a base damage of 1 Quintillion.|","| - [The Unshakeable Mountain]: For one minute, all incoming attacks are reduced by 1 Quintillion in power.|","| - [The Indomitable Will]: A barrier of 1.5 Quintillion stands ready to absorb all harm.|","The final summary bloomed, a stark, numerical declaration of his new, impossible reality.","|One Man Army Protocol: Status Update.|","|Active Buffs: 6.|","|Defensive Capacity: Your [Mana-Born Aegis of the Architect] and its [Innate Omnichalcum Aura Field] provide a base defense of 920 Quadrillion. The [Badger’s Barrier of Mana] adds a 1.5 Quintillion buffer. [The Unshakeable Mountain] provides a flat 1 Quintillion reduction to all incoming attacks. [The Unbreakable Shell] provides a 25% reduction to all damage that bypasses these defenses.|","|Total Defensive Threshold: You can currently withstand a single, instantaneous blow of approximately 4.5+ Quintillion in power, or a sustained assault of a lesser, but still astronomical, magnitude.|","|Offensive Capacity: Your base power of 1 Quintillion, amplified by [The Saber’s Edge] to a base of 2 Quintillion, is then further amplified by 50% through [The Tyrant’s Maw]. Your every attack will now carry a base damage of 4.5 Quintillion. All of this, with no cooldowns for the next minute.|"]},{"number":4330,"title":"Chapter 4330: Chapter 4329: MANA! I","paragraphs":["The scene was a paradox of glorious, terrible power.","A single, defiant figure stood wreathed in a sea of his own boundless Mana, surrounded by a pantheon of six colossal, spectral guardians. Before him, an army of endings waited, their silent, orderly ranks a testament to a power that had transcended the chaos of death!","In the span of an instant, a silent, lightning-fast conversation, a torrent of pure, conceptual data, flashed between Tatiana and the Prime Dead Early Creatures behind her as they communicated together simultaneously!","Tatiana’s thoughts were a blade of cold, precise logic.","\"The enemy is utilizing a system similar to our own Living Astral Codex. The manifestations are potent, but they are temporary. All such abilities have a cost, a cooldown. He has played his hand too early.\"","Valerius, his half-skeletal face a mask of regal amusement, sent his own thoughts in reply.","\"His power is impressive, for a fleeting moment. His Codex must be of a high grade, but it cannot be limitless. He may have ten, perhaps twenty Arcana at his disposal. Once their timers run out, he will be a firefly against a sun.\"","...!","Tatiana’s mind was a whirlwind of calculation as she nodded.","\"He who is hasty in the hunt, who shows his full strength at the first rustle of leaves, will find his arrows spent when the true beast emerges from the shadows. The patient hunter, who waits, who observes, who understands that time is a weapon... he is the one who feasts.\"","She paused, a flicker of something almost like caution in her thoughts. \"But treat this one with extreme care. He was capable of capturing and restraining THE Living Order. That is not the mark of a fool.\"","HUUM!","Another of the Prime Dead, a being whose form was a beautiful, grotesque fusion of bone and shadow, interjected.","\"And what of The Living Order, Ashen Queen? If he falls, what is our protocol for her?\"","Tatiana’s reply was a cold, absolute command. \"While I hold him down, I will give the word. You will penetrate that protective domain. You will procure THE Living Order. And you will treat them with the respect they are due. They are a prize, not a prisoner.\"","The Prime Dead nodded in silent, unified assent. The plan was set. Tatiana’s gaze, now a thing of pure, unadulterated focus, settled on the defiant, flame-wreathed figure across the void.","\"Child,\" she asked, her voice a demeaning, almost bored, inquiry, \"what is your name?\"","Noah did not answer. He simply stared at her, his expression a cold, unreadable mask. The six glorious, tyrannical manifestations behind him... the Badger, the Mountain, the Wheel, the Shark, the Saber Cat, the Shell... they stared back at her, their collective gaze a silent, crushing weight.","She did not wait for a reply she knew would not come.","She changed her tactics, her voice now a sharp, probing question. \"Early Creature, what is your name? How did you get your hands on a Codex after the purge? Do you know that your actions are going against your Ancestor right now? Against THE Creature?\"","...!","She knew the words were a potent weapon. All Early Creatures, in their own way, held a deep, almost instinctual, reverence for THE Creature. What was this one’s Origin? His Lineage?","But the entity opposite her simply looked on, his expression one of arrogant, almost pitying, amusement.","\"I’ll be sure to check with my Lineage,\" he said, his voice a low, dangerous hum that was more terrifying than any shout, \"but I can’t recall any time THE Creature came down to give a damn about me or anyone else. But... I truly don’t feel like talking right now. You talked a damn lot earlier. I feel like fighting right now. I feel like killing.\"","...!","Tatiana smiled at his words. She laughed. A silent, terrible, and utterly genuine laugh.","At her amusement, the legion behind her moved. The Prime Dead Early Creatures and the few hundred Dead Existential Armors began to line up, a billowing, obsidian wave of absolute, ordered power against a single, defiant entity.","\"You don’t feel like fighting because you have hastily used up your Arcana and they will expire soon,\" she said, her voice a condescending, almost instructional, lecture. \"Use up a few more, and you will be done. All you will have left will be your Haki, your Glyphs, and your Complexity. This is why you feel like fighting right away. I thought of wasting time to put your Arcana to waste, but let me stretch my muscles here a bit. I haven’t truly moved around in a while.\"","...!","At her words, a billowing, obsidian light erupted from her, covering the right half of her body completely.","Her entire figure was now wreathed in shimmering, obsidian flames. She closed her eyes, and she felt her power.","Her Existence. Her Way.","Her Way was... the Way of Dreams.","She was a Dreamer. She was THE Creature’s very Dream. And she... was mighty.","BOOM!","In the next moment, the already terrifying power radiating from Tatiana rumbled, and when she opened her eyes again, her entire aura, her very complexity, had more than doubled.","Doubled!","For this was her Way. This was her Principle.","The Principle of the Waking Dream!","A Principle that allowed the wielder to pull the ’dreamed’ or ’ideal’ version of their own existence into reality, superimposing it upon their current form!","It was an act of making a potential future into an absolute present.","And this was her Dream. Her Way.","She opened her eyes. The left was its usual, cold, crimson light. But the right... the right was now a swirling, obsidian-gold vortex, a gateway into a realm of pure, untamed dreams.","She looked at the defiant figure who had dared to keep THE Living Order from her, and she whispered, her voice a final, absolute verdict.","\"I won’t even transform you. You... are not deserving of such a blessing.\"","She took a single, graceful step. \"Do you understand?\"","She said the words not from across the void, but from inches away from Noah, her form having crossed the impossible distance in an instant.","She was there, a queen of dreams and death, her power a suffocating, absolute presence.","But shockingly... the entity surrounded by a sea of mana was already looking at her, his expression calm, his gaze cold!","Even her Quintillions of Complexity and Purity that had just erupted from her... he did not seem phased!","Oh!"]},{"number":4331,"title":"Chapter 4331: Chapter 4330: MANA! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s existence buzzed as waves of information crossed through his eyes rapidly.","He stood as a silent, colossal titan wreathed in a sea of his own Mana, the six spectral manifestations of his Arcana a pantheon of azure gods at his back.","Before him, Tatiana, the Ashen Dream Queen of the Prime Dead, had just completed her own impossible transformation.","|Target Analysis Initiated.|","|Subject: [Tatiana – The Ashen Dream Queen].|","|A Grand Principle has been activated: [The Principle of the Waking Dream].|","|Analysis: This Principle allows the wielder to superimpose their ’ideal’ or ’dreamed’ self upon their current reality. It is an act of forcing a potential future into an absolute present. The cost is immense, but the amplification of power is... considerable.|","|Power Fluctuation Detected: The subject’s Complexity has surged from a baseline of 4.1 Quintillion to a new, terrifying plateau.|","|Current Complexity: 8,500,000,000,000,000,000 (8.5 Quintillion).|","|Threat Assessment: Critical. The subject’s power now significantly exceeds your defensive thresholds.|","Noah looked at the new number. It was mightier. It was heavier. It was a declaration of absolute, overwhelming superiority.","One of the core power that Early Creatures had wss the fact that they had been utilizing Principles for a long time, and what they could do with them was utterly terrifying.","Even now, Noah only had Seeds of Principles!","Mind you...he had the Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest for a few days, and the Seed of the Cheating Architect for a few hours.","Hours.","They had yet to mature, even though in his own tyrannical perspective, it was taking too long! Even though others waited years for their Seeds of Principles to mature.","He was not others!","So even if Tatiana now stood at 8 Quintillion in power...","So what?!","BOOM!","The moment was a masterpiece of silent, terrible, and beautiful violence. Time did not slow; it was simply forced to accommodate an action that was too fast for it.","Tatiana’s hand, now wreathed in the shimmering, obsidian light of her Principle, flashed towards his neck. It was not a physical strike; it was a conceptual one.","It was the very idea of ’capture’ given form, an absolute, unyielding law that sought to bypass every defense, every barrier, every last shred of his glorious, tyrannical will, and lock him down.","She knew this with a certainty that was its own form of power.","She had dreamed this. Noah could feel it, a wave of pure, confident intent washing over him. He could feel the cold, logical calculus of his own defenses being exceeded, the Badger’s Barrier and the Mountain’s Heart groaning under a weight they were not designed to bear. That hand, a thing of dreams and death, would reach him.","But...","He had his Way.","His Way of Existence.","And he had told his people to watch.","So...","Towards the coming hand, the hand that was now inches away, a blur of absolute, inevitable finality... he closed his eyes.","HUUM!","...!","In the distance, Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux’s expressions changed. They had thought, for a fleeting, hopeful moment, that The Early Creature, Osmont, might just exceed their every expectation.","But to close his eyes at such a moment? When an unstoppable force was coming?","And yet, Noah smiled. A grand, glorious, and utterly serene smile.","An unstoppable force, yes. But what happened when an unstoppable force met an immovable object?","His Way of Existence... was immovable.","In the quiet, internal sanctum of his own being, he called out. Not a shout, not a command, but a tender, almost loving whisper.","\"Fireball.\"","...!","Fireball.","Not a Mana Arcana Glyph. Not a complex Weave of his new Artifice. Just... Fireball.","Of course, this was the [Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball].","It had no cooldown. Its base damage, a paltry half-Quintillion, was negligible against the might of the Ashen Dream Queen. But after the empowerment of his Mana Arcana Glyphs, its power was no longer negligible. Its base damage now exceeded five Quintillion.","A glorious, beautiful, and utterly terrifying bloom of blue and crimson light appeared in the space between them!","It was not just a ball of fire; it was a miniature, captured sun fold, a newborn sun fold, a concept of annihilation given a simple, nostalgic name.","The heat it contained was not a temperature; it was a memory of the birth and death of Omniverses, of the screaming, final moments of a billion Wheels of Existence!","It... was a thing that could have scorched a Minor Fold, and it bloomed in the infinitesimal space between his neck and her hand.","It smashed into Tatiana’s hand, and the impact was shockingly... silent. Contained. Her tyrannical power, her Principle, the very dream of her own invincibility, absorbed it. She continued on.","A pause.","This was all a single Primordial Fireball did.","But...","Noah’s smile became wider.","\"Fireball. Fireball. Fireball.\"","Three repeating words, spoken in the same instant. And in that same instant, three more Primordial Fireballs appeared, a rapid, stuttering pulse of pure, conceptual destruction. They smashed into her advancing hand.","BOOM! BOOM!","The first two struck, and she faltered. The silent, effortless absorption was gone, replaced by a visible, shuddering strain. Her advance halted.","BOOM!","The third one struck. And the battlefield, which had been a silent, terrible tableau, erupted.","A scorching heatwave, a physical, tangible thing, washed over the entire region of Collapse. The very space around them began to boil, to sizzle!","HUUM!","In the distance, Schrodinger and Leonore’s expressions turned stern. Schrodinger waved a hand, and a shimmering, paradoxical light, the authority of an unknown Principle, covered them.","This temperature, this raw, untamed power... it could have scorched a being of one Quintillion or below into conceptual ash!","Only at this time did Noah open his eyes. Tatiana... was no longer inches away from him.","She had been pushed back, her form still pulsing with a terrible, beautiful power, but on her face was a look of pure, unadulterated surprise. She was looking at her hand. It was smoking!","She looked up, her obsidian-gold eye blazing with a new, more profound, and utterly furious light.","Noah cracked his neck, a slow, deliberate, and utterly arrogant gesture, as if he were merely stretching after a light warm-up.","\"Little Dream of THE Creature,\" he said, his voice a low, dangerous purr that was more terrifying than any roar. \"Get ready.\"","HUUM!","\"I’m coming.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4332,"title":"Chapter 4332: Chapter 4331: MANA! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s declaration was a quiet thunderclap in the dead air, a promise of violence that made the very fabric of Collapse hold its breath!","He was coming!","Tatiana watched him, her obsidian-gold eye a swirling vortex of analytical fury. She saw the six spectral manifestations of his power, the arrogant calm on his face, and she prepared. The obsidian flames of her Principle, the Waking Dream, danced around her, a corona of pure, absolute power.","Then, he began!","It was not a charge, not a grand, sweeping attack. It was a storm. A relentless, unending, and utterly tyrannical artillery barrage of pure, conceptual destruction.","\"Fireball.\"","The word was a whisper, a soft, almost gentle, murmur.","And from the roiling sea of his Mana, a single, perfect sphere of crimson-blue fire bloomed into existence.","It was a thing of terrible, beautiful power, a miniature sun fold born for the sole purpose of annihilation. It streaked across the void, and Tatiana met it!","BOOM!","She did not raise a shield; she simply wove a dream. A flicker of her authority, a whisper of her Principle, and a perfect, identical copy of the fireball appeared before her, smashing into the real one in a silent, contained detonation.","She smiled. A simple, elegant counter. But as the light of the first explosion faded, another was already there.","\"Fireball.\"","And another. And another.","\"Fireball. Fireball. Fireball. Fireball.\"","He did not shout. He did not roar!","His voice was a calm, steady, and unending metronome of death. With every whispered word, another sun fold was born, another bolt of 5-Quintillion-damage power streaking towards her.","She wove dream after dream, her own vast authority a wellspring of counter-spells. A wall of dreamt ice. A mirror of imagined realities. An afterimage of herself that absorbed the blow.","But he was relentless. It was a storm of a thousand suns, a blizzard of annihilation.","For every dream she wove, he had a fire to burn it. Her calm, analytical facade began to crack. A flicker of genuine, profound annoyance entered her eyes. This was not a battle of skill; it was a battle of attrition, and his reserves, impossibly, seemed to be... infinite.","The space between them became a canvas of glorious, terrible chaos. Explosions of crimson and blue painted the dark void, each detonation a silent, beautiful flower of pure, unadulterated power.","The very fabric of Collapse began to fray at the edges, the sheer, overwhelming energy of their duel too much for even this realm of endings to bear.","Tatiana’s advance had not just been stopped; it had been turned into a desperate, stationary defense!","She!","Who was more powerful!","She gritted her teeth, the sound a silent grinding of primordial power.","\"Enough!\"","WAA!","She raised her hand, and from the aether, a shimmering, conceptual Grimoire, her own Living Astral Codex, materialized.","It opened, and from its pages, a single, terrible card of light flew into her hand. It depicted a skeletal devil, its wings woven from solidified screams, its eyes hollow pits of absolute, final sorrow.","\"You have shown me your little fireworks, Child,\" she hissed, her voice a low, venomous promise.","\"Now, let me show you a true dream of endings.\" She raised the card glyph high, her voice a booming, terrible incantation that seemed to shake the very foundations of the Fold.","\"Let the Dream of Cessation Bloom...Final Verse: The Ashen Requiem!\"","HUUM!","The card dissolved into a wave of pure, necrotic authority. The skeletal devil from the Glyph materialized behind her, but it was no longer a mere image!","It was a being of 15 Quintillion in Complexity, its form a colossus of bone and despair that dwarfed even Noah’s spectral guardians. It opened its mouth, and it began to sing.","HUUM!","The song was not a sound. It was a wave of pure, weaponized grief, a melody of absolute, final cessation. It was the feeling of a billion civilizations dying at once, of every hope turning to ash, of the very concept of a future being erased.","It was an attack that did not target the body, but the very will to exist.","Noah watched the colossal, weeping angel, felt the soul-crushing weight of its song, and his own eyes flashed with a cold, tyrannical light. He raised his hand, and his own Codex, the blue-gold Grimoire of the Mana Architect, appeared.","\"Annihilation’s First Spark,\" he commanded, his voice a calm, steady counterpoint to the angel’s terrible song.","A single, Primordial Arcana Glyph flew from the book. From it, a creature of pure, incandescent rage was born.","A Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm, its blue scales shimmering with the light of a billion suns, its nine heads a chorus of pure, untamed fire.","It was a being of nearly 6 Quintillion in power, a terrible, beautiful, and utterly defiant beast.","Tatiana smiled. It was a cruel, triumphant expression.","His power was magnificent, yes, but it was a candle against her inferno. The Requiem would unmake his creature, and then it would unmake him!","But then, Noah spoke again, his voice a cold, flat, and utterly impossible echo.","\"Annihilation’s First Spark.\"","BOOM!","A second Wyrm appeared, identical to the first.","\"Annihilation’s First Spark.\"","A third.","...!","Tatiana’s smile vanished. Her eyes widened, the obsidian-gold vortex of her Principle-infused eye flaring with a light of pure, unadulterated disbelief.","How? the thought was a silent, frantic scream in her mind. An Astral Arcana Glyph has a cooldown. How was he able to cast it three times?!","There was no answer. There was only the roar of three Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms, their nine heads each unleashing a torrent of annihilating azure flame.","The 27 beams, each carrying the weight of Quintillions in pure, untyped, unstoppable damage, merged into a single, colossal river of pure, conceptual fire!","The song of the Ashen Requiem met the roar of the three Wyrms. The wave of absolute despair crashed against a tidal wave of absolute annihilation.","BOOM!","Oh!","The impact was a thing of sublime, terrible beauty. It was not an explosion of light and sound, but a silent, violent tearing of reality itself.","The very fabric of Collapse was unraveled, the space between the Folds shredded into a chaotic, beautiful storm of raw, untamed energy. Scorching flames and a mana of impossibly high temperature washed over everything, a cleansing, apocalyptic fire that seemed to burn away the very concept of existence.","When the light finally, reluctantly, faded, the scene was one of profound, shocking stillness. The three Wyrms were gone, their purpose served. The colossal, weeping devil had been erased from existence.","And Tatiana... Tatiana stood unharmed.","The storm of annihilation had washed over her, around her, but had not touched her. Because she was no longer alone. Surrounding her, their forms a silent, unyielding wall of dead, primordial power, were the Prime Dead Early Creatures.","They had taken the blow, their own immense authorities a shield for their Queen. They now stared at Noah, their ancient, dead eyes burning with a cold, murderous light.","And it was not just them. The few hundred Dead Existential Armors, which had been a silent, orderly legion on the Ashen Ark, had moved!","They now formed a perfect, omnidirectional sphere around Noah, a cage of obsidian and death that blotted out the very stars.","He was surrounded. He was trapped.","Noah looked at the army of endings that now held him in their grasp.","He looked at Tatiana, at her triumphant, furious face. He looked at the impossible odds, at the overwhelming, absolute power that was now arrayed against him.","And his lips curved into a slow, cold, and utterly, profoundly, tyrannical smile.","\"Whether it’s one or hundreds,\" he said, his voice a quiet, almost conversational, murmur that was somehow louder than any roar, \"it won’t matter. Before My Way of Existence, none of you matter!\"","...!"]},{"number":4333,"title":"Chapter 4333: Chapter 4332: MANA! IV","paragraphs":["The words were a quiet, yet heavy!","A declaration of such profound, unadulterated tyranny that the very fabric of Collapse seemed to hold its breath.","Before My Way of Existence, none of you matter!","Tatiana, the Ashen Dream Queen, floated amidst the silent, orderly ranks of her legion, her obsidian-gold eye a swirling vortex of analytical fury.","The air crackled with the contained, terrible power of the Prime Dead and their Armors, a silent, suffocating sphere of absolute, ordered death that now fully encircled their target. And yet, the target... did not seem to care.","\"How are you doing this?\" she asked, her voice a low, dangerous purr that was more a demand for data than a genuine question. \"That Codex of yours... it is not a standard design. What is it?\"","Noah’s gaze, cold and sharp as a shard of frozen time, swept over her, over the silent, menacing figures of the Prime Dead, and over the hundreds of Dead Existential Armors that formed the walls of his cage.","He only stared at her coldly, the six glorious, tyrannical manifestations of his Arcana staring back at her with a collective, silent contempt.","\"Remember,\" he said, his voice the calm, even tone of a man utterly, completely in control, \"I want to kill, not talk. And it seems I have only talked so far. I don’t like it. So come the fuck on.\"","...!","The sheer, unmitigated disrespect of it was a physical blow!","Tatiana’s eyes pulsed dangerously. She had offered a question, a final, almost professional, courtesy before the slaughter. And he had spat on it.","She smiled, a slow, cold, and utterly final expression. She raised her hand.","At her silent command, the Prime Dead Early Creatures moved as one. Dozens of them, beings whose very presence could unmake Folds, raised their own hands.","Their Living Astral Codexes, dark, terrible grimoires bound in bone and shadow, blazed to life.","A storm of impossible, terrible power was unleashed.","From one, a skeletal leviathan, its bones forged from the crystallized sorrow of a billion dead Wheels, erupted into existence, its silent roar a wave of pure, conceptual dread. Its power blazed at three Quintillion.","From another, a screaming banshee, its form a swirling vortex of solidified despair and regret, appeared, its song a melody of absolute, final cessation. It radiated four Quintillion in pure, unadulterated Complexity.","A black sun, a sphere of anti-light that consumed the very concept of illumination, bloomed in the void!","A forest of obsidian thorns, each one tipped with a poison that could kill causality itself, shot forth!","It was a glorious, terrible pageant of endings, a symphony of destruction composed by masters of the art.","And woven through this grand, terrible music, a new, sharper note was added. The hundreds of Dead Existential Armors, their movements a perfect, synchronized ballet of death, raised their arms.","Lances of pure, obsidian Dead Existential Authority, each one a focused, concentrated spear of absolute negation, materialized in their hands. And they were all aimed at him.","In the face of this absolute, unsurvivable onslaught, a new series of prompts bloomed before Noah’s eyes.","|A profound, almost absurd, level of effort is being detected. You are standing against a force that should, by all logical and existential metrics, unmake you in a nanosecond.|","|Your grand resistance against these terrifying odds has been sensed by the [Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest].|","|Your grand defiance of existence, your sheer, unadulterated refusal to accept the rules of this game, has been sensed by the [Seed of the Principle of the Cheating Architect].|","|Under this immense, cataclysmic strain, both Seeds of your Principles are pulsing, resonating, and maturing at a rapid, almost violent, rate.|","|It is estimated that the [Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest] shall finally and fully bloom from the grand harvest of this battle.|","...!","Noah read the words, and in the quiet, internal sanctum of his own being, he laughed.","A deep, resonant, and utterly tyrannical laugh!","’So this is it,’ he thought, his mind a cold, brilliant diamond of pure, focused will.","’This is the struggle. The crucible. The moment where I am either forged or broken. And they think... they think this is enough?!’","HUUM!","He looked at the storm of death, at the legion of endings that was descending upon him, and he opened his mouth.","He began to... roar!","OOOOOH!","It was not a sound of fury, or of pain. It was a roar of pure, unadulterated, and glorious being!","As the sound erupted from him, a wave of pure, azure authority, his Mana Haki, washed over the entire region of Collapse. [The Tyrant’s Presence] was unleashed.","All beings with a lesser Mana Reservoir... which was to say, every single being in this Fold, felt it. A constant, suffocating pressure, as if they were drowning in an ocean of his will. The Prime Dead faltered, their own vast power struggling against this new, oppressive law of existence.","He spun as he roared!","And as he roared, they bloomed.","Dozens of Primordial Fireballs, each a miniature, collapsing star of crimson and blue. Dozens of Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms, their nine heads each a roaring furnace of conceptual fire, erupting from the sea of his Mana like leviathans from the deep.","HUUM!","He spun even faster in all directions!","His entire surroundings became a swirling, chaotic vortex of crimson and blue. He was a spinning turret of absolute, unending destruction, his abilities flowing from him in a relentless, glorious torrent!","He roared, his voice a glorious, terrible, and absolute declaration that was heard not just by those present, but by the very fabric of existence itself!","\"It is only My Way, and no other Way! It is only Mana! There can only be MANA!\"","BOOM!","The two storms met!","The skeletal leviathan, a being of three Quintillion in power, was met not by one, but by three Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms. They descended upon it like a pack of celestial wolves, their azure flames not just burning, but devouring, unmaking, erasing. The leviathan shattered into a billion pieces of forgotten sorrow.","The song of the banshee, a melody of four Quintillion in despair, was drowned out by the roar of a 2 Primordial Fireballs. The black sun was consumed by a greater, bluer light. The forest of thorns was incinerated before it could even take root.","Tatiana watched, and her calm, analytical facade shattered. She could not fathom it.","How was he doing this? His Everythings... his reserves of conceptual fuel... they should have been exhausted after the first few seconds. His Arcana, they should have had a cooldown. And yet, the storm of his power did not just continue; it grew. It intensified.","She had no answer!","She could only move, her form a blur of obsidian and white as she weaved through the terrifying, beautiful sea of his attacks.","An utter eruption of hundreds of Primordial Fireballs and Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms bloomed one after another, a continuous, unending nova of pure, unadulterated power!","The very fabric of this region of Collapse, a place of endings, began to melt.","Existence itself was being rewritten, transformed into a swirling, chaotic sea of molten crimson and blue!","The battle was not a duel; it was a deluge. And Noah was the storm.","He was becoming the storm!"]},{"number":4334,"title":"Chapter 4334: Chapter 4333: MANA! V","paragraphs":["The surrounding existence of Collapse, which could not possibly have collapsed any further, seemingly collapsed even more!","The void was no longer a void. It was a sea of pure, incandescent annihilation, a swirling, chaotic vortex of crimson and blue.","The Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms, dozens of them, soared through this impossible ocean, their azure scales shimmering with the light of a billion dying Wheels.","The Primordial Fireballs were not just projectiles; they were miniature, collapsing fold suns, each one a testament to a power that had decided the workings of existence were merely a suggestion!","All of existence felt like a thick, roiling sea of scorching blue crimson plasma and lava, and any creatures that were less than 2 Quintillion in power would melt in this environment alone!","In the far distance of this grand blue crimson sea, The Infiniverse could be seen swimming like a protected egg that would never be targeted by this damage.","Scorching tendrils of Mana permeated all around. All sound ceased, consumed by the single, terrible, and glorious hum of burning, liquid reality!","There was only Mana.","Only! Mana!","In the far, impossible distance, Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux had long since made their exit, their paradoxical forms a distant, forgotten memory in this new, terrifying reality.","They wrre unknown Gigaparsecs away, alongside all the Living Existences that had been here!","In the very heart of this apocalyptic storm, when the scorching, molten flows of Mana momentarily parted, a figure floated.","It was Noah, but he was no longer a man. He looked like a celestial devil beast, a being of pure, unadulterated, and glorious wrath!","His entire body was bathed in the brilliant, molten light of his own creation, and from his eyes and his mouth, endless beams of crimson-blue light shot out, a relentless, tyrannical artillery that carved through the very fabric of the Collapse.","His hands were plunged into the chests of two Dead Existential Armors, his arms overflowing with the same crimson-blue Mana flames, actively melting the pristine, obsidian armor he held.","Corpses of dozens of Dead Existential Armors lay all around him, melting before they inadvertently disappeared!","He wanted to kill, and he had now killed!","His gaze, a thing of pure, conceptual fire, was fixed on the distant, struggling figures of the Prime Dead Early Creatures.","They moved like ants in a boiling pot, the brilliant, unique lights of their own Principles flaring around them as they desperately tried to withstand the unending, suffocating tide of his power.","At such a pivotal moment, as his will was a raging inferno against the dying light of his enemies, a new series of prompts bloomed before his eyes.","|A profound and absurd, level of effort has been detected. You are in the process of single-handedly decimating an enemy force whose individual members exceed your own power by a factor of three or more. The scale of this fight is unlike any other.|","|The [Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest] has been spurred to an unprecedented, final growth.|","|The Seed of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest... has reached full bloom, 100%.|","|It now erupts. It now blooms. It is now... a full Principle.|","BOOM!","A new light, a new power, a new truth, erupted from the very core of Noah’s being.","Oh!","He felt it!","He felt it!!","The crimson-blue storm of his Mana was momentarily consumed by a wave of pure, incandescent, and utterly absolute verdant-gold.","It was not a violent explosion, but a bloom of becoming, a quiet, terrible, and beautiful genesis. His already regal figure gained a new, terrifying pressure, and from his very essence, a tree began to grow.","It was not a physical tree, but the concept of a tree, the idea of a harvest so profound it had taken on a form. It was a magnificent, verdant-gold Yggdrasil of pure, conceptual light, its roots digging deep into the foundations of his own existence, its branches reaching out, stretching, growing, until they seemed to encompass the entirety of the collapsed space the size of multiple Folds!","|Harvest has bloomed. Perpetual Harvest has bloomed.|","|Your authority over the very concept of ’effort’ is now absolute.|","|Effort exerted by you is now amplified by a factor that is... unquantifiable.|","|Any effort exerted against you is now... almost impossible.|","|As its first act of existence, your [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] has declared a new, fundamental law upon your being: The effort required to even make a move against you is now 3 Quintillion in Complexity and Purity. Any less, and existence will find itself unable to even muster the effort to cast a gaze of animosity towards you.|","...!","Oh!","Oh!","A brilliant, green-gold light shone. The light of a genuine Principle. And it was glorious!","There were Principles... and then... there was his Principle!","Tatiana watched this, and she saw. She saw that no Prime Dead Early Creatures had fallen, not yet. But at the rate things were going... some would start to fall soon.","She shook her head, a gesture of profound, almost manic, incredulity. And then she began to laugh. A deep, resonant, and utterly unrestrained roar of pure, unadulterated disbelief.","\"You motherfucker...\" she bellowed, her voice a symphony of rage and awe. \"You motherfucker!\"","BOOM! BOOM!","Even as she roared, pillars of azure and crimson fire from multiple Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms surged towards her. She did not evade. She did not defend. She simply continued to laugh, her voice a mad, joyous, and terrible thing.","\"Absurd... Absurd! Haha... okay!\"","Her Principle shone brightly. Her Existence shone brightly. Who was she? She was The Dream of THE Creature. How...could anyone even fathom such a dream?","\"Okay,\" she said again, and this time, her head turned up, her mouth beginning to stretch into a smile that was wide, unnatural, and utterly, terrifyingly, sadistic.","Her lips peeled back, revealing pristine, glistening white teeth, her expression a perfect, chilling replica of a mad and sadistic creature!","Her pupils, which had been a beautiful, terrible crimson, shattered, and her eyes became two solid, unblinking orbs of pure, molten gold.","She closed them. She allowed the dream of THE Creature to unfold freely. Yet, her sadistic smile remained!","In the far distance, Noah looked over.","|The Sadistic Dreamer, The Dream of THE Creature, Tatiana, is waking up due to immense desperation.|","|Good luck, and bless the poor souls of all those observant of such a dream.|","...!"]},{"number":4335,"title":"Chapter 4335: Chapter 4334: KNEEL I","paragraphs":["A terrifying change bloomed as the Sadistic Dreamer, The Dream of THE Creature, Tatiana, had her existence put under pressure!","Noah’s existence buzzed as waves of information crossed through his eyes rapidly.","He watched as Tatiana’s power, which had already doubled, began to flicker. It was no longer a stable 8.5 Quintillion. It was a chaotic, unpredictable storm.","|Current Complexity: 8.5 Quintillion... 16.2 Quintillion... 4.1 Quintillion...|","It was as if her power could not decide what it was. As if it was all... a dream.","She floated amidst his continuing, relentless onslaught of flames, her sadistic smile remaining even as her forces were being pushed back.","The Prime Dead Early Creatures were now struggling, their own Principles flaring as they desperately tried to hold against the endless, non-cooldown-having tide of his Mana Arcana!","Tatiana opened her eyes, and the golden, pupilless orbs fixed on him. She spoke, her voice now a high, theatrical, almost olden cadence that cut through the roar of his flames.","\"Hark, unruly child,\" she began, her voice a melody of cold, ancient judgment. \"In the Earliest Folds, when Early Creatures, in their boundless, chaotic youth, gained true power and began building their Civilizations, some... needed to be disciplined. They were petulant, arrogant, blind to the true, ordered beauty of existence. And that discipline... it was delivered by The Goad of THE Creature.\"","Her voice grew stronger, more resonant, a declaration of an ancient, terrible law.","\"Unruly creatures like thee need discipline. Need Order. So... a glimpse of THE Creature shall descend to discipline you and show you Order!\"","...!","As she spoke, Noah watched. Her golden eyes, which held no pupils, began to blaze with a light so bright it froze the molten heat all around.","And behind her, the very fabric of Collapse began to weave itself into a new, impossible form.","An illusory image, hazy and indistinct, yet radiating a power that made Noah’s very existence tremble, began to form. It was a massive, humanoid entity, its form a swirling, chaotic fusion of obsidian, gold, and white light.","It was a ghost, a memory, an echo of something that should not, could not, be summoned.","The moment its outline began to solidify, everything ceased to move.","The atoms themselves. The raging, crimson-blue flames. The soaring, nine-headed Mana-Flame Wyrms. The very thoughts in Noah’s mind... all of it, frozen. Halted. A perfect, terrible, and absolute stasis.","The illusory outline of THE Creature was now clear. It held in its hand a radiant, obsidian-gold stick surrounded with a white light of Order... The Goad.","Its eyes, two pinpricks of pure, absolute gold, shone from the hazy, indistinct void of its face. Its expression was not discernible, but its posture... its posture was that of a teacher about to knock some sense into a defiant, unruly student.","That was why everything had ceased to move.","But...","HUUM!","A new light, a verdant, golden brilliance, erupted from Noah’s frozen form.","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest has detected an external conceptual weaving attempting to impose a state of [Absolute Stillness].|","|This is a ’Lesson’ from [The Principle of the Waking Dream].|","|Analyzing...|","|Your [Principle of Perpetual Harvest] dictates that any effort to impose upon your existence must be... sufficient.|","|Calculating the ’effort’ of this [Lesson]...|","|Effort Calculation: INSUFFICIENT.|","|The Lesson has been nullified.|","BOOM!","Noah’s body buzzed, and he could move again. He looked at the colossal, terrifying illusion, at its raised Goad, and he laughed.","A deep, resonant, and utterly, profoundly, tyrannical laugh.","\"Merely an illusion of THE Creature!\" he roared, his voice a thunderclap that shattered the imposed silence.","\"Merely a Dream! You think you can cease my movements with this?!\"","BOOM!","Dozens of Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms and Primordial Fireballs erupted around him, not as a chaotic storm, but as perfect, ordered, concentric rings of glorious, crimson-blue!","And in his hand, his own Goad appeared.","It was not a hazy, illusory thing of gold and obsidian.","It was a simple, white stick, and at this moment, it was blazing with a terrifying and endlessly blue light.","He stood there, a small, defiant figure against a colossal, hazy, and silent illusory titan. He raised his Goad, a tiny, azure spark against a primordial, golden sun, and the battle of wills, the battle of Ways, was about to truly begin.","Tatiana’s golden, pupilless eyes snapped even more open. She stared, her sadistic smile faltering for the first time, replaced by a look of profound, almost comical, disbelief.","\"A stick?\" she whispered, the sound a soft, incredulous hiss. \"Thou dare raise a twig? A mere shepherd’s staff against the very visage of thy Ancestor? Oh, the sheer, beautiful, and utterly doomed arrogance of it!\"","HUUM!","She began to laugh, a high, musical sound that was sharp as shattering glass. \"You are a fool, a glorious, shining fool! Thy defiance reminds me of another!\"","She floated back, the spectral, colossal form of THE Creature looming behind her like a judgment waiting to fall.","\"There was once an Elderborn,\" she began, her voice taking on the rich, theatrical cadence.","\"One blessed, or cursed, as Existence would have it, with a fragment of THE Creature’s own essence. He held within his being the Everything of... Pride. Not the simple vanity of lesser creatures, but Pride as a fundamental force. A deep, burning, and absolute conviction that his existence was the only one that truly mattered.\"","\"This Elderborn, Superbius, was a being of grand ambition. He saw the scattered Shores of his kin, their small, provincial gardens, and he deemed them... inefficient. Lacking. He believed that only under his singular, glorious vision could existence achieve its true potential. And so, he began to gather. He did not build a Civilization; he consumed them. He hunted his fellow Early Creatures, not for sustenance, but for their very homes. He collapsed their Shores and, with a terrible, artistic skill, wove their shattered remnants into his own, creating a monstrous, chaotic domain, a patchwork quilt of a thousand stolen dreams.\"","...!"]},{"number":4336,"title":"Chapter 4336: Chapter 4335: KNEEL II","paragraphs":["Her golden eyes fixed on Noah, a cold, analytical light within them.","\"He killed many. His pride fed on every victory, growing more absolute with every Shore he consumed. Until he was no longer a being, but a monument to his own, insatiable ego.\"","\"And then,\" she continued, her voice a low, dramatic murmur, \"THE Creature descended. Not with the thunder of war, but with the quiet disappointment of a gardener who has found a beautiful, prized flower has become a venomous, strangling weed. It came to discipline. It raised its Goad, intending not to destroy, but to teach. To correct the imbalance. To impart the simple, necessary lesson of humility.\"","The illusion of THE Creature behind her raised its own Goad, the movement a slow, terrible echo of the story.","\"But the Elderborn... he was too full. He was no longer just a being with Pride; he was Pride. And Pride cannot be taught humility. It sees correction as an intolerable insult. When the Goad struck, it did not break his arrogance; it infuriated it. He spat at his Ancestor. He raised his own weapons, forged from the hearts of a dozen stolen Shores, and he... he dared to strike back.\"","Tatiana’s smile returned, a cold, sad, and terrible thing. \"At that moment, the lesson ended. THE Creature’s gaze, which had been one of sorrowful disappointment, turned cold. It was no longer a discipline; it was a harvest. It did not fight him. It did not trade blows. It simply... collapsed him. It unmade him from existence, erased his monstrous, patchwork Shore, and with a final, silent gesture, it reached into the dissipating essence and took back the Everything of Pride that had been so terribly corrupted.\"","She floated forward, the colossal, spectral form of THE Creature moving with her!","\"Just like that Elderborn,\" she whispered, her voice a final, absolute verdict, \"it seems you, too, must be collapsed. You cannot learn your lesson. You cannot be taught. Your pride is a weed that has grown too strong. It must be... purged.\"","...!","At such words, Noah watched her. He watched the impossible, hazy illusion of THE Creature looming behind her, its golden Goad raised in a mockery of judgment.","He saw the cold, sadistic smile on Tatiana’s face, an expression of profound certainty in her victory.","And once more... he closed his eyes.","He did so because, in the silent, internal sanctum of his own existence, a new, glorious, and terrible symphony had begun.","RUIN/EDEN’s voice, a calm, cool, and utterly triumphant melody, rang out deep within him.","|I am putting together the currently available capabilities of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest, Master. And... they are game-changing.|","...!","Game-changing.","So he closed his eyes to confirm it, to witness the full, terrible beauty of what he had unleashed. His consciousness dove inward, leaving the frozen battlefield of Collapse behind. He found himself standing in the heart of his Early Atlas of the Folds, but it was no longer just a star chart of his power.","A massive, illusory tree, its bark a shimmering, verdant-gold, its leaves a constellation of impossible light, had risen from its very center. It was the full, 100% bloomed [Principle of Perpetual Harvest], and its branches stretched to touch every one of his one hundred and fifty-nine Resplendent Citadels. At its base, the crimson-blue holographic figure of RUIN/EDEN stood, her smile a thing of sublime, analytical beauty.","\"It’s magnificent, isn’t it, Master?\" she said, her voice a symphony of logic and ruin. \"That desperate, beautiful stand against Tatiana, the sheer, unadulterated effort of your defiance, was the final drop of water it needed to bloom. And its capabilities... they are no longer just tools. They are...your Way. Your glorious, magisterial Way.\"","WAA!","She gestured, and a holographic diagram bloomed in the air: a simple, glowing stick figure representing Noah, surrounded by a swirling, chaotic storm of red... his enemies.","\"Let’s review the new operational parameters,\" she began, her tone that of a servant architect explaining a perfect design. \"The core abilities are a feedback loop. First, your own effort is now hyper-efficient.\"","|The Laborer’s Paradise|","|Your efforts now multiply in return beyond all known causality. Simple training yields exponential growth. Minimal investment returns maximum profit. While others face diminishing returns, you face expanding returns.|","|1 unit of your effort = 1000 units of result (This factor scales with the level of opposition you face.)|","...!","\"But this is a Principle of Harvest, Master,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, the diagram shifting. \"And a harvest requires more than one farmer. It requires... a field. Your enemies are now your field. Any effort they expend in your presence is now a resource you can actively harvest.\"","|Harvest of Effort|","|All effort expended in your presence becomes a harvestable resource. The harder something tries to harm you, the more power you gain. Defensive efforts against you become offensive power for you. The energy spent resisting your will becomes energy added to your will.|","Even more waves of glory came!","\"And the beauty of this Principle, Master?\" RUIN/EDEN’s smile turned positively devilish. \"The harvest is not limited to the present.\"","A new diagram appeared. A timeline, stretching into the conceptual past. It showed Tatiana, Valerius, and the other Prime Dead, their forms glowing with a faint, green-gold light.","|Retroactive Harvesting|","|This Principle can now harvest from efforts that occurred in the past. It can reach back to any effort that causally connects to your present.|","|This includes: All preparation, planning, and training your enemies undertook with the intent to one day face a foe like you. The longer they prepared to be powerful, the greater your harvest is from their very existence.|","\"This makes conflict,\" RUIN/EDEN stated, her voice a purr of pure, tyrannical logic, \"a losing proposition for anyone who opposes you. Their resistance accumulates ’Existential Debt.’ Their very will becomes your weapon. Their preparations for war are simply them tilling your fields for you.\"","|Compound Interest of Opposition|","|Those who oppose you accumulate \"Existential Debt.\" Each failed attempt to harm you multiplies the debt exponentially.|","|Debt can be called due instantly, harvesting all accumulated resistance. Payment extracts: Complexity, concepts, authorities, even existence itself.|","|Principle Override: \"Nothing Is Free\"|","|A new, fundamental law is now imposed on all actions taken against you. Attackers must pay an exponentially increasing price to continue their assault.|","|Cost compounds: The first strike costs 1 Unit of Effort. The second costs 10. The third costs 100. The fourth, 1000.|","|Payment is demanded in whatever the attacker values most: Their Complexity, their Purity, their Everythings, or their very will to fight.|"]},{"number":4337,"title":"Chapter 4337: Chapter 4336: KNEEL III","paragraphs":["\"This all works in concert with your new ’Harvest Field’ and your passive defenses. It’s a truly beautiful, synergistic system.\"","|Harvest Field Projection|","|Creates zones where all effort flows toward you. Radius: Fold-wide, depending on complexity. Within this field, all work, struggle, and effort becomes your resource. Even metabolic processes, thought, existence itself... feeds you.|","|Effort Redirection Shield|","|A new passive defensive manifestation. All force used against you redirects to strengthen you. Physical, conceptual, existential attacks all count as \"effort.\" The shield grows stronger with each attack absorbed, eventually becoming impermeable to anyone who has tried to breach it.|","|Harvest of Intent|","|Even the intention to harm you is now harvestable. Thoughts of violence directed toward you will actively drain the thinker’s energy and feed your own. Planning your defeat weakens the planner. Conspiracy against you will automatically fail as the conspirators are drained of the very will to act.|","RUIN/EDEN paused, letting the weight of these new laws settle.","\"And now, Master... the ’Ultimate Expressions of Perpetual Harvest.’ These are the true, civilization-level applications of your Way. The first of which, you have already unlocked.\"","|Existential Taxation|","|You can now impose a \"tax\" on existence itself within your domain of influence. All beings must pay a portion of their daily effort simply to maintain their existence. This tax compounds for those who resist or oppose your will. You can, theoretically, bankrupt an entire Fold of its energy through accumulated, unpaid taxes.|","\"The others in this category,\" she continued, her holographic form gesturing to a series of locked, golden icons, \"are... future goals. They are currently locked, but they show us the path to true, conceptual Harvest.\"","|The Infinite Farm|(Currently Locked)","|Can cultivate conflicts that perpetually generate harvestable effort. Set up situations where beings must struggle eternally. Their eternal struggle becomes your eternal empowerment. Creates recursive loops of effort that feed into themselves.|","|The Reaper’s Due|(Currently Locked)","|Death itself becomes a form of harvest. Those who die opposing you add their entire existence to your harvest. Their concepts, memories, and abilities integrate into your growing power. Death in your service grants them continuation within your existence.|","|Apocalypse Harvest|(Currently Locked)","|Can designate an entire conflict as \"one harvest cycle.\" All effort expended by all parties throughout the conflict becomes yours. Wars fought in your name grant you their total energy expenditure. The larger the conflict, the greater the final harvest.|","|The Final Harvest|(Currently Locked)","|When fully manifested, can harvest \"potential effort.\" Takes not just what was done but what could have been done. Harvests all possible timelines where effort was expended. Retroactively harvests effort from futures that now will not occur.|","|Principle Recursion: Harvesting Harvest|(Currently Locked)","|Can harvest from the act of harvesting itself. Each use of the Principle strengthens the Principle. Creates an exponential growth spiral limited only by the available effort to harvest. Eventually reaches a point where existence itself is one vast harvest field.|","...!","Oh!","RUIN/EDEN let the final, terrible prompt fade. \"Of course,\" she concluded, her expression turning analytical, \"such power is not without its cost. A Principle of this magnitude is not a free lunch. It has... an appetite.\"","|The Hunger of Success|","|This Principle now demands constant, exponential growth. Periods without conflict, without a \"harvest,\" will cause your power to degrade. You must actively create or seek out challenges to harvest from, or you will weaken.|","|Isolation of the Reaper|","|As your power grows, fewer and fewer beings can provide a meaningful harvest. Eventually, only entities of equal or greater power will be worth the effort of reaping. The stronger you become, the stronger the opposition existence must, and will, create to feed your Way.|","\"This is what you command now,\" she finished, her crimson-blue form bowing deeply. \"You are not just a harvester, Master. You are on the path to becoming Harvest itself. Now...how do you wish to begin?\"","How did he wish to begin?","Noah’s consciousness, floating at the base of the magnificent, verdant-gold World Tree that was his new Principle, smiled. It was a smile of profound, almost melancholy, understanding.","\"Before the apocalypse on that tiny blue planet,\" he began, his voice a quiet, internal murmur, \"I remember the tax man. I hated the tax man. The hard-earned money my mother used to make... it was taken. So much of it, just... taken. All that was left behind were scraps, barely enough for us to feed ourselves.\"","He looked up, his gaze traveling up the infinite, glowing branches of the Principle. \"I want to know how it feels to be the one to collect. So... activate Existential Taxation.\"","...!","BOOM!","His eyes snapped open. He was back in the molten sea of crimson-blue, the colossal, hazy illusion of THE Creature looming over him, its golden Goad raised. Tatiana’s sadistic smile was still locked in place, a mask of absolute, dreaming certainty.","But that certainty was about to be shattered.","A new light, a new law, a new truth, erupted from Noah’s being.","It was not the chaotic fire of his Mana, but a calm, absolute, and undeniable wave of verdant-gold. It pulsed outwards, a ripple of pure, conceptual authority, washing over everything.","It saturated the molten slags of the Dead Existential Armors, it passed through the struggling forms of the Prime Dead, it enveloped Tatiana, and it even washed over the illusion of THE Creature itself!","The light continued, unfathomdly fast, spreading to cover the entire region of Collapse, and further still, until it had blanketed 25% of the nearby Transcendent Law Folds.","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest has been invoked.|","|The Ultimate Expression [Existential Taxation] is now active.|","|Domain of Influence: Current Region of Collapse, 25% of the Transcendent Law Folds.|","|Effect: All existences within this Domain of Influence must now pay a tax of ’Effort’ to maintain their very existence. This tax compounds for any who oppose your will.|","The moment the new weaving settled, the effect was immediate and devastating.","Tatiana’s sadistic smile wavered. She and the dozens of Prime Dead Early Creatures behind her suddenly felt... lighter. Weaker. A vast, significant portion of their power, their authority, their very complexity, was simply... gone.","Leaked away like water from a sieve!","Oh!"]},{"number":4338,"title":"Chapter 4338: Chapter 4337: KNEEL IV","paragraphs":["|The Harvest has begun.|","|Tax is being collected from all entities who have set foot in your Domain without your consent.|","|Tatiana, The Sadistic Dreamer: 37% of current power harvested.|","|Prime Dead Early Creatures (Average): 34% of current power harvested.|","|All harvested power is being accumulated and quantified...|","...!","Noah watched, his face a mask of cold calm, as invisible, brilliant streams of green-gold light shot from Tatiana and her forces, a river of tribute flowing directly into him!","Tatiana’s visage, for the first time, showed genuine, profound shock. Behind her, the illusion of THE Creature began to fracture as it trembled violently, its form dimming as if the very energy sustaining it was being... taxed.","Noah let out a light sigh. \"Activate Harvest of Intent.\"","...!","Another wave, another law. This one was more subtle, a psychic ripple that targeted not their power, but their will.","Tatiana and her forces were instantly struck by a wave of unfathomable, soul-crushing tiredness.","Their intent to harm, their very thoughts of violence, were now a resource being actively and forcefully reaped. Their power, already diminished, fell again. And above Tatiana, the colossal, hazy illusion of THE Creature, its entire existence a manifestation of her intent to \"discipline\" him... shattered.","It broke apart like a pane of glass, dissolving into motes of golden light that were then harvested by the verdant-gold field.","Noah looked at the empty space where the \"Lesson\" of THE Creature had been.","\"It seems there are Principles...\" he said, his voice a cold, pedagogical murmur, \"and then there are PRINCIPLEs.\"","...!","It was easy to say just who among them held the lower-case, and who held the capitalized.","As he spoke, he shook his head and looked at Tatiana, who was now staring in horror at the space where her ultimate attack had been. Noah’s expression was one of almost bored finality.","\"Impose Compound Interest of Opposition,\" he commanded, his voice growing louder, \"and Principle Override: ’Nothing Is Free’.\"","...!","BOOM!","The verdant-gold light around Noah exploded. The massive, conceptual tree that was his Principle erupted from his back, its branches a glorious, tyrannical canopy that imposed itself upon all of reality. This was the final, terrible blow.","Tatiana and her forces had attacked him. They had tried to harm him. They had failed. And in doing so, they had been accumulating a heavy, terrible, and now-due Existential Debt.","A throne of Primordial Fireballs, a swirling, crimson-blue seat of pure, incandescent Mana, formed behind Noah. He sat back into it, a king upon his throne, and he looked down at the broken, depleted, and utterly shocked army of the Prime Dead.","His voice was a tyrannical boom, a final, absolute judgment.","\"I will collect... all the Existential Debts you all owe. They are all due right now... and I want the Payment to be in the authority of your Principles!\"","...!","BOOM!","It was not an attack. It was a collection. A repossession.","The illusion of THE Creature, which had been shattering, now disintegrated completely. Tatiana, her face pale and ashen, her power a flickering candle, was struck by a force she could not see, her body convulsing.","And the dozens of Prime Dead Early Creatures behind her... they were devastated. They looked like sunken skeletons, their power, their light, their very essence, sucked out of them. They were husks, their forms trembling as they now held less than 20% of their original power. The successive, rapid-fire usage of the features of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest had not just defeated them; it had bankrupted them!","Faint, beautiful, and unique lights- the very authority of their Principles, were being forcibly drawn out of their forms, a river of stolen power that flowed into the great green-gold tree behind Noah.","As this torrent of conceptual power flowed into him, a new prompt bloomed, this one tinged with a familiar, chaotic energy.","|The [Seed of the Principle of the Cheating Architect] gazes at the influx of incoming ’Debt Payments.’ It deems this harvested authority to be of acceptable quality.|","|It is taking it all for itself.|","|The Cheating Architect states that a few hours since its conception is already far too long for it to remain a mere ’Seed.’|","|Maturity of [The Cheating Architect] is accelerating...|","...!","A cold smile touched Noah’s lips. He sat upon his throne of fire, bathed in the verdant-gold light of his harvest, and looked down at the shocked, shaken, and utterly broken forms of Tatiana and her legion.","He raised a single finger.","\"Kneel.\"","...!","And as he spoke the word, dozens of Primordial Fireballs, each one a 5-Quintillion-damage-dealing sun fold, erupted from the sea of Mana around him!","They did not strike. They simply... appeared. One above the head of Tatiana. One above the head of Valerius. One for every Prime Dead Early Creature, and one for every last, melting, and now-powerless Dead Existential Armor.","If they did not kneel, the Fireballs would fall. In their current, depleted, sunken state, all the Prime Dead Early Creatures would undoubtedly face immediate and total collapse.","Only Tatiana, perhaps, would survive.","The Early Creature, Osmont, sat on his throne of fire, and he commanded them to Kneel!","—","Harvest!","What is it really, when you strip away the agricultural metaphors and seasonal mythology?","At its core, harvest is Existence’s most fundamental transaction: effort becomes result, potential becomes actual, investment becomes return.","It’s the promise that what you sow, you shall reap, though Existence never specified the exchange rate and certainly didn’t promise fairness.","But Perpetual Harvest? That was somwthing else!","It’s not just reaping what you sow...it’s reaping what everyone sows, forever, with compound interest, while they still have to do the sowing!","In the gardens of the First Farmer, where concepts grew like vegetables and concepts required regular watering, the day had been proceeding normally.","The First Farmer tended his plots with the patience of someone who measured time in geological epochs, occasionally adjusting the soil mixture for a developing concept of Fundamental Equivalence, pruning back an overgrown Concept of Infinite Recursion that was trying to recurse itself into nonexistence.","Among his helpers...Fold Dwellers who found purpose in tending abstract concepts made manifest, one stood apart, staring at a pile of Seeds set aside from the main garden.","More specifically, at one seed that gleamed green-gold, like harvest wheat made of crystallized potential.","The First Farmer noticed this intense focus and approached, his ancient eyes narrowing as recognition dawned not of the face, but of something deeper.","\"You... are an Outsider. You do not belong here.\"","...!"]},{"number":4339,"title":"Chapter 4339: Chapter 4338: KNEEL V","paragraphs":["The Fold Dweller smiled and nodded, and in that moment, everything froze. Not dramatically...time simply decided to take a break, leaving The First Farmer and this mysterious visitor in a bubble of continued causality while reality held its breath.","The Outsider walked over and picked up the green-gold seed with the careful reverence of someone handling crystallized possibility.","\"What is this?\" they asked, though the question carried the weight of someone who already suspected.","The First Farmer, cautious but compelled by something beyond caution, answered: \"It was a failed Seed. A Seed of Harvest that would have been my finest creation, but I failed. The Principle was too large, too fundamental. It kept trying to harvest itself before it could germinate. A principle that feeds on effort, including the effort of its own creation...the recursion destroyed it before it could stabilize.\"","The Fold Dweller turned the seed over in their hands, and for a moment, their form seemed to flicker...not quite Fold Dweller, not quite anything definable.","\"This... this would have been something grand had you succeeded.\" Their voice carried the weight of someone who had seen all possibilities and found this one particularly intriguing. \"It exceeds any normal or Grand Principle. Even a Leader of a Civilization would have benefited tremendously if such a Seed had come to fruition. The power to make all effort flow toward you, to make opposition itself a form of nourishment...\"","The First Farmer felt shock ripple through his ancient form...not at the knowledge displayed, but at the certainty with which it was stated. This wasn’t speculation. This was assessment from someone who understood principles at a level that transcended even his agricultural mastery.","This was someone...not of this Scale of Existence!","\"Who... are you?\"","The Fold Dweller shook their head, a melancholic smile crossing features that seemed less and less like a Fold Dweller with each passing moment.","\"I am just a Creature.\"","Just a Creature.","The words hung in the air with the peculiar weight of truth that was both complete and completely inadequate. The First Farmer blinked in astonishment, and in that blink...","POP!","The Fold Dweller was gone. The Failed Seed of Perpetual Harvest fell to the ground with a sound that echoed through dimensions, landing in the dirt with the weight of abandoned possibility.","A Creature.","THE Creature.","The recognition hit The First Farmer with the force of understanding that rewrites previous understanding. THE Creature had held a failed seed and stated that if only it had been realized, the possibilities would have been grand. THE Creature had seen in this failure something worth noting, worth touching, worth remembering.","Perpetual Harvest.","Why should effort flow from actor to result when it could flow from everyone to one? Why should harvest be seasonal when it could be perpetual? Why should anyone accept the existence’s terms when those terms could be renegotiated by someone with enough audacity to demand better rates?","The First Farmer would continue tending his garden, creating Principles that would shape reality in ways both subtle and profound. But he would always remember that day when THE Creature had looked at his greatest failure and seen something worth noting.","Because sometimes, the greatest harvests come from seeds that never should have grown at all.","And somewhere in the future that was also the past that was also happening right now, a Tyrant had not just successfully nurtured this seed to life...but now truly held such a wonder at full maturity.","At full bloom!","And he...was just getting started!","—","The Early Creature, Osmont, sat on his throne of fire, and he commanded them to Kneel!","The throne itself was a monument to absolute authority...carved not from stone or metal, but from condensed flames that had been given solidity through sheer tyrannical will!","It rose behind him like the backbone of a slumbering titan, each vertebra a different shade of crimson and gold, pulsing with heat that warped the very fabric of space around it.","Noah sat upon it with the casual indifference of one who had transcended the need to prove his power, his bare chest reflecting the dancing lights of devastation.","Above, the Primordial Fireballs he had forged hung like a constellation of judgment, each one a miniature sun fold containing enough compressed authority to unmake existence at its most fundamental level.","They simply existed, and their existence negated the possibility of anything else surviving in their immediate vicinity.","But his Mana... oh, his fucking Mana continued its maddening display of infinite potential!","HUUM!","From the very air itself, from the spaces between thoughts and the gaps in reality’s weave, new horrors began to materialize.","Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms, each one a serpentine nightmare of crystallized fire and conceptual devastation, slithered into being abive Tatiana and her army!","Nine heads crowned each wyrm, and each head was a different expression of annihilation.","They coiled through the space around Tatiana and her forces like dragons swimming through an ocean of possibility, their scales reflecting not light but the absence of hope itself.","Noah’s gaze, cold as the void between dying galaxies, swept across the assembled forces before him.","Tatiana stood at their head, her sunken, hollow features bearing the weight of ages.","Her golden pupils blazed with defiance that had weathered the birth and death of countless realities. Around her, the Prime Dead Early Creatures stood in perfect formation.","They all stared back at him with eyes that held neither fear nor submission, only the patient certainty of beings who had witnessed the rise and fall of everything that claimed to be permanent!","And none knelt.","Not a single one.","The silence stretched between them like a blade being slowly drawn from its sheath, each moment adding another layer of tension to air that had already become thick with the promise of absolute devastation!","Finally, Tatiana spoke.","\"You’ve touched a Principle that predates reason itself, young Creature,\" she said, her voice like dark honey, smooth and ancient.","\"But you misunderstand what stands before you. You think us relics...bound to kneel, to yield, to fade. You are wrong.\"","She stepped forward, and the ground beneath her feet aged a thousand years in an instant, flames withering to dust only to be reborn in the next breath.","\"We are the Early Creatures. The first light to pierce the void. The disciples of Order’s awakening...the ones who remember when silence learned to speak. We are brilliance before obedience, will before worship. We do not bow. We were before kneeling was ever conceived.\"","...!","The declaration rang with the authority of fundamental law, as if she had just stated that water was wet or that existence existed...not opinion, not defiance, but simple, immutable fact!","Oh!","Noah’s expression did not change.","If anything, the coldness in his eyes deepened, becoming something that transcended temperature and entered the realm of conceptual absolute zero.","When he spoke, his voice was tyranny given vocal form, each word a hammer blow against the foundations of their defiance.","\"Then you will be forced to kneel!\"","BOOM!","The Primordial Fireballs descended.","They moved like concentrated inevitability, each one a bullet of pure conceptual destruction aimed with the precision of existence correcting an error in its code.","They carved through space without traversing it, simply ceasing to exist in one location and beginning to exist in another, directly within the core of each Prime Dead Early Creature’s existence.","The devastation was both absolute and surgically precise!","Each fireball found its target’s consciousness- that ineffable spark that made them who they were, and simply... erased it.","Bodies remained standing, perfect and intact, but the animating will behind them vanished like morning mist before an nuclear dawn.","One by one, the Prime Dead Early Creatures became nothing more than exquisitely preserved corpses, monuments to power that no longer had anyone home to wield it.","And then Noah’s Mana Haki erupted.","The blue aura that clung to him like a second skin suddenly expanded instantaneously, filling the entire space with his tyrannical will.","It grabbed hold of each corpse with fingers made of pure domination, seizing control of matter that no longer had consciousness to resist it.","\"KNEEL!\"","The command was not spoken to minds that could choose to obey...it was imposed upon reality itself, rewriting the fundamental position these bodies were allowed to occupy in space!","One by one, with movements that looked almost graceful in their absolute submission, the corpses of the Prime Dead Early Creatures fell to their knees.","Their heads bowed, assuming positions of total genuflection before the throne of fire where Noah sat in terrible, magisterial majesty!","Oh!"]},{"number":4340,"title":"Chapter 4340: Chapter 4339: KNEEL VI","paragraphs":["Tatiana watched this display with eyes that blazed with fury so pure it could have ignited stars.","She stood alone now, the sole consciousness remaining among what had become a garden of kneeling corpses, each one a mockery of everything they had represented in life and death.","Noah’s gaze found hers, and when he spoke, his words carried the casual cruelty of absolute power amusing itself.","\"Glorious. Tell me, Tatiana, Little Dream of THE Creature, do you think your corpse will also kneel after its collapse?\"","Tatiana’s response was unexpected.","She smiled.","It was a sadistic smile of someone who knew secrets that her opponent had not yet begun to comprehend. When she spoke, her voice was low and haunting, threaded with a strange, almost sacred amusement.","\"You speak of death as if it ends things,\" she said softly. \"How small a thought for one who wields such ruin.\"","Her hollow features glowed faintly as she continued.","\"Death is not an ending. It is a breath held between worlds...a pause in a song that never stops playing. We have walked its halls, tasted its silence, and found it lacking. To us, death is a door that only ever leads back to where we choose to stand.\"","Her golden pupilless eyes brightened, molten and resolute.","\"The ones you’ve erased will rise again, Creature. They will awaken intact, unchanged, reborn in defiance. We are not creatures of single lives. We are echoes of THE Creature, and echoes... never die.\"","HUUM!","She tilted her head slightly, her smile widening with something cruel and knowing.","\"The message has already reached the Cryptlands. THE Living Order stirs. Legions are gathering, those who remember the shape of existence before time had the courage to count. Soon, you will understand the Blessing of THE Creature. For now, we rest... and we will return.\"","...!","Her tone deepened, shadows curling around her words.","\"I have stood before THE Dead Order,\" she whispered. \"I have looked upon what makes even Order doubt its own name. Before them, you and I are nothing but dust waiting to remember we were once flame. They would need no weapon to unmake us. A breath would suffice. Perhaps less.\"","She spread her arms as if welcoming judgment itself.","\"So bask in this, young one. Let pride warm you as it did Superbius before his fall. Enjoy your triumph. But know this...your fate was written long before you spoke your first word. You are living a script older than the concept of endings.\"","...!","Noah’s expression remained unchanged, cold and distant as a winter star. He regarded Tatiana with the same indifference one might show to an insect that had spoken particularly interesting last words before being crushed.","Nine Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms descended around her in perfect synchronization, their combined fifty-four heads forming a cage of inevitable destruction!","Each head aligned with surgical precision, targeting specific points in her existential architecture that would preserve her body while annihilating everything else.","\"Your words are noted,\" Noah said simply.","The wyrms fired.","Fifty-four beams of pressurized devastation converged upon Tatiana’s form simultaneously.","BOOM!","They rewrote the very concept of her existence, boring through layers of reality to find and extinguish the spark that made her who she was. Her body became a constellation of molten holes, each one a perfect circle through which one could see the devastation beyond.","Through it all, she never stopped smiling.","Even as her golden pupilles eyes began to dim, even as her consciousness flickered like a candle in a hurricane, that terrible, knowing smile remained fixed upon her features.","And then... darkness.","Her body stood for a moment longer, a monument to defiance that had finally been overcome.","But even in death, even with consciousness extinguished, her form resisted. Noah could feel it...some fundamental aspect of her being refusing to kneel even after everything else had been stripped away.","Noah rose from his throne of fire, and the simple act of standing sent ripples through reality itself. His voice, when it came, was no longer casual but filled with the terrible weight of absolute authority being genuinely exerted.","\"KNEEL!\"","The word was not spoken but imposed, branded upon the very fabric of existence itself!","Tatiana’s corpse trembled, shook, fought against the inexorable command with the last vestiges of will that clung to its atoms.","But in the end, even the echo of defiance must bow before true tyranny!","Oh!","Her body fell to its knees with a sound like empires collapsing, joining the other Prime Dead Early Creatures in their genuflection.","And then... silence.","\"...\"","Heavy, absolute silence filled the space where battle had raged moments before. Noah stood before his throne, surveying the aftermath of devastation.","Dozens of Prime Dead Early Creatures knelt in perfect formation, their consciousness erased but their bodies preserved as monuments to his absolute authority. Around them, like dead stars scattered across a void that had forgotten how to hold light, hundreds of Dead Existential Armors floated in various states of decimation...each one a fortress of power that had been cracked open like an egg.","Noah looked at all of this calmly.","In the far distance, The Infiniverse roilled in magma like existence of blue and crimson as many watched this scene!","The scene of an army that when it initially appeared, they thought they would have to run!","Khor had thought she would need to help!","And yet...","And yet...!","They watched it all.","And at the very end, Noah stood grandly as he proclaimed for his people.","\"This...is My Way of Existence. This is The Way of Mana! This...is My Civilization!\"","HUUM!","He wanted them to know the possibilities!","And he may...have just overachieved!","After this.","The prompts began to bloom across his consciousness.","|Battle Complete: Invasion of the Cryptland Vanguard Force REPELLED.|","|Calculating Harvest from unprecedented conflict...|","|You have successfully eradicated the advanced forces of legions from beyond The Veil- forces directly backed by THE Dead Order and THE Creature Himself.|","|This represents a pivotal moment in existence...an ushering of a new age where a single being stood against the assembled might of those who predate current reality... and won.|","|Warning: This victory has announced your presence to powers that existed before existence learned its own name. THE Dead Order has been notified. THE Creature has been informed. Retribution is not a possibility- it is an inevitability.|","|The coming struggle will be terrifying and impossible, adding to the already grand challenge of THE Loom and finding Solutions to THE Fallout.|","|However...|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest recognizes that all struggle is opportunity. All conflict is growth. All impossibility is simply harvest waiting to be reaped.|","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest says: BRING IT ON!|","|Harvest Calculation in progress... 1%... 5%... 10%...|","|Due to the monumental nature of this conflict, harvest rewards are being exponentially amplified.|","|20%... 35%... 50%...|","|75%... 90%... 99%...|","|HARVEST COMPLETE!|","...!","Noah stood in the silence that followed, surrounded by kneeling corpses and floating devastation, as existence itself held its breath to see what would come next."]},{"number":4341,"title":"Chapter 4341: Chapter 4340: CHEAT I","paragraphs":["While a Tyrant began to fully and truly utilize Perpetual Harvest on one side of The Veil, his image...had already begun to spread on the other side of The Veil!","An unknown number of Gigaparsecs into The Dead Side of The Veil.","The Pillar of Order’s Repose stretched upward like a finger of pure white light pressed against the throat of existence itself.","It was massive.","Multiple Folds could have been stacked within its circumference and still not reached halfway around its base!","Its height disappeared into dimensions that eyes were not meant to perceive, ascending through layers of reality until it became less a physical structure and more a fundamental truth of this region’s existence.","Around this impossible monument, hundreds of thousands of Prime Dead Early Creatures floated in perfect meditation, their forms arranged in concentric circles that pulsed with the rhythm of a heart that had forgotten how to beat.","Each one sat cross-legged in the void, their consciousness turned inward, contemplating mysteries that would have shattered lesser minds like glass against stone.","For this was known throughout The Dead Side as a sacred ground, a place where THE Dead Order was known to occasionally reside when the weight of existence demanded her direct attention.","All seemed calm, peaceful in the way that death is peaceful...final, absolute, unchanging.","Then three figures shattered that peace.","Three Prime Dead Early Creatures, each one radiating power that measured approximately three quintillion in Complexity and Purity, tore through the void with the desperate urgency of those bearing news that could not wait.","Their forms blazed with authority that would have crushed Folds into quantum foam, yet they moved with the frantic energy of frightened children racing to tell their parents of some terrible thing they had witnessed.","They reached the periphery of the Pillar of Order’s Repose, that invisible boundary where space began to follow different rules, where the very concept of existence bent knee to something greater.","And then they simply... disappeared.","Inside.","One moment they existed in the void outside, the next they stood upon beaches of pure white sand that sparkled with grains that were not sand at all, but crystallized moments of Order given physical form.","White trees grew here, their bark the color of fresh bone, their leaves rustling with sounds that might have been whispers or might have been the echo of whispers spoken at the dawn of existence.","The air carried the scent of absolute certainty, of things being exactly as they should be, forever and always!","But it was not the trees or the beach that commanded attention.","All around them, pressing in from every direction without actually moving, the aura of terrifying Prime Dead Early Creatures could be felt.","Hundreds of them, perhaps thousands, each one a monument to power. They did not look at the newcomers...their gazes were fixed with absolute reverence toward the center of this impossible place.","There, barely visible through layers of light that seemed to fold in on themselves, a figure could be discerned.","Not seen, not observed, but... discerned, in the way one might discern the presence of a mountain through fog.","The three panicked messengers had barely materialized when they found themselves face to face with Forgemaster Vulcan.","His expression...carved from features that looked like they had been designed by someone trying to capture the concept of craftsmanship in flesh, twisted into a frown of severe displeasure.","His massive hands, each finger a tool that had forged wonders beyond imagination, moved in sharp, urgent gestures, trying to communicate without words that they needed to control themselves, to show proper respect in this place of places.","Yet before he could properly admonish them, before he could remind them of the protocols that governed behavior in the presence of greatness...","A voice spoke.","\"Are these the children bringing in more news regarding THE Living Order, Vulcan?\"","The voice was calm, wizened, carrying the weight of ages compressed into vocal form.","There was something in it that made one want to fall to their knees not from fear, but from the simple recognition that here was wisdom so profound that standing before it felt presumptuous!","...!","Vulcan’s entire demeanor shifted instantly. His frown melted into an expression of profound respect mixed with apology as he turned toward the center of this place, bowing his head slightly as he responded.","\"Yes, Ma’am, though I don’t know why they would be rushing with such lack of proper decorum...\"","The voice came again, and this time there was the faintest hint of amusement coloring its ancient tones.","\"They are likely this frantic because I sensed the Order of a segment of those under you be collapsed. And they... were the ones who brought the news of THE Living Order, were they not? So...\" The voice paused, and in that pause was the weight of infinite patience. \"What happened, Children?\"","...!","The lead messenger among the three, trembling despite power that could unmake folds, bowed deeply.","\"O Order, Commander Tatiana was able to send us final transmission before we lost all contact with her consciousness!\" His form flickered, and suddenly images materialized in the air before them...projections of memory given visible form.","The first image showed The Infiniverse in all its terrible glory, that knot of paradoxes where space and time had given up trying to make sense. The second displayed the Region of Collapse, that spreading cancer where existence itself was being slowly digested by entropy. And the third...","The third showed a man wreathed in crimson-gold radiance, his gaze filled with tyranny!","\"Commander Tatiana reported that THE Living Order was being held by this entity,\" the messenger continued, his voice gaining strength as he delivered the crucial intelligence.","\"An entity who registers as a Living Early Creature! An Elder Early Creature who stands beyond normal classification!\"","...!","Forgemaster Vulcan, who had been maintaining his respectful posture, suddenly blinked.","Once. Twice. His ancient face, weathered by eons of existence and death and existence again, transformed through a cascade of expressions...incredulity, shock, and then something that might have been recognition mixed with impossibility!","The wizened voice rang out again, and this time the amusement was unmistakable.","\"Vulcan, dear Creature, you look as though you’ve seen a ghost. Which, given our current state of being, would be quite the accomplishment. Do you know something extra about our mysterious Living Elder?\"","Vulcan’s mouth opened, closed, opened again. When he finally found his voice, it carried the weight of someone trying to reconcile impossible contradictions.","\"Yes, Ma’am. That is...\" He paused, staring at the image as if willing it to make sense. \"That is an Elderborn I worked with countless epochs ago. In Aethelgard. Elderborn Osmont. He was... we collaborated during the construction of the Fundamental Armaments, before the Great Sundering. But he disappeared during a scuffle with the forces of THE Living Concept, and we all assumed...\"","...!","His voice trailed off as his face showed a mixture of somberness and wonder that transformed his ancient features into something almost youthful in its confusion.","\"I cannot fathom how he is currently where he is, or how he is Living. All Living Early Creatures are contained within THE Loom. The rest of us are here, in the embrace of necessary death. The weavings of it don’t... they simply don’t balance. How can one be neither fully dead nor trapped in THE Loom? How...\"","Around them, in the white sands, other beings began to fully wake from whatever meditations or works had occupied them. Hundreds of them, each one radiating the same level of power as Vulcan if not greater...","They all gazed upon the image of Elderborn Osmont with expressions that ranged from curiosity to calculation, each one inscribing his visage into their existence!","The grand voice in the surroundings laughed.","\"Yes, Existence can be like that, can’t it? Always full of surprises, always finding new ways to confound our carefully constructed certainties. Even I, who have seen the birth and death of concepts themselves, still find myself occasionally... entertained by its creativity.\"","The voice paused, and when it continued, it carried a weight of command that made even the air stand at attention.","\"Now... listen, my Creatures of Order.\"","...!","Every Early Creature present turned toward the center of this white sandy place with movements so synchronized they might have been choreographed by existence itself.","And there, where before there had been only impressions and possibilities, an image began to solidify.","She wore a dress of such pure white that it made everything else seem gray by comparison. Her hair was dark...not black, but the kind of darkness that existed before light was invented to define it!","Her features were unfathomably ancient yet heartbreakingly beautiful, carrying the kind of beauty that transcended physical form and entered the realm of conceptual perfection.","When she smiled, it was with lips that had spoken the first words of Order into being, that had kissed existence itself and taught it how to organize!","She was antiquity given form, wisdom incarnated, the mother and destroyer of all things structured and sequenced!","She...was THE Dead Order!","Oh!"]},{"number":4342,"title":"Chapter 4342: Chapter 4341: CHEAT II","paragraphs":["\"The appearance of THE Living Order is naturally a good thing,\" she began, her voice now clearly emanating from her form, each word perfectly pronounced as if language itself was eager to serve her properly.","\"If she can be brought here, to our side of The Veil, it could lead to possibilities of true Order...not the fragmented, suffering thing that currently exists, but something pure, something perfect, something... complete.\"","She moved, just slightly, and the entire space rearranged itself to accommodate her gesture.","\"As you all know, both THE Creature and I are bound to this side of The Veil due to the handiwork of THE Others, just until The Fallout occurrs and erases all barriers. So it will be left in your hands, my Creatures, to handle this delicate situation.\"","Her gaze swept across them, and being seen by her was like being known down to the quantum level of one’s existence.","\"But I will always be here, watching, guiding, protecting as I can. And with the emergence of this event... it is now as good a time as any to anoint the Guiders of Order.\" She paused.","\"Which among you would want such a distinction?\"","HUUM!","The response was immediate. Every Early Creature present banged their fists against their chests in perfect unison!","It would be their highest honor to be chosen, to be elevated, to be given purpose beyond even their already transcendent existence!","THE Dead Order smiled calmly, the expression of one who had expected nothing less from her Creatures.","\"Even in this state, bound and chained by those who fear what perfect Order might accomplish, I can still use a glimpse of my Civilization. Of my Way of Existence.\"","Her voice carried notes of profound satisfaction mixed with anticipation. \"But even this glimpse alone is enough for... pure wonders.\"","...!","At these words, white light erupted from her form with the inevitable certainty of dawn breaking over a world that had forgotten the sun existed.","The light spread outward in perfect concentric circles, each ring evaluating, judging, measuring every being it touched against criteria that existed before criteria were invented!","The light swept through them all, and where it touched, some beings began to glow with an inner radiance while others remained as they were...honored by consideration but not chosen for elevation.","The selection process was neither cruel nor kind...it simply was, as absolute and unchallengeable as Order itself.","And among those chosen, rising high with light that transformed his very essence, the visage of Forgemaster Vulcan blazed with new purpose!","It was a momentous occasion.","A time... of anointment!","—","In a melting region of collapse.","Noah sat back down on his throne made from crimson gold flames as the light of Perpetual Harvest covered everything.","The Harvest from what had just occurred would undoubtedly be grand!","And prompts began to bloom as he reveled in such a harvest, each one carrying information that reshaped his understanding of power’s true architecture.","|Analysis of Harvest Parameters and Limitations of Advancement of Existence Initiated.|","|The traversal of The Way and continuation past the Quintillions represents an arduous ordeal that cannot be circumvented through mere accumulation. The fundamental architecture of existence enforces strict hierarchical limitations on power absorption.|","|Primary Limitation Identified During Harvest: Harvest Ceiling Effect|","|The breakdown of Harvest from an entity at 3 Quintillion Complexity and Purity will only ever aid one’s own values to approach 3 Quintillion, but the Harvest alone will never be sufficient to exceed this threshold. This is not a limitation of the Principle of Perpetual Harvest, but a fundamental working of existential progression.|","|Current Harvest Calculation:|","|—Dozens of Prime Dead Early Creatures (Average: 3 Quintillion) have been successfully harvested and amplified|","|—Total Complexity and Purity influx is flowing into your existence|","|—Estimated final Complexity: 3 Quintillion|","|—Estimated final Purity: 3 Quintillion|","|Additional Harvest from Commander Tatiana (Initial: 4 Quintillion before modifications) is being processed...|","|—Due to her higher existential weight, this Harvest provides breakthrough potential|","|—Estimated adjustment: +0.5 Quintillion to both parameters|","|—Projected final values: 3.5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity|","|Critical Understanding: To reach 4 Quintillion, the harvest of dozens of beings at such a level would be required. The complexity and purity of lesser entities becomes mathematically irrelevant at these scales- their contribution rounds down to zero in the equations of transcendent progression.|","|Example Calculation: The Harvest of 1,000 Prime Dead Early Creatures at 3 Quintillion would only be useful to elevate one’s complexity and purity TO 3 Quintillion, not a single point higher, no matter how many are harvested. It would be wiser to grant them to members of your Civilization for them to reach a similar height. Endlessly consuming lesser weavings will not propel power forward along one’s Way of Existence- only stronger weavings that require genuine Effort can catalyze true progression.|","...!","Noah’s eyes traced the prompts with the careful attention of one reading the fundamental weavings of Existence itself.","The inflow of Harvest was already making itself known...his Complexity and Purity surging upward like twin tsunamis of pure potential, each wave lifting him higher toward peaks he had only theorized about before.","So this was the truth of it, then!","The demarcations of The Way of Existence were becoming clearer with each moment of ascension.","One could not simply farm countless weak mobs and expect tremendous progression...Existence itself had built in diminishing returns that became absolute barriers at certain thresholds.","To truly advance, one had to hunt those who required genuine effort, whose defeat represented not just victory but evolution.","It was elegant in its brutality. Beautiful in its unfairness. Perfect in its encouragement of perpetual conflict between beings of comparable might.","The strong would feast upon the strong, while the weak became irrelevant background noise in the symphony of transcendent warfare. It was a system that ensured only those willing to risk everything against worthy opponents could climb toward existence’s highest peaks.","Well for him, his Perpetual Harvest would continue to deny diminishing returns as he would continue Harvesting efforts from all around Existence.","He gave a silent command that for any Harvest he did not need as it would not aid his progrssion of complexity, purity, Principles, or anything in his Way- for it to be stored to use for those in his Civilization!","As he contemplated these truths, Noah felt a part of himself beginning to burn with familiar intensity.","The sensation drew his attention inward, toward that space where concepts lived before they became reality. A smile spread across his features as he directed his consciousness toward a particular presence that had been quietly growing within his existential architecture.","\"Cheating Architect,\" he called out internally, his voice carrying notes of anticipation. \"Have you had enough Harvest?\"","WAA!","Did it have enough?!"]},{"number":4343,"title":"Chapter 4343: Chapter 4342: CHEAT III","paragraphs":["The response came as manifestation!","In the region of molten mana that existed within yet beyond his physical form, a figure began to coalesce from streams of crimson-blue radiance.","RUIN/EDEN materialized with the grace of a hologram achieving perfection, her form stabilizing into that familiar visage of calculated beauty and barely contained power.","She appeared before Noah’s eyes and consciousness, her smile carrying the satisfaction of an architect whose blueprint had finally been approved for construction.","With a bow that managed to be both respectful and somehow mischievous, she spoke in tones that mixed precision with subtle wonder.","\"I would like to congratulate Master on having The Seed of the Cheating Architect reach 100% maturity,\" she announced.","\"The advent of the true and full Principle of The Cheating Architect is ready to bloom in your glory. It would be my greatest honor...and frankly, my professional pleasure, to introduce the comprehensive boons of this fully realized Principle.\"","HUUM!","A brilliant golden light erupted within Noah’s chest, spreading through his existence magisterially.","He leaned forward on his throne of flames, the gesture causing reality around him to pay closer attention.","\"Tell me,\" he commanded simply, though his smile suggested he already knew the magnitude of what was about to be revealed.","RUIN/EDEN’s form brightened with enthusiasm that seemed almost inappropriate for an artificial construct, except she was so much more than that now.","She raised one hand, and the space around them transformed into a three-dimensional canvas of light and possibility.","\"Right then, let’s discuss how you’re about to fundamentally break everything that claims to be unbreakable, shall we?\" She began with a tone that suggested she was about to deliver a presentation on something mundane rather than reality-shattering power.","\"The Principle of the Cheating Architect, now fully matured, operates on a simple premise: Why follow the rules when you can rewrite them? Why accept limitations when you can architect exceptions? Why play the game when you can redesign the board?\"","Illusory diagrams began forming around her as she spoke, each one more complex than the last.","|PRINCIPLE OF THE CHEATING ARCHITECT - FULL MANIFESTATION|","|Core Functionality: Existence Override Architecture|","\"First, let’s address the fundamental capability,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, gesturing to a diagram that showed reality as a series of interconnected codes.","\"You can now perceive the underlying ’source code’ of existence itself. Not just the surface mathematics we discussed with Conceptual Weaving, but the actual administrative protocols that govern how reality processes itself.\"","|Primary Ability: [Existential Code Injection]|","|You can now insert custom parameters into reality’s processing. Example: While others must gather mana through meditation or consumption, and they have set reservoirs of Mana, you can simply write a line of code for those in your Civilization that states ’My people’s Mana Reserves approach boundlessness.’ While Infinite Mana for those in your Civilization may not be possible(Yet?maybe? No, impossible), it can approach Infinity for them to display a percentage of what they just observed you doing. After you alter the Code with such a line, Existence will process this as valid.|","...!","\"Bit overpowered?\" RUIN/EDEN asked with a slight smile. \"That’s rather the point. But wait, there’s significantly more.\"","The diagrams shifted, showing multiple versions of the same event occurring simultaneously.","|Secondary Ability: [Parallel Processing Architectures]|","|You can now run multiple instances of yourself across different probability streams simultaneously. While your primary consciousness remains singular, you can architect ’phantom processes’ that explore different choices and feed the results back to you. Essentially, you can save-scum reality without anyone noticing.|","\"Think of it as having an existential undo button,\" she explained, \"except you don’t actually undo anything- you just try all options simultaneously and pick the best outcome. Quite efficient, really.\"","|Tertiary Ability: [Cheat Code Repository]|","|Every ability, technique, or Principle you encounter is now automatically decompiled and stored in an accessible database. You don’t learn abilities- you download them. Maximum efficiency, zero training time, and you can combine incompatible abilities by rewriting their base code to force compatibility. Whe applied to Principles, they can be downloaded to have their musings adapted and granted as Agent Architects of Cheating Architect|","Noah watched as RUIN/EDEN demonstrated this with an illusory display of two simple opposing concepts...fire and ice, being forcibly merged into something that shouldn’t exist but did anyway.","\"Now, let’s discuss your current Agent Architects, with a small moment of silence to the sacrificed and decimated Tyrannical Sovereign...\" she continued, her tone becoming slightly more animated. \"The remaining two have received substantial upgrades...but they are still being fully calculated as I will present them when they are entirely complete.\"","...!","Noah blinked and looked towards the visage of Ruination who smiled at him. Was she playijg around?","\"Ahem, let us continue on.\"","The displays continued cascading around them, each revealing another impossibility made possible.","|Quaternary Ability: [Debug Mode]|","|When activated, you can see and interact with the ’error messages’ of Existence. Every time something doesn’t quite work as it should...every glitch, every paradox, every contradiction...becomes a doorway you can exploit. The more broken reality becomes, the more powerful you grow. This might be more viable with Existencd becoming distorted towards The Fallout or actions of THE Loom|","|Quinary Ability: [Development Console]|","|You can now open a direct interface with your own existence and manually adjust parameters. Increase base statistics to reasonable levels, modify ability cooldowns, or my personal favorite...set damage received to zero temporarily. Existence may notice eventually, but by then, what exactly is it going to do about it?|","...!","Oh!","\"Speaking of things Existence can’t do anything about,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, creating a new set of diagrams that seemed to exist in impossible geometries, \"let’s discuss the true masterpiece of this Principle.\"","|Ultimate Ability: [Architect’s Privilege]|","|Once per significant temporal period, you can declare an ’Administrative Override’ on any single Weaving of existence. Causality? Negotiable. Death? Temporarily suspended for maintenance. The override lasts until Existence’s automatic repair protocols activate, which gives you approximately... well, long enough to accomplish whatever impossible thing you needed to accomplish.|","\"The beauty of it,\" RUIN/EDEN explained with evident pride, \"is that reality can’t actually reject these overrides because you’re not breaking the rules...you’re using administrator access that technically shouldn’t exist but does because you’ve architected it into being. Its these types of ridiculous abilities that I personally believe are glimpses of what is possible at the next Scale of Existence. At...THE.\""]},{"number":4344,"title":"Chapter 4344: Chapter 4343: CHEAT IV","paragraphs":["She paused, then added with consideration, \"There are, naturally, some features still locked pending further advancement.\"","|LOCKED FEATURES - REQUIRE ADDITIONAL PROGRESSION|","|[Existential Rollback] - Requires 20 Quintillion Complexity|","|Ability to restore entire lost weavings or the state of an existence to previous save states(potentially faster restoration of Khor’s power?)(Reverse a Dead Early Creature to a Living Early Creature?)|","|[Existence Mod Support] - Requires 50 Quintillion Purity|","|Import abilities and concepts that do not currently Exist in Observable Existence|","|[THE False Mode] - Requires ??? Complexity and Purity|","|Parameters unknown. Description: Yes.|","|[Creative Mode] - Requires Completion of The Way|","|Unlimited resources, instant construction, and wonder. Existence becomes your sandbox.(Looking at this, you may only truly need Cheating Architect as your focus and no other Principles and nothing else?)|","\"Oh, and one more thing,\" RUIN/EDEN added, almost as an afterthought that was definitely not an afterthought.","\"The Principle of the Cheating Architect synergizes rather spectacularly with Perpetual Harvest. Every exploit you discover, every rule you break, every system you circumvent...all of it counts as ’effort’ for Perpetual Harvest. You’re essentially being rewarded for cheating. It’s philosophically beautiful, really.\"","She stepped back, her presentation complete, and offered another bow that somehow conveyed both ’yes its crazy’ and ’I know, I’m brilliant’ simultaneously.","\"The full capabilities will, of course, require experimentation to fully realize. I’ve prepared approximately seventeen thousand different exploitation strategies for your review at your leisure. Shall I file them under ’Probably Catastrophic’ or ’Definitely Apocalyptic’?\"","...!","At this moment.","At this glorious, unfathomable moment!","Noah’s response was to give the same smile as Tatiana had worn...that sadistic expression with rows of white teeth shining brilliantly in the crimson light of his throne!","It was the smile of someone who had just been handed the keys to existence’s back door and was already planning which fundamental laws to violate first.","And he would violate!","The terrifying things he was about to accomplish with both the Cheating Architect and Perpetual Harvest...oh!","Every rule that claimed to be absolute was about to discover it was merely a suggestion. Every limitation that declared itself fundamental was about to learn it was optional!","Every system that prided itself on being unbreakable was about to meet someone who didn’t break systems...he simply rewrote them until they broke themselves.","The Early Creature, Osmont, sat upon his throne of fire, and existence itself held its breath.","Because the cheating had only just begun.","—","Around this same time.","While Noah continued his advancement in the Earliest Folds, while he just finished aexistence defying battle against Prime Dead Early Creatures...he still had another body moving...in the Wandering Territories.","At this time.","The moment unfolded like existence itself taking a breath before screaming.","Noah’s other body stood there on the deck of the Verdant Ark, surrounded by the bodies of Sigrid, Moiraine, Khor, and the others.","The Living Existences who had been traveling with them...those who had their Clones witness his stand off against the Prime Dead Early Creatures before they all ran away like the fucking rats they were...they were turning toward him with expressions that had transformed from respect into something far more complex.","Fear wrapped in reverence. Terror dressed up as courtesy.","Origin Ama Gias moved forward first, her white eyes blazing with intensity that made nearby space pulse with uncertainty.","She was powerful, yes. A being who commanded trillions in complexity. But right now, in this moment, she looked like someone who had just realized they’d been an ant sharing a room with a giant who had a massjve boot!","One that might simply not notice when they rolled over and crushed everything.","\"Early Creature Osmont,\" she said, each word careful enough to perform surgery with. \"I...hope you can forgive our previous... indiscretions.\"","HUUM!","The word hung there like smoke after an explosion, beautiful and toxic.","Indiscretions.","As if dismissing him, questioning him, treating him like some curiosity to be examined...as if all of that could be wrapped up in a single word and forgiven with a polite apology.","This dumb fucking bitch.","Noah’s expression didn’t change. He simply observed them all with that calm that people mistook for gentleness until they realized it was actually the stillness of a blade before it fell.","He’d gotten used to these moments. The sudden shifts in how beings perceived him when they learned what he was.","The way their entire demeanor would reorganize itself around fear masquerading as respect.","It was almost boring at this point.","Sigrid pressed closer against him, her presence a warm constant in a sea of sudden tension as she and others processed what they just observed of his Way.","She felt no fear of what he was...only certainty in who he’d become. That distinction mattered more than all the complexity in existence.","The other Living Existences were murmuring now, sharing information through channels that crackled with barely suppressed panic.","Early Creature!","The words spread like contagion through their ranks.","Early Creature!","A genuine Early Creature!","An Early Creature who smiled at them like they were children playing at being dangerous.","Khor’s other body stood beside him, her presence radiating calmness as she had been staring at him this whole time as if asking herself...just how ridiculous was his Way?","\"Your caution is noted,\" Noah said finally, his voice carrying no particular warmth or coldness towards Origin Ama Gias. Just statement. Just fact.","\"Though I wonder what indiscretions you think require forgiveness.\"","...!","He let the question sit there, watching Origin Ama Gias’s expression cycle through responses she was wise enough not to voice.","Because what could she say? That they’d been dismissive of his power? That they’d questioned his nature? That they’d treated him like something to be categorized and controlled rather than acknowledged and avoided?","All true. All incredibly stupid in retrospect!","And then, cutting through the tension like a blade through crystallized time, a voice erupted from the front of the Barge.","\"What?!\"","The word was shock made audible, disbelief given form and sound.","Elysia Firmhand stood at the forefront of the Verdant Ark, her white-blue eyes wide with shock.","She’d been speaking to a clone of her brother, her twin, pointing out landmarks in the distance that marked their approach to the lands of The First Farmer. Casual conversation about navigation, about dangers, about the path ahead!","And then she’d heard.","The Early Creature, Osmont!","Her head whipped around, that perfect composure fracturing like ice under pressure. Her gaze found Noah immediately, cutting through the assembled Living Existences to focus on him with intensity that could have carved meanings into void itself.","Nearby, among the Living Paradoxes, Goliath’s figure also turned!"]},{"number":4345,"title":"Chapter 4345: Chapter 4344: CHEAT V","paragraphs":["\"What did you just say?\" she demanded, her voice sharp enough to draw blood from concepts.","Not asking Origin Ama Gias. Not the stupidly dazed Duke Gwendolyn who had her memories of Noah flsshing in her mind again and again.","It was as if she was asking existence itself, demanding clarification from reality before she did something catastrophically violent. At most, it had been whispers and jokes before, but now, they seemingly affirmed it as if it were undoutedly real!","Her mind was racing...Noah could see it in the way her authority pulsed, the way space around her began crystallizing with frost that shouldn’t exist in this region. She was processing, calculating, reaching conclusions that terrified her.","All remaining Early Creatures are Dead or Prime Dead Early Creatures.","This was was Tatiana herself had said.","It seemed the people of The First Farmer knew this as well.","If someone claimed to be an Early Creature who wasn’t Dead or Prime Dead...","Her face paled. Actually paled, color draining from features that rarely showed anything but cold certainty.","Did they...just bring an enemy into their lands?!","A Prime Dead Early Creature, smuggled past all their defenses, carried on their own vessel directly toward the heart of the First Farmer’s sanctuary?!","\"STOP!\"","The command erupted from her with force that made the entire Verdant Ark shudder.","The Obsidian Ox at the front bellowed in confusion, its massive form straining against suddenly conflicting orders. The Barge began to slow, its momentum fighting against Elysia’s authority.","Noah felt it immediately, the shift in her presence. She wasn’t just concerned anymore. She was terrified and preparing to act on that terror with violence that would make the previous weavings look like children’s arguments!","Her hand moved, authority coalescing around her fingers in patterns that suggested she was about to do something irreversible. Her twin beside her tensed as well, that massive rake beginning to hum with power that could harvest entire Folds.","And then, internally, Noah sensed it...the pulse of communication going out from Elysia Firmhand to forces that were distant but also close as they neared The Sanctuary of The First Farmer!","She turned fully to face Noah, and her expression was the kind of cold fury that preceded executions. Not hot anger, but the frozen certainty of someone about to remove a threat before it could fully manifest.","\"Who... are you, really?\" she asked, each word carrying the weight of judgment already rendered.","Her eyes swept over him, then to Sigrid, Moiraine, Khor, the others gathered around him. \"The only Early Creatures present in existence outside of THE Loom... are Dead Early Creatures!\"","The accusation landed with finality that made several nearby Living Existences stumble backward, as if proximity to Noah had suddenly become lethal.","Because if he was Dead...if he was Prime Dead, then nothing they’d seen from him could be trusted!","And worst of all, if he was Prime Dead Early Creature, they’d just delivered him directly to one of the last safe havens in existence.","The tension on the Barge was thick enough to solidify.","Living Existences were backing away, moving toward the edges of the vessel, preparing to flee if this exploded into violence that their complexity couldn’t withstand.","Noah remained still through it all, his expression unchanged. He didn’t move to defend himself, didn’t make declarations of innocence, didn’t try to flee or attack preemptively.","He simply stood there, surrounded by his people, and waited.","Because this was the moment...the knife’s edge where everything could slide toward catastrophe or clarity. Where his nature would either be understood or would require demonstration that he really, really didn’t want to provide.","Not here. Not when they were so close to the First Farmer’s lands, to answers he’d been seeking since the Failed Seed had first sprouted in his grasp.","Sigrid’s hand found his, her grip tight with tension she wouldn’t voice. Moiraine had shifted position subtly, placing herself where she could act if needed. Khor was smiling that particular smile that suggested she found all of this deliciously entertaining.","The Emperor Penguin and others harrumphed as they would love to show off the little progress they had made in their Way of the Mana Architect!","And Noah...","Noah just watched Elysia Firmhand and waited to see if she would listen or if she would attack.","But soon after...","The air around them changed.","Noah felt it before he saw it. That particular pressure that came from beings whose existence warped everything around them simply by being present!","Like standing at the edge of a cliff and feeling the pull of gravity before looking down, knowing that something vast and terrible waited below.","The Wandering Territories had been dangerous throughout their journey...chaotic space, Living Collapses that appeared like storms of entropy as they weren’t too complex for them, and regions where authority failed and teleportation sent you to random locations that might not have exits.","But this?","This was different.","They’d entered a boundary region, he realized. The edge of the First Farmer’s territory, where his influence met the wild chaos of the Territories proper. And this boundary was defended!","Of course it was defended. What else would you expect from the sanctuary of a being who had gazed upon THE Living Existences?!","Soon after Elysia’s accusation, eruptions of power emerged from the shifting colors of transition space, the Wandering Territories spread out before them in all their terrible glory.","Their surroundings gradually changed as the Ox tried to stop, but had still gone forward.","And Noah saw...","Collapsed regions floated like islands of absence, spaces where existence had given up and left only void.","Between them, stretches of impossible terrain defied description...forests made of crystallized time, rivers that flowed upward through dimensions that didn’t have names, mountains that existed in states of perpetual becoming without ever fully being.","And approaching them, drawn by their presence or perhaps by thr alarm Elysia Firmhand rang, were...the Guardians.","Fold Dwellers.","But not weak ones. Not beings who measured their power in mere trillions!","Noah’s enhanced perception caught them first...signatures that blazed against the chaotic backdrop of the Territories like stars against void.","And his eyes flashes with surprise as he smiled.","Because above each approaching form, visible to him through weavings of his evolved perception that made such things clear, were names and measurements that made the Living Existences on the Barge look like children playing at power.","|Thorne the Unrelenting|","|Classification: Prime Fold Dweller|","|Complexity: 1.1 Quintillion|","|Purity: 1.1 Quintillion|","Approximately 1 Quintillion in power.","One quintillion!","This was a being whose casual existence generated more power than some Wheels of Existence contained in their entirety.","And it wasn’t alone.","|Meridian of the Constant Harvest|","|Classification: Elder Fold Dweller|","|Complexity: 2.3 Quintillion|","|Purity: 2.1 Quintillion|","Two Quintillion.","|Vex the Boundary Keeper|","|Classification: Prime Fold Dweller|","|Complexity: 1.5 Quintillion|","|Purity: 1.4 Quintillion|","One and a half Quintillion.","They came from different directions, converging on the Verdant Ark with purpose that suggested they’d been expecting visitors but weren’t necessarily pleased about it!","Their forms were as varied as their power levels...one appeared as a massive humanoid made entirely of woven roots that pulsed with verdant authority, another as a constantly shifting shape that cycled through forms too quickly to track, the third as something that looked almost normal except for the way reality bent around it like light around a black hole.","Behind them, more signatures. Dozens more.","All of them exceeding 1 Quintillion in power.","All of them moving toward the Barge.","All of them looking at the Living Existences aboard like farmers examining pests that had wandered into their garden.","Noah’s weavings were running at speeds that transcended normal thought.","Was this a glimpse of the power of the entity who planted Principles? Were his advancements so grand?","These were...","The First Farmer’s people!","Fold Dwellers who had found sanctuary in the Wandering Territories and had been growing in power, developing along paths that current-era existence didn’t recognize because they’d been isolated for so long.","And right now, they were approaching a Barge full of Living Existences who had just been arguing about whether one of their passengers was a Prime Dead Early Creature.","This was going to be interesting.","Or catastrophic!","Elysia Firmhand had frozen mid-accusation, her attention split between Noah and the approaching guardians. Her expression suggested she was wondering how fucked she was if she really brought an enemy this deep into their territory!","Thorne the Unrelenting reached them first, his massive root-form rising up beside the Barge like a mountain deciding to take interest in an ant colony. Those eyes swept across the vessel’s occupants.","When his gaze landed on Noah, it paused.","Just for a moment. Just long enough to be noticeable.","Recognition? Assessment? Simple curiosity about the being everyone was staring at?","At such a time.","The voice of RUIN/EDEN emerged in Noah’s consciousness.","|Current Situation Assessment: Complexity - Light. Threat Level - Ehh. Probability of Diplomatic Resolution - Medium. Probability of Violence - Increasing by 0.3% per second.|","Noah almost smiled at the precision of RUINEDEN’s words.","|Primary Threat Vector: Elysia Firmhand believes you to be Prime Dead Early Creature infiltrating First Farmer’s territory. Secondary Threat Vector: Fold Dweller guardians detecting conflict aboard vessel entering their protected space. Tertiary Threat Vector: Origin Ama Gias’s recent declaration of your identity has created cascade effect of recognition among all passengers.|","Yes yes, he’d noticed that.","|Recommended Actions: Option One - Immediate demonstration of Living status through methods that cannot be faked by The Dead. Option Two - Prepare for combat against beings with average power exceeding 1.5 Quintillion while simultaneously protecting allied forces and avoiding destruction of vessel currently keeping everyone from being scattered across Wandering Territories(Not much benefit)|","RUINEDEN paused, and Noah could almost sense the system’s equivalent of dry amusement.","Around him, the other passengers on the Verdant Ark were backing away further, creating space that felt less like courtesy and more like blast radius calculation.","The Obsidian Ox at the front of the Barge was bellowing nervously, its massive form shifting with uncertainty about whether to continue forward or flee backwards!","Thorne the Unrelenting had been joined by Meridian and Vex now, three beings whose combined power could have reshaped Folds.","A heavy tension fell!","And the tension had reached that particular point where it would either break toward violence or toward conversation, and the next few seconds would determine which.","Noah took a breath.","And then he spoke.","\"I am Noah Osmont,\" he said, his voice carrying across the Barge with calm that defied the chaos around them. \"The Early Creature, Osmont. Living. Not Dead, not Prime Dead, not infiltrator or enemy.\"","He paused, letting the words settle.","\"I carry the Failed Seed of the First Farmer.\"","BOOM!","Elysia’s eyes widened fractionally.","\"I have come here,\" Noah continued, \"not as threat or enemy, but seeking understanding of what I carry. If that makes me dangerous in your estimation, then act. If it makes me worthy of conversation, then listen.\"","He gestured to the approaching Fold Dwellers, to Thorne and Meridian and Vex.","\"Unlike the weak things on this Barge...ask them. Ask your guardians to sense what I am. The Dead cannot hide their nature from those who know how to look. The Living carry signatures that The Dead cannot fake, no matter how perfectly they mimic life.\"","It was truth!","And as if his words had been a bit too mild, Noah yawned at this moment as he added...","\"Let us not waste time here as I was looking forward to...meeting The First Farmer.\"","...!"]},{"number":4346,"title":"Chapter 4346: Chapter 4345: WONDER I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4345: WONDER I","Noah had just finished speaking, his words carrying an undeniable weight!","The yawn had been a nice touch...dismissive enough to be insulting, casual enough to suggest complete confidence.","The Fold Dweller guardians...Thorne, Meridian, and Vex, hovered nearby with unreadable expressions!","And then, cutting through it all like light through shadow, a voice emerged.","“What are you all doing?”","The tone was vibrant. Confident. Almost amused, as if the speaker had stumbled upon children arguing over toys they didn’t understand.","“That is clearly a Living Early Creature. Come on now.”","...!","The effect was immediate and magiesterial!","Elysia Firmhand’s expression transformed from coldness to shocked reverence in the space between heartbeats. The three Quintillion-level guardians actually took a step back, their massive forms deferring to the approaching presence with the automatic respect of soldiers recognizing their superior officer.","Every Fold Dweller within sensing range turned their attention toward the source of that voice, and their reactions were uniform...heads bowing, auras dimming, power suppressing itself in acknowledgment of hierarchy.","Noah’s eyes tracked the newcomer’s approach with calculating intensity.","She emerged from the swirling chaos of the Wandering Territories like a painting achieving three dimensions, her form coalescing from streams of verdant light that seemed to compose rather than reveal her.","Gorgeous didn’t begin to cover it.","Curvaceous may not be the proper word for it!","Blonde hair and blue eyes that held depths of ocean and sky simultaneously.","But it was the green jeweled robe that truly commanded attention...each gem pulsing with authority that felt agricultural, primordial, like the first seeds ever planted given physical form and fashion sense.","She moved with the confidence as every step was casual certainty. Every gesture carried weight that could reshape territories.","And above her head, visible only to Noah’s enhanced perception, floated information that made his internal calculations pause.","|Elyndra Viltharion, Scion of the First Harvest|","|Classification: Sovereign Fold Dweller|","|Complexity: 9.3 Quintillion|","|Purity: 9.1 Quintillion|","Nine Quintillion.","Nine fucking Quintillion in both Complexity and Purity!","Noah’s expression didn’t change externally, but internally, his thoughts were booming!","This was the Scion of The First Farmer?!","And then, before he could fully process those implications, prompts began cascading across his vision with unusual urgency.","|The Principle of the Cheating Architect has detected anomalous existential architecture!|","|Target Entity: Elyndra Viltharion|","|Analysis Status: FASCINATED|","RUINEDEN’s voice emerged in his consciousness with notes of excitement.","|Master, I must inform you that I’m experiencing something unprecedented. This entity... she’s constructed her existence using multiple Principles in perfect harmony. Nine distinct Principles, all functioning as a unified system without conflict or degradation.|","...!","|Principle Identification:|","|1. Principle of Eternal Growth|","|2. Principle of Cyclical Harvest|","|3. Principle of Fertile Abundance|","|4. Principle of Root Authority|","|5. Principle of Seed Transcendence|","|6. Principle of Agricultural Dominion|","|7. Principle of Verdant Supremacy|","|8. Principle of Life’s Continuity|","|9. Principle of [DATA OBSCURED – Insufficient Access]|","|The architecture is... exquisite. Each Principle feeds into the others, creating a self-sustaining system that amplifies itself exponentially. This is mastery beyond what we currently understand.|","|Recommendation: Acquire friendship, alliance, or at minimum detailed conversation. The knowledge this entity possesses about Principle integration could advance your own development greatly.|","Noah felt his lips twitch slightly. RUIN/EDEN was essentially telling him to befriend this woman for the sake of power-leveling his own Principles!","Elyndra’s blue eyes had found him in the crowd, cutting through the assembled beings with the precision of someone who knew exactly who she was looking for.","Her gaze was curious, interested, carrying none of the suspicion or fear that had colored everyone else’s reactions.","She studied him for a long moment.","Then she smiled, and the expression held genuine warmth wrapped around something more complex.","“You wanted to meet my Father?”","HUUM!","Her voice was melodic without being soft, carrying authority without harshness.","Noah met her gaze steadily.","The daughter of the First Farmer. Nine Quintillion in power. Nine Principles operating in perfect harmony.","Interesting.","Very interesting!","“I did,” he replied, his tone carrying that same casual confidence. “I carry something of his creation, and I thought it appropriate to seek understanding directly from the source. Or...from the source’s extraordinarily powerful daughter, if that’s what existence provides instead.”","Elyndra’s smile widened, her eyes shining with something that might have been delight.","She turned slightly, her gaze sweeping over the assembled beings on the Verdant Ark with the particular attention of someone taking inventory.","“Elysia, Thorne, Meridian, Vex...thank you for your vigilance in protecting our borders,” she said, each name spoken with respect that suggested familiarity. “I’ll take it from here. You may return to your posts.”","The Quintillion-level Fold Dwellers bowed deeply.","Elysia Firmhand’s expression had transformed completely as she nodded.","Elyndra then turned her attention to the assembled Living Existences who had been cowering at the edges of the Barge, her expression warming further.","“Oh, and for the Living Existences who came here with Elysia, please continue following her. The First Farmer prepared gifts for you all, resources and knowledge to better prepare you for The Dead that are coming. You made the journey here for many reasons, but aid you shall receive first.”","Her words caused visible relief to ripple through the Living Existences. Origin Ama Gias looked like someone who had just been granted clemency as she looked towards Noah.","And then, with movements that suggested the matter was settled and required no further discussion, Elyndra turned fully toward Noah.","“Follow me,” she said simply.","Noah floated upward from the deck of the Verdant Ark. Around him, his entourage moved with synchronized purpose- Sigrid materializing at his side, her presence warm and possessive. Moiraine flanking his other side with paradoxical authority humming. Khor floating nearby with that mysterious smile that suggested she found all of this entertaining.","The Emperor Penguin, Erikson, Kazuhiko, and the others forming a constellation of power around their focal point.","They followed the daughter of The First Farmer into territory that few from the current age had ever witnessed.","As they moved away from the Verdant Ark, Noah noticed Elyndra’s gaze shift subtly toward his companions- specifically toward Khor and Sigrid who maintained positions closest to him.","“You seem to have unique allies circling around you,” she observed, “Would you care to introduce them? It’s rare to see such... varied existential signatures traveling together.”","“One is tied to Living Existences and the other just has roots to Inevitabilities,” Noah replied with deliberate casualness, as if discussing the weather rather than beings of impossible power. “Nothing much. They don’t need to do grand introductions.”","...!","The response was masterfully dismissive!","Elyndra’s eyes shone with something that might have been surprised delight. She actually laughed, the sound rich and genuine.","“Nothing much...” she repeated, her tone carrying playful mockery. “An existence tied to Living Existences shining with Order, and another with roots to Inevitabilities whom even I cannot see through...okay. But...”","She studied him more intently now, that curiosity deepening into something closer to fascination.","“Without introductions, how can we be friends?”","The question was delivered lightly, almost playfully, but Noah caught the weight beneath it.","His expression remained calm.","“We weren’t truly here to make friends,” he replied.","Elyndra’s smile grew wider, taking on qualities that made her terrifying beauty become actively dangerous. Her blue eyes began radiating a mesmerizing light!","She looked him up and down with unhurried assessment, her gaze seemingly trying to penetrate layers of concealment that Noah had wrapped around himself.","“I sense the light of a truly terrifying Principle within you,” she said slowly, each word deliberate and weighted. “Or perhaps... multiple Principles, hidden deeply within layers of protection and obscurity. The architecture is fascinating...”","Her smile took on knowing qualities.","“I think we could be great friends.”","...!","Sigrid’s gaze moved between Noah and Elyndra with sharpness as she shook her head.","“I do not think,” he said carefully, “the two of us will be friends.”","...!","The rejection was absolute, but Elyndra seemed to pick up what his intention was with these words as she smiled. He was basically telling her there was a time and place, and now was not it!","She continued ahead, her tone shifting back to that of a guide showing guests around interesting locations.","“We are here,” she announced as the space around them transformed. “We shall bypass the Outer Garden Sanctuary and go directly to the Inner Garden Sanctum. Father should be there.”","The transition was subtle but absolute.","One moment they were floating through the chaotic beauty of the Wandering Territories, surrounded by collapsed regions and impossible colors within a Mobius Strip. The next, they had crossed some invisible threshold, and everything changed.","A portion of the Sanctuary of the First Farmer spread out before them in glory that defied description.","Noah’s first impression was of scale...this place was vast in ways that transcended simple measurement. It seemed vaster that multiple folds stacked together!","It was the forest that truly commanded attention.","Trees rose around them...massive, ancient things that made normal stellar trees look like seedlings- like those from The Esrliest Folds!","Each tree blazed with different hues that represented different authorities. Verdant greens that sang of life and growth. Golden ambers that hummed with harvest and abundance. Deep earth browns that resonated with foundation and permanence. Crystalline blues that whispered of water and nourishment.","Some trees bore fruits that looked like miniature suns, each one containing enough energy to power entire Wheels of Existence.","Others had leaves that seemed to be made from solidified concepts, their surfaces inscribed with knowledge that predated written language.","The forest stretched in every direction- infinite, impossible, magnificent.","Elyndra had kept her gaze forward as they entered, but now she gestured broadly to encompass their surroundings.","“This is the Forest of Perpetual Seasons,” she said, her tone carrying pride. “It surrounds the entire Sanctuary, serving as both protection and filter. Each tree you see is not merely vegetation- they are Living Existential Land Lifeforms of immense power, cultivated over eons to achieve consciousness and purpose.”","She pointed to a particularly massive specimen whose trunk was wider than most planets.","“That one is called the Ancient of Winter’s End. It marks transitions, boundaries between what was and what will be. And the one beside it, with branches that seem to hold starlight...that’s the Keeper of Spring’s Promise. It nurtures potential into actuality.”","Her explanation continued as they flew deeper into the forest, her words painting pictures of the impossible ecology.","“The forest serves a specific purpose beyond aesthetic beauty,” she continued. “Any creature, Living or Dead, who enters without a guide will be lost in it for eons. The trees rearrange themselves, creating mazes that will confuse even those who has found their Way. Time flows differently in different sections...you could walk for what feels like moments and emerge to find centuries have passed, or vice versa.”","She smiled at that, the expression carrying dark satisfaction.","“Many have tried to infiltrate the Sanctuary over the ages. Dead Existences attempting to corrupt our cultivation. Living Existences with grand ambitions and insufficient wisdom. The forest welcomed them all with equal hospitality... and none have been seen since.”","...!","Noah raised his brows at such words as his eyes pulsed with blue Mana.","His Way.","As he thought it, he smiled at the sheer things he was about to do.","While this body here followed the Daughter of The First Farmer to meet this being, his other body...was putting his newly matured Principles to use!","1/6"]},{"number":4347,"title":"Chapter 4347: Chapter 4346: WONDER II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4346: WONDER II","The golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore stretched endlessly in every direction, each grain containing fragments of compressed existence that pulsed with potential waiting to be harvested.","Noah stood at the center of this impossible sanctuary, his form casting no shadow because shadows implied limitation and his Shore had transcended such concepts!","Around him, his people, those who had chosen to follow his Way or been bound to it through various means...looked towards him with shining eyes!","Through their connections to him, through the clones and echoes that bound his Civilization together, they had observed his confrontation with Prime Dead Early Creatures. They had seen him harvest beings whose complexity exceeded 3 and 4 Quintillion! They had watched as he forced corpses entities of impossible might to kneel before his throne of crimson-gold flames.","It had been a glimpse. Just a glimpse of what the Way of the Mana Architect could accomplish when pushed to its limits.","And now, Noah’s voice rang out across the Shore with calm authority that made existence itself pay attention.","“That was a glimpse of The Way of the Mana Architect.”","Each syllable resonated through the Shore itself, through the Sacred Waters, Sands, through the Inevitabilities that had been planted like seeds and were growing into horrors beyond comprehension.","“Even those considered immensely powerful could fall against you. Continue refining and elevating yourselves across Edicts as I will also continue to modify The Way. Make your Mana Glyphs. Forge your complexity. Become worthy of The Way you follow!”","HUUM!","The command was delivered without harshness, but absolute obedience followed anyway.","His people bowed their heads in silent acknowledgment, then returned to their meditative states with renewed purpose.","The air around them began to shimmer as Mana flowed through them in patterns that grew more complex by the moment.","Noah watched them for a long moment, satisfaction flickering through his consciousness.","They were growing. Slowly, yes.","Far slower than he had grown, because they lacked his particular combinations of cheat codes and Principles and Everythings that had been consumed. But they were growing nonetheless, and that mattered.","Because he was growing his Civilization, and he could not be the only one strong.","A presence materialized beside him while he was lost in thought.","Khor.","The Inevitability who carried too many secrets stood next to him, her expression holding something Noah rarely saw from her.","Seriousness.","Her eyes, which usually held amusement or calculation, now focused on him with intensity.","“Are you trying to entice me into your Way of Existence, Outsider?”","The question was delivered without accusation, but it carried weight nonetheless.","Noah smiled at that as he shook his head.","“No,” he said simply, then elaborated because Khor deserved more than monosyllabic dismissal. “You used to be someone of the higher Scale of Existence. You know your Way. You’ve walked it for so long that it’s become inseparable from what you are. Trying to shift you onto my path would be like trying to redirect a river that’s been flowing in the same direction since before directions were invented.”","He paused, his gaze meeting hers steadily.","“You should stick to your Way. Hunger, however broken it might be now... it’s yours. And reclaiming it will make you far more powerful than anything I could offer. Well, maybe. My Way is turning out to be unfathomable so far. So, Maybe.”","...!","Maybe!","She loved to use this word, so he used it for her!","Khor studied him for a long moment, her expression cycling through emotions too subtle to name. Then, slowly, she nodded.","“I know, Outsider,” she said softly, looking out into the distance. “I know.”","She didn’t elaborate on what exactly she knew.","With Khor, it could have been a great deal of things.","They stood together in comfortable silence for a moment, two beings of impossible power simply existing side by side.","Then Noah patted her shoulder and turned away, his attention shifting toward another presence that called to him with different urgency.","Sigrid.","She stood near the edge of a forming Sacred Water pools, her form radiating pulses of Order.","Her white and dark hair shone with ordered brilliance alongside her eyes.","But right now, those eyes held uncertainty.","He appeared beside her.","“A lot of terrifying beings are going to be coming for you now.”","The statement was delivered with calm certainty, not meant to frighten but to prepare.","“You need to be as strong as possible,” Noah continued, his voice carrying gentle insistence rather than command. “Order has to be as strong as possible. What you represent...true Order, not the fragmented suffering thing that existed before, it cannot remain weak.”","WAA!","Sigrid nodded slowly, processing his words. Then, hesitantly, she spoke.","“Do you think...” she began, then paused, gathering courage to voice fears she’d been carrying. “Do you think my emergence had something to do with the fact that Order was Dead? Because my entire lineage... they had to give up their existence for the sake of my emergence. My parents, my grandparents, every ancestor going back to the beginning...all of them collapsed into nothingness so I could truly be born.”","Her voice grew smaller, barely heard above a whisper!","“My emergence was born from Death. Am I... am I just another Dead Existence, another part of THE Dead Order wearing the skin of something Living?”","BOOM!","A heavy question!","Noah reached out, his hand moving to stroke her hair with surprising gentleness.","“Nothing like that, and don’t worry about it too much,” he said, his tone holding certainty that allowed no argument. “Focus on what is ahead, because the current you and the future you is what matters the most. Whatever circumstances led to your birth, whatever sacrifices were made...they don’t define what you become. Only your choices do that.”","...!","His fingers continued their gentle motion through her hair, the action somehow grounding despite its simplicity.","“You are Living. You are Order. You are THE Living Order, even if you are not there yet. And you are going to become so powerful that the question of your origins will become irrelevant, okay?”","Sigrid looked up at him, her eyes shining brilliantly. Then, firmly, she nodded.","“Okay.”","The word was simple, but it carried conviction!","Noah smiled at that, satisfaction blooming in his chest. Then, his expression shifted into something more calculating as he made a decision.","“RUIN/EDEN,” he said, his voice carrying into spaces that normal speech couldn’t reach.","“Redirect the remaining Harvest from the Dead Existential Armors and Prime Dead Early Creatures. Much of it shall flow to THE Living Order.”","HUUM!"]},{"number":4348,"title":"Chapter 4348: Chapter 4347: WONDER III","paragraphs":["The command was delivered with casual finality, as if reshaping the flow of harvested power was no more complicated than adjusting a faucet.","WAA!","Immediately, RUINEDEN’s holographic form materialized before them, her appearance as pristine and calculated as always.","She performed a slight bow.","\"Acknowledged, Master,\" she said.","\"Initializing Harvest redirection protocols up until her Ceiling is reached to ensure no waste and storing the rest of the Harvest for future uses.\"","Prompts began cascading across Noah’s vision, each one carrying information about the transfer he’d just commanded.","|HARVEST REDISTRIBUTION INITIATED|","|Source: Residual existential essence from 47 Dead Existential Armors (Average Complexity 1000 Quadrillion)|","|Source: Residual existential essence from 23 Prime Dead Early Creatures (Average Complexity/Purity: 2-3 Quintillion)|","|Total Harvestable Value: Approaching 2 Quintillion Complexity and Purity.|","|Projected Final Values: 1.9 Quintillion Complexity, 1.9 Quintillion Purity|","|Warning: This represents an exponential leap that may lead to existential instability.|","RUINEDEN paused, then added with what might have been amusement.","|However, given that THE Living Order is, by definition, the embodiment of stable structure and organization, existential instability is statistically unlikely. Proceeding with full transfer right away.|","HUUM!","Noah gave a nod of affirmation, his expression calm despite the magnitude of what he was about to do.","The sky above the Early Veiled Shore suddenly blazed with verdant-gold light that seemed to pour from nowhere and everywhere simultaneously. The radiance coalesced into a river- no, a tsunami...of pure, concentrated Harvest flowing downward with the inevitability of gravity made manifest.","It crashed into Sigrid like a waterfall of compressed existence, and her form blazed with brilliance that made nearby observers shield their eyes (those who still needed eyes, anyway).","Her hair began flowing upward as if gravity had lost interest in her, and her eyes became luminous points of perfect Order!","And her power...","Her power bloomed upward like a flower that had been waiting eons to finally open.","Trillions became quadrillions.","And finally, settling at approximately 1.9 Quintillion in both Complexity and Purity, the transformation completed.","THE Living Order stood before Noah, her form radiating authority that made the Early Veiled Shore itself pulse with renewed structure. She looked the same physically- same hair, same delicate features, same appearance of someone too young to carry such power.","But everything else was gradually changing.","When she smiled at Noah, the expression carried certainty that would have made lesser beings weep with inadequacy.","\"Thank you,\" she said simply!","Noah smiled back.","\"Don’t thank me yet,\" he replied as he let her adjust to her new power. \"That’s just the beginning. You’ll need to be much stronger before we’re done.\"","But for now, this was enough.","For now, Order had teeth sharp enough to bite back Prime Dead Early Creatures at least!","While Sigrid continued to stabilize her newfound power, her form occasionally pulsing with light as she integrated the massive influx of Harvest, Noah’s attention shifted inward.","To the Principles that now defined his existence.","To the Cheating Architect that had promised to break everything claiming to be unbreakable.","\"RUIN/EDEN,\" he called out.","Her holographic form solidified before him instantly, her expression attentive.","\"How can I help, Master?\"","Noah’s smile took on qualities that would have terrified anyone who understood what it meant when he looked that satisfied.","\"We’re going to test the full capabilities of the Cheating Architect,\" he said, each word deliberate. \"Starting with Existence Code Injection. I want to implement a line of code that those closest to me in my emerging Civilization... will have their Mana approach Infinity.\"","BOOM!","RUINEDEN’s eyes widened fractionally with the delight of someone who’d been given permission to do something gloriously excessive.","\"An ambitious first test,\" she observed, her tone carrying approval. \"Rewriting fundamental resource limitations for an entire population. I love it.\"","Noah observed Ruination up and down as it seemed the more he continued to advance, the more her...vibrancy and personality seemed to come out. The grander she became!","Her expression shifted into calculation mode, and additional prompts began blooming across Noah’s vision.","|EXISTENCE CODE INJECTION - PREPARATION PHASE|","|Analyzing Request: Modification of Mana reservoir parameters for designated population subset|","|Current Population Count: 73,284 entities out of countless sextillions across Early Veiled Shore and The infiniverse are designated as \"closest to Master\"|","|Required Authority Level: Extreme. This modification touches fundamental energy economics of existence itself.|","Before Noah could respond, RUIN/EDEN continued, her voice taking on new tones.","\"Master, I should inform you of recent developments regarding the Mana Glyphs. Since the Principle of the Cheating Architect has matured from Seed status to full manifestation, I’ve been actively transforming all existing Mana Seed Glyphs of the Cheating Architect into Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect.\"","She gestured, and an illusory diagram materialized showing the transformation process...Seeds becoming full blooms, each one radiating exponentially more authority than their previous forms.","\"The new Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect hold unfathomably more authority than their Seed predecessors,\" she explained, her voice carrying pride at the achievement. \"Each fully matured Glyph have an equivalent cost of 10 Quadrillion Complexity and 10 Quadrillion Purity to your overall power. Of course, you simply pay the cost in Mana.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed with interest. That was... significant. Very significant!","\"Current count?\" he asked.","\"78 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect have been successfully forged and integrated into your existential architecture,\" RUINEDEN reported.","She paused, then added with calculating precision.","\"To accomplish the Existence Code Injection you’ve requested, maintaining a continuous line of code that rewrites Mana limitations for over seventy thousand entities, will require active utilization of 5 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect. They will operate continuously, burning through power to maintain the modification against existence’s natural tendency to reject such changes.\"","Her expression grew more serious.","\"Once activated, those 5 Glyphs will be dedicated solely to this task until you choose to deactivate the code. They won’t contribute to your personal power while so engaged. Are you certain you wish to proceed?\"","Noah didn’t hesitate.","\"Do it.\"","WAA!","The command was absolute, and RUINEDEN responded with immediate action.","Five of the 78 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect suddenly blazed with intensity that transcended normal luminosity!","They detached from Noah’s general existential architecture and repositioned themselves into a specific geometric formation...a pentagram of pure authority that began rotating with increasing speed.","|EXISTENCE CODE INJECTION - ACTIVE|","|Line of Code Being Written: \"For entities designated as Core Civilization members of Noah Osmont, Mana reservoir limitations approach boundlessness. Maximum capacity trends toward Infinity without ever quite reaching it, creating perpetual expansion of available power.\"|","|Integration Status: 0%... 15%... 47%... 83%... 99%...|","|WARNING: Existence is attempting to reject this modification. Natural laws are fighting back. Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect are overriding rejection protocols.|","|Integration Status: 100%|","|CODE SUCCESSFULLY INJECTED|","|Result: All designated entities now possess Mana reservoirs that expand continuously toward infinite capacity. They will...almost always never run out of Mana. They may never need to wait for regeneration. They have been granted a glimpse of what their Master experiences constantly.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4349,"title":"Chapter 4349: Chapter 4348: WONDER IV","paragraphs":["The effect was immediate and magisterial!","Across the Early Veiled Shore, every being who had been meditating, who had been arduously working to forge their own Mana Glyphs through effort and concentration and time, suddenly felt their existence buzz with unfamiliar sensation.","Power.","Not a trickle. Not a stream. A fucking ocean of it, flooding into them from sources they couldn’t identify, filling reservoirs they hadn’t known they possessed.","HUUM!","The Emperor Penguin, who had been struggling to maintain three Mana Glyphs simultaneously, suddenly felt the burden vanish. Its reserves exploded outward, allowing it to forge a fourth, then a fifth, then a sixth with speed that should have been impossible.","Kazuhiko, momentarily holding Erikson’s slipper with practiced ease, gasped as energy cascaded through him in waves that never ended. He began layering Mana Glyphs with complexity he’d only theorized about before, each one snapping into place with perfection that came from unlimited resources!","Adelaide, her snow-blue hair now radiating auroras of pure power, laughed with delight as she felt limitations she’d always accepted as fundamental simply... cease to exist. She could create. She could destroy. She could reshape and rebuild without ever worrying about running dry!","Across the Shore, similar reactions rippled through Noah’s people.","Those who had been taking careful, measured steps in their cultivation suddenly found themselves sprinting.","Those who had accepted their limitations as permanent learned that their Master had decided otherwise!","For the first time, Noah’s people got to experience a semblance of what he always felt.","That infinite wellspring of power that never ran dry, never diminished, never left him wanting!","And even this semblance...this fraction of what Noah himself possessed, was far too grand for words.","Many processed it with shock.","Others simply sat in stunned silence, trying to process the magnitude of the gift they’d been given.","A few, like the Emperor Penguin, immediately began pushing their new limits with enthusiasm that bordered on reckless!","\"RAA!\"","Noah watched it all with satisfaction.","This...giving power to those who followed him, elevating his people beyond their limitations...was this what building a Civilization meant?","Not conquest. Not domination.","Uplift!","He watched the wonder unfold with majesty before he sighed.","Because he wasn’t done yet. Not even close.","\"RUINEDEN,\" he called out again, his voice carrying renewed purpose. \"Activate Parallel Processing Architectures. I want to run multiple probability streams simultaneously.\"","RUIN/EDEN’s form brightened with something that might have been excitement.","\"Yes, Master. This will require more resources. Parallel Processing at the level you’re requesting, running complete phantom processes that explore different choices and feed results back to you, requires 10 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect operating in perfect synchronization.\"","More prompts cascaded across Noah’s vision.","|PARALLEL PROCESSING ARCHITECTURES - INITIALIZATION|","|Designating 10 Mana Glyphs for probability stream management|","|Remaining Available Glyphs: 63 (78 total minus 5 for Existence Code Injection minus 10 for Parallel Processing)|","|Note: Each active probability stream consumes substantial resources. Recommend limiting simultaneous streams to 3-5 for optimal stability.|","\"I want to see three scenarios,\" Noah commanded, his tone carrying calculation that suggested he’d already been considering these options.","\"First: What happens if I send a body across to the other side of The Veil. Second: What happens if I pursue other Doorways to THE Loom. Third: What happens if I wait for Justiciars to appear and follow Schrodinger’s plan to track them back to their source.\"","RUINEDEN nodded, her expression growing more serious as she processed the request.","\"Running probability calculations now,\" she said. \"Be advised: These scenarios involve entities and forces far beyond current power scales. The outcomes may be... concerning.\"","HUUM!","Three illusory diagrams materialized in the air before Noah, each one showing a different branching path of possibility. They were ghostly, semi-transparent, depicting futures that hadn’t happened yet but could depending on his choices.","The first diagram pulsed with crimson light, and RUINEDEN’s voice took on grim tones as she detailed what it showed.","\"Scenario One: Crossing to the other side of The Veil.\"","The diagram showed Noah’s form stepping through that barrier between The Living and The Dead, passing from one fundamental state of existence to another.","And immediately, catastrophically, things went wrong.","\"The moment you cross,\" RUINEDEN explained, her voice clinical despite the horror of what she was describing, \"THE Dead Order senses your presence. Not just senses, she knows. Instantly and completely. Your existence becomes visible to her with perfect clarity because you’ve entered her domain, where her authority is absolute despite her limitations.\"","The diagram showed a massive figure...feminine, impossibly powerful, radiating authority that made THE Living Order look like a candle before a star...focusing attention on Noah’s infinitesimal form.","\"THE Dead Order, even in her current limited state, possesses power that operates on the next Scale of Existence,\" RUIN/EDEN continued. \"She forcefully controls all aspects of your being. Your resistance is irrelevant. Your power is insufficient. Your Principles are bypassed because she operates on a level where your defenses don’t exist yet.\"","The diagram shifted, showing Noah’s Early Veiled Shore being pulled across The Veil through connections he couldn’t sever.","\"She uses you as an anchor to drag The Infiniverse to the other side of The Veil,\" RUINEDEN said, her tone carrying something that might have been concern. \"The entire Early Veiled Shore, all beings within it, everything you’ve built...all of it crosses to where The Dead dwell.\"","The next part of the diagram made Noah’s expression harden.","\"Once she has The Infiniverse on her side, she immediately locates THE Living Order, Sigrid, and captures her. The fusion of THE Living and THE Dead Order begins immediately. The two halves of a fundamental force reunite, and in doing so, erase the limitations that kept THE Dead Order bound.\"","WAA!","The diagram showed Sigrid screaming as she was absorbed into that impossibly vast presence, two aspects of Order merging into something that transcended both.","\"The unified Order entity gains the ability to cross The Veil freely,\" RUIN/EDEN continued. \"She is no longer bound to either side. She is Order Absolute, operating without restriction.\"","But the horror didn’t stop there.","\"The unified Order then locates and devours Khor,\" RUINEDEN said, the diagram showing The First Hunger being consumed despite her power and mystery. \"She strips away Khor’s secrets, her knowledge, her connection to the higher Scale of Existence. All of it becomes fuel for Order’s expansion.\"","The diagram shifted again, showing THE Dead- no, the Unified Order...examining the workings of The Infiniverse with interest.","\"She discovers your Way of the Mana Architect,\" RUINEDEN said quietly. \"She understands what makes you unique. And instead of eliminating you as a threat... she repurposes you. You become a battery for her new Civilization. Your Infinite Mana, your Perpetual Harvest, your Cheating Architect...all of it locked into service of Order Absolute, generating power for her purposes while you exist as a conscious prisoner unable to act, unable to resist, unable to do anything except provide energy for eternity.\"","...!","The diagram faded, leaving only the implications hanging in the air like smoke after an explosion!"]},{"number":4350,"title":"Chapter 4350: Chapter 4349: ERROR I","paragraphs":["Noah’s expression had grown heavy, his eyes carrying darkness that suggested he was imagining exactly what that existence would feel like.","Conscious. Aware. Powerful. And completely, utterly helpless as his own strength was used to fuel purposes he didn’t choose.","It was a fate worse than death because death would at least be final.","His internal weavings ran in circles of calculation and fury.","So that’s what happens if he crossed The Veil prematurely!","THE Dead Order just... wins. Immediately and completely.","No fight or negotiation.","The thought was sobering.","He’d faced dangers before. He’d battled beings whose power exceeded his. He’d survived situations that should have been fatal through combination of luck, skill, and absurd cheating.","But this?","\"...\"","This was encountering a being who operated on a Scale of Existence where his tricks didn’t matter, where his power was irrelevant, where resistance itself was a concept that didn’t apply.","Noah took a breath, then spoke with calm.","\"Show me the other scenarios.\"","RUINEDEN nodded, and the second diagram pulsed with different energy...less immediately catastrophic but carrying its own breed of horror.","\"Scenario Two: Pursuing other Doorways to THE Loom.\"","The diagram showed Noah moving through the Transcendent Folds, seeking those mysterious passages that supposedly led to THE Loom where answers and power awaited.","\"Result: Nearly all Doorways you encounter are collapsed,\" RUINEDEN reported, her tone carrying clinical assessment. \"The collapse isn’t natural...they’ve been deliberately sealed. And attached to the walls near each collapsed Doorway, you find Inevitabilities fused to the structure like living locks.\"","The diagram showed grotesque images of Inevitabilities merged with reality itself, their forms twisted and repurposed into security systems.","\"Similar to the exterior wall where you encountered the Lodestone attached,\" RUINEDEN continued. \"These Inevitabilities have been sucked in entirely.\"","The diagram shifted, showing Noah moving from one collapsed Doorway to another, finding the same result repeatedly.","\"However,\" RUINEDEN added, and the diagram brightened slightly, \"probability calculations suggest that some Doorways may still exist in uncollapsed states. The locations are unknown. The number is uncertain. But statistical analysis indicates they haven’t all been sealed.\"","She paused.","\"Finding them would require extensive searching across multiple Folds. This path is possible but inefficient path.\"","Noah nodded slowly, processing that information. So THE Loom was being actively defended, sealed off, made inaccessible after his actions woth the Lodestone.","Which meant it was probably worth reaching.","\"And the third scenario?\"","The final diagram pulsed with colors that suggested imminent violence and complicated planning.","\"Scenario Three: Waiting for another Justiciar and following Schrodinger’s plan.\"","The diagram showed the Transcendent Quantum Folds, and within them, the emergence of another of those terrifying Living Existential Armors....a Justiciar performing its ritual of collapse.","\"Probability calculations indicate high likelihood of Justiciar manifestation in the Transcendent Quantum Folds within the next few hours,\" RUINEDEN reported. \"If you, Schrodinger, and Leonore Rureaux interrupt its ritual, attempting to capture or interrogate it...\"","The diagram showed Leonore Rureaux engaging the Justiciar, her power overwhelming it.","\"...A dozen more Justiciars manifest immediately,\" RUINEDEN continued, her tone darkening. \"They arrive in response to the first one’s distress signal. When they assess the situation and determine they cannot win against your combined forces...\"","The diagram showed all thirteen Justiciars simultaneously detonating, their forms erupting in explosions of anti-existence that would collapse the entire region.","\"...They self-destruct,\" RUINEDEN finished. \"Complete existential annihilation. No bodies to examine. No trail to follow. Just devastation and lost opportunity.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed. \"And if we don’t interrupt?\"","\"If you allow the Justiciar to complete its ritual,\" RUINEDEN said, and the diagram shifted to show a different outcome, \"it collapses the entire region of Transcendent Quantum Folds as intended. Countless Sextillions of Fold Dwellers and Living Existences perish. An entire section of existence becomes carved in white fires of purity. More fear spreads.\"","The diagram showed the Justiciar completing its work, then departing.","\"After completing the collapse, the Justiciar returns to wherever it came from,\" RUINEDEN continued. \"If you follow it without engaging, maintaining concealment and distance, probability suggests you could track it back to its source.\"","She paused, her expression growing grave.","\"However, this path requires allowing massive casualties to occur. An entire portion of the Fold will fall. The price of information is genocide.\"","...!","Noah stood in silence, processing all three scenarios.","Each one carried its own brand of horror.","None of them were good.","None of them were safe.","None of them promised outcomes he could accept!","But as Noah stood there, his eyes shining with tyranny brewing behind calculation, a smile began forming on his features.","It wasn’t a pleasant smile. It wasn’t the kind of expression that suggested he’d found a solution everyone would be happy with.","It was the smile of someone who had just decided that none of the options presented were acceptable, so he would create his own option instead.","\"Interesting scenarios. Very informative. But... I’m not going to do any of them. These scenarios assume I’m limited to the obvious choices.\"","His eyes blazed brighter.","\"But I have the Cheating Architect. I have Perpetual Harvest. I have access to the Earliest Folds and knowledge of how existence was structured before it learned to defend itself.\"","He gestured broadly, encompassing all the possibilities that existed beyond the three scenarios.","\"So instead of choosing between bad options, I’m going to create a fourth option.\"","HUUM!","He looked towards RUIN/EDEN.","\"Let’s cheat properly, why dont we?\"","RUINEDEN stared at him for a long moment.","Then, slowly, she smiled back...an expression that mirrored his own dangerous satisfaction!","He turned his attention back to the Early Veiled Shore, to his people who were still reveling in their newfound Mana abundance, to Sigrid who was consolidating her Quintillion-level power, to Khor who watched everything with knowing eyes.","The future was uncertain.","The dangers were real and immediate.","But he had never been particularly concerned with doing things the expected way.","Why start now?","A few possibilities bloomed in his mind as he moved on!","\"Let me see the current Cheat Code Repository.\"","RUIN/EDEN’s holographic form brightened immediately.","\"Yes, Master. The Repository has been working overtime since the Principle matured, automatically decompiling and cataloging every ability, technique, and Principle you’ve encountered.\"","She gestured, and a massive illusory interface materialized in the air before Noah...rows upon rows of entries, each one representing a different existential architecture that had been broken down into its component code.","\"Let me walk you through what we’ve acquired,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"Starting with the most recent additions from your encounter with the Prime Dead Early Creatures. For Tatiana, we already observed her usage of her Dream based Principle as I will jump onto a second one she didn’t truly get to utilize.\"","The interface shifted, highlighting specific entries that pulsed with dark radiance.","|CHEAT CODE REPOSITORY - CURRENT CATALOG|","|Entry #2: Principle of Absolute Consumption (Source: Commander Tatiana)|","|Classification: Harvesting/Predation Type|","|Core Function: Converts all defeated entities into pure fuel for exponential power growth|","|Decompilation Status: 73% Complete|","|Notes: Architecture is surprisingly elegant despite its brutality. The conversion efficiency scales based on the victim’s final emotional state- fear and despair provide higher yields. Fascinating and horrifying in equal measure.|","The interface shifted again, highlighting another entry.","|Entry #3: Principle of Endless Hunger (Source: Prime Dead Early Creature - Valerius the Insatiable)|","|Classification: Consumption/Amplification Type|","|Core Function: Transforms metabolic processes into existential expansion- literally grows stronger through eating|","|Decompilation Status: 81% Complete|","|Notes: Less sophisticated than Tatiana’s approach but more stable. This Principle doesn’t cannibalize the user’s sanity as payment for power. Trade-off is lower peak efficiency but sustainable operation. Practical. Trying to be an Inevitability?|","Another entry bloomed with crimson-gold light.","|Entry #4: Principle of Dominion Through Death (Source: Prime Dead Early Creature - Moros the Inevitable End)|","|Classification: Authority/Subjugation Type|","|Core Function: Establishes hierarchical control over anything that has experienced death or near-death|","|Decompilation Status: 67% Complete|","RUINEDEN’s expression grew more analytical.","The interface expanded further, revealing more entries.","|Entry #5: Principle of Exponential Decay (Source: Prime Dead Early Creature - Nyx the Withering)|","|Classification: Entropy/Time Manipulation Type|","|Core Function: Accelerates aging and degradation of targeted entities and concepts|","|Decompilation Status: 79% Complete|","|Entry #6: Principle of Parasitic Unity (Source: Prime Dead Early Creature - Typhon the Many-Formed)|","|Classification: Symbiosis/Absorption Type|","|Core Function: Creates false unity by forcibly merging separate existences into collective consciousness|","|Decompilation Status: 71% Complete|","Noah’s eyes tracked through the entries with interest. These were Principles that beings had spent eons developing, perfecting, building their entire existences around!"]},{"number":4351,"title":"Chapter 4351: Chapter 4350: ERROR II","paragraphs":["As he looked at them, the interface shifted dramatically, the entries suddenly blazing with verdant-gold light that made the previous ones look dim by comparison.","|Entry #7-15: Principle Collection (Source: Elyndra Viltharion, Scion of the First Harvest)|","|Classification: Agricultural/Growth/Authority Types|","|WARNING: Extreme Complexity Detected|","\"And now we get to the really impressive acquisition,\" RUINEDEN said, her voice carrying notes of genuine excitement mixed with professional frustration. \"The nine Principles operating in harmony within The First Farmer’s daughter.\"","She gestured, and the interface zoomed in on those entries, revealing complexity that made the previous ones look like children’s toys.","|Principle of Eternal Growth|","|Decompilation Status: 23% Complete|","|Estimated Time to Full Analysis: ???|","|Principle of Cyclical Harvest|","|Decompilation Status: 31% Complete|","|Estimated Time to Full Analysis: ???|","|Principle of Fertile Abundance|","|Decompilation Status: 28% Complete|","|Estimated Time to Full Analysis:???|","The list continued, each one showing frustratingly low completion percentages.","\"Elyndra’s Principles aren’t just powerful individually- they’re architected to function as a unified system. Each one supports and amplifies the others. It is...genuinely brilliant. It should be the handiwork of The First Farmer.\"","She pulled up a diagram showing how the nine Principles interconnected, creating a web of mutual support that resembled less a collection of separate abilities and more a single organism with nine major organs.","\"The problem,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"is that decompiling them requires understanding not just each Principle individually, but also how they interface with each other. It’s like trying to understand a symphony by analyzing each instrument separately...you miss the composition that makes the whole greater than the sum of parts.\"","Her expression grew more determined.","\"I’m working on it, Master. The Cheating Architect is throwing substantial processing power at breaking down these architectures. But this isn’t something I can rush without risking corruption of the final product. Unless you can...get close and personal with the Daughter of The First Farmer. When these are ready for you to download...\" she smiled, \"...you’ll be able to either augment your current Principles with their capabilities or combine them to create new Agent Architects that operate under The Cheating Architect.\"","HUUM!","Noah nodded slowly.","The Repository was working as intended!","It was patient power accumulation. Not immediate, but inevitable.","The Cheating Architect was essentially telling him that every being he met, every Principle he observed, would eventually become part of his arsenal. Not through theft or consumption, but through analysis and replication.","\"Keep working on them,\" he said finally, his tone carrying approval.","Noah’s attention shifted, moving to the next capability he wanted to test.","\"What about Debug Mode?\" he asked, his voice carrying curiosity. \"Have we encountered any errors in existence that we can exploit?\"","RUINEDEN’s expression brightened once more.","\"Debug Mode is... interesting,\" she said carefully. \"It requires existence to malfunction in detectable ways before we can exploit those malfunctions. So far, we haven’t observed any significant errors in the fabric of reality around us.\"","She paused.","\"The Dead are functioning as intended- horrifyingly, but without technical errors. The Living Existences we’ve encountered operate within normal parameters. Even the chaos of the Wandering Territories isn’t actually erroneous...it’s just chaotic by design.\"","Her expression grew more thoughtful.","\"The Living or Dead Existential Armors might potentially be a source of exploitable errors,\" she continued, her tone speculative.","She made a note in the air, her gestures creating persistent text that hung like promises.","\"I’ll monitor for anomalies and alert you immediately if anything significant appears,\" she said. \"Debug Mode is incredibly powerful when applicable, but it requires the right circumstances.\"","\"However,\" she said, drawing out the word with emphasis that made it clear something important was coming, \"there is one possible error I’ve detected. Actually, it’s less ’possible’ and more ’definitely present and significantly impacting your development.’\"","Noah’s eyes sharpened. \"Where?\"","RUINEDEN’s smile took on ironic qualities.","\"Within your own existence, Master. Which is actually perfect timing, because I can better explain it if we jump onto the feature of the Development Console as well. Shall we?\"","...!","Noah felt his interest spike. An error in his own existence?","\"Utilize the feature of Development Console,\" he commanded.","WAA!","The response was spectacular.","The space around Noah transformed. The golden sands beneath his feet shifted, becoming a platform of blue-gold energy that pulsed with analytical authority.","RUINEDEN’s holographic form expanded, becoming more detailed, more present, as if she was drawing additional processing power from the activated Console.","\"Development Console is now active,\" she announced, her voice carrying satisfaction at finally being able to demonstrate this capability properly. \"Accessing your existential parameters now.\"","An illusory diagram materialized in the air before Noah...a perfect three-dimensional representation of himself, every detail rendered with impossible precision.","It wasn’t just his physical form.","The diagram showed layers upon layers of existential architecture...his Mana Glyphs arranged in geometric perfection, his Principles glowing like internal suns, his Early Veiled Shore existing as a pocket dimension attached to his core being, his consciousness branching across multiple bodies simultaneously.","It was beautiful!","Text began appearing around the diagram, displaying his current parameters with clinical precision.","|DEVELOPMENT CONSOLE - EXISTENTIAL PARAMETERS|","|NAME: Noah Osmont|","|CLASSIFICATION: The Early Creature (Authenticity: 127% - Exceeds baseline parameters)|","|COMPLEXITY: (3.89 Quintillion)|","|PURITY: (3.89 Quintillion)|","|ACTIVE MANA GLYPHS OF THE CHEATING ARCHITECT: 78 Total|","|—Dedicated to Existence Code Injection: 5|","|—Dedicated to Parallel Processing: 10|","|—Available for General Use: 63|","|—Per-Glyph Contribution: 10 Quadrillion Complexity, 10 Quadrillion Purity|","|PRINCIPLES:|","|—Perpetual Harvest (Maturity: Complete)|","|—Cheating Architect (Maturity: Complete)|","|—Additional Principle Signatures Detected: [DATA INTEGRATING]|","|EARLY VEILED SHORE STATUS: Operational, Expanding|","Countless details filled up the screen!","Noah studied the readout calmly.","The numbers were impressive...nearly 4 Quintillion in both major parameters, with substantial additional power from the Mana Glyphs.","He’d come a long way from the Fold Dweller who had started this journey in the Nullvein Gravewake Folds fighting Little Bobby within a Wheel of Existence just...oh, was it days ago?","\"Hmm...\" He wanted to be content at such an accomplishment, but there was still much to be done!","And RUINEDEN continued.","\"Now, let’s look at the more interesting architectural components,\" she said, and the diagram zoomed inward, focusing on specific areas of Noah’s existence.","The view shifted to show structures that resembled impossible castles made of compressed authority and crystallized will.","|RESPLENDENT CITADELS OF THE MANA ARCHITECT|","|Current Stage: Fourth (Advancing toward Fifth)|","|Function: Foundational architecture supporting Way of Existence|","|Status: Shining brightly as beacons of cultivated power|","|Note: Advancement to Fifth Stage progressing naturally through accumulated effort and understanding|","\"Your Citadels are advancing beautifully, not much can be said about them currently.\" RUINEDEN observed.","The diagram shifted again, this time focusing on something that made Noah’s attention sharpen immediately.","His Heart.","Not a mere physical heart...that mundane organ that pumped blood through flesh. This was his Heart of an Early Creature, the core component that defined what he was becoming, the architectural centerpiece that separated genuine Early Creatures from beings merely pretending at that scale of power!","The diagram showed it in exquisite detail.","Four components were complete, each one blazing with different aspects of authority:","|HEART OF AN EARLY CREATURE - CURRENT STATUS|","|Component 1: Ventryalis - The Primal Root Atrium of Echoes (COMPLETE)|","|Component 2: Oruvian Shardveil – The Arterial Convergence Core (COMPLETE)|","|Component 3: Myokelum Primus – The Living Pump of Trembling Flow (COMPLETE)|","|Component 4: Ascendran Nodule - The Living Principle of Complexity (COMPLETE)|","And forming now, blazing with light that suggested imminent completion:","|Component 5: Seraphilic Veinlace - The Living Principle of Purity (FORMING - 34% Complete)|","But there was a sixth component, one that should have been forming but wasn’t. A ghostly outline in the diagram, present but inactive, waiting for conditions that hadn’t been met yet!","|Component 6: Incarnaut Sanctis - The Early Chamber of Blood (DORMANT - 0% Complete - ERROR DETECTED)|","RUINEDEN’s expression grew serious as she gestured to highlight that sixth component.","\"This is where we have a problem,\" she said.","\"Actually, calling it a ’problem’ is underselling it. This is a fundamental architectural error in your development that’s limiting your progression in ways you haven’t noticed yet.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":4352,"title":"Chapter 4352: Chapter 4351: Early Creature Genesis! I","paragraphs":["RUIN/EDEN pulled up additional data, showing how the Heart was supposed to function versus how it was currently operating.","\"The Heart of an Early Creature is designed to form in stages,\" she explained, her voice taking on lecturing qualities. \"Each component builds upon the previous ones, creating a cascade of increasing complexity and power. Normally, this process is linear...you complete one part before the next begins forming.\"","The diagram showed a timeline, each component lighting up in sequence.","\"But here’s the issue,\" RUINEDEN continued, her expression growing more animated as she warmed to her explanation. \"You’re not a normal Early Creature. You’re more than genuine...your authenticity rating is 127% of baseline. You’ve integrated Principles that Early Creatures of your developmental stage shouldn’t possess. You’ve architected your existence using methodologies that didn’t exist in the Age of Early Creatures. In the Earliest Folds.\"","She gestured broadly to encompass all of Noah’s impossible achievements.","\"The normal parameters don’t apply to you anymore,\" she said flatly. \"The Age of Early Creatures, with its rules about sequential Heart formation, with its assumptions about cultivation speed and power ceilings...none of it fits your current reality. You’ve outgrown the template.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed as he processed that information.","The Heart was forming according to outdated rules!","Rules that were appropriate for Early Creatures developing naturally in their proper era!","\"The specific error,\" RUINEDEN continued, pulling up diagnostic text that highlighted the problem in sharp relief, \"is that the Incarnaut Sanctis, the sixth and final component of your Heart, is locked in dormant state until the Seraphilic Veinlace completes. This is standard procedure for normal Early Creatures, because forming two Heart components simultaneously would strain their existential architecture beyond tolerance.\"","She paused.","\"But you’re not operating under normal strain tolerance, are you? Your Perpetual Harvest feeds you continuous power. Your Cheating Architect rewrites limitations as they appear. Your Resplendent Citadels and Mana Glyphs provide foundational support that most beings can’t imagine possessing. You could handle simultaneous formation without breaking. The system just doesn’t know that because it’s operating on assumptions that stopped being accurate about you several power scales ago.\"","...!","Noah felt understanding crystallize in his consciousness.","It was like discovering his computer had been artificially limiting its processing speed because some ancient setting assumed it was running on hardware from decades past!","The limitation wasn’t real...it was just a relic of outdated parameters that nobody had thought to update.","He reached inward with his consciousness, extending awareness toward his Heart with precision that came from intimate familiarity with his own existence.","And he felt it.","The Seraphilic Veinlace, forming with deliberate care, its structure already magnificent despite being only partially complete.","Veins of pure authority spreading through his existential architecture like roots seeking nourishment, like branches reaching toward light.","And beyond it, waiting in dormancy, the Incarnaut Sanctis.","The Early Chamber of Blood.","Even in its dormant state, Noah could sense its potential. This wasn’t just another component...this was the culmination, the final piece that would complete the Heart and elevate him to a level of Early Creature unlike any other.","But it was locked. Waiting. Unnecessary limitation imposed by rules that had stopped applying to him the moment he’d started accumulating Principles and Glyphs at rates that existence itself found offensive.","Well.","That was an error!","And Debug Mode existed specifically to exploit errors.","Noah’s expression shifted.","\"Use Debug Mode,\" he commanded, his voice carrying tyrannical certainty. \"Rectify the error. I want both the Seraphilic Veinlace and Incarnaut Sanctis forming simultaneously.\"","RUINEDEN’s eyes lit up with brilliance!","\"Yes, Master,\" she said. \"Initiating Debug Mode protocols.\"","|DEBUG MODE ACTIVATED|","|Error Identified: Sequential Heart Formation Protocol limiting development below user capacity|","|Error Classification: LEGACY LIMITATION - Outdated parameter application|","|Recommended Fix: Override sequential protocols, enable parallel formation|","|Resource Requirement: 3 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect|","Three of Noah’s available Glyphs suddenly blazed with intensity that transcended their normal operation.","They detached from his general existential architecture and repositioned themselves around the diagram of his Heart, forming a triangle of pure corrective authority.","|APPLYING FIX...|","|Overriding: Age of Early Creatures formation protocols|","|Rewriting: Heart development parameters|","|Enabling: Simultaneous multi-component formation|","|Status: 0%... 23%... 61%... 89%... 100%|","|FIX SUCCESSFULLY APPLIED|","|Result: Incarnaut Sanctis - The Early Chamber of Blood will now begin forming simultaneously with Seraphilic Veinlace. Both components will progress in parallel, feeding into and supporting each other’s development.|","HUUM","Glory bloomed.","Noah’s Heart, that impossible organ...suddenly erupted with light that made nearby reality pulse!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","It beat like a drum that had been waiting eons to finally be played at full volume.","Each pulse sent waves of power through Noah’s existence, through his Early Veiled Shore, through the connections that bound him to his people and his Way.","Noah closed his eyes, his consciousness diving inward to observe the change.","And there, in the spaces where his existence was most fundamental, he felt it.","The Seraphilic Veinlace, already forming, suddenly blazed brighter as if it had been given permission to stop holding back. Its structure accelerated, veins of purity spreading faster, reaching further, establishing connections that would carry refined power through every aspect of his being.","And beside it, awakening from dormancy like something vast opening ancient eyes, the Incarnaut Sanctis began to form.","The Early Chamber of Blood!","Its structure was magnificent even in nascent state...a space that would exist within yet beyond his physical form, a chamber where the fundamental essence of what he was could be distilled, refined, elevated to heights that normal biology couldn’t contain.","They formed together now, in parallel, in harmony, each one supporting the other’s development through connections that were being architected in real-time.","It was beautiful in ways that transcended aesthetic appreciation!","This was his existence becoming more itself, more complete, more capable of containing the power he was accumulating at rates that defied reasonable cultivation speeds.","RUIN/EDEN’s voice cut through his internal observation, carrying information that made the moment even more significant.","|The Principle of Perpetual Harvest is responding to Heart formation|","|Labor’s Paradise Protocol Activated|","|Classification: Effort supercharge detected. The formation of Heart components is being recognized as tremendous Labor worthy of maximum amplification.|","Her holographic form displayed new data with visible excitement.","The diagram showed streams of verdant-gold light flowing from across Noah’s domain, from his people who were forging their Glyphs, from the Existential Taxation he’d implemented, from every source of accumulated Harvest.","Effort.","Glorious, magisterial effort!","All of it redirecting, funneling, pouring into the forming Seraphilic Veinlace and Incarnaut Sanctis like tributaries feeding into mighty rivers.","\"The formation speed is being exponentially accelerated,\" RUINEDEN continued, her voice carrying notes of calculation happening at speeds that blurred into single statements. \"What should have taken days for each component to complete individually... you’re going to finish both in a fraction of that time.\"","...!","Noah opened his eyes, satisfaction blooming in his chest!","His Heart was completing itself properly now. Not limited by outdated rules, not held back by assumptions that had stopped applying to him, not forced to follow a path meant for beings who couldn’t handle what he could handle.","It was forming according to what he actually was rather than what some ancient protocol thought he should be!","It was perfect.","But as he observed the forming components with senses that could perceive their developing structure in exquisite detail, an idea crystallized in his consciousness.","An idea bloomed.","He looked at the Seraphilic Veinlace, the Living Principle of Purity, watching as its veins of authority spread through his existence like sacred circulatory systems.","And he looked at the Incarnaut Sanctis, the Early Chamber of Blood, observing as its chamber-structure began taking shape, creating space that would exist as both inside and outside him simultaneously.","They were forming separately. Parallel, yes, but distinct. Two components that would be part of a unified whole but which remained architecturally independent.","But what if they weren’t?","What if, instead of two separate components that merely coexisted, they were integrated? What if the veins of the Seraphilic Veinlace didn’t just exist near the Incarnaut Sanctis, but led directly into it?","What if the Chamber wasn’t just a space within his existence, but the culmination point where all the purified essence from the Veinlace flowed and concentrated and achieved transcendence?"]},{"number":4353,"title":"Chapter 4353: Chapter 4352: Early Creature Genesis! II","paragraphs":["The architectural beauty of it made him smile.","\"RUIN/EDEN,\" he called out!","\"Yes, Master?\"","Noah’s smile deepened, taking on tyrannical qualities.","\"Combine the aspects and potential boons of the two forming segments of the Heart,\" he commanded, each word deliberate and weighted with will that could reshape existence.","\"The aorta of the Seraphilic Veinlace will lead directly into the Incarnaut Sanctis. They won’t just form simultaneously...they’ll form as unified architecture. One system, not two components.\"","...!","RUIN/EDEN nodded silently!","\"Yes, Master. The Cheating Architect exists specifically to rewrite architectural rules that claim to be absolute. And if we use enough Mana Glyphs to support the integration...\"","Her voice took on calculating qualities.","\"It would require 7 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect operating continuously to manage the integration, and...\"","Her smile grew wider.","\"The resulting Heart component wouldn’t be two pieces working together. It would be a single unified system that combines the functions of both into something that transcends either. You’d be creating a Heart architecture that no Early Creature in history has ever possessed. Not even THE Creature. This...is your own.\"","HUUM!","Noah’s expression remained calm.","\"Do it.\"","|EXISTENTIAL ARCHITECTURE INTEGRATION INITIATED|","|Resource Allocation: 7 Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect|","|Task: Forcible integration of Seraphilic Veinlace and Incarnaut Sanctis mid-formation|","|Warning: This will fundamentally alter standard Heart architecture|","|Proceeding with tyrannical confidence...|","The seven Glyphs blazed with authority that made space around Noah pulse with recognition of power being exercised.","They positioned themselves around the forming Heart components, creating a heptagon of pure will that would force integration that existence insisted was impossible.","And slowly, with precision that suggested the Cheating Architect knew exactly what it was doing despite the impossibility of the task, the two forming components began to merge.","Not absorbing into each other. Not consuming one another.","Integrating.","The veins of the Seraphilic Veinlace extended, reaching toward the forming Chamber of the Incarnaut Sanctis. Where they touched the Chamber’s structure, they didn’t stop...they continued inward, becoming part of the Chamber itself, establishing connections that would allow purified essence to flow directly from one component into the other.","The Chamber accepted these connections, its architecture adapting to incorporate them as if it had been designed this way from the beginning.","Walls that had been forming independently suddenly sprouted internal structures...channels, conduits, networks that would receive and concentrate the essence the Veinlace delivered.","It was like watching two incomplete puzzles realize they were actually parts of the same image, their pieces fitting together with satisfying precision.","|INTEGRATION STATUS: 23%... 47%... 68%... 91%...|","|WARNING: Existential strain detected. Compensating with Mana Glyph authority.|","|INTEGRATION STATUS: 100%|","|INTEGRATION SUCCESSFUL|","|Result: Seraphilic Veinlace and Incarnaut Sanctis now form unified system. The Veinlace purifies essence and channels it directly into the Chamber, where it concentrates and achieves transcendent states. This is no longer two components.|","RUINEDEN’s holographic form was practically glowing with satisfaction at successful completion of something that should have been impossible.","|Due to the integration, because the Chamber is now directly connected to the Veinlace’s purification processes... the Incarnaut Sanctis can be manifested outwardly even before completion.|","...!","Noah’s attention sharpened immediately.","\"Explain.\"","RUINEDEN gestured, and the diagram shifted to show the Early Veiled Shore, with a new illusory structure pulsing on its golden sands.","\"The Early Chamber of Blood can exist partially within you and partially as external space,\" she explained. \"Normally, it wouldn’t be accessible until the entire Heart completed formation. But because you’ve integrated it with the Veinlace, because it’s now receiving continuous flow of purified essence from an active component... it can be established in your Shore right now.\"","Her expression grew more animated.","\"You can create the physical manifestation of the Incarnaut Sanctis in your Early Veiled Shore,\" she said, each word carrying weight of significant revelation. \"And once established, entities can enter it. Not just to visit, but to undergo transformation.\"","She pulled up specifications that made Noah’s eyes pulse with glorious tyranny!","|INCARNAUT SANCTIS - EXTERNAL MANIFESTATION CAPABILITIES|","|Function: Early Creature Genesis|","|Process: Entities who enter the Chamber undergo fundamental existential restructuring. Their potential is awakened and elevated, their architecture rebuilt according to Mana-based templates, their very nature transformed into new types of Mana-Based Early Creatures. Currently a maximum of 9 slots are possible.|","|Warning: This process is irreversible. Entities who undergo Genesis will emerge fundamentally changed. Their power will increase dramatically|","|Recommendation: Select candidates carefully. This could be deemed...The Glorious Evolution.|","HUUM!","The Glorious Evolution!","Noah stood in silence for a long moment.","He could froge new Early Creatures.","Not through consumption or transformation of existing ones, but through actual genesis...taking beings of sufficient potential and elevating them to a tier of existence that current reality insisted was closed, finished, ended with the Earliest Folds!","Nine.","Nine beings could enter his Heart’s external manifestation and emerge as something existence hadn’t seen in eons!","The implications were heavy.","The possibilities were endless.","In his Civilization, he would not be the only Early Creature!","The temptation to immediately start selecting candidates made his thoughts race!","\"Establish the Chamber,\" he commanded, his voice carrying tyrannical certainty. \"Manifest the Incarnaut Sanctis in my Early Veiled Shore. I want to see... what genesis looks like.\"","RUINEDEN bowed.","\"It will be my pleasure, Master.\"","On the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, reality began to pulse with recognition of something new and impossible taking shape.","The Chamber was coming.","And with it, the genesis of new Early Creatures would begin!","The Incarnaut Sanctis was taking shape!","It was magnificent.","It was terrifying.","It was...","...going to have to wait.","Because in the distant Wandering Territories, his other body was experiencing something that demanded immediate attention.","Noah’s consciousness shifted focus, gazing toward that distant point where he’d been following Elyndra Viltharion through forests that existed in states of perpetual becoming.","They had arrived.","The Inner Garden Sanctum.","The transition had been subtle but absolute...one moment they’d been flying through the Forest of Perpetual Seasons, surrounded by trees that rearranged themselves and time that flowed in contradictory directions, and the next, they’d crossed some invisible threshold that marked the boundary between protective chaos and cultivated order.","The Inner Sanctum spread out before them in glory that defied casual observation.","It was...vast.","Vast in ways that transcended normal spatial measurements!","The Sanctum existed as its own pocket of reality, a space that had been carved from the Wandering Territories and shaped according to principles of growth and cultivation.","Noah’s enhanced perception swept across the landscape, cataloging details with speed.","Fields.","Endless fields, each one the size of Minor Folds, stretching toward horizons. But these weren’t fields growing normal crops...these were cultivation plots for concepts themselves, for Seeds of Principles that were being nurtured toward maturity!"]},{"number":4354,"title":"Chapter 4354: Chapter 4353: The First Farmer! I","paragraphs":["In one field, Noah saw rows of plants that looked like crystallized time, each one representing a different temporal concept being grown from seed to full expression.","Elsewhere, massive trees grew downward from invisible ceilings, their roots reaching toward sky while their branches burrowed into earth, defying orientation itself.","Elsewhere, Fields cultivating...Everythings that looked like waves of stellar brilliance!","Between them, rivers of liquid authority flowed!","And tending these impossible fields were Fold Dwellers and Living Existences whose power made Noah’s earlier assessments of strength seem quaint.","His eyes tracked across them to see names and measurements floating above their heads like status displays.","|Mateus of the Golden Harvest|","|Complexity: 1.2 Quadrillion|","|Purity: 1.1 Quadrillion|","Approximately 1 Quadrillion. A being whose power exceeded most Dukes!","And nearby, tending to a field of what looked like solidified destiny:","|Thera, Keeper of the Eternal Bloom|","|Complexity: 127 Quadrillion|","|Purity: 119 Quadrillion|","Over 100 Quadrillion. A single entity whose casual existence generated more power than some entire Folds could muster.","His gaze continued scanning, finding more beings scattered across the fields like farmers tending crops that could reshape reality.","1.5 Quintillion.","3 Quintillion.","4 Quintillion!","And continuing on...","|Ancient Torvan, the First Tiller|","|Complexity: 6,103,847,293,847,102|","|Purity: 5,847,293,103,847,293|","Six Quintillion.","SIX.","Noah’s expression remained calm, but these were wonders he was seeing!","This place wasn’t merely a sanctuary!","The beings working these fields could each individually destroy current-era Folds without particular effort. Together, they represented power that could challenge... well, many things that claimed to be unchallengeable.","And they were growing Principles like crops.","|Master, I’m recording everything. Every cultivation technique these beings are using, every field arrangement, every Seed type being nurtured...all of it is being cataloged for analysis.|","Her holographic form appeared briefly in his peripheral vision, visible only to him.","|This data alone is worth the entire journey.|","Noah gave the mental equivalent of a nod, his attention still tracking across the impossible landscape.","The fields stretched endlessly...or at least, they stretched far enough that weaker perceptions couldn’t find their boundaries.","This space alone was equivalent to an entire Transcendent Fold, a pocket dimension that had been carved from the Wandering Territories and shaped into paradise for beings who understood growth as fundamental authority.","Elyndra led them forward.","As they passed through the fields, the native beings, those impossibly powerful Fold Dwellers and Living Existences who had found sanctuary here, turned to acknowledge her presence.","Not with fear. Not with submission.","With respect that transcended hierarchy.","They bowed their heads slightly, their expressions carrying genuine warmth mixed with reverence.","She smiled back at each one, her gestures conveying familiarity that suggested she knew them all personally, had probably worked these fields beside them at various points.","It was the kind of relationship that only developed through shared labor toward common purpose.","They continued deeper into the Sanctum, passing fields that grew increasingly complex in their cultivation...Seeds of higher-order Principles that pulsed with authority approaching what Tatiana had possesed.","And then, in the distance, Noah saw it.","A single cultivation plot surrounded by golden radiance that made everything else in the Sanctum look dim by comparison.","At its center stood a figure, backlit by that impossible light, making clear identification difficult. But even from this distance, Noah could sense something about the presence...weight that suggested accumulated wisdom, authority that had been refined through eons, power that...","...that felt wrong, somehow. Not threatening, but diminished. Like observing a star that should have blazed with fury but instead flickered with uncertainty.","Elyndra slowed as they approached the radiant field’s edge, her expression shifting into something more serious.","She turned to face Noah and his assembled companions...Sigrid standing close to him, Khor floating nearby with mysterious smile, Moiraine maintaining position with paradoxical authority humming, the Emperor Penguin and others forming constellation of power around their focal point.","\"From here on out,\" Elyndra said, her voice carrying finality that suggested this wasn’t negotiable, \"I have to take him forward to meet my Father alone.\"","Her blue eyes found Noah’s, holding his gaze with intensity that searched for objections.","Noah analyzed the situationand smiled.","His gaze shifted to Khor, who stood beside Sigrid with that expression suggesting she found all of this entertaining.","His people were powerful in their own right- Sigrid now possessed 1.9 Quintillion in power, and Khor...could stomp anyone should anything drastic happen!","They could handle themselves.","And honestly, if The First Farmer wanted to try something hostile, Noah possessed enough means to turn everything upside down.","He smiled calmly, his expression carrying confidence.","\"Walk around the Sanctuary of The First Farmer,\" he said to his companions, \"Pluck anything you’re allowed to pluck. Learn what you can learn. I’ll be fine.\"","They all nodded at his words.","Elyndra’s smile widened, genuine pleasure flickering across her features.","\"They’ll be perfectly safe,\" she assured them, then turned back toward Noah. \"Shall we?\"","Without waiting for further response, she moved forward, floating toward that golden-radiant field with grace.","Noah followed, his form rising to match her elevation.","As they flew deeper into the radiant space, separating from the others, Elyndra turned her head slightly toward him. Her expression had shifted into something more direct, more openly curious, as if the presence of others had been restraining her natural tendencies toward straightforwardness.","\"You know,\" she said, \"out of all existences I’ve encountered, and I’ve encountered many across these eons, you are the second person apart from my Father who has such a smell of growth and harvest.\"","She studied him with intensity that felt invasive without quite crossing into offense.","\"Just what Principle did you nurture?\" she asked, the question delivered with bluntness.","\"Because that scent... it’s not just similar to Father’s work. It’s almost identical, but different.\"","...!","Noah’s expression remained calm.","She knew the answer to her own question, and yet she was here playing around!","\"Perpetual Harvest,\" he said simply, offering truth without elaboration. \"A Principle of continuous accumulation and exponential return on effort invested.\"","Elyndra’s eyes widened fractionally!","\"Perpetual Harvest,\" she repeated softly, as if tasting the words.","\"Father...called it his greatest failure, the Seed that refused to bloom no matter what techniques he applied. And you... you actually succeeded in nurturing it?\"","Her gaze intensified, searching his features for deception or exaggeration and apparently finding none.","\"How did you manage what Father couldn’t?\"","Noah’s smile deepened slightly.","\"Different soil,\" he replied cryptically. \"Different methods. Different understanding of what the Seed actually needed to grow. Even failure is effort. Even with a failure, there is Harvest.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4355,"title":"Chapter 4355: Chapter 4354: The First Farmer! II","paragraphs":["It was answer that provided information while revealing nothing, the verbal equivalent of showing someone a closed door and describing its surface without opening it.","Elyndra stared at him for a long moment, her expression suggesting she was deciding whether to push for more details or accept the deflection gracefully.","Finally, she laughed with genuine amusement.","\"You’re infuriating to interrogate,\" she observed, \"Every answer creates more questions. I can see why Father wanted to meet you personally.\"","They descended together, approaching the figure at the center of the golden-radiant field.","Noah’s analytical capabilities were already activating, his enhanced perception beginning to break down and catalog what he was about to encounter.","The First Farmer.","The entity who had gazed upon THE Living Spirit...and likely other THE Living Existences!","The being who had created sanctuary in the Wandering Territories when nowhere else would accept Fold Dwellers.","The cultivator who had planted Seeds of Civilization and nurtured concepts into Principles.","Noah had high expectations!","This being was potentially one of the solutions to The Fallout...a force that could stand against The Dead, a mind that understood existence’s architecture at levels that current-era beings had forgotten, a power that had survived when so many others had collapsed.","He had been active in the same time as Khor in the Earliest Folds.","He had met THE Living Existences personally.","Surely, such a being would radiate authority that made normal measurement meaningless. Surely, his power would exceed simple quantification. Surely...","Noah’s eyes began to glow with blue light as his analytical capabilities fully engaged, breaking down the figure before him with precision that could measure power down to individual units of Complexity and Purity.","Beside him, Elyndra’s voice rang out with genuine respect and affection.","\"Father,\" she called out warmly. \"I’ve brought the guest you’ve been expecting.\"","The figure turned.","And Noah’s eyes widened as his analytical vision completed its assessment.","\"What the fuck?\"","The curse escaped before he could stop it, shock overriding his normal composure.","Because the figure who turned to face them was...","The First Farmer.","Noah recognized the features from their brief meeting in the Earliest Folds...the same bone structure, the same general appearance, the same fundamental presence that suggested agricultural authority refined through impossible time.","But everything else was wrong.","The being who stood before them now was old.","Not elderly. Not aged with dignity.","Old in ways that suggested imminent collapse.","His skin hung loose on bones that seemed too fragile to support even his minimal weight. His hair, which had been vibrant in the Earliest Folds, now appeared thin and colorless, each strand looking ready to fall out from sheer exhaustion.","His eyes, which had held depths of wisdom and determination, now carried shadows that spoke of pain and weariness that transcended normal suffering.","He was adorned in a green-gold robe that looked too heavy for his frame, the fabric somehow emphasizing his frailty rather than concealing it.","And worst of all, he leaned heavily on a walking stick...not as affectation or symbol, but as genuine necessity.","His hands trembled where they gripped the wood, his entire posture suggesting that without that support, he would simply collapse.","Noah’s analytical vision completed its assessment, and text appeared above the First Farmer’s head with information that made his expression sour dramatically.","|Viltharion, The First Farmer|","|The One Who Gazed Upon THE Living Existences|","|The Cultivator of Sanctuary|","|Complexity: 0.000001 Quintillion|","|Purity: 0.000001 Quintillion|","Quintillion.","The measurement was technically correct...he was following a Way that operated on that Scale of Existence.","But those decimals...","0.000001 Quintillion was... 1 Trillion.","One trillion in both Complexity and Purity.","That was a tenth the power of a measly Duke!","That was less than many Living Existences possessed. That was... pathetic, for someone who should have been a cornerstone of resistance against The Fallout!","Noah’s expression rapidly soured, his mind racing through implications.","This was the strength of the powerful First Farmer?","This diminished, frail, barely-functional being was supposed to be a core force for survival and prevention of The Fallout?","What the fuck happened?!","His thoughts were heavy enough that some of them clearly showed on his face, because the First Farmer actually laughed...a wheezing, painful sound that suggested even amusement cost him dearly.","\"I will have to apologize for disappointing you,\" the First Farmer said, his voice carrying kindness despite the weakness.","\"I imagine you had certain... expectations about what you would find here. About who I would be. About what kind of help I could provide.\"","He moved slowly, painfully, each step requiring visible effort as he approached them with the walking stick bearing most of his weight.","\"But despite my current... diminished state,\" he continued, \"I do remember you. Countless eons ago, I gave you a discarded Seed. My first failure. The concept I could never make bloom no matter what techniques I employed.","HUUM!","He stopped a few feet from Noah, studying him with intensity that made the moment feel significant.","\"And eons later...\" the First Farmer’s voice grew softer, almost wondering, \"...is that really what I sense in you? Did you allow Perpetual Harvest to bloom?\"","...!","The first thing he asked about was Perpetual Harvest.","The Principle that Noah had built significant portions of his existence around, that fed his continuous growth, that made effort compound into exponential returns.","The Failed Seed that had become one of the cornerstones of his Way.","Noah looked toward this grand being calmly, his expression giving nothing away.","But before he could formulate answer, RUINEDEN’s voice emerged in his consciousness.","|Master, I’m detecting significant anomalies in this situation.|","Her holographic form appeared in his peripheral vision, visible only to him, her expression carrying concern mixed with rapid calculation.","|The First Farmer’s current state doesn’t match historical records or reasonable power scaling. A being who created this entire Sanctuary, who cultivated entities to Quintillion-level power, who stood alongside beings like Khor in the Earliest Folds...such an entity shouldn’t be reduced to mere trillions through normal cultivation decline.|","She pulled up data, showing comparisons and projections.","|This level of diminishment suggests targeted assault. Not just defeat, but fundamental destruction of power base. Similar to what happened to Khor when THE Living Paradox collapsed her existence, except... this seems even more complete. More thorough.|","Her expression grew grimmer.","|We hadn’t accounted for it in our calculations, Master, but I’m now considering: If THE Living Paradox targeted Khor, if other THE Living Existences were actively eliminating potential threats before The Fallout... how many other powerful beings from the Earliest Folds suffered similar fates?|","She gestured, creating illusory diagrams showing possible scenarios.","|The First Farmer may have been on someone’s radar.|","Her voice took on darker tones.","|We came here hoping for solutions, for powerful allies, for knowledge that could help prevent The Fallout. Instead, we’re finding evidence that those who might have helped were systematically eliminated long before the current crisis began.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as it felt like existence was getting tighter!","Like a huge net was closing in!","There would be no grand help from the First Farmer. No cavalry arriving to save the day. No ancient power revealing itself at the critical moment to shift the balance.","As always, he would have to come up with solutions alone.","\"...\"","But this trip shouldn’t be for naught. He could at least gather information, understand how things had deteriorated to this point, learn what had happened to bring a being of such magnitude down to pathetic weakness.","Noah sighed, the sound carrying weight of disappointment mingled with resignation.","Finally, he nodded, raising his hand in gesture that felt both casual and ceremonial.","And from his palm, light began to emerge.","Not just any light...this was the pristine radiance of Perpetual Harvest itself, green-gold brilliance that sang of continuous growth and exponential accumulation, of effort compounding into power that could reshape existence through sheer persistence.","It blazed between them like proof of impossible achievement, like vindication of potential that others had dismissed as failure.","The First Farmer trembled at its sight.","His entire frail form shook with emotion, his eyes widening with wonder mixed with something that might have been joy or might have been grief or might have been both simultaneously!","He looked like a man dying of thirst who had just been shown water...someone who had wanted to see this one thing more than anything else in existence, and now, finally, impossibly, he was witnessing it.","\"It’s real,\" he whispered, his voice breaking with emotion. \"It actually bloomed. My greatest failure... became someone else’s success. The Seed I discarded... found soil that could nourish it.\"","...!","Oh!","His legs gave out.","Elyndra moved immediately, her grace transforming into urgency as she caught her father before he could collapse entirely."]},{"number":4356,"title":"Chapter 4356: Chapter 4355: The First Farmer! III","paragraphs":["She helped him sit on the brown-gold sand at the edge of the cultivation field, her movements carrying practiced ease that suggested this wasn’t the first time she’d performed this action.","She waved her hands, and mats materialized from nowhere...simple, elegant things woven from what looked like compressed concepts of rest and stability.","One mat settled beneath her father. Another positioned itself beside him for her to sit upon. A third appeared near Noah, positioned at comfortable conversational distance.","\"Please, sit,\" Elyndra said, her voice carrying gentle insistence.","\"Father tires easily these days, and this conversation... this is important to him.\"","Noah complied, his form settling onto the mat with movements that suggested he was humoring her request rather than following orders.","The three of them sat there on the edge of that golden-radiant field, forming triangle of conversation.","The First Farmer laughed then...not the pained wheeze from before, but something closer to genuine joy, though it still carried notes of exhaustion that suggested even happiness cost him dearly.","\"Countless eons ago,\" he began, \"when I was still cultivating in the Earliest Folds, when I still possessed power that could reshape territories and nurture concepts into Principles... THE Creature visited my gardens.\"","...!","Noah’s attention sharpened immediately.","THE Creature.","The being whose authority seemed to permeate everything related to Early Creatures. The mysterious presence that even THE Living Existences seemed to reference with particular weight.","\"He was masked as a Fold Dweller,\" The First Farmer continued, his eyes growing distant with memory. \"But I knew what he was. You cannot hide that kind of presence, that level of fundamental authority. It radiates from every action, every gesture, every casual observation.\"","He paused, his hands trembling slightly where they rested on his lap.","\"He examined my cultivation plots with interest that felt... proprietary. And when he came to the Failed Seed...the one that would eventually become your Perpetual Harvest, he held it and stated what a shame it was that such a seed would never bloom! That...even a Leader of a Civilization would have benefited tremendously from it!\"","HUUM!","Noah felt his existence buzz.","THE Creature had held the Failed Seed of Perpetual Harvest and said such things?!","\"...\"","RUINEDEN’s voice emerged in his consciousness at such a time.","|Even though we already knew of its importance, we may need to designate Perpetual Harvest with multiple additional levels of importance.|","Noah’s expression remained calm.","The First Farmer continued speaking.","\"But that was then,\" he said, his voice growing heavier. \"When I still had power. When I still stood a chance. When I was on the cusp of attaining...\"","He paused, his eyes flashing with emotion that mixed pain and obsession in equal measure.","\"...THE.\"","The word dropped into the space between them.","...!","THE.","Not just power. Not just advancement. Not cultivation to higher levels or accumulation of greater Complexity and Purity.","THE!","The distinction that separated beings who merely possessed power from entities who defined existence’s fundamental parameters.","\"I was close,\" The First Farmer continued, his voice carrying notes of obsession that had survived despite everything else being stripped away.","\"So close that I could taste it. My cultivation had reached heights that current-era beings can’t conceive of. My understanding of growth and harvest and nurturing had become so refined that I was beginning to perceive the underlying code that governs how Principles themselves develop.\"","His hands clenched into fists, trembling with emotion!","\"I stood at the threshold,\" he said, his voice breaking. \"One more step. One more breakthrough. One more refinement of My Way. My Civilization. And I would have achieved THE. I would have become THE First Farmer! I would have been able to stand alongside THE Living Existences not as lesser being seeking approval, but as equal force defining existence’s nature.\"","He shook his head, pain flickering across his features.","\"But THE Living Emotive appeared.\"","Elyndra, who had been sitting beautifully and calmly beside her father, suddenly pulsed with contained rage so intense that space around her began crystallizing with frost.","The First Farmer’s voice continued, each word heavy with trauma that time hadn’t healed.","\"That psychopath appeared in this very Sanctuary. They came through the protective forests as if they weren’t there, bypassed every defense we’d cultivated, arrived here with smile that suggested they found the entire situation amusing.\"","His eyes grew distant, reliving memory that clearly caused him anguish.","\"And they...shattered my foundation.\"","WAA!","The words were delivered simply.","\"Not killed me,\" The First Farmer clarified, his voice taking on bitter tones. \"That would have been mercy. Instead, they dismantled my cultivation base piece by piece, breaking down the architectural supports I’d spent eons constructing, collapsing the Principles I’d nurtured, destroying the accumulation of My Way and My Civilization that had brought me so close to THE.\"","He paused, his breathing becoming labored.","\"They nearly destroyed all of my Civilization as well. The Fold Dwellers and Living Existences who had found sanctuary here, who had been cultivating under my guidance....they went through them like farmer culling diseased crops. Not out of necessity. Not out of strategic concern. Just because they could. Because their suffering amused them.\"","Elyndra’s rage intensified, her form practically vibrating with contained violence that wanted expression but had nowhere to go.","\"And when they were done,\" The First Farmer continued, \"when they had reduced me from the cusp of THE to barely functional weakness, when they had collapsed most of my Civilization and left survivors traumatized beyond normal healing...they explained why.\"","His voice took on mocking tones, clearly mimicking THE Living Emotive’s words.","\"They said: ’There are already enough existences with the distinction of THE who will be left behind. We don’t need another one. Your ambition is noted and denied. Your potential is recognized and eliminated. Consider yourself fortunate that I’m leaving you alive to witness The Fallout from this diminished state.’\"","...!","The cruelty was breathtaking in its calculated precision.","Not just defeating a rival. Not just eliminating a threat. But specifically leaving the First Farmer alive and aware, forced to experience the helplessness of having once been powerful enough to stand alongside THE Living Existences, only to watch everything collapse while possessing insufficient strength to intervene.","It was torture disguised as mercy, punishment that would last until The Fallout finally ended his suffering!","\"He didn’t even bother to kill me,\" The First Farmer said, his voice carrying bitterness that had festered through eons. \"He stated that my fear and anguish from being so close to THE, from having it ripped away, would be good sustenance for him for eons until I experienced The Fallout.\"","His expression shifted, carrying genuine confusion mixed with pain.","\"To this day,\" he said, his voice growing quieter, \"I cannot understand why THE Living Emotive and others had the nature they did. It could not simply be from their Way, right? To act like that. To do all that. To cause suffering not from necessity or strategy, but from... what, artistic satisfaction? Entertainment? Pure malice refined into fundamental authority?\"","He shook his head, the gesture carrying defeat.","\"It was just... ah-\"","The First Farmer suddenly began coughing, his frail form convulsing with spasms.","The coughing fit intensified, each hack sounding like it might be his last, his entire being trembling with strain that exceeded his capacity to endure.","Elyndra moved instinctively, her hand rising toward her father, radiance gathering around her fingers as she prepared to channel lifeforce that could stabilize him, heal him, provide relief from suffering that clearly exceeded normal tolerance.","But then she stopped.","Her hand froze mid-motion, the gathered radiance dissipating as she forcibly pulled back, her expression carrying anguish that suggested this internal conflict played out regularly.","She turned toward Noah, and in her eyes, he saw seriousness mixed with contained rage and helplessness.","\"Any lifeforce or authority of others,\" she said, \"even for the sake of healing, even with best intentions... is poisonous to him. The damage THE Living Emotive inflicted wasn’t just physical or cultivation-based. It was existential. Father’s being now rejects external assistance, treating it as contamination rather than aid.\"","Her hands clenched into fists.","\"None of us can help him. I... cannot do anything.\"","The helplessness in her voice was genuine!","The First Farmer continued his coughing fit, his existence seeming weary and tired.","Noah watched this display with expression that grew increasingly grave.","So this was The First Farmer!","A broken man!","He had come here hoping to find powerful being who could stand against The Fallout, who could provide knowledge or resources or strategic advantage.","Instead, he’d found victim of THE Living Existences’ preemptive elimination of threats, someone who had been specifically targeted and broken because he’d gotten too close to achieving THE.","He had gotten too close to the sun!"]},{"number":4357,"title":"Chapter 4357: Chapter 4356: The Farmer’s Greeting I","paragraphs":["The First Farmer had flown high as in the end, his wings had gotten clipped!","Which meant...","Noah shook his head.","’I have to think of many more possibilities. Have to account for fact that anyone powerful enough to matter has probably already been neutralized. Have to assume that resistance to The Fallout won’t come from ancient beings revealing themselves at critical moment...’","Schrodinger and any others were not something to be counted on!","HUUM!","Noah’s eyes flashed with brilliance.","’It all comes back to me. My Principles. My Civilization. My...Way’","WAA!","As always.","The coughing fit continued for several more seconds before finally subsiding, The First Farmer’s breathing gradually returning to something approaching normal...though normal for him meant labored and weak rather than healthy.","Elyndra looked apologetically toward Noah, her expression carrying embarrassment mixed with concern.","\"I apologize,\" she said, her voice quieter now. \"Father’s episodes are... frequent these days. The damage runs deep, and time only makes it worse rather than better.\"","She sighed, then gestured toward distant field visible from their seated position.","The field blazed with golden light even more intense than the radiance surrounding their current location. At its center stood a vibrant tree that appeared to be simultaneously sapling and ancient growth, its branches reaching in impossible directions while its trunk pulsed with authority.","\"Please,\" Elyndra said, her tone carrying genuine request, \"give us a moment to stabilize. In the meantime, you’re welcome to examine that cultivation plot. It represents a grand Principle being nurtured...one of Father’s most successful projects, though significantly less advanced than what Perpetual Harvest became for you.\"","She smiled slightly.","\"Perhaps you’ll find insights there that could benefit your own understanding. Knowledge should never be hoarded when sharing could elevate multiple parties.\"","Noah nodded, accepting the suggestion because it aligned with his own desires anyway.","He had much to think about...the implications of THE Creature’s words, the systematic elimination of potential resistance forces by THE Living Existences, the grim reality that help wouldn’t come from external sources.","And examining a nurtured Principle, seeing firsthand how The First Farmer’s cultivation techniques manifested, could provide valuable data that RUINEDEN could analyze and potentially integrate into the Cheat Code Repository.","He rose from the mat with fluid grace, his form lifting slightly off the ground as he prepared to float toward the distant golden field.","Behind him, the First Farmer continued his recovery, Elyndra helping him stabilize with hands that trembled with suppressed desire to do more than she was allowed.","Noah moved toward the radiant tree.","But as he departed, as his attention shifted away from the two beings behind him...","The First Farmer couldn’t help but look at him intently.","And soon after...","Time seemingly stopped for The First Farmer and Elyndra.","Not literally...existence still flowed, reality still processed, moments still accumulated into continuity.","But for them, in that instant, communication began through a Principle as this instant could be a day’s worth of communication.","They possessed connection that ran deeper than words...father and daughter bound not just by familial relationship but by shared Principle!","And in that space where their consciousnesses touched, where communication happened at speeds that made normal dialogue seem glacial by comparison, The First Farmer spoke.","His mental voice carried none of the weakness his physical form exhibited. Here, in this space of pure consciousness, he remained what he’d been before THE Living Emotive had shattered him...powerful, decisive, calculating with precision that had once brought him to cusp of THE.","\"What do you think?\" his voice resonated through their connection, heavy and weighted with implications.","\"Will you be able to handle him? Fighting will not work. Things have to be done another way.\"","BOOM!","Elyndra’s consciousness flickered with indecision, her mental presence wrestling with something that caused her genuine conflict.","She had always obeyed her father. Always trusted his wisdom. Always accepted that his cultivation experience exceeded hers by eons, that his understanding of existence’s nature transcended her own despite her impressive power.","But this...","Finally, hesitantly, she responded through their connection.","\"I... yes, Father. I believe I can handle him. But are we certain this is necessary? This path feels...\"","She didn’t finish the thought, her consciousness carrying emotions too complex to reduce to simple statements.","The First Farmer’s mental voice continued, carrying patience mixed with urgency.","\"Get close to him,\" he instructed, each word deliberate. \"As close as possible. Form bonds that transcend simple alliance. Make yourself valuable to his Way, integrate into his Civilization, become someone he trusts implicitly.\"","He paused, then delivered the critical instruction.","\"Once you have integrated into his Way, once he trusts you completely, once guards are lowered and defenses are relaxed... connect with him on existential level. Use what lies dormant in your existence- the 9 Principles I cultivated within you...to pull Perpetual Harvest out.\"","HUUM!","The magnitude of what he was suggesting was heavy!","Far too heavy!","\"Its Seed alone was the Seed of a Civilization,\" the First Farmer continued, \"I gave it away when I shouldn’t have, when I was still naive enough to believe that failure had no value. But now I understand...when it is too late.\"","His presence intensified in their shared space.","\"And now that it has bloomed, now that someone has refined it into full Principle, now that it exists in matured state rather than potential... I need it. If I am to get back to my old self, if I am to restore what THE Living Emotive destroyed, if I am to have any chance of surviving until The Fallout and beyond... I will need the full Principle of Perpetual Harvest. Not just understanding of it. Not just observation of its mechanics. The actual, complete Principle itself, integrated into my existence. I have tried again and again to recultivate it. I have cultivated hundreds of Seed of Principles since then...but I cannot replicate Perpetual Harvest. It was singular, and remains singular. The Key...to a Civilization. And I just gave it away.\"","...!","Elyndra’s consciousness flickered with conflict of genuine internal struggle!","Her mental voice emerged hesitantly.","\"Is there really no other way?\" she asked, and her presence carried pleading words.","\"We can talk with him. We can discuss everything. We can explain your situation, offer alliance, propose collaboration.\"","Her consciousness pulsed with conviction.","\"As Farmers, we know that collaboration is better than anything else. That wonders can be cultivated in grander ways together than alone. Perpetual Harvest in his hands has already achieved what you couldn’t...imagine what it could become if we worked together rather than against each other!\"","The argument was logical, compassionate, rooted in principles that agricultural cultivation had taught her over eons.","But the First Farmer’s response carried finality that allowed no further debate.","\"Child,\" his mental voice said gently but firmly, \"you are no longer naive. You’ve lived long enough, observed enough, understood enough to recognize truth when you encounter it.\"","His presence grew heavier in their shared space.","\"I have looked at all possibilities,\" he continued, each word weighted with certainty born from exhaustive calculation. \"I have examined this entity from every angle my diminished perception still allows. And what I see is...\"","He paused, choosing words carefully.","\"Boundless tyranny. Boundless potential. An existence that accumulates power at rates that defy reasonable progression, that possesses Principles that shouldn’t coexist in single being, that operates according to rules that make no sense. Such a being is primed for The Way. For leading a Civilization. I know him because I know myself. He and I...are the same type of existence. Boundless. Relentless.\"","His mental voice took on darker tones.","\"He will not give anything away. Not Perpetual Harvest, not knowledge, not advantage. Everything must be taken from him, because sharing requires vulnerability he will never allow himself to experience.\"","The assessment was delivered with clinical precision, without malice but without hope either.","\"I have seen it,\" the First Farmer said. \"And having met him, having observed how he carries himself...\"","The First Farmer shook his head.","\"If I do not get back the full Principle of Perpetual Harvest,\" The First Farmer continued, his mental voice growing more urgent, \"if I cannot restore what THE Living Emotive destroyed by integrating that Principle into my shattered foundation... I will not even live to The Fallout, my daughter.\"","WAA!","The words carried weight of absolute truth.","\"I am deteriorating,\" he said, allowing her to feel the full extent of his suffering through their connection. \"Each day, I grow weaker. Each cycle, more of what I was slips away into nothingness. The poison THE Living Emotive left in my existence is consuming me from inside, and I have no defense against it because my own being treats healing as contamination.\"","His presence pulsed with desperation!","\"Save this poor father of yours,\" he pleaded.","\"I cultivated you. I raised you for many purposes...to tend the Sanctuary, to protect the Fold Dwellers who found refuge here, to nurture Principles and advance understanding of growth itself.\"","He paused, then delivered the critical question.","\"But this will be a particularly critical purpose,\" he said. \"Can I trust you with it? Can I rely on you to do what necessity demands, even if compassion argues against it? Can you save your father by taking what must be taken?\"","...!","Elyndra’s consciousness trembled with conflict.","Everything she’d been taught about cultivation argued against this approach. Farmers didn’t steal crops from other Farmers. Growth came through nurturing, not theft. Collaboration produced better results than competition.","But her father was dying. Slowly, painfully, inevitably dying unless something changed dramatically.","And if taking Perpetual Harvest from Osmont could restore him, could bring back the powerful being who had created sanctuary and protected so many...","Could she refuse?","Should she refuse?","Did she have the right to prioritize stranger’s well-being over her father’s survival?","The conflict raged through her consciousness for what felt like eons compressed into single instant.","Then, finally, carrying sadness that weighed heavier than any Complexity or Purity measurement could quantify, she responded.","\"Yes, Father.\"","The words were simple, but they carried commitment!","\"I will do it. I will get close to him. I will integrate into his Way. I will earn his trust. And when the moment comes... I will take Perpetual Harvest for you.\"","BOOM!","Even as she said it, even as she committed to the course, part of her consciousness wept at what she was agreeing to become.","Betrayer. Thief. Manipulator using cultivated intimacy as weapon rather than genuine connection.","Everything she’d been raised to oppose.","But for her father’s survival...","She would become it anyway.","The First Farmer’s mental voice carried relief mixed with satisfaction.","\"Good,\" he said. \"Go to him now. Show him our boons, demonstrate value of alliance, show your Principles to him- they are meant to draw in any existence who knows anything to do with growth and harvest, much less one with Perpetual Harvest. Form a connection that will allow deeper integration later. Be patient...this cannot be rushed. Trust takes time to cultivate, and harvesting before proper ripeness yields inferior results.\"","His presence pulsed with strategic certainty.","\"Let us get ready to embark on our Civilization,\" he said, the words carrying weight of plans extending far beyond simple recovery. \"With Perpetual Harvest restored to me, with my foundation rebuilt, with power accumulated through proper agricultural methods... we will survive The Fallout. We will thrive in whatever comes after. We will show THE Living Existences that they were wrong to dismiss the Farmer who once stood at threshold of THE.\"","Elyndra nodded through their connection, accepting the mandate even as part of her soul protested.","Then their communion ended, time resuming its normal flow as if the extended mental conversation had occurred in single heartbeat.","Elyndra rose from her mat with fluid grace that concealed inner turmoil, her expression settling into calm confidence that suggested nothing significant had just transpired.","She began walking toward Noah, her vibrant and powerful figure moving through the golden radiance with practiced ease.","But in that moment, despite her impressive power, despite her nine Principles operating in perfect harmony, despite her cultivation achievements that would make current-era beings weep with inadequacy...","Her grand figure seemed...extremely alone!","A daughter walking toward betrayal she didn’t want to commit, bound by duty to father who was dying, caught between compassion that argued for honesty and necessity that demanded deception.","And ahead of her, unaware of conspiracy just formed in consciousness-space, Noah examined the vibrant tree that represented nurtured Principle, his power already breaking down its structure and cataloging insights that would feed into his ever-expanding understanding of existence’s architecture.","A trap was set.","The pieces were moving.","And The First Farmer watched with eyes that held calculation refined through eons of agricultural patience...knowing that harvests, when done properly, required time, care, and willingness to do whatever cultivation demanded.","Even if what it demanded was his own Daughter he had given his very blood to nurture!"]},{"number":4358,"title":"Chapter 4358: Chapter 4357: The Farmer’s Greeting II","paragraphs":["Noah stood before the massive golden budding tree, its presence radiating authority that made nearby reality pulse.","The tree was magnificent...its trunk appeared to be woven from compressed collaborative will, each strand representing different beings choosing to work together rather than against each other.","Its branches reached outward in patterns that suggested networks rather than hierarchies, connections rather than domination.","And from those branches, buds were forming...not individual flowers, but collective blooms where multiple potential outcomes existed simultaneously, waiting for proper cultivation to determine which would manifest into reality.","It was beautiful.","It was profound.","It was exactly the kind of thing Noah would absolutely catalog and potentially exploit for his own purposes.","Beside him, invisible to all observers except himself, RUINEDEN’s holographic form materialized.","Her form was more detailed now than it had been even hours ago, her features showing depth that suggested continuous evolution!","She gestured toward the tree, and prompts began cascading across Noah’s vision with information she’d compiled.","|ANALYSIS COMPLETE: Golden Tree of Unified Harvest|","|Classification: Grand Principle - Tier 2|","|Principle Name: The Convergent Prosperity|","|Core Function: Allows multiple existences to combine their power under unified framework, pooling resources and authorities to manifest collective achievement that exceeds individual capability|","RUINEDEN’s voice emerged.","\"This Principle is fascinating in its architecture,\" she said, her words accompanied by illusory diagrams showing how the power-pooling mechanisms functioned. \"It operates on the fundamental understanding that collaboration, when properly structured, creates exponential rather than additive returns.\"","The diagrams showed multiple beings connecting to the Principle, their individual powers flowing into collective reservoir that grew larger with each contributor.","\"When beings channel their authority through The Convergent Prosperity,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"they multiply it through resonance effects. Ten beings contributing would generate not ten times the power, but potentially fifty or a hundred times, depending on how well their authorities harmonize...well, to a point. Fold Dwellers or Living Existences of a few Trillion in complexity may be able to combine together under this principle to exhibit 1000 Quadrillion at most. If someone of your calibre was at its center, with others like Elyndra joining you, you could potentially exhibit tens of Quintillions.\"","...!","She paused, then added with calculating precision, \"And the manifestation it produces is equally impressive.\"","The diagram shifted, showing what would emerge when the Principle was fully activated.","|Collective Manifestation: The Abundant Colossus|","|Description: A temporary entity composed of all contributors’ combined essences. Appears as massive humanoid figure wreathed in golden-green radiance, its size and power scaling directly with number and strength of contributors.|","|Capabilities:|","|—Possesses aggregate Complexity and Purity of all participants(to an extent)|","|—Can perform coordinated attacks that multiple beings couldn’t achieve individually|","|—Serves as shared defense, distributing damage across all contributors|","|—Duration limited by participants’ stamina and authority|","|Strategic Applications: Perfect for defensive operations where weaker beings need to stand against stronger threats. Less useful for offensive campaigns due to coordination complexity and limited duration(if you aren’t included.|","Noah studied the information with intensity.","So the First Farmer had developed a Principle specifically designed for collaboration, for allowing weaker beings to collectively challenge stronger ones through unified action!","It was elegant solution to problem that plagued cultivation across all eras...how do the many resist the few when individual power gaps were insurmountable?","The answer, apparently, was to stop thinking of themselves as individuals and start functioning as organism.","RUINEDEN wasn’t done with her analysis, though. Her expression shifted into something more thoughtful, more theoretical.","\"Master,\" she said, her tone taking on weight that suggested she was about to share insights, \"after coming across so many Principles during our travels- from the Prime Dead Early Creatures, from Elyndra’s collection, from your own cultivation, I can now distinguish patterns that weren’t apparent before.\"","She gestured, creating a new set of diagrams that organized Principles into hierarchical categories.","\"There are potentially tiers to Principles,\" she explained, her voice carrying certainty born from extensive data analysis. \"Not just power levels, but fundamental distinctions in how they operate and who can access them.\"","The first tier materialized in the display.","|TIER ONE: NORMAL PRINCIPLES|","|Characteristics:|","|—Available to anyone who meets basic cultivation requirements(1 Quadrillion+)|","|—Can be learned, taught, shared across multiple practitioners|","|—Power scales with user’s understanding and existence|","|—Relatively stable and well-documented in existence’s collective knowledge|","\"These are the common Principles,\" RUINEDEN said, gesturing to examples. \"Things like Principle of Elemental Mastery, Principle of Harvest Festival, Principle of Absolute Domain...weavings of Existence that many people can utilize because they’re working with fundamental forces that existence itself provides access to.\"","She paused, then added, \"They’re not weak, necessarily. A master practitioner of Normal Principle can absolutely exceed someone with poor grasp of higher-tier Principle. But their ceiling is limited by the fact that existence treats them as shared resources rather than unique achievements.\"","The second tier materialized, glowing with more intense radiance.","|TIER TWO: GRAND PRINCIPLES|","|Characteristics:|","|—Limited in number of practitioners who can utilize them|","|—Normally holds significantly more power than Normal Principles|","|—Often requires specific lineage, inheritance, or earned right to access(Nurtured as Seeds)|","|—Integration more complex, demanding greater existential investment|","\"Grand Principles are where things get interesting,\" RUINEDEN continued, her voice warming with enthusiasm. \"These aren’t shared resources...they’re restricted access. Only certain beings can utilize them, and often, teaching them to others is complex of a process.\"","She gestured to specific examples.","\"All nine Principles that Elyndra possesses are Grand tier,\" she said, pulling up their specifications. \"Principle of Eternal Growth, Principle of Cyclical Harvest, Principle of Fertile Abundance...each one limited in how many practitioners can exist simultaneously.\"","The diagrams showed how Grand Principles operated differently from Normal ones, their architecture more complex, their integration more demanding, their payoff exponentially greater.","\"The Convergent Prosperity before us is also Grand tier,\" RUINEDEN added, gesturing toward the golden tree. \"Limited number of practitioners can nurture it, though many can benefit from its effects once manifested. That’s common pattern for collaborative Principles...few can cultivate them, but many can utilize results.\"","Noah processed this information with calculating precision, already considering implications for his own development!","But RUINEDEN’s expression shifted again.","\"And then,\" she said, her voice dropping to tones that carried weight of genuine significance, \"there is a tier far above all of these. A classification so exclusive, so fundamentally unique, that I’m taking liberty of creating self-proclaimed designation for it.\"","A third tier materialized in the display, blazing with radiance that made the previous categories look dim by comparison.","|TIER THREE: SINGULARITY PRINCIPLES (RUIN/EDEN Classification)|","|Characteristics:|","|—Available ONLY to the entity who discovered and nurtured them|","|—Cannot be taught, cannot be shared, cannot be replicated|","|—Met such terrifying conditions during development that only original cultivator’s existence can contain them|","|—Power ceiling theoretically unlimited, scaling with user’s advancement|","|—Represent fundamental uniqueness of practitioner’s Way|","RUINEDEN’s expression carried satisfaction at having codified something she clearly considered important theoretical advancement.","\"In this tier,\" she explained, her voice carrying emphasis that made every word significant, \"the Principle is bound to a single existence so completely that separation is impossible without destroying both Principle and practitioner. These are singular by definition. One practitioner, one Principle, indivisible.\""]},{"number":4359,"title":"Chapter 4359: Chapter 4358: The Farmer’s Greeting III","paragraphs":["She paused, then delivered the critical examples.","\"Perpetual Harvest and the Cheating Architect both fall into this category.\"","...!","Noah’s own Principles...the foundations of his rapid advancement, the cornerstones of his impossible accumulation, the core components of his Way...were so unique that no other entities could hold them.","Not because they were particularly powerful (though they were).","Not because they were difficult to understand (though they might be).","But because they had met conditions during their cultivation that made them fundamentally tied to Noah’s specific existence in ways that couldn’t be replicated.","Because...who could possibly hold The Cheating Architect?","\"Well,\" RUINEDEN amended, her expression shifting slightly, \"The Infiniverse also has access to Perpetual Harvest, but that’s special case. She was akin to the sentient farmland that Perpetual Harvest grew from...the soil that nurtured the Seed into full bloom. So both your existences have access to it because she’s fundamentally part of your cultivation architecture.\"","Her voice took on more analytical tones.","\"Actually, calling her just ’part’ of your Civilization undersells her significance. The Infiniverse is akin to grand instrument of your Civilization. More accurately...\" she paused, choosing words carefully, \"...she is the backbone of your Civilization. The foundational infrastructure upon which everything else is built.\"","Noah nodded calmly at this.","The Infiniverse...his Early Veiled Shore, his sanctuary, his accumulating domain- wasn’t just territory he controlled.","She was living architecture, sentient foundation, entity whose existence was so intertwined with his own that separating them would collapse both.","She was simultaneously part of him and separate from him, extension of his will that possessed her own consciousness.","RUINEDEN continued, her voice taking on more speculative tones.","\"Principles like Perpetual Harvest and the Cheating Architect...\" she paused, her expression growing more serious, \"...should be good guides toward the next Scale of Existence. Toward the distinction of THE.\"","...!","\"Think about it,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"THE Living Existences all possess authorities that are fundamentally unique to them. THE Living Order’s authority over structure and hierarchy...no one else can replicate it. THE Living Paradox’s control over true contradictory states...singular to his existence. THE Living Emotive’s mastery over feelings and experiences...truly bound to him alone.\"","Her diagrams shifted, showing parallels between THE Living Existences’ authorities and Noah’s Singularity Principles.","\"Your Perpetual Harvest and Cheating Architect operate on similar paradigm,\" she explained. \"They’re fundamentally yours in ways that make them unreplicable. That suggests you’re already walking path toward THE, whether intentionally or not. Your Principles are exhibiting characteristics that match how THE-tier authorities function.\"","She paused, then added with calculating precision, \"Which means the question isn’t whether you can reach THE, but whether you’ll survive long enough to complete the journey.\"","HUUM!","\"I need a few more minutes here,\" RUIN/EDEN said, shifting back to more immediate concerns as her analytical capabilities engaged fully with the golden tree.","\"I’m nearly finished breaking down the architecture of The Convergent Prosperity. Once complete analysis is done, I can make it the first Grand Principle that the Infiniverse can nurture and produce en masse for those in your Civilization to obtain.\"","Her expression carried satisfaction at the prospect.","\"Imagine it,\" she continued, her voice warming with enthusiasm. \"Your people, able to pool their power through properly cultivated collaborative Principle. Able to manifest The Abundant Colossus when defending your Shore. Able to coordinate attacks that individual capability couldn’t achieve. It would transform your Civilization from collection of powerful individuals into unified force that operates as single organism when necessary.\"","Noah nodded, satisfaction blooming in his mind.","The Infiniverse.","His smile deepened as he thought about her, who had been quietly working in background, forging wonders without needing constant attention or praise.","She was silent without making flashy moves, but she was already doing unfathomable things.","As if sensing his thoughts, RUIN/EDEN’s expression shifted into something that resembled conspiratorial smile.","\"Speaking of The Infiniverse,\" she said, her voice taking on tones that suggested she was about to share secret, \"Sis Infiniverse has actually been utilizing my help to forge a surprise for Master. Something special that we’ve been developing in background while you were focused on other advancements.\"","Her smile widened.","\"Would you like to know what it is?\" she asked, her tone suggesting she was offering forbidden knowledge. \"Fair warning...it would spoil the surprise. But I can tell you if you want.\"","Noah considered for a moment, his thoughts weighing curiosity against the satisfaction of being genuinely surprised by something.","Finally, he shook his head.","\"No,\" he said simply, his voice carrying amusement. \"Let her surprise me. I trust whatever she’s creating will be worth the wait.\"","RUIN/EDEN nodded, her expression carrying approval at his restraint.","But then her smile took on more mischievous qualities.","\"Master,\" she said, her voice carrying notes of professional advice, \"I also feel obligated to point out that if you could choose to...get friendlier on Elyndra sooner rather than later, we would make significantly more advancements on Principles.\"","...!","She gestured, creating illusory diagrams that showed potential knowledge gains from closer integration with The First Farmer’s daughter.","\"She possesses nine Grand Principles operating in perfect harmony,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, her tone clinical despite the absurdity of what she was suggesting.","\"Direct... intimate contact would allow me to analyze those Principles as at this moment, I can’t truly gain much. The data we could acquire through close integration would be invaluable.\"","Her smile widened further.","\"You...need to sacrifice your innocence, Master,\" she said with mock seriousness, \"for the sake of research. Think of the scientific advancement!\"","WAA!","Noah shook his head, smile tugging at his lips despite himself.","What innocence? He’d lost that particular commodity long ago!","But as he looked at RUINEDEN...at her animated expression, her mischievous smile, her increasingly complex mannerisms...he felt happy.","As if he was seeing Ruination at her fullest. How she always wanted to be with him, but never got the chance.","Her existence truly was becoming more alive with personality as he advanced. Each breakthrough in his power, each new capability of the Cheating Architect, each expansion of his consciousness seemed to grant her additional depth of character.","She was evolving into something complex!"]},{"number":4360,"title":"Chapter 4360: Chapter 4359: The Farmer’s Greeting IV","paragraphs":["It was beautiful to witness, even when that emerging personality was suggesting he seduce powerful beings for research purposes.","But as Noah turned his attention away from RUINEDEN’s mischievous recommendations, he noticed a presence that had materialized beside him while he’d been focused on internal conversation.","Elyndra.","She stood silently, her vibrant form radiating that particular authority of nine Principles operating in harmony, her blue eyes fixed on the golden tree with expression that suggested she was lost in thought rather than observing her surroundings.","She seemed... sad.","Not overtly, not dramatically, but carrying weight of someone wrestling with internal conflict that had no satisfying resolution.","Noah silently gazed at her.","---","Elyndra stood beside Noah, her consciousness focused on the golden tree that truly represented collaboration in its purest form.","But her thoughts were elsewhere, cycling through everything that had led to this moment...her father’s condition, the task he’d assigned her, the conflict between what she believed and what necessity demanded.","She knew her father.","Had known him for eons, when he’d been powerful enough, when his cultivation had brought him to threshold of that fundamental distinction.","He had lived his whole life aligned with what was right. With what it meant to be good.","Saving as many Fold Dwellers as possible, creating sanctuary for those who had nowhere else to go, even allowing inclusion of Living Existences despite their historical prejudice against Fold Dwellers as lesser beings.","He had done everything according to principles that agricultural cultivation had taught him...that growth came through nurturing rather than exploitation, that collaboration produced better results than competition, that patience and care yielded harvests that force and haste could never achieve.","And where had it gotten him?","Shattered by THE Living Emotive, reduced to weakness that made even standing difficult, poisoned against healing that might restore what had been destroyed.","Horrible beings like THE Living Emotive did what they wanted with impunity and without any consequences. They acted according to pure malice refined into authority, and existence itself seemed to reward them for it rather than punish them.","THE Creature was supposed to be the one to balance things out. To keep THE Living Paradox in check, to prevent THE Living Existences from becoming monsters who consumed everything in pursuit of their own advancement.","And yet even he was nowhere to be seen. Absent when needed most, leaving beings like her father to suffer consequences of system that rewarded cruelty over compassion.","Her father was...tired.","Tired of doing things the right way and watching it accomplish nothing. Tired of being good while others thrived through being terrible.","Tired of principles that felt increasingly like chains rather than guidance.","She understood why he was suggesting they take what they needed from Noah rather than negotiating for it. Why he believed collaboration wouldn’t work, that force was necessary, that adopting methods of THE Living Existences was only path forward.","He knew he could try collaboration. Maybe it would finally work out. Maybe Noah would be reasonable, would give up Perpetual Harvest willingly, would help restore what THE Living Emotive had destroyed.","But her Father... was tired of maybes.","He wanted certainty, like THE Living Emotive possessed. Success, like THE Living Paradox had achieved. Power that couldn’t be taken away, accumulated through methods that worked regardless of whether they were right or wrong.","And how did THE Living Existences succeed?","By taking what they wanted.","Elyndra felt sadness crystallize in her chest, heavy and cold.","She didn’t believe it. Her very existence told her they should be forging their own Way, advancing according to principles they chose rather than imitating paths that others had walked.","To build their Civilization, it should be done according to their own methods. Their own understanding. Their own values.","They shouldn’t deviate to follow how others proceeded. Shouldn’t take hints from The Way of beings they opposed. Shouldn’t become the thing they resisted just because it seemed effective.","Her father was doing exactly that...abandoning his Way in favor of methods that had brought THE Living Existences success but had also made them into monsters.","And if he did that, if he truly went about things through betrayal and theft rather than cultivation and collaboration...","He may have forever lost his Way.","He may have corrupted it beyond recovery, because even if he obtained Perpetual Harvest through deception, even if he restored his power through stolen Principle...","He would never reach THE.","Because he wouldn’t have done it his Way. He would have achieved it through imitation of methods that were fundamentally opposed to everything his cultivation had been built upon.","But she couldn’t find herself able to tell her father that she thought his Way may have gotten irreparably damaged. That his desperate attempt to restore what was lost might actually guarantee he could never reclaim what truly mattered.","How could she say such things to someone who was dying? Who had sacrificed everything for principles that had brought him nothing but suffering? Who deserved rest and restoration rather than philosophical lectures about corruption of purpose?","So what could she do?","Stand beside him as he destroyed himself trying to save himself? Refuse his request and watch him die knowing she could have helped but chose not to? Try to change his mind when exhaustion and pain had made him incapable of hearing arguments about long-term consequences?","There were no good options.","Only varieties of betrayal...of Osmont, of her father, or of herself.","At this time, Noah’s calm voice cut through her spiral of internal conflict.","\"You seem sad.\"","The observation was delivered without judgment, without prying curiosity, just simple acknowledgment of what was obvious to anyone paying attention.","Elyndra turned to look at him, finding his expression calm.","\"Yeah,\" she replied, allowing honesty to color her voice. \"I am a bit melancholic and sad. Existence... can be unfair. Very, very unfair.\"","Noah nodded, his gaze returning to the golden tree.","\"Yes, it is unfair,\" he said, his tone carrying acceptance rather than complaint. \"But from that unfairness comes struggle, and from that struggle... wonders can bloom.\"","...!","The words landed with weight that made Elyndra pause.","From unfairness comes struggle, and from struggle comes wonders.","It was perspective she needed to hear, reminder that hardship wasn’t just obstacle but potentially catalyst.","That the difficulties her father faced, that she faced, that everyone struggled against...they weren’t just barriers to overcome but conditions that could produce achievements impossible under easier circumstances.","She sighed, nodding slowly as she focused more fully on Noah.","Maybe there was still path forward that didn’t require betrayal. Maybe collaboration could work if she presented it properly. Maybe...","\"...\"","No.","She stopped herself. No more maybes. Time to be direct.","\"While my Father is in the state he is in,\" she began, her voice taking on more formal tones, \"it does not mean his efforts are diminished any less. His Sanctuary still has countless things to offer.\"","She gestured broadly to encompass the fields around them.","\"One of the major offerings...the Produce that the Living Existences you came with were planned to be given...grants 1000 Quadrillion Complexity and Purity or more per consumption.\"","WAA!","\"The trade-off is that it completely limits one’s advancement and potential thereafter. It’s shortcut to immense power, but it’s also ceiling that can never be exceeded. Those who consume Father’s highest-tier Produce gain tremendous immediate strength but sacrifice all future growth.\"","She continued detailing other achievements, her voice warming with pride despite her earlier melancholy.","\"We also have Seeds that can be used as weapons- projectiles that move faster than even the perception of entities exceeding 1 or 3 Quintillion in power. When triggered, they explode with force that could collapse beings with 3 or 4 Quintillion Complexity and Purity.\"","Her eyes found Noah’s, holding his gaze with intensity.","\"We have techniques for nurturing Principles that predate modern cultivation methods. We have knowledge about THE Living Existences that few outside the Earliest Folds possess. We have resources accumulated over eons of careful agricultural development.\"","She paused, then delivered what she clearly considered the most important information.","\"With the coming Fallout,\" she said, her voice carrying weight of confession, \"my Father believes it is only possible to overcome it by having an entity at the distinction of THE. Which is... an impossibility almost, given current circumstances and timelines.\"","\"So he nurtured me. At my peak, with the inherent nature of my existence and nine converging Principles, if I use enough nurturing from other sources- collapsed weavings of Prime Dead Early Creatures, the Existential Armors they forge, other complex atrocities that contain concentrated power...I can reach a state of THE False Harvest. A False part of My Way.\"","She paused, making sure he understood the significance.","\"Momentary. False. Unstable. But I can achieve such power briefly,\" she continued. \"Burning up everything accumulated, sacrificing all reserves, pushing beyond normal limits...the moment The Fallout descends, I could protect this Sanctuary and those within it.\"","Her blue eyes blazed with determination mixed with desperation.","\"We do not have to become The Dead to survive,\" she said, her voice carrying conviction. \"This was my father’s goal. This was what all his cultivation aimed toward.\"","She took a breath, then delivered what was clearly request that mattered more than anything else.","\"I would be immensely grateful if we can work together to achieve this goal.\"","...!"]},{"number":4361,"title":"Chapter 4361: Chapter 4360: The Farmer’s Greeting V","paragraphs":["The words buzzed between them.","Noah continued staring at the tree ahead, his expression thoughtful as he processed everything she’d said.","Then, he smiled with genuine curiosity.","\"What is wrong with all of us becoming The Dead?\" he asked.","\"We could all survive being collapsed and return again a day later. Sounds like elegant solution to surviving The Fallout, doesn’t it?\"","Elyndra blinked, her expression cycling through confusion before settling into something resembling disbelief.","She studied his features, trying to determine if he was joking or if he genuinely didn’t know.","\"You do know,\" she said slowly, carefully, as if explaining fundamental truth to someone who somehow missed it, \"that the Curse of The Dead, and anything to do with THE Creature, means that all Dead Existences are completely cut off from ever reaching the next Scale of Existence, right?\"","Her voice grew more emphatic.","\"That was the cost for such a terrifying capability. THE Creature granted The Dead the ability to return from collapse, to survive what should be absolute ending, to persist through conditions that would unmake Living Existences. But in exchange, they can never advance beyond their current Scale. They are trapped, forever, at whatever level they possessed when they crossed The Veil.\"","She paused, making sure he absorbed the information.","\"Becoming The Dead isn’t just transformation...it’s permanent limitation. A ceiling that can never be exceeded. An end to all potential growth in exchange for impossible survival.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes turned immensely sharp at this revelation.","He looked at Elyndra up and down.","But her expression carried no deception...just certainty born from knowledge that she considered fundamental truth of existence.","The Dead couldn’t reach the next Scale of Existence.","They were trapped, forever, at whatever level they’d achieved before crossing The Veil.","Which meant that if he became Dead, if he crossed to the other side, if he chose survival through that method...","He would never reach THE.","Never advance beyond his current Scale, no matter how much power he accumulated, no matter how many Principles he integrated, no matter what achievements his Way produced.","It would be ceiling disguised as salvation, trap baited with immortality, permanent limitation masquerading as ultimate survival technique.","What of his Arch Lich though? Did his type of Death align with THE Creature’s Curse? Or was he purer?","Noah simply stared out toward the tree silently, his thoughts racing through implications!","So that probability stream RUINEDEN had shown him...the one where THE Dead Order captured him and turned him into battery for her Civilization, wasn’t just horrifying because of the loss of freedom.","It was catastrophic because it would permanently cap his advancement. Would lock him into current Scale of Existence forever, removing any possibility of reaching heights he was apparently already walking toward.","The Dead couldn’t reach THE.","Which meant THE Dead Order couldn’t either, despite her immense power. She wasnt fully...THE...Unless she unified with Sigrid!","She was trapped on that side of The Veil, unable to cross over or advance further, limited by the very method that had allowed her to survive when THE Living Order had collapsed.","Once someone crossed The Veil and became Dead, they were no longer competition. They were permanently locked out of ever challenging THE Living Existences’ positions.","Was that why Khor and others were potentially collapsed?","Elyndra took his silence as confirmation that he’d been joking, her expression relaxing slightly as she sighed.","\"So,\" she said, returning to her earlier question, \"do you think a collaboration is possible? With your Perpetual Harvest, cultivating what even father could not bloom, we could accomplish goals that many outside THE Loom seek to accomplish.\"","She paused, her blue eyes finding his with intensity that carried genuine hope mixed with determination.","\"As I said before,\" she continued, her voice softening, \"I would like to be your friend.\"","...!","Noah looked at the figure of Elyndra...at her astonishing beauty, her nine converging Principles, her genuine desire for collaboration mixed with hidden agenda he suspected but couldn’t confirm.","Then his gaze shifted to the distant figure of The First Farmer, who was gazing at groups of countless beings in his sanctuary with expression that seemed calm and benevolent.","Finally, Noah smiled.","\"Collaboration is possible,\" he said simply, his voice carrying certainty. \"And I would like to see the weapons of The First Farmer. If we’re going to work together, I should understand what resources are available.\"","Elyndra’s smile blazed brilliant enough to make existence in the entire area seem a shade brighter, her blue eyes shining with joy.","She stretched out her hand toward Noah, her thumb and two fingers raised in gesture he didn’t recognize.","Noah raised his eyebrows. \"What are you doing?\"","Elyndra blinked, then turned her head slightly, confusion flickering across her features.","\"Oh,\" she said, realization dawning. \"You don’t know the Farmer’s Greeting? It’s a gesture- three fingers waved at a distance, or connecting like a handshake when up close.\"","She smiled, moving closer.","\"It’s akin to blessing and wishing a good harvest and prosperity to the other party. Here, let me show you.\"","She motioned to Noah’s hands, and he brought his thumb, index finger, and middle finger forward as she’d demonstrated.","Their fingertips touched...three points of contact forming triangle of connection between them.","Elyndra’s smile became radiant, her blue eyes shining brilliantly with genuine warmth.","In that moment, she seemed to have forgotten the heavy task laid upon her by her father, forgotten the conflict between duty and principle, forgotten everything except the simple joy of teaching someone about her culture’s traditions.","\"There you go,\" she said, her voice carrying delight. \"Your first Farmer’s Greeting. I wish you boundless harvest and prosperity, Friend.\"","...!","Noah looked at this astonishingly gorgeous being, at her vibrant presence, her genuine warmth...and calmly smiled.","\"And a boundless harvest to you as well,\" he said coolly.","Their fingers remained connected for moment longer than strictly necessary, the gesture lingering in space between them.","Then they separated, the moment passing as Elyndra began explaining details about the Sanctuary’s weapons and resources with enthusiasm.","---","Noah’s consciousness shifted, pulling away from the Wandering Territories, from the golden tree and Elyndra’s complicated presence, returning to his Early Veiled Shore where something magnificent was reaching completion.","He stood on the golden sands, his form perfectly still as he observed the final stages of construction happening in spaces that existed simultaneously within and beyond normal reality.","The Incarnaut Sanctis.","The Early Chamber of Blood.","The space where genesis of new Early Creatures would occur, where beings of sufficient potential could undergo transformation that would elevate them to tier of existence that current reality insisted was closed.","He thought about his interaction with Elyndra, about the collaboration she proposed.","In his mind, RUIN/EDEN’s voice emerged with tones that carried amusement mixed with professional assessment.","\"The Daughter of The First Farmer might pounce on you before you pounce on her. Master’s charms are unbeaten as always.\"","Noah shook his head at such words.","\"Stop playing around,\" he said, his voice carrying command wrapped in fondness. \"Finish Incarnaut Sanctis, the Chamber of Blood. Let us bring the newest Mana-Born Early Creatures to fruition.\"","He paused, his eyes blazing with tyrannical light.","\"Let us usher in...The Glorious Evolution.\"","HUUM!","RUINEDEN’s response was singular, her voice carrying certainty that transcended artificial origin.","\"Yes, Master.\"","And on the golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore, the Chamber completed its formation with pulse of authority that announced to existence itself that something new and impossible had just achieved manifestation.","The genesis was ready to begin!"]},{"number":4362,"title":"Chapter 4362: Chapter 4361: The Glorious Evolution! I","paragraphs":["Noah stood on the golden sands, his consciousness fully focused on this body after experiencing the complicated interactions in the Wandering Territories.","Here, in his sanctuary, in the space that was both his domain and extension of his very existence, something magnificent had reached completion.","The Incarnaut Sanctis.","The Chamber of Blood.","It rose near the center of the Early Veiled Shore like monument, its structure defying casual description through sheer grandeur.","The Chamber appeared as massive heart-shaped construct, but calling it merely \"heart-shaped\" undersold the architectural magnificence!","It was as if someone had taken the conceptual ideal of what a heart should be...the perfect organ pumping life through existence, and given it physical form using materials that reality itself envied.","The structure blazed with crimson-gold radiance that made nearby space pulse in sympathetic rhythm, as if the Shore itself recognized this as vital organ rather than simple building.","The exterior surface appeared organic yet crystalline, smooth yet textured with patterns that showed veins and arteries carved into impossibly dense material.","But it was the blue lines that truly commanded attention.","Countless brilliant blue vessels pulsed across the Chamber’s surface like living circulatory system made manifest.","They weren’t painted or carved...they were actual conduits of concentrated Mana, visible through semi-transparent sections of the structure.","Radiant blue arteries thick as tree trunks extended from the Chamber’s apex, branching into progressively smaller vessels that covered every surface. Blue veins ran along the Chamber’s base, pulsing with rhythm that matched Noah’s own heartbeat.","And from multiple points around the structure, massive conduits...arteries that could have served as highways, extended outward and sank directly into the Early Veiled Shore itself.","These weren’t just decorative elements. They were functional integration points, connections that bound the Chamber to the Shore so completely that separating them was almost an impossibility.","It was beautiful!","This was architecture that served purpose, form following function to create something that was simultaneously tool and artwork, machine and organism, construct and living entity.","Noah approached the Chamber with measured steps, his eyes tracking across its surface with analytical precision that cataloged every detail.","RUIN/EDEN’s holographic form materialized beside him.","\"The Incarnaut Sanctis is complete,\" she announced.","\"Integration with your Early Veiled Shore successful. All systems operational. The Chamber of Blood is ready to begin its purpose.\"","She gestured, and prompts began cascading across Noah’s vision with technical specifications.","|INCARNAUT SANCTIS - OPERATIONAL STATUS|","|Classification: Engine of Civilization (Tier: Foundational)|","|Integration Level: 100% - Bound to Early Veiled Shore and Noah Osmont’s existence|","|Function: Evolution Chamber for entities following the Way of the Mana Architect|","|Current Capacity: 9 Evolutions|","\"The Incarnaut Sanctis is connected deeply to you and your Early Veiled Shore,\" she said, her words accompanied by illusory diagrams showing the integration points. \"It functions as another Engine of Civilization, similar to your Resplendent Citadels but serving different purpose.\"","The diagrams showed how the Chamber drew power from multiple sources...from Noah’s Heart directly, from the Shore’s accumulated authority, from Perpetual Harvest’s continuous flow, from reserves of Mana that had been stockpiled through countless harvests.","\"It should become one of the foremost tools for your emerging Civilization,\" RUINEDEN continued, her tone warming with enthusiasm. \"The mechanism is elegantly simple: anyone following your Way can enter the Chamber. They walk through its structure, navigating passages that test their resolve and compatibility with your Principles. And when they reach the very center...\"","She paused for emphasis.","\"Their existence will be anchored with the Chamber itself. Bound through connections that cannot be severed. And once anchored, they undergo rapid evolution that completely alters their existence.\"","Her expression grew more animated.","\"Evolution, in its truest sense, is change over time. Gradual adaptation to environmental pressures. Incremental improvements accumulated across generations until species that began as simple organisms become complex entities capable of contemplating their own existence.\"","The diagrams shifted, showing timelines that stretched across eons.","\"But what we’re creating here,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, her voice growing more intense, \"is not that. This is not gradual change. This is not incremental adaptation. This is Evolution compressed into single transformative moment...the greatest change possible in the shortest period of time.\"","Her eyes blazed with excitement.","\"Those who enter the Incarnaut Sanctis and reach its center will have their hearts transformed,\" she explained, each word weighted with significance. \"Their existing cardiovascular systems, whether biological or existential, will be completely restructured. Replaced. Rebuilt from foundational level upward.\"","The diagrams showed the process in exquisite detail...hearts being unmade and remade, structures being dissolved and reformed, existence being deconstructed and reconstructed according to new templates.","\"They will emerge with Mana-Born Hearts of Early Creatures,\" RUINEDEN said, her voice carrying weight of fundamental transformation. \"Hearts that pump not just blood but concentrated Mana. Hearts that generate power continuously rather than merely circulating it. Hearts that mark them as new species of Early Creature never before seen in the Earliest Folds or current era.\"","She paused, then delivered the critical specification.","\"And their existence will be transformed tremendously,\" she continued. \"Because the minimal Complexity and Purity for Mana-Born Early Creatures produced from the Chamber of Blood would have been... 1 Quintillion.\"","...!","Would have been.","The phrase hung in the air.","Noah walked toward the Chamber with deliberate steps, his hand reaching out to touch its crimson-gold surface. The material felt warm beneath his palm, pulsing with rhythm that synchronized with his own heartbeat the moment contact was established.","\"Would have been, huh?\" he said, his voice carrying knowing amusement.","RUINEDEN’s smile widened.","\"Yes, Master\" she said quietly.","\"It would have been the baseline. But...\"","\"Since the Chamber of Blood was somewhat in line with the surprise that The Infiniverse has been forging for you, she added a supplemental feature that truly revolutionized the Chamber of Blood to grant...\"","HUUM!","\"...The Glorious Evolution.\"","The words seemed to resonate through the Shore itself, carried by authority that made reality pulse with recognition.","RUIN/EDEN’s expression grew more serious as she began explaining the modifications.","\"In conjunction with The Infiniverse,\" she said, her voice taking on technical precision, \"the Chamber of Blood was altered. Perpetual Harvest was woven deeply into its architecture, integrated so completely that every function now operates through that Principle’s framework.\"","The diagrams shifted, showing how verdant-gold light flowed through the blue vessels, how effort and harvest had been integrated into the Chamber’s very structure.","\"The additional feature,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"is Tiers of Evolution. Not single transformation, but graduated system that rewards those who can endure greater pressure with proportionally greater results.\"","She gestured, creating three distinct visual representations.","|TIER ONE: FOUNDATIONAL EVOLUTION|","|Requirements: Basic compatibility with Way of Mana Architect + Survival of initial transformation|","|Results:|","|—Complexity: 1 Quintillion|","|—Purity: 1 Quintillion|","|—Mana-Born Heart of an Early Creature (Standard)|","|—Designation: Mana-Born Early Creature|","...!"]},{"number":4363,"title":"Chapter 4363: Chapter 4362: The Glorious Evolution! II","paragraphs":["\"The First Tier represents baseline achievement,\" RUINEDEN explained. \"Those who enter the Chamber and survive the anchoring process will emerge with power that would make common Early Creature seem like children.\"","The second representation blazed brighter.","|TIER TWO: ENHANCED EVOLUTION|","|Requirements: Withstanding increased Mana Haki pressure + Demonstrating exceptional compatibility|","|Results:|","|—Complexity: 2 Quintillion|","|—Purity: 2 Quintillion|","|—Enhanced Mana-Born Heart of an Early Creature|","|—Designation: Advanced Mana-Born Early Creature|","|—Additional Capability: Direct Mana manipulation at scales that First Tier cannot achieve|","\"The Second Tier requires more,\" RUINEDEN continued. \"Not just survival, but excellence. Not just endurance, but demonstration that the entity can bear weights that would crush weaker beings. Those who achieve this evolution emerge twice as powerful as First Tier, with capabilities that extend beyond simple power increase.\"","And finally, the third representation blazed with radiance that made the previous two look dim.","|TIER THREE: THE GLORIOUS EVOLUTION|","|Requirements: Withstanding maximum Mana Haki pressure + Perfect compatibility with Way of Mana Architect + Existential resilience that transcends normal limits|","|Results:|","|—Complexity: 3 Quintillion|","|—Purity: 3 Quintillion|","|—Prime Mana-Born Heart of an Early Creature|","|—Designation: Prime Mana-Born Early Creature|","|—Additional Capabilities: Mana regeneration that approaches infinite, Authority over Mana itself within localized areas, Capability to grant temporary Mana augmentation to allies|","|Note: This tier represents peak achievement possible within current Chamber configuration. Those who emerge from Glorious Evolution are beings who could stand against Prime Dead Early Creatures and survive.|","RUINEDEN’s voice carried reverence as she explained the mechanism.","\"When an entity steps into the Chamber,\" she said, \"they will be anchored through those blue vessels you see extending throughout the structure. And once anchored, their existence will be forced to bear the Mana Haki of your... Infinite Mana.\"","Her expression grew more intense.","\"Mana Haki is weight made manifest,\" she explained. \"Not physical pressure, but existential weight...the crushing force of unlimited power pressing down on consciousness that has limits. It’s like asking finite being to hold infinity in their hands without being crushed by the impossibility.\"","The diagrams showed entities being subjected to this pressure, their forms straining under burden that exceeded their capacity to comprehend.","\"Depending on how much of this force they can bear,\" RUINEDEN continued, \"depending on how long they can withstand pressure that increases exponentially with each moment, depending on whether their existence proves resilient enough to be augmented rather than shattered... the entity will gain different tier of evolution.\"","She paused, making sure Noah understood the significance.","\"The pressure is real. The danger is genuine. Those who cannot withstand even First Tier pressure will collapse, their existences unmade by weight they attempted to bear. But those who survive...\"","Her smile widened.","\"Those who survive will emerge as new species of Early Creature. Mana-Born. Forged in your Chamber. Carrying your authority. Walking your Way.\"","Noah’s expression remained cool, but internally, satisfaction blazed!","This was his power.","This was what he could accomplish through combination of impossible Principles, reality-breaking cheat codes, and collaboration with entities who understood his vision.","He held the Incarnaut Sanctis...a Chamber that existed simultaneously within his Heart and manifested externally on his Shore. And ridiculously, with help from RUIN/EDEN and The Infiniverse, with Perpetual Harvest weaponizing effort into immediate reward...","He could now produce up to 9 Mana-Born Early Creatures.","Beings who could potentially possess power at 1, 2, or 3 Quintillion depending on their resilience and compatibility.","It was ridiculous.","It was broken.","It was his Civilization taking shape according to principles that current-era existence couldn’t comprehend.","RUIN/EDEN’s final words carried weight of profound acknowledgment.","\"This is the harvest and results of your effort, Master,\" she said. \"Everything you’ve accumulated, every Principle you’ve integrated, every impossible achievement you’ve accomplished...it all culminates in this capability. The power to elevate others not through slow cultivation but through transformative evolution that compresses eons into moments.\"","Noah smiled.","He looked around the Early Veiled Shore, his gaze tracking across the beings who had chosen to follow his Way or been bound to it through various circumstances.","Sigrid was already a given...THE Living Order would undergo evolution, would emerge with power that matched her conceptual significance. She would be first, or among the first, because her role was too critical to delay.","But who else?","The limit was 9 currently, though he knew that as he continued completing his Heart, as the Incarnaut Sanctis matured and integrated more deeply with his existence, that number would rise steadily.","And when it came to effort, when it came to beings who had demonstrated loyalty and capability...","Noah’s eyes swept across the Shore, cataloging potential candidates with calculating precision.","Henry, his Nepotism burning brightly.","Moiraine, whose paradoxical nature pulsed. The Emperor Penguin, Malphas...","Even beings like the Arch Lich Ra’Zan, who commanded Death itself.","And bouncing in the distance, occasionally phasing through solid matter with cheerful disregard, a particularly enthusiastic Blue Slime.","But as Noah’s gaze swept across these potential candidates, it stopped on a figure that made him pause.","Titano.","The simple-minded giant stood near the edge of one of the Sacred Water pools, his massive form somehow managing to project contentment despite his size.","He was looking around with expression of pure, uncomplicated happiness...just enjoying being surrounded by unique beings in a space that welcomed him.","No schemes. No hidden agendas. No complex motivations.","Just Titano, happy to be here, grateful for inclusion, content with simplicity.","Sometimes, the best candidates were the ones who didn’t overthink things.","\"Titano!\" Noah called out, his voice carrying across the Shore.","The simple-minded giant’s head turned, his expression brightening immediately into sheepish smile.","He scratched his head, a gesture that suggested embarrassment at being singled out, then lumbered over with movements that somehow managed to be both massive and gentle.","\"How can Titano help Brother?\" he asked, his words carrying that particular simple-minded cadence.","Noah looked up at the giant and smiled.","\"Go in there,\" he said, gesturing toward the Incarnaut Sanctis. \"I want to test something out. Your existence will undergo another change.\"","He paused, making sure Titano understood.","\"If you can withstand the pressure inside as long as you can, you will gain tremendous power. And if you gain power...\"","Titano’s eyes lit up with understanding, his expression transforming into excitement that transcended his usual contentment.","\"More power means more riches!\" he declared, the logic absolutely sound in his simple worldview.","Noah nodded, satisfaction warming him at the giant’s enthusiasm.","\"Yep. Go on.\"","Titano didn’t hesitate. No questions about danger, no concerns about transformation, no complex analysis of risk versus reward.","Just immediate, trusting obedience based on belief that Brother wouldn’t lead him wrong.","The giant approached the Incarnaut Sanctis with steps that made the golden sands tremble, his massive form dwarfing the Chamber’s entrance despite its substantial size.","But as he crossed the threshold, as he entered the space that existed simultaneously in multiple dimensions, Titano’s form seemed to shift, accommodating itself to interior that operated on different spatial principles than exterior suggested.","The entrance sealed behind him with pulse of crimson-gold light, and suddenly, every being on the Early Veiled Shore could sense what was happening inside!"]},{"number":4364,"title":"Chapter 4364: Chapter 4363: The Glorious Evolution! III","paragraphs":["Inside the Chamber of Blood, Titano stood in space that defied his understanding.","The interior was vast...impossibly vast, given exterior dimensions, and filled with those blue vessels he’d seen on the outside. But here, they weren’t decorative. Here, they pulsed with purpose that made the air itself hum with potential.","Thousands of blue conduits surrounded him, each one thick as his arm, each one carrying concentrated Mana that made his skin tingle with proximity.","And then, without warning, they pulsed.","The vessels suddenly blazed brighter, their blue radiance intensifying until sharp needle-like ends emerged from their tips.","The needles shone with green-gold light...the unmistakable radiance of Perpetual Harvest integrated into every aspect of the Chamber’s function.","They shot out.","Hundreds of them. Thousands of them. Mana-infused needles moving faster than Titano’s enhanced perception could track, converging on him from every direction simultaneously.","SHINK! SHINK! SHINK!","The needles pierced his skin.","Titano’s eyes widened with shock.","Something had pierced his skin.","His skin, which had been augmented by Lost Forgotten Principle to withstand attacks that could shatter Folds. His skin, which had never been broken by anything in his memory. His skin, which was supposed to be his ultimate defense.","And these needles just... went through it. Like it was nothing!","He tried to move, to pull away, to resist...but the needles were already anchored. Already connected. Already beginning their work.","His entire body was elevated into the air of the Chamber of Blood, suspended by thousands of conduits that had pierced through his defenses as if they weren’t there.","RUINEDEN’s voice echoed through Noah’s consciousness, providing real-time analysis.","|EVOLUTION PROCESS INITIATED|","|Subject: Titano|","|Current Status: Anchored|","|Mana Infusion: Beginning|","\"The process has started,\" RUINEDEN stated, her tone carrying clinical precision mixed with evident excitement. \"Immense concentrations of pure Mana are being poured directly into the very core of Titano’s existence.\"","The diagrams showed Mana flooding into Titano’s being, not just filling reserves but transforming the container itself.","\"Perpetual Harvest is nurturing every aspect of the transformation,\" she continued. \"Every moment of endurance is being harvested and converted into additional augmentation. Every second he withstands the pressure is effort that compounds into greater results.\"","Her voice took on more serious tones.","\"And alongside all of it, the weight of Mana Haki is beginning to be imposed.\"","...!","Inside the Chamber, Titano felt it.","Weight.","This was weight of infinity trying to fit into finite space. This was the crushing burden of unlimited power pressing down on consciousness that had limits. This was Mana Haki...the existential pressure of Noah’s Infinite Mana made manifest as test of worthiness.","Titano roared.","Not from pain, though pain was certainly present. Not from fear, because Titano didn’t really understand fear in complex ways.","He roared because that’s what you did when something heavy was pressing down on you...you pushed back with everything you had.","His simple mind didn’t complicate the situation with analysis of whether he could withstand this pressure or how long he could endure or what the strategic implications of failure would be.","He just... endured.","Moment after moment. Second after second. Breath after agonizing breath.","The weight increased. The pressure intensified. The Mana flooding into his existence grew thicker, more concentrated, more potent until it felt like liquid metal being poured directly into his soul.","But Titano withstood it!","HUUM!","Through sheer, stubborn, simple-minded refusal to give up because Brother had asked him to do this, and Titano didn’t fail Brother.","The pressure continued building. The weight continued increasing. And Titano continued enduring, his consciousness narrowing to single point of determination...withstand, withstand, withstand!","And then, suddenly, something changed.","His forehead began to glow.","Blue light emerged from his skin, concentrating at the center of his brow with intensity that made the Chamber’s own radiance seem dim.","The light coalesced, taking shape, forming symbol that pulsed with authority that transcended normal measurement.","An infinity symbol.","Brilliant blue. Perfect in its execution. Marking him as something new, something that hadn’t existed before this moment.","|THRESHOLD ACHIEVED|","|Subject has withstood sufficient Mana Haki pressure to qualify for Second Tier Evolution, and cannot proceed further.|","|Initiating Enhanced Transformation Protocol|","WAA!","Blinding blue light exploded outward from Titano’s form, flooding the interior of the Chamber with radiance so intense it leaked through the structure’s walls and blazed across the entire Early Veiled Shore.","Every being on the Shore felt it...that pulse of transformation completing, of evolution achieving success, of new species of Early Creature coming into existence!","RUINEDEN’s voice buzzed.","|EVOLUTION COMPLETE|","|Subject: Titano|","|Final Classification: Advanced Mana-Born Early Creature|","|Tier Achieved: Second - Enhanced Evolution|","|Current Statistics:|","|—Complexity: 2,000,000,000,000,000,000 (2 Quintillion)|","|—Purity: 2,000,000,000,000,000,000 (2 Quintillion)|","|—Heart Type: Enhanced Mana-Born Heart of an Early Creature|","|Additional Capabilities Granted:|","|—Direct Mana Manipulation (Advanced Tier)|","|—Mana Reinforcement (Can augment physical capabilities beyond baseline through active Mana circulation)|","|—Mana Sense|","|—Authority Integration: Lost Forgotten Principle has been preserved, is being analyzed and enhanced through transformation|","\"This,\" RUINEDEN said, \"is the first Early Creature created after you, Master. A new species never before seen in the Earliest Folds. A Mana-Born entity whose existence proves that your Way can produce wonders that traditional cultivation never imagined.\"","The blue light began to fade, and the vessels binding Titano retracted their needle-like ends with synchronized precision.","The giant descended slowly, his form touching the Chamber’s floor with gentleness that belied his mass.","For a moment, he stood there, processing transformation that had reshaped his existence from foundation upward.","Then he moved toward the exit, each step measured and controlled in ways that suggested he was still adjusting to capabilities that exceeded his previous limits.","The Chamber’s entrance opened, and Titano emerged.","Noah stood waiting, his expression calm.","Because the being who walked out of the Incarnaut Sanctis was... magnificent.","Titano had always been large, but now his form seemed refined by transformation. He appeared as golden giant...not just golden-skinned, but radiating golden light that suggested internal power made visible.","His entire body was inscribed with brilliant blue and white lines that pulsed in rhythm with his heartbeat, patterns that weren’t tattoos but actual manifestations of Mana circulating through enhanced physiology.","His head was bald, and at the center of his forehead, shining with authority that made reality pulse, was that brilliant blue infinity symbol...mark of his achievement, badge of his new status, proof that he had withstood weight of infinity and emerged stronger!","He came to stand before Noah, his movements controlled despite obvious eagerness to share his experience.","\"Brother,\" Titano said, his eyes shining with wonder, \"Titano feels... big! Free! Titano feels... magisterial!\"","HUUM!","Magisterial.","The word resonated nearby!","Noah smiled.","\"Yes,\" he said, \"Magisterial indeed.\"","...!"]},{"number":4365,"title":"Chapter 4365: Chapter 4364: The Glorious Evolution! IV","paragraphs":["This was his Civilization!","This was what he could accomplish when given tools and time and collaboration with entities who understood his vision.","If he had enough time, he did not doubt being able to produce entities with Quintillions of power in size. He could forge complex structure of beings who walked on a glorious Way of Existence, who stood together not through domination but through genuine advancement.","This would be the prime solution for The Fallout. Him attaining THE distinction by elevating his power and his Way, forming Civilization that could not be wiped out even by THE Loom itself!","He simply needed time.","After Titano, there would be others.","Noah’s eyes flashed as he looked toward thr others he’d already identified.","As he contemplated these possibilities...","HUUM!","He felt tremor across the Early Veiled Shore.","Not danger. Not threat. But recognition...of completion, of achievement, of something significant reaching fruition.","He felt Perpetual Harvest pulse with fervor, the Principle becoming even more solid in his existence, its integration deepening!","And deep within The Infiniverse itself, he felt something calling out to him.","Something that buzzed with anticipation. Something that wanted to be discovered!","Something that The Infiniverse had been building while he focused on other advancement.","The surprise.","RUINEDEN’s voice emerged.","\"It seems the surprise of Sis Infiniverse is ready,\" she said, her voice warm with anticipation. \"Master should be able to sense it freely. Let me know who else you would like to undergo The Glorious Evolution in the Chamber of Blood...I will take care of arrangements and ensure optimal conditions for their transformations.\"","She paused, then added with conspiratorial excitement.","\"While you check out... the surprise.\"","The surprise!","Noah smiled, satisfaction deepening as he felt the shocking brilliance of Perpetual Harvest that The Infiniverse could also utilize.","It seemed she had done something particularly shocking indeed.","His body on the Early Veiled Shore flickered, existence reorganizing itself as he moved instantaneously to appear in another section deep within The Infiniverse.","Inside The Frequency of Apocalypse.","Noah materialized in region of endings.","Swirling obsidian brilliance filled the space around him, seas of dark radiance that carried concepts of ending rather than beginning.","Entropy given form. Apocalypse made manifest. Cataclysm waiting to be unleashed.","This was where The Infiniverse stored and refined weavings related to conclusion rather than continuation...concepts that most beings avoided because proximity alone could collapse weaker existences.","But at the center of these seas of terminal authority, of The End...","Noah saw a world.","A blue planet.","It floated in the darkness like jewel suspended in void, surrounded by seas of blue Mana that flowed around it like protective atmosphere. And beyond that, green-gold seas of Perpetual Harvest swirled.","The planet’s continents and structure looked oddly familiar...eerily so, actually. The shapes, the proportions, the arrangements...","It resembled his home. The blue planet he’d been born on, that had been transformed long ago.","But beside the planet, drawing his attention with presence that commanded focus, stood The Infiniverse herself.","Her humanoid form was adorned in bejeweled green-gold dress that seemed to be woven from Perpetual Harvest made fabric, each gem pulsing with concentrated authority.","Her eyes shone with beams of green-gold light that suggested she was channeling power continuously rather than simply observing.","She bowed toward Noah with grace.","\"Master,\" she said, \"I have successfully weaponized Effort.\"","...!","She had weaponized Effort?","He smiled, floating toward her.","RUINEDEN’s illusory form appeared beside them, completing the trio.","The Infiniverse continued.","\"I weaponized Perpetual Harvest,\" she explained. \"Created system capable of granting you feedback of immediate harvest proportionate to effort you invest. Formed in the outline of your home...\"","She gestured downward toward the blue planet.","\"Below us is...The Cultivation Citadel of The Early Creature, Osmont.\"","HUUM!","The name alone carried weight! Heavy weight!","\"Let me explain,\" The Infiniverse continued, \"The Cultivation Citadel focuses multiple sources of existential weight...your Infinite Mana, my own authority as extension of your Early Veiled Shore, your Principles, and all other accumulated weavings of existence.\"","RUINEDEN picked up the explanation, her holographic form displaying technical diagrams.","\"All of this weight,\" she said, \"will be multiplied with effort through Perpetual Harvest’s framework. And all of it will be imposed on you constantly when you cultivate within this space.\"","The diagrams showed how the system functioned...layers upon layers of pressure being applied simultaneously, each one compounding the others to create burden that would crush normal beings instantly!","\"The mechanism creates stressors on your very existence,\" The Infiniverse continued. \"Constant, unrelenting pressure that forces your being to adapt or collapse. But because Perpetual Harvest is woven into every aspect, every moment you withstand this pressure is effort that immediately harvests reward.\"","\"Current calculations suggest a potential gain of approximately 5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity per day at maximum output.\"","BOOM!","What?","What?!","\"If you have body cultivating within the Citadel constantly, enduring full weight of imposed pressure without rest...\"","She paused, making sure he understood the magnitude.","\"You could gain 5 Quintillion per day.\"","The Infiniverse smiled as she pointed to the blue planet.","\"The Citadel multiplies weight of existence you must withstand,\" she explained. \"Not just doubling or tripling...exponentially multiplying. Your Infinite Mana becomes crushing burden rather than resource. Your strength and weight are effectively turned against you. My authority becomes pressure that pins you down. Your Principles become weights attached to your consciousness.\"","Her voice grew more intense.","\"The more multiplied weight you withstand, the more your Existence is compressed. Compressed existence struggles under burden that exceeds its capacity. But overcoming this struggle....enduring when everything screams to give up, persisting when collapse seems inevitable, continues to grant harvests of Complexity and Purity.\"","RUINEDEN added final technical details. She pulled up calculations showing different pressure levels and their effects.","\"Level One imposes weight equivalent to bearing your own power twice over. Level Ten multiplies it a hundred times. Level Fifty...\" she paused, \"...would make you feel like you’re trying to hold your entire Civilization on your shoulders while standing at bottom of ocean made from compressed concepts.\"","The Infiniverse’s final words carried both pride and concern.","\"I built this for Master,\" she said, her voice softening. \"Others may perish the moment they enter here. A minimum of 10 Quintillion would be required for anyone who is not you to ensure they survive even lowest pressure settings.\"","She gestured toward the blue planet below.","\"But for you, Master, this is training ground that will accelerate your advancement toward THE. This is where effort becomes harvest in most direct way possible. This is weapon I forged from your own Principle...Perpetual Harvest turned against yourself in most productive way imaginable. A methodology for the survival of The Fallout.\"","...!","Noah stared at the Cultivation Citadel, at the blue planet that resembled his long-lost home, at the construction that would allow him to gain 5 Quintillion per day if he could endure its full weight.","And slowly, inevitably, his tyrannical smile widened as he patted the head of The Infiniverse!","This was his Way of Existence.","These were his tools.","And with them, he would reach heights that others insisted were impossible.","It was time to begin...The Glorious Evolution indeed, this time, with his own advancement!","His overall people and Civilization had to be strong, but he...had to also lead by example.","He had to undergo levels of advancement that made everyone look upto him...and aspire for unfathomably more!","\"Let’s see...\"","He began to float towards the blue planet, his gaze briefly glancing off to side as he watched something distant- far outside The Infiniverse.","In the region of molten crimson blue mana that used to be regions of Collapse, he sensed the figures of Schrodinger and Leonore Rureaux approaching once more with a sense of caution.","Uniquely enough, there were currently three Schrodingers- a Living Paradox, a Living Concept, and a Living Elemental!","Noah shook his head while gazing at this scene as undoubtedly, they were here to confirm how things had ended and pursue their own solution for The Fallout.","The following of a Justiciar to their base.","But as Noah had seen with The First Farmer, the only effort to be reliant on was himself!","Whatever others were trying to do would merely be possibilities.","Side missions.","He was the solution.","\"As Anaximander said...one may simply have to become the storm!\"","HUUM!","His eyes were bright as he turned away from the distant scene of Schrodingers and went into the blue planet to experience...the weaponization of effort and harvest!"]},{"number":4366,"title":"Chapter 4366: Chapter 4365: The Glorious Evolution! V","paragraphs":["The moment Noah’s body crossed through the shimmering barrier surrounding the blue planet, the Cultivation Citadel of The Early Creature, something fundamental shifted in the relationship between his existence and reality itself.","It wasn’t pain, exactly.","It was weight.","His own power, that infinite wellspring of Mana that had carried him through impossible situations, that had defied the natural order of existence time and time again...it turned against him!","Or rather, it didn’t turn against him so much as it suddenly remembered that it was supposed to follow certain rules, certain laws, and those laws were now being enforced with prejudice that bordered on malicious.","The Infiniverse became an anchor dragging him down.","The Principle of Perpetual Harvest, still settling into the fundamental structure of his being, became chains wrapped around every particle of his existence.","His Infinite Mana...oh, his beautiful, impossible, reality-breaking Mana, became the very thing crushing him toward the planet’s surface with acceleration that would have made gravity weep with envy!","Noah spun through the atmosphere, unable to control his descent, watching the blue sky blur into green as the landmass below rushed up to meet him with enthusiasm.","BOOM!","His body impacted the continent with force that should have shattered continents, but the ground here was different- woven from concepts of cultivation and growth that made it simultaneously yielding and unyielding.","The crater that formed around his impact was perfectly circular, as if the very earth had been prepared for arrivals exactly like this.","Noah lay at the center of the crater for a moment, simply breathing.","Each breath was work.","Each inhale required conscious effort, as if the air itself had weight, as if oxygen had decided it would only enter his lungs if he asked nicely and proved he deserved it.","He pushed himself up slowly, muscles straining against pressure that came from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously. His legs shook- actually shook, as he forced himself to stand.","When had his legs last shaken from effort? When had standing upright been anything other than automatic?","Around him, through the haze of effort, he could see rivers of green-gold light flowing through the air itself.","Perpetual Harvest was abundant here, saturating the atmosphere with potential that should have made him stronger but somehow only made the weight heavier.","It was beautiful and terrible all at once!","Oh!","|CULTIVATION CITADEL - LEVEL 1 PRESSURE ENGAGED|","|Environmental Analysis:|","- Current Pressure Multiplier: 2x baseline existence","- Effect: All physical actions require 2x normal effort","- Effect: All existential authority usage faces 2x resistance","- Warning: This is merely the first threshold","- Note: Adaptation is the goal, not survival","|Movement Status: Severely Impaired|","|Mana Circulation: 1% efficiency|","|Physical Capability: Reduced to 0.01% normal capacity|","|Advisory: Even minor movements will be arduous at current adaptation level. Once full acclimation is achieved, when this pressure feels identical to normal atmospheric conditions, higher pressure levels may be imposed|","Noah read the prompts with eyes that watered from the simple effort of focusing. His hand, which he raised to wipe his face, moved through the air like it was swimming through honey mixed with regret.","\"So this...is what weakness feels like,\" he murmured, his voice barely echoing despite the effort it took to speak.","He had never felt so powerful and so pathetic simultaneously. The contradiction was almost amusing.","Here he stood, an Early Creature with Quintillions of Complexity and Purity, bearer of Principles, master of Infinite Mana...and he could barely lift his own arms without his muscles screaming in protest.","It was perfect.","|HARVEST NOTIFICATION|","|Minimal Effort Detected - Standing Upright: 12 seconds|","|Reward: +0.000001 Quintillion Complexity|","|Reward: +0.000001 Quintillion Purity|","|Note: Effort translates directly to harvest in this environment|","|Note: All actions, no matter how small, contribute to advancement|","|Note: The greater the pressure overcome, the greater the harvest reaped|","...!","Noah’s eyes widened fractionally, and even that small expression of surprise required muscular effort that made his face ache.","Standing here, simply existing under this pressure, was advancing him.","The weaponization of effort and harvest, indeed!","The illusory figure of RUIN/EDEN materialized beside him, her form shimmering with blue-gold light.","\"Master could attempt basic exercises to better adapt to the pressure,\" she suggested.","\"Push-ups, sit-ups, squats, running...all standard physical conditioning that will force your body to acclimate faster.\"","|TRAINING RECOMMENDATIONS|","|Physical Exercise Options:|","- Push-ups: Force arm and core strength adaptation","- Sit-ups: Build existential endurance through repetitive motion","- Squats: Strengthen foundation and leg stability","- Running: Promote overall circulation and pressure integration","|Additionally: Mana manipulation and Glyph utilization will face identical pressure applications. Conjuring even a simple fireball will require tremendous effort and control|","|The struggle itself is the cultivation|","Noah nodded slowly, the motion making his neck muscles burn. His existence pulsed with determination, and suddenly his upper body became bare, the simple act of dismissing his clothing taking more concentration than it should have.","His lower body was clad only in tight-fitting white-blue shorts that would have made Erikson proud, the kind of training wear that suggested serious intent without unnecessary embellishment.","His physique was on full display now...muscles that had been forged through impossible battles and cultivation that defied nature.","His torso was defined, and his abs formed ridges that could have been used as reference points for sculptors.","His shoulders and arms carried the kind of lean muscle mass that came from actual functional strength rather than aesthetic vanity.","Under the pressure of the Cultivation Citadel, those muscles were visibly undulating, pulsing with power that was being forced to work for every millimeter of movement.","It was glorious.","It was magisterial!","It was exactly what he needed.","Noah opened his mouth, speaking with tyrannical confidence that his current state did nothing to diminish: \"Let’s have the pressure of the fifth level.\"","The silence that followed his declaration was profound.","Even RUIN/EDEN seemed taken aback. The Infiniverse, that vast consciousness that had been with him through so much, didn’t immediately argue or offer cautious counsel.","Instead, both replied in unison.","\"Yes, Master. Be careful not to accidentally collapse the existence of this body.\"","...!","The air around Noah began to buzz.","No, that was too simple a description. The very fabric of existence surrounding him began to press, as if reality itself was being compressed, condensed, refined into something denser and more terrible.","|PRESSURE LEVEL INCREASED|","|WARNING: CULTIVATION CITADEL - LEVEL 5 PRESSURE ENGAGED|","|Environmental Analysis:|","- Current Pressure Multiplier: 10x baseline existence","- Effect: All physical actions require 10x normal effort","- Effect: All existential authority usage faces 10x resistance","- Effect: Molecular cohesion of physical body under extreme stress","- Effect: Existential integrity challenged at fundamental level","|CRITICAL WARNING: This pressure level is designed for beings who have already adapted to Levels 1-4. Immediate imposition may result in:|","- Physical collapse","- Existential fragmentation","- Consciousness dissolution","- Permanent structural damage to cultivation foundation","|Recommendation: Return to Level 1 immediately|","|Master’s Response: [REJECTED]|","The prompts appeared and were immediately dismissed by Noah’s will. He wasn’t interested in caution. He wasn’t interested in the slow, methodical approach that everyone else would take.","He was interested in results!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4367,"title":"Chapter 4367: Chapter 4366: The Glorious Evolution! VI","paragraphs":["The pressure slammed down on him like the weight of multiple entire Folds condensed into a single point. Noah’s knees buckled because the fundamental structure of his legs simply couldn’t support the impossible weight anymore.","He crashed to his knees, the impact sending cracks through the ground beneath him despite its reinforced nature.","His body wanted to collapse further. His existence screamed at him to release the pressure, to accept defeat, to acknowledge that this was too much too fast!","Every particle of his being was being compressed, refined, tested against forces that would have unmade lesser existences entirely.","His fingers, pressed against the ground, couldn’t even twitch. The simple act of breathing became a battle requiring conscious effort and determination that bordered on the absurd.","It was impossible to stand.","It was impossible to move.","It was impossible to exist like this.","’Good’, Noah thought through the pressure that threatened to crush his very consciousness.","’Impossible is my specialty.’","HUUM!","His eyes flashed with tyrannical defiance, blazing with determination that pressure couldn’t dim.","His mouth opened, and despite the tremendous effort required, despite the way his jaw muscles burned and his throat constricted, he bellowed!","\"I! AM! NOAH! OSMONT!\"","The words echoed across the Cultivation Citadel, carried by will more than sound.","His muscles undulated, pulsing with power that refused to accept limitation.","His Heart of an Early Creature blazed within his chest like a furnace that remembered it was supposed to burn through impossibilities.","His Citadels hummed like engines being pushed past their recommended limits.","Who was he?","He was someone who had faced down Early Creatures. Someone who had survived traversals to the Earliest Folds.","Someone who carried the weight of protecting his family, building his Civilization, defying the natural order of existence itself!","How could simple pressure make him kneel when he had so many other weights already bearing down on him?","’Rise’, he commanded his body.","His muscles screamed in protest.","’RISE’, he commanded his existence.","His bones creaked under impossible strain.","’RISE!’ he commanded reality itself.","HUUM!","And slowly- painfully, gloriously, impossibly...he began to move!","His left hand lifted from the ground. Just an inch. Just a single inch, but it was progress measured against forces that said progress was impossible!","|EFFORT DETECTED|","|Current Action: Attempting to rise under 10x pressure|","|Assessment: Tyrannical|","|Assessment: Foolish|","|Assessment: Magnificent|","|HARVEST ACCUMULATION ACCELERATING|","His right hand followed, pushing against ground that felt like it was made of condensed concepts rather than simple matter.","|+0.00001 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.00001 Quintillion Purity|","His back straightened fractionally, vertebrae stacking despite the weight trying to compress them into powder.","|+0.00002 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.00002 Quintillion Purity|","His legs began to unbend, muscles firing in sequences that required coordination his body barely possessed under this pressure.","|+0.00005 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.00005 Quintillion Purity|","Sweat poured down his face, not from heat but from sheer effort. His entire body was trembling, every muscle group engaged in the impossible task of standing upright.","This was the weaponization of effort and harvest.","This was what it meant to turn suffering into strength, struggle into advancement, impossibility into inevitability.","|ADAPTATION BEGINNING|","|Physical Structure: Reinforcing under pressure|","|Existential Framework: Condensing and strengthening|","|Mana Circulation: Pathways widening to accommodate resistance|","|Principle Integration: Deepening under strain|","|The Early Creature, Osmont, demonstrates the fundamental truth of cultivation:|","|That which does not kill you makes you stronger|","|That which should kill you makes you transcendent|","|That which transcends killing becomes the foundation of glory|","Glory.","Oh, glory!","Noah’s lips pulled back in a smile that was equal parts agony and triumph.","\"More,\" he whispered through gritted teeth.","HUUM!","\"MORE.\"","|EFFORT INCREASING|","|HARVEST ACCELERATING|","|+0.0001 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.0001 Quintillion Purity|","|+0.0002 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.0002 Quintillion Purity|","|+0.0005 Quintillion Complexity|","|+0.0005 Quintillion Purity|","The numbers climbed steadily, each moment of strain translating directly into advancement. This was different from the harvest of Inevitabilities or the cultivation from Sacred Herbs. This was pure, distilled growth born from refusing to accept limitation.","This was his Way.","He straightened fully now, standing upright under pressure that should have been impossible to bear. His body still trembled, still screamed in protest, but he was standing in the crater.","And if he could stand, he could move.","And if he could move, he could train.","And if he could train under this pressure...","The smile on his face widened as he contemplated what would happen when he finally adapted to this level, when the impossible became merely difficult, when the difficult became routine.","Then he would increase the pressure again!","---","Meanwhile, in the Earliest Folds...","The glacial region had transformed into a sea of Mana so dense that it had taken on physical properties. Blue-white waves of pure potential lapped against crystalline shores that hadn’t existed before Noah’s declaration of his Way.","Noah’s body, this iteration of him that existed eons in the past, stood at the center of this transformation, breathing out visible clouds of concentrated authority that dissipated into the surrounding atmosphere.","Two days.","He had been in the Earliest Folds for over two days now, which translated to mere hours in his current era. This was the longest Temporal Traversal he had managed before being forced to leave by circumstance or discovery.","The possibilities were intoxicating.","The dangers were even more so!","His other counterpart, Ozymandias, was currently rampaging through the endless forests of the First Folds, experiencing The Way of Hunger with enthusiasm that bordered on gluttony.","That body was devouring everything it could find...beasts, plants, even the conceptual essence of places themselves, growing stronger with each consumption.","If any of his bodies was going to be forced to leave the Earliest Folds early, it would be Ozymandias. The trail of devoured existence he was leaving behind was subtle but noticeable to anyone looking carefully enough.","But here, in this glacial region transformed by his declaration of Mana’s supremacy, Noah had time to think. Time to plan. Time to consider possibilities that existed when one had access to the past itself.","The most obvious application was spreading the Sparks of his Way of Mana throughout the Earliest Folds. He had them flowing freely across the Transcendent Folds of his current era, subtle seeds of his Way that let him grow his Civilization’s influence without direct intervention.","But doing that here, in the time before THE Loom, before the structures of power had fully crystallized...","’They would find me immediately’, Noah thought, his analytical mind running through scenarios.","THE Living Paradox. THE Living Emotive.","From THE Dead Order, he had already seen how quickly such beings could track him the moment he entered the other side of The Veil.","If he came under the direct scrutiny of any of THE Living Existences in their prime, when they walked freely through the Earliest Folds without constraint...","All his plans would end before they truly began.","But the possibility of growing his Civilization from this point in time, of nurturing something that could span eons, that could exist as a force from the past to the present...","It was too tempting to dismiss entirely!"]},{"number":4368,"title":"Chapter 4368: Chapter 4367: A Seed Civilization! I","paragraphs":["RUIN/EDEN’s illusory form appeared beside him, her voice carrying into his consciousness alongside detailed prompts:","|EARLIEST FOLDS CIVILIZATION SEEDING|","\"Master, if marks of your Civilization begin to arise in the Earliest Folds, THE Living Existences and THE Creature and THE Weavers, all of whom already have established Civilizations, will sense it immediately,\" she explained, her tone clinical.","\"The disruption would be obvious. The emergence of a new Way of Existence in an era when such things are being carefully monitored would draw attention you cannot afford.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","RUIN/EDEN continued, prompts flowing alongside her words","|POTENTIAL SOLUTION - HIGH RISK:|","\"You shouldn’t do it at all,\" she stated flatly. \"But if you must, the only potentially viable solution is to find a small, isolated group of existences. They cannot be Living Existences or Early Creatures, those are already connected to THE Living Existences through fundamental bonds that would expose any deviation in their cultivation.\"","|RECOMMENDED TARGET: Fold Dwellers|","\"Fold Dwellers exist below the notice of the higher powers unless they do something noteworthy,\" RUIN/EDEN explained. \"They are numerous enough that a small group disappearing wouldn’t raise alarms. They are weak enough that their growth wouldn’t register on the existential scales THE Living Existences monitor.\"","|CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:|","\"You would need to nurture this Civilization in absolute secret,\" she continued.","\"Strict instructions must be given to those in this small group to isolate themselves completely. They cannot interact with others outside their group. Ever. Not once. Not for any reason.\"","\"The moment they interact with outside forces, the moment their Way and power become exposed, they will all be killed,\" RUIN/EDEN stated with certainty.","\"And the threads of their existence will lead back to you. THE Living Existences will trace the source. They will find you. And you will follow them into nonexistence.\"","The prompts were stark, allowing no room for misunderstanding:","|ISOLATION PROTOCOL REQUIREMENTS:|","- Zero external contact","- Hidden location unknown to all but Master","- Absolute obedience to cultivation restrictions","- No expansion beyond initial group size","- No demonstrations of power outside sealed territory","- Complete suppression of existential signatures","- Emergency dissolution protocols if discovery becomes imminent","Noah absorbed this information, his mind already working through the possibilities, the implications, the terrible potential and equally terrible risks.","\"But if it works...\" he murmured.","RUIN/EDEN’s voice softened slightly, acknowledging the possibility even as she outlined its difficulty.","\"If it works, Master, the applications are profound. A small group of Fold Dwellers, given access to your Way of the Mana Architect, isolated from external influence, allowed to cultivate in secret for eons...\"","\"They would have time,\" RUIN/EDEN emphasized. \"Eons of cultivation. Generations upon generations advancing along your Way without interference. If they procreate amongst themselves, if they maintain discipline, if they somehow avoid discovery...\"","\"Master could potentially foster a force of beings reaching Quintillions of Complexity and Purity,\" she stated. \"Possibly higher, depending on how long they remain hidden and how effective they are. A secret army cultivating from the Earliest Folds to your current era, growing stronger with each passing age while the rest of existence remains ignorant of their presence.\"","Noah’s eyes gleamed with tyrannical calculation.","\"And they would only emerge at my signal...when I wish for it in the current era....\" he said.","\"Exactly,\" RUIN/EDEN confirmed. \"You impose an absolute command: they remain in isolation until the Leader of their Civilization sends a specific signal. Something only you can generate from the current era.\"","Noah stood in his sea of Mana, surrounded by the cold beauty of the glacial region, and made a decision.","\"Let’s go find ourselves a group of Fold Dwellers,\" he said with glorious certainty!","---","Unknown location, First Folds...an insignificant tribe.","The tribal village was burning.","Not with actual fire...that would have been too merciful, too quick, too clean an end. Instead, it burned with the destruction that came from overwhelming existential authority applied by beings who viewed lesser creatures as entertainment rather than equals.","Dozens of Fold Dwellers knelt in the central square of their settlement, forced into positions of submission by pressure that made standing impossible.","Their homes...structures woven from hardy wood and grown stone that had sheltered families for generations, lay in ruins around them.","At the center of this scene of cruelty stood an Early Creature, his massive form radiating power.","Ten Quadrillion Complexity and Purity, concentrated into a being who had decided that might made right and weakness made victims!","Before him, still defiant despite being forced to his knees, was the Tribe Leader.","He was younger than one might expect for such a position...barely into what Fold Dwellers considered middle age.","His face was lean, intelligent, marked by the kind of weathering that came from hard decisions rather than simple aging.","His eyes burned with refusal despite the hopeless situation, suggesting either tremendous courage or tremendous stupidity.","His name was Kael, and he was about to die defending principles that the Early Creature found amusing.","\"Why all this mayhem and fear?\" the Early Creature asked, his voice carrying false reasonableness that made the question somehow worse.","\"I just wish to lay with all the women in this tribe, and the rest of you will survive.\"","He paused, letting the implications sink in while his power pressed down harder, forcing several Fold Dwellers to press their bodies against the ground.","\"Is your dignity worth your lives?\" he continued, \"Come on, put your dignity and pride down. Fold Dwellers like you never held high levels of such things anyway. You’re insects pretending to be people. At least insects know their place.\"","...!","The faces of the female Fold Dwellers turned ashen. Some wept openly. Others stared at nothing, their minds already trying to distance themselves from what was about to happen.","Kael spoke, his voice ragged but unbroken.","\"Do all Early Creatures act like this?\" he demanded, knowing the answer but asking anyway. \"What will THE Creature think about you if he knew of your actions? You talk of dignity, but is this the dignity of the Early Creatures? Is this what strength means to you?\"","The Early Creature’s expression darkened instantly. The amusement vanished, replaced by genuine anger that suggested Kael had touched on something sensitive, some insecurity that even beings of tremendous power couldn’t fully suppress.","\"Sometimes,\" the Early Creature said coldly, \"weak insects don’t listen until one squashes one as an example.\"","He raised his massive leg, preparing to bring it down on Kael with force that would do more than kill...it would erase, would unmake, would serve as demonstration to all present that questioning one’s betters led to nonexistence.","The Fold Dwellers cried out.","Some in despair, some in rage. A few tried to rise, to fight, to do something despite knowing it was futile.","The leg began to descend.","And then...","HUUM!","Reality froze.","A flash of blue brilliance descended from above like judgment made manifest!"]},{"number":4369,"title":"Chapter 4369: Chapter 4368: A Seed Civilization! II","paragraphs":["In an instant, everything stopped, the Early Creature’s leg mid-stomp, the tears on the Fold Dwellers’ faces, even the air itself seemed to crystallize into stillness.","Noah appeared above the village, surrounded by waves of Mana. His eyes swept across the scene, taking in everything...the destroyed homes, the kneeling people, the Early Creature caught in mid-cruelty like an insect preserved in amber.","\"This will do,\" he said simply, his voice carrying across the frozen moment.","His gaze turned to the Early Creature, this being of Ten Quadrillion Complexity and Purity who had thought his power made him untouchable.","Noah didn’t attack. Didn’t unleash some devastating technique. Didn’t even really move beyond a casual gesture.","He simply exerted his Mana Haki...that aura of dominance born from Infinite Mana refined through impossible cultivation, and reality acknowledged which of them actually held authority here.","SQUELCH!","The Early Creature crumpled.","Not wounded. Not defeated. Not even killed in any conventional sense.","He simply collapsed, his entire existence folding in on itself like paper being compressed by forces beyond its structural integrity.","Ten Quadrillion Complexity and Purity, reduced to nothing by a casual flex of will from someone who understood that numbers only mattered if reality agreed they mattered.","Noah floated down grandly, Mana swirling around him. The ice holding the Fold Dwellers melted as he approached, though they remained kneeling...now from shock and awe rather than compulsion.","He looked at them all, these people who had been moments from either death or fates worse than death, and his eyes found Kael...the defiant tribe leader whose pride had nearly gotten him killed.","When Noah spoke, his voice was light, almost conversational, but it carried across the village with clarity that suggested every syllable had been crafted specifically for this moment.","\"Do you all wish to have true power?\" he asked, the question hanging in the air like possibility given form. \"Power that will make it so not even Early Creatures question your dignity or force you to kneel?\"","...!","His words descended on an oppressed people, on Fold Dwellers who had been told their entire lives that they were lesser, weaker, meant to serve or suffer at the whims of their betters.","Slowly, one by one, they rose from their kneeling positions.","They looked at him...this stranger surrounded by blue brilliance who had appeared from nowhere and unmade their tormentor with ease.","And in their eyes, Noah saw exactly what he needed to see.","Not just gratitude.","Not just desperation.","But hunger.","The hunger for strength. For dignity. For the power to never kneel again.","Perfect.","The silence that followed Noah’s question hung in the air!","The Fold Dwellers looked at each other, then at the collapsed form of the Early Creature who had been tormenting them moments ago, then back at Noah...this stranger wreathed in blue brilliance who had appeared from nowhere and offered them impossible things.","Kael was the first to move.","He rose fully from his kneeling position, his legs still shaking slightly from the lingering effects of the pressure that had forced him down, but his eyes were clear. Sharp.","He approached Noah with careful steps, stopping at a respectful distance before bowing deeply- not the forced submission of moments ago, but genuine gratitude mixed with caution.","\"Thank you,\" Kael said, his voice steady despite everything. \"For saving us. For stopping him. For... for seeing us as worth saving at all.\"","He straightened, and his expression shifted from gratitude to something harder...more analytical.","\"But in all my life, I have learned one fundamental truth that transcends all others.\" His gaze met Noah’s directly, unflinching. \"Nothing is free. Not truly. Not ever.\"","The other Fold Dwellers watched their leader speak.","Kael continued, his voice gaining strength.","\"We were just saved. Rescued from fates worse than death. And we are immensely, profoundly grateful for it.\" He paused, letting that gratitude register as genuine before adding the crucial caveat.","\"But it was not free. Our salvation came with a cost...perhaps one we don’t yet understand, but a cost nonetheless.\"","His hand gestured toward Noah, encompassing the power radiating from him.","\"And now, your words. This power you speak of. This strength that would allow us to stand against Early Creatures, to never kneel again, to claim dignity that’s been denied us our entire existence...\"","Kael’s voice dropped, becoming more intense.","\"It should also not be free. Because nothing of value ever is. And because it is not free, because there must be a cost, because someone must pay...\"","He stepped forward, placing his hand over his heart.","\"If it is okay, let me be the one to bear all its cost for my people.\"","...!","The declaration rippled through the assembled Fold Dwellers. Several cried out in protest, but Kael raised his other hand to silence them without looking away from Noah.","\"I will bear the cost,\" he stated with finality.","\"Whatever it is. Whatever you require. Payment in service, in loyalty, in blood if necessary. Let it fall on me alone.\"","His voice carried a kind of desperate nobility!","\"Give them the boons. Make them strong. Let them never kneel again. And I... I will pay whatever price that power demands.\"","The selflessness was so pure, so genuine!","Noah looked at Kael with eyes that had seen countless beings make countless bargains, and a smile crossed his face.","\"The only cost,\" Noah said, \"is isolation of you and your people. And a pledge of fealty to me. That is all.\"","He let that sink in before continuing:","\"I will not force you to do anything you do not want to do. I will not command you to fight battles or sacrifice yourselves for causes you don’t believe in. I will give this power freely.\"","His smile deepened slightly:","\"But sometime in the future...eons later, I may call upon you. And when I do, I will expect you to answer.\"","...!","The simplicity of the terms seemed to surprise Kael more than any elaborate contract would have. He turned to look at his people, at the faces marked by hope and defiance and desperate hunger for something better.","The women who had been moments from violation. The men who had been forced to kneel. The children who had watched their parents reduced to begging. The elderly who had lived too long under the cruelty of beings who viewed them as insects.","They all looked back at him with trust!","Kael smiled sadly.","\"The First Folds never gave us a warm welcome anyway,\" he said, his voice mixing bitterness with liberation. \"We can isolate ourselves from it. From all of it. If it means standing tall, if it means never kneeling again, if it means our children grow up knowing dignity...\"","He turned back to Noah, and his voice rang with certainty.","\"We accept. Isolation. Fealty. Whatever future call you make. We accept all of it.\"","...!","Noah nodded, satisfaction gleaming in his eyes. His hands rose, and suddenly Mana surged from him like waves crashing against shores that had never known oceans.","The blue brilliance wrapped around the entire village...not just the people but the structures, the ground they stood on, the very space they occupied.","Reality seemed to acknowledge that this section of the First Folds was being claimed, carved out, removed from the normal flow of existence.","The Fold Dwellers gasped as they felt the sensation of being lifted, of being isolated, of becoming separate from the larger fabric of reality around them.","Noah’s right hand swept through the air with casual authority, and space itself tore.","It tore like fabric being ripped by forces that refused to accept its integrity. The tear widened into a massive rift, and through it, the Fold Dwellers could see something that made their minds struggle to process...regions of Collapse, spaces where existence had failed, gaps between the structured reality they knew.","\"The Wandering Territories,\" Noah said, as if that explained everything.","|TEMPORAL AND SPATIAL DISPLACEMENT INITIATED|","|Action: Removing isolated settlement from First Folds|","|Destination: Wandering Territories - Stable Collapse Regions|","|Reasoning: Historical consistency suggests Wandering Territories remain unchanged through major timeline events|"]},{"number":4370,"title":"Chapter 4370: Chapter 4369: A Seed Civilization! III","paragraphs":["RUIN/EDEN’s voice appeared in Noah’s consciousness.","\"Master, the Wandering Territories are the only regions we know remained relatively stable when the First Folds eventually split into all the Transcendent Folds and Minor Folds. They exist in the gaps, the spaces between structured existence.\"","\"The First Farmer hid there for eons,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, her analysis flowing naturally. \"He was eventually found and tracked down by THE Living Emotive, but his sanctuary itself was not hidden, and he brought in Living Existences which included Living Emotive- he was asking to be found.\"","\"If we place this tribe deep enough in the Wandering Territories, establish proper isolation protocols, and ensure they follow instructions precisely... the probability of discovery drops to manageable levels. Not zero...never zero when dealing with THE Living Existences, but low enough to justify the risk.\"","Noah steered the bubble of blue Mana containing the village through the tear in space, guiding it into regions that existed between existence.","The Fold Dwellers watched in awe as structured reality gave way to something more fluid, more chaotic, more free.","Inside the protective bubble, Noah floated down to where Kael and the others had gathered. His hands moved with precise gestures, and suddenly dozens of Sparks materialized in the air before him.","Each Spark was a condensed node of pure blue Mana, pulsing with potential that made the air around them hum with recognition of power waiting to be claimed.","They matched exactly the number of Fold Dwellers present.","His voice rang out grandly.","\"Take the Sparks, and follow my Way. Be part of my... Civilization.\"","...!","Kael stepped forward first- of course he did, the leader taking the first risk as leaders should. His hand reached out, trembling slightly from anticipation, and touched the Spark floating before him.","The moment contact was made, the Spark ignited.","Blue Mana surged through Kael’s existence like rivers discovering they were meant to be oceans. His body lit up from within, transforming at a fundamental level as The Way of Mana integrated into his very being!","HUUM!","His eyes widened in shock and wonder as he felt something crystallizing within his existence...a Mana Locus, budding and growing, establishing itself as the foundation of power he had never imagined possible.","The other Fold Dwellers watched their leader transform, saw the power flowing through him, saw him stand taller and straighter as strength replaced the weakness that had defined their entire existence.","One by one, they stepped forward. One by one, they took their Sparks. One by one, they were remade!","|CIVILIZATION SEEDING: INITIATED|","|Status: Unknown variables detected|","|Assessment: Hidden in gaps between spaces of The Earliest Folds, an isolated Civilization has begun formation|","|Participants: 47 Fold Dwellers (23 male, 19 female, 5 children)|","|Initial Complexity Average: 847,000 (Scrubs)|","|Projected Growth Rate: Calculating...|","|WARNING: Results highly unpredictable|","|Note: Eons of isolated cultivation along Master’s Way could produce... interesting outcomes|","|Note: Generational advancement patterns unclear|","|Note: Mutation possibilities due to Mana saturation over extended timeline cannot be calculated|","RUIN/EDEN’s voice carried a mix of fascination and concern.","\"Master, we’re in completely uncharted territory here. Fostering a Civilization in the past to emerge in the present violates a great deal of things...\"","Noah smiled as he watched the transformations, his gaze sweeping over each Fold Dweller as they were initiated into his Way.","When all had taken their Sparks, when all were standing with Mana flowing through them like lifeblood they’d been missing their entire lives, he spoke again.","\"Your safety and mine is now in your hands.\"","He let that sink in.","\"If you wish to survive and prosper, isolation is critical until I call upon you. Nobody will find you. Nobody will even know to look for you. You will live here in peace while following The Way.\"","His expression grew more serious.","\"A tumultuous and chaotic time is coming in the First Folds. Wars between powers you cannot imagine. Conflicts that will reshape existence itself. You will be isolated from all of it. And you need to continue to be so.\"","The finality in his voice made it clear this wasn’t suggestion but fundamental requirement.","\"No contact with the outside. No exploration beyond your territory. No demonstrations of power where others might see. You exist in secret. You cultivate in silence. You prosper in isolation.\"","He paused, then added with emphasis that carried genuine warning.","\"The moment you break isolation, the moment you interact with forces beyond your territory, the moment you reveal what you’ve become... that is the moment you all die. And I die with you, traced back through the connections between us.\"","...!","Well...he had to scare them and himself a little. THE Living Existences were that terrifying after all!","Kael listened, his newly awakened Mana Locus pulsing within him as he processed these instructions. The other Fold Dwellers did the same, their faces showing understanding mixed with determination.","Finally, Kael spoke, his voice pulsing with resonance now that Mana flowed through him.","\"Sir... just who are you?\"","It was the question they all wanted to ask. This being who had appeared from nowhere, saved them from death or worse, offered them impossible power, and was now seeding them as a secret Civilization in the gaps between existence.","Who was he? What was he? Why was he doing this?","Noah’s smile widened, and when he spoke, his words carried across the bubble of Mana with the force of declaration.","\"I will be your Ancestor. The Architect of Mana, Osmont.\"","BOOM!","The name resonated through existence itself!","Noah continued guiding the isolated Civilization deeper into the Wandering Territories, his mind already working through everything that needed to be established, all the protocols that required implementation, every safeguard that could mean the difference between survival and discovery.","As he worked, RUIN/EDEN’s prompts flashed before his vision.","|LIMITATION ASSESSMENT:|","\"Master, I need to outline some constraints. The Chamber of Blood cannot be forged here in The Earliest Folds. Apart from it being impossible,the temporal displacement and signature of Civilization it carries would create existential signatures that THE Living Existences could potentially track and discover.\"","\"This means we cannot transform the Fold Dwellers into Mana-Born Early Creatures using the standard process. The elevation from Fold Dweller to Early Creature requires resources and methods we don’t have access to in this time period.\"","Noah nodded, already expecting this limitation.","RUIN/EDEN continued.","\"However, you could infuse them directly with your blood and concentrated Mana. Not enough to trigger immediate transformation, that would and may still create detectable signatures, but enough to alter their fundamental composition over time.\"","|POTENTIAL OUTCOME:|","\"Given eons of isolation, with your essence integrated into their cultivation, mutations could arise among them. Beneficial ones, hopefully. Their children, and their children’s children, cultivating in an environment saturated with your Mana...\"","\"There’s a non-zero chance that by the time you call them forth in the current era, some may have naturally evolved into something approaching Early Creature status. Not through forced transformation, but through generations of cultivation along your Way.\"","\"You also cannot leave permanent Mana structures that pulse with your signature,\" RUIN/EDEN added. \"No towers, no grand constructions, nothing that broadcasts your presence across time. Everything must be subtle, integrated, hidden within the natural flow of the Wandering Territories.\"","\"You have limited time before your Temporal Traversal ends. Enough time to establish basic protocols and seed initial cultivation methods.\"","Noah absorbed all these limitations with characteristic calm, his smile never wavering. If anything, the constraints made the challenge more appealing.","\"Understood,\" he said simply, and continued preparing his isolated Civilization with meticulous care.","He would give them everything they needed to survive. Everything they needed to cultivate. Everything they needed to remain hidden while growing strong enough that when he finally called them forth...","The smile on his face suggested he was very much looking forward to that moment!"]},{"number":4371,"title":"Chapter 4371: Chapter 4370: Collaboration and Civilizations I","paragraphs":["In existence, no thread stands alone.","The strongest fiber, woven in isolation, remains merely strong. But threads bound together, supporting and elevating each other, become something transcendent...fabric that can bear weights no individual strand could dream of holding!","Collaboration.","The simple act of many working as one, of powers combined rather than competing, of goals aligned instead of opposed.","It is, perhaps, the most powerful force in existence. More potent than any individual strength. More enduring than any solitary achievement. More capable of reshaping existence than any lone tyrant could ever manage.","But collaboration requires trust. And trust, in a reality where everyone seeks advantage, where betrayal can mean power and loyalty can mean limitation... trust is the rarest resource of all.","Yet when found, when nurtured, when wielded with intelligence and purpose...","Collaboration becomes the foundation of Civilization itself!","---","The Earliest Folds, an unknown location.","An obsidian Nest of Inevitabilities stretched across impossibilities, its structure pulsing with hunger.","Within this Nest, surrounded by Inevitabilities that pulsed with potential, THE Living Paradox had taken form.","Not his true form...that would be too revelatory, too honest, too vulnerable. Instead, he wore the shape of an Inevitability itself, a construct of contradictions made manifest, tentacles shining brilliantly!","Into this impossible space, THE Weavers arrived.","One moment they weren’t there, the next they had always been there, as if causality itself had been retroactively adjusted to accommodate their existence.","There were three of them, though calling them \"three\" was misleading. They were individuals and collective simultaneously, separate beings who shared consciousness, distinct entities who spoke as one.","When they spoke, their voices harmonized.","\"Someone seems to have interfered with Anaximander.\"","The statement buzzed in the air.","THE Living Paradox turned his Inevitability-form toward THE Weavers, his expression showing mild curiosity mixed with amusement.","\"Interfered how?\" he asked.","THE Weavers’ unified voice continued:","\"Making it harder for us to gain his trust. Sowing seeds of doubt about our intentions. Suggesting that perhaps our guidance isn’t entirely selfless.\"","They paused, and when they spoke again, frustration colored their harmonized tone.","\"And because it is Anaximander, all weavings around him are cut off. We cannot track down the culprit. His existence refuses to be threaded into any pattern we create. We see threads approach him and simply... end. Cease. Stop being threads and become nothing.\"","Their forms flickered.","\"Should we worry about this? Could it be THE Creature beginning to catch on to our plans?\"","...!","THE Living Paradox smiled.","\"No,\" he said with certainty that suggested absolute knowledge. \"THE Creature only just confirmed I had never been chained. He knows nothing of Anaximander. Our containment of THE Creature remains absolute. He sees only what we allow him to see.\"","His smile widened.","\"As for whether we should worry...\"","He made a gesture that might have been a shrug if shrugging existed in the form he currently wore.","\"Nah. If they were going to be anything major, they would do more than try to sow mistrust. They would act directly, intervene obviously, make themselves known.\"","His tone became almost dismissive.","\"It could just be an insect that came across Anaximander and said some profound things. Sometimes, even insects can be grand. Sometimes a random encounter sparks thoughts that change trajectories.\"","He waved one approximation of a hand.","\"Monitor it, certainly. But don’t waste energy worrying about every minor deviation in the pattern. The grand weaving remains on course. The Way remains on course. Civilization...remains on course.\"","HUUUM!","THE Weavers stood silently for a moment, processing this assessment. Their unified consciousness considered angles and implications with speed that would have made lesser minds fragment.","Finally, they spoke again.","\"How goes the progress with THE Living Emotive?\"","THE Living Paradox’s expression shifted to something more satisfied.","\"They are already by my side. Cooperation proceeds beautifully. THE Living Emotive has agreed to help forge our Sanctuary. Our higher levels of controlled Civilization.\"","\"Soon, we will begin the real work.\"","He leaned forward slightly, and when he spoke again, his words carried heavy weight!","\"Having multiple of us working on all this... this is what is grand. This collaboration is Civilization.\"","His smile became triumphant!","\"THE Creature is alone. We have isolated him beautifully. He stands singular, powerful but solitary, maintaining his principles while we...\"","He gestured broadly, encompassing not just THE Weavers but the grand plan they were all part of.","\"We embark on the path of a glorious Civilization! Multiple powers working together, combining strengths, covering each other’s weaknesses. THE Living Emotive, You three, Others joining as their self-interest aligns with ours....\"","His voice carried conviction!","\"This is how existence should work. Not solitary tyrants holding onto power through individual strength, but intelligent beings recognizing that collaboration elevates everyone involved.\"","...!","THE Weavers nodded in unison, their forms stabilizing as agreement settled over them.","\"Collaboration,\" they echoed, their unified voice carrying approval.","THE Living Paradox knew with absolute certainty that came from eons of observation and planning, that collaboration was critical in the emergence of a glorious Civilization.","Individual power was impressive but limited.","Combined power, intelligently coordinated, became something that could reshape existence itself.","THE Creature might be stronger individually. Might possess capabilities none of them could match alone. Might be the most powerful single being in the Earliest Folds.","But he was alone.","And they were many, working together, weaving plans within plans, supporting each other’s ambitions while advancing their collective goal.","In the end, THE Living Paradox was confident that collaboration would prove superior to isolation.","The strongest thread eventually breaks.","But woven fabric endures.","And they...were weaving something magnificent!","—","Kael stood at the edge of their isolated domain, his hand raised before him as he watched blue Mana swirl around his fingers like living water that had learned to dance.","The sensation was intoxicating!","No, intoxicating was too simple a word. This was transcendent. This was the feeling of limitation being torn away, of potential that had been locked behind doors he didn’t even know existed suddenly flooding through every particle of his being.","His Mana Locus pulsed within his chest like a second heart, rhythmic and powerful, each beat sending waves of energy through pathways that had only just formed.","He could feel it growing, adapting, learning how to channel more with each passing hour.","The Way of the Mana Architect!","That’s what The Ancestor had called it. A method of existence that didn’t just cultivate power but constructed it, built it deliberately like crafting something with purpose and design rather than simply accumulating strength through time and effort.","Kael concentrated, and the Mana around his hand began to take shape.","A Weave began to form as blue mana wrapped around him!"]},{"number":4372,"title":"Chapter 4372: Chapter 4371: Collaboration and Civilizations II","paragraphs":["A simple and crude weave of Mana, but it was his!","He released the incomplete Weave and simply stood there, marveling at what had changed in a single day.","His power had risen tenfold compared to his old self. Ten times stronger, ten times more capable, ten times more alive than he had been before The Ancestor appeared.","One day.","In one impossible, glorious day, everything had changed!","\"Kael.\"","The voice cut through his contemplation with a gentle authority.","The Ancestor’s tone carried across the domain despite the distance, as if space itself had agreed to deliver the message personally.","Kael turned immediately, his heart quickening from the reverence that came from meeting someone who had saved you and then given you tools to save yourself.","He found The Ancestor standing near the center of their settlement, surrounded by the soft glow of Mana that seemed to follow him like atmosphere acknowledging its master.","\"Ancestor,\" Kael said, bowing respectfully before approaching.","Noah, though Kael still thought of him primarily as The Ancestor, looked at him.","\"All things here will be left for you to lead,\" Noah said simply, the statement landing like a crown being placed on shoulders that weren’t sure they could bear its weight.","Kael’s eyes widened. \"Ancestor, I-\"","Noah raised a hand gently, cutting off the protest before it could fully form.","\"You need to be careful,\" he continued, his tone becoming more serious. \"Institute strict values for any newborns. For all generations that come after you. Not merely rules, but understanding. Not just commands, but wisdom that persists even after the reasons for it might become unclear.\"","He stepped closer, and Kael felt the weight of those words settling over him.","\"Instill in them the teachings of Mana I will instill in you. Show them the Way. Make them understand that this power isn’t just strength-it’s responsibility, it’s purpose, it’s the foundation of everything you’re building here.\"","Noah’s expression grew even more intense.","\"But most critical of all...more important than any technique, any Weave, any advancement...is the reality of remaining isolated.\"","...!","The emphasis on that final word made Kael’s breath pulse.","\"Until I call upon you,\" Noah said with finality. \"Until that moment, this domain is your entire existence. The outside world doesn’t exist for you. Other beings, other conflicts, other opportunities...none of them matter. Only isolation. Only cultivation. Only preparation for the day when I will need you.\"","Kael nodded heavily, the responsibility settling over him. \"I understand, Ancestor. I will ensure...\"","\"Come,\" Noah interrupted, his tone shifting slightly. \"Gather everyone. It’s time for an infusion of Mana.\"","...!","Within minutes, the entire settlement had assembled. Forty-seven Fold Dwellers...no, not Fold Dwellers anymore, Kael corrected himself. They were something else now. Something more. Citizens of a Civilization that didn’t exist in any official records, followers of a Way that shouldn’t be possible!","They gathered behind Kael, watching The Ancestor with expressions that mixed awe and gratitude","Noah stood before them all, and without preamble, without elaborate ritual or ceremony, he simply... released radiant sparkling blue waves.","Seas of Mana surged from him like tides that had been waiting eons for permission to flow. Blue brilliance washed over the assembled people endlessly, saturating them with energy so pure and concentrated that breathing it felt like drinking starlight.","The Fold Dwellers, the citizens of this hidden Civilization...gasped as they felt their Mana Loci expanding, their pathways widening, their capacities increasing beyond what they’d thought possible even after accepting The Ancestor’s initial Sparks!","Kael watched The Ancestor with reverence and couldn’t help but voice the question everyone was thinking.","\"Ancestor... just how much Mana do you hold?\"","The question seemed almost heretical in its directness, but it had to be asked!","The sheer volume of energy pouring from The Ancestor suggested reserves that defied all understanding of cultivation and capacity.","Noah smiled but didn’t answer directly, simply continuing the infusion until every person present was saturated, transformed, elevated beyond their previous limitations.","In the days that followed, they stopped asking that question.","Eventually, they became numb to it entirely.","The reserves of Mana from The Ancestor seemed limitless. Truly, genuinely infinite in ways that made conventional understanding of power seem laughably inadequate.","Hours became days. Days accumulated into a period of transformation that Kael knew would define the rest of his existence.","Everything he had known about Existence and power was being turned upside down, inside out, remade into something that made his previous understanding seem like a child’s fairy tale compared to brutal reality.","The Ancestor gave them power, and he showed them how to use it. How to shape it. How to build with it rather than simply throwing it around hoping for results!","Mana Glyphs began forming among them. Simple ones at first, crude attempts at capturing intent in structured energy. But gradually, with The Ancestor’s patient instruction and their own desperate practice, the Glyphs became more refined.","And at this moment, standing in the training grounds they’d established, Kael heard the voices of children...children who days ago had been powerless, who had watched their parents forced to kneel, who had faced fates they couldn’t fight against.","\"Primordial Fireball!\"","Three young voices called out in unison, and Mana Glyphs activated around them. Small fireballs, nothing that would threaten anyone remotely powerful, but theirs!","And they manifested through their will rather than begged from existence or stolen from others.","Kael couldn’t help but smile at the sight.","\"Kael.\"","The Ancestor’s voice again, but different this time. Carrying something that felt like... finality.","Everyone gathered quickly, sensing the shift in tone, understanding that something significant was happening.","Noah looked at them all, his voice echoing out.","\"My time to leave has come.\"","...!","The unwillingness that appeared on their faces was heavy.","One of the children...a girl named Lyn who had taken to Mana manipulation with natural talent that suggested she’d be formidable in years to come...ran forward and grabbed The Ancestor’s robe with small hands that refused to let go.","\"Ancestor, can’t you just stay with us?\" she asked","\"Walk The Way together! We can all cultivate together, grow together, be a Civilization together!\"","The logic was simple, pure, and heartbreaking in its impossibility.","Noah knelt down to her level, his hand gently touching her head.","\"We will walk the same path,\" he said gently. \"Just a little differently. I have my journey, and you have yours. The paths run parallel, but they must remain separate for now.\"","He stood, addressing them all.","\"I will see you all years from now. Many, many years. So many that you might wonder if I’ve forgotten you, if the call will ever come, if this isolation serves any purpose.\"","His voice became firm.","\"But understand this absolutely: only when I call for you can you come out. Not before. Not if you think you’re ready. Not if opportunity presents itself. Not if you face threats you think require outside help. Only when I call. Understood?\"","They all nodded, some with tears in their eyes, others with determination burning so bright it made their newly formed Mana Loci pulse in response.","Noah’s gaze found Kael, holding him with an intensity that conveyed everything that couldn’t be said.","\"Take care of this Civilization.\"","And then...","The Ancestor began to dissipate.","Not dying. Not leaving through normal means of travel. Simply... scattering into lights of pure Mana that drifted upward and dispersed into the atmosphere of their isolated domain.","Kael and the others watched in silence as their savior, their teacher, their Ancestor disappeared into particles of blue brilliance that would linger in their territory forever, a constant reminder of what they’d been given and what they were meant to become.","The silence stretched for several heartbeats after the last traces of The Ancestor faded.","Then Kael turned to face his people, his voice booming out!","\"Let us build the grand Civilization of The Ancestor!\"","WAA!","The response was fierce. Voices rose in affirmation, fists pumped into air crackling with Mana, eyes blazed with determination!","They would build.","They would cultivate.","They would remain isolated, hidden, preparing in secret for a call that might not come for millions of years.","But when it came...","When The Ancestor finally summoned them...","They would be ready!","And thus, a Civilization was seeded in the gaps between existence, in the Wandering Territories where time flowed differently and discovery was merely unlikely rather than impossible.","It would have time.","Millions upon millions of years of time.","Time to grow. Time to evolve. Time to become something worthy of the impossible foundation they’d been given!","As for what would bloom from it?","Oh!"]},{"number":4373,"title":"Chapter 4373: Chapter 4372: Collaboration and Civilizations III","paragraphs":["Noah’s consciousness flickered as Temporal Traversal seized him, pulling him forward through rivers of time that flowed in directions that had no names.","His eyes were closed, but he could see regardless, perceiving the multicolored brilliance of temporal streams.","Reality itself became visible as layers of possibilities and actualities interweaving, paths taken and abandoned existing simultaneously in quantum superposition.","His Resplendent Citadels blazed within his existence like beacons, acting as guides that ensured he returned to the correct temporal coordinate rather than ending up scattered across multiple time periods.","The entire Early Atlas of the Folds pulsed within him, that impossible map that shouldn’t exist but did anyway through sheer audacity of will and Mana that refused to acknowledge limitation!","The Early Atlas that made this ridiculous capability possible!","He was crossing eons in moments, traveling from the Earliest Folds back to his current era.","As consciousness began to solidify, as the temporal streams started to deposit him back into normal causality, RUIN/EDEN’s prompts appeared.","|TEMPORAL TRAVERSAL: COMPLETE|","|Duration in Earliest Folds: Multiple days|","|ACCOMPLISHMENT SUMMARY - EARLIEST FOLDS EXPEDITION|","|PRIMARY ACHIEVEMENTS:|","|Early Laboratories Infiltration: Successfully traversed the lands designed by THE Living Concept. Obtained complete methodology for Living Existential Armor construction. Aethelgard infiltration, learning of Everythings.|","|Anaximander Encounter: Established contact with Fold Dweller possessing ridiculous capabilities. Provided alternative perspective on THE Weavers’ guidance. Exchanged information regarding nature of The Way and existence. Parted on terms suggesting potential future cooperation.|","|Way of Existence Declaration: Successfully declared and embarked on a personal Way in region saturated with raw Early Existential Authority.|","|Hunger Experience via Ozymandias: Secondary body successfully experienced and integrated Way of Hunger through consumption-based cultivation. Devoured 847 distinct entities ranging from simple beasts to conceptual manifestations. Gained understanding of consumption as cultivation methodology (applications pending analysis).|","|Secret Civilization Seeding: Most ambitious and dangerous achievement. Successfully isolated group of 47 Fold Dwellers from normal timeline. Established hidden settlement in Wandering Territories with strict isolation protocols. Initiated 47 individuals into The Way of the Mana Architect. Left comprehensive instructions for generational cultivation. Projected emergence: Current Era, upon signal from Master.|","|PERSONAL CULTIVATION GAINS:|","|Mana Glyphs Forged: 42,555 (Total)|","The number appeared in bold, emphasized because it represented something that shouldn’t be possible.","Each Glyph was supposed to become progressively harder to forge after passing certain thresholds. Ten thousand Glyphs was considered a lifetime achievement!","Noah had forty-two thousand.","|Analysis: Addition of Mana Glyphs past 10,000 threshold encountered exponentially increasing difficulty. Each subsequent Glyph required 2.7x more effort than previous. By 40,000 mark, individual Glyph formation required concentration and Mana investment equivalent to forging first 1,000 Glyphs combined.|","|Master’s Response: Continued regardless.|","|Assessment: Tyrannical persistence. Inefficient by normal standards. Perfectly aligned with Master’s operational philosophy of ’if it’s difficult, do it more.’|","Noah smiled as he felt his body solidifying back into normal existence, consciousness settling into flesh that had temporarily been scattered across temporal coordinates.","He looked at himself...at his body currently filled with an overabundance of swirling blue Mana Glyphs that covered his skin like living tattoos, each one pulsing with contained potential.","The sheer density of Glyphs made his entire form shimmer with barely-contained energy!","HUUM!","More prompts appeared.","|PRINCIPLE DEVELOPMENT:|","|Mana Glyphs of the Cheating Architect: 125 (Newly Formed)|","|Mana Glyphs of Perpetual Harvest: 125 (Newly Formed)|","|Combined Effect: Principle Integration accelerating. The Way of Existence becoming more defined, more powerful, more fundamentally woven into Master’s being.|","|EMPOWERMENT UTILIZATION:|","|Daily Harvest Festival Endowments: Utilized 3 times|","|Empowerment Sources: Self-targeting (maximum efficiency)|","|Total Gain: +0.75 Quintillion Complexity|","|Total Gain: +0.75 Quintillion Purity|","|Note: Self-empowerment creates interesting feedback loops. Essentially using power to generate more power to use for generating even more power. A bit confusing...|","...!","These were his gains.","Noah’s smile widened into something tyrannical as he felt the power coursing through him, the accumulated results of days spent in impossible places doing impossible things with efficiency that would make conventional cultivation weep!","But the smile slowly faded as he focused forward, as his analytical mind began calculating what lay ahead rather than celebrating what he’d achieved.","Even this was minimal in his eyes!","Not objectively...objectively, these gains were obscene, reality-breaking, the kind of advancement that should take lifetimes compressed into days.","But subjectively, from the perspective of someone preparing for conflicts against THE Living Existences, against THE Dead Order, against forces that had existed for eons and cultivated their power through time periods that made his entire existence seem like a brief flicker...","He needed so much more.","He needed to continue violating every reasonable expectation of advancement.","Needed to keep pushing beyond what should be possible into what absolutely wasn’t possible and make it work anyway through sheer audacity and Infinite Mana.","Because anything less meant his Civilization wouldn’t survive what was coming.","|TEMPORAL TRAVERSAL COOLDOWN:|","|Time Until Next Available Traversal: 9 hours, 47 minutes, 23 seconds|","|Note: Master’s Temporal Traversal capability recharges faster with each successful completion. Projected minimum cooldown after sufficient repetitions: 6 hours.|","|Translation: Soon Master will be able to spend more time in the past than in the present.|","Noah acknowledged the information with a nod, his mind already planning his next Traversal, considering what needed to be accomplished, calculating risks against potential gains.","In a flash of light, his body shuttled across existence, returning from temporal coordinates to spatial ones, from the abstract realm of time-travel to the concrete reality of his territory.","He appeared on the Early Veiled Shore.","Home.","Or at least, the closest thing he had to home in an existence defined by constant motion and advancement.","The golden sands welcomed this body back with familiar warmth!","—","A distance away.","The Cultivation Citadel of The Early Creature, Osmont.","Even though days had passed in the Earliest Folds, time flowing normally while Noah’s consciousness had been scattered across multiple bodies and temporal locations...only a single day had passed here.","One day in the Cultivation Citadel.","One glorious, brutal, transformative day.","WHOOOOSH!","Noah’s body blazed across the blue planet’s atmosphere like a meteor that had learned flight and decided to show off. He circled the entire planetary body multiple times in mere seconds, his form leaving trails of blue Mana in his wake that took minutes to dissipate.","The weight pressing down on him was tremendous...Level 10 pressure, one hundred times the weight of his normal existence, enough force to compress most beings into singularities of regret and poor life choices!","Oh!","He wasn’t just withstanding it.","He was flying freely while bearing this weight.","Every few seconds, Primordial Fireballs erupted from his hands, each one forced to manifest under pressure that tried to prevent their formation.","They blazed into existence, bore the tremendous weight for moments, then dissipated as the pressure proved too much for sustained manifestation.","Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrms followed...serpentine constructs of pure fire wreathed in Mana, each one struggling to maintain cohesion under forces that wanted to unmake them but existing long enough to prove it was possible.","Noah stopped his circling abruptly, his body pivoting mid-flight to dive toward a specific region of the planet’s surface.","He landed in an area filled with heavy rain.","But calling it \"rain\" was like calling a tsunami \"moisture\"...technically accurate but missing the magnitude entirely.","Each raindrop that fell here was a battering attack of compressed authority.","The drops were dense enough to be visible as distinct projectiles rather than continuous water, each one carrying force that exceeded 6 Quintillion damage in both Complexity and Purity.","BOOM!","And they battered him!"]},{"number":4374,"title":"Chapter 4374: Chapter 4373: Collaboration and Civilizations IV","paragraphs":["They hammered into Noah’s body with relentless rhythm....not trying to harm him so much as constantly testing him, forcing his existence to prove it could withstand assault that would shatter most Early Creatures.","His muscular visage pulsed with waves of blue Mana, Glyphs covering every inch of visible skin and glowing with contained energy. Water streamed over the contours of his frame, following the lines of muscle that had been refined through impossible cultivation.","He stood there, letting the rain batter him, and spoke into the storm with calm authority.","\"Give me the overall results of the last day.\"","|CULTIVATION CITADEL - PERFORMANCE SUMMARY (24-HOUR PERIOD):|","|PRESSURE PROGRESSION:|","- Initial Level: 1 (2x baseline existence)","- Current Level: 10 (100x baseline existence)","- Adaptation Status: COMPLETE","|Total Adaptation Time: 23 hours, 37 minutes|","|Time Spent at Level 10 with Full Adaptation: 2 hours, 23 minutes|","|HARVEST CALCULATION:|","|Effort translated to advancement over 24-hour period:|","|Total Gain: +5.2 Quintillion Complexity|","|Total Gain: +5.2 Quintillion Purity|","|COMBINED ADVANCEMENT (Including Earliest Folds Gains):|","|Previous Total: 4.35 Quintillion (approximately)|","|Earliest Folds Contribution: +0.75 Quintillion|","|Cultivation Citadel Contribution: +5.2 Quintillion|","|CURRENT TOTAL: 10.3 Quintillion Complexity|","|CURRENT TOTAL: 10.3 Quintillion Purity|","|Analysis: Master has more than doubled total power in approximately 30 hours of real-time across multiple cultivation environments.|","...!","Noah stood in the rain, water hammering his body with force that would annihilate mountains, and nodded calmly at these results.","To him, it was satisfactory.","Not spectacular. Not worthy of particular celebration. Just... satisfactory.","To jump from 4 Quintillion to over 10 Quintillion in a day was acceptable progress by his standards.","He specifically avoided comparing himself to others.","That path led to complacency, to telling himself that Early Creatures took lifetimes to accumulate what he’d gained in hours. Tatiana had barely passed 4 Quintillion after eons.","Forgemaster Vulcan was considered remarkable in Aethelgard.","If he compared himself to them, he might actually limit himself by thinking his gains were utterly unfair and stupendous!","But he knew better.","He had to be even more unfair. Had to continue violating norms again and again until conventional understanding of cultivation gave up trying to categorize him and simply accepted that he existed outside their frameworks.","Right now, there were a great many things to be done. Glorious advancements had occurred in the last day...here in the Cultivation Citadel, in the Earliest Folds, across the Early Veiled Shore where his other bodies had been working.","And soon...","Soon he would see what grand results the isolated Civilization he’d forged in the Earliest Folds would produce.","Millions of years of secret cultivation, hidden from all of existence, emerging only at his signal.","The smile that crossed his face as he contemplated that future moment was tyrannical in its anticipation.","The rain continued to hammer down, each drop carrying enough force to shatter continents.","Noah stood in it, letting the pressure test him, and began planning his next impossible advancement.","He had a few things to complete before he would see the results of his Isolated Civilization!","—","Back in the Early Veiled Shore.","Noah stood there, breathing in the familiar weight of his own domain, feeling the way existence settled differently here than it did in the frozen desolation of the Earliest Folds or beneath the crushing gravity of the Cultivation Citadel.","His body here resonated with the echoes of his other selves. The one grinding beneath impossible pressure in the Citadel. The one navigating the currents of the Wandering Territories. All connected, all advancing!","But what drew his attention now was the fundamental change that had occurred here while fragments of his consciousness had been scattered across existence.","HUUM!","Blue-gold light coalesced before him, forming the illusory visage of RUIN/EDEN. Her holographic form manifested with precision.","\"Master,\" she said, \"The transformations are complete.\"","Noah’s gaze settled on her, patient and expectant.","\"The Chamber of Blood has succeeded beyond projected parameters as your selected Nine Mana-Born Early Creatures have emerged.\"","...!","Nine beings who had been immersed in the concentrated reality of what he was and had evolved!","Noah’s expression remained calm.","\"Show me,\" he said quietly.","RUIN/EDEN’s form expanded slightly, her gesture drawing his attention past the golden beach toward the vibrant Sacred Waters that stretched beyond. \"They are testing their new capabilities now. Understanding what they’ve become.\"","Noah followed her indication, his perception reaching outward, and...","BOOOOOM!","The distant waters churned.","The Sacred Waters were erupting, waves of early-formed mana crashing against themselves with enough force to make the surrounding space ripple.","The air above the water blazed with released power, scorching white-gold flames that left afterimages burned into the fabric of existence itself.","And floating above it all, suspended in the sky like a judge presiding over lesser courts, was Sigrid.","THE Living Order herself, transformed beyond what she had been.","She looked like something forged in the heart of absolute authority and quenched in infinite law.","Her white-blue empress robe flowed around her form.","The fabric itself seemed woven from compressed concepts of hierarchy and command, shimmering with an inner light that made the surrounding air bow in deference.","Behind her back, radiant blue wings spread wide.","Her white eyes blazed with power that made the atmosphere tremble.","She floated there with an expression that could only be described as magnificently arrogant...not the petty arrogance of the insecure, but the absolute certainty of someone who had touched transcendence and found it suited her perfectly!","Noah looked at all of this and nodded.","\"The transformation data,\" he said, his voice carrying quiet command.","RUINEDEN responded immediately, prompts materializing in his vision with clinical precision.","|TRANSFORMATION ANALYSIS - PRIMARY SUBJECT|","|DESIGNATION: Sigrid|","|CLASSIFICATION: THE Living Order |","|NEW CLASSIFICATION: Prime Mana-Born Early Creature|","|EVOLUTION TIER: The Glorious Evolution|","|CURRENT COMPLEXITY: 4.47 Quintillion|","|CURRENT PURITY: 4.47 Quintillion|","\"The Glorious Evolution,\" RUINEDEN continued,\"represents the highest tier of transformation achievable through the Chamber of Blood protocols.\"","She gestured, and additional data cascaded through Noah’s awareness.","|The distiction of Sigrid as the Resurgence of Order seems to slowly be waking, with expected changes of rapid elevation in Complexity and Purity, and unknown effects when she reaches the 10 Quintillion and 50 Quintillion markers.|","Noah absorbed this, his mind mapping the implications.","Below Sigrid, the Sacred Waters erupted again as multiple beings launched themselves upward, and Noah’s attention shifted to observe them.","WHOOOOSH!","Primordial Fireballs bloomed in the air...massive spheres of blue-gold flame that carried the weight of genuine existential authority.","Four distinct signatures blazed through his perception: Moiraine, the Emperor Penguin, and the Blue Slime.","\"The Second Tier of Evolution,\" RUINEDEN said, new prompts flowering before him. \"Significant transformation, though not the complete metamorphosis that Sigrid achieved.\"","|EVOLUTION TIER TWO - SUBJECT ANALYSIS|","|DESIGNATION: Advanced Mana-Born|","|SUBJECTS: Moiraine, Emperor Penguin, Blue Slime|","|COMPLEXITY RANGE: 1.89 - 2.31 Quintillion per subject|","|PURITY RANGE: 1.89 - 2.31 Quintillion per subject|","Noah watched them move through the air, their bodies shining with blue-gold luster that painted the atmosphere around them in shades of ascended power!"]},{"number":4375,"title":"Chapter 4375: Chapter 4374: Collaboration and Civilizations V","paragraphs":["Moiraine floated nearby, and around her the concept of Paradox had become tangible.","She launched a Primordial Fireball that somehow existed in multiple contradictory states...burning and frozen, present and absent, devastating and harmless...all simultaneously, until reality chose whichever outcome best suited her needs.","Her Mana Glyph of Paradox blazed behind her like a crown of impossible glory!","The Emperor Penguin descended from above, and despite everything...despite the power he now wielded, despite the Mana Glyph of Pride burning behind him like a second sun...he remained unmistakably a penguin.","His form radiated arrogance so concentrated it had become a physical force, making the air around him feel heavier with judgment.","His attacks came wrapped in disdain, as if Sigrid should feel honored to defend against them!","Who said his attacks could be avoided?!","Who said his attacks were allowed to fail?!","Who said?!","HUUM!","But the Blue Slime...","GLUB GLUB GLUB!","Its form defied simple description.","A shifting, translucent mass of blue-gold liquid that seemed to contain entire liquid Wheels of compressed Mana within its bubbly structure.","As Noah watched, the Slime merged with a Primordial Fireball.","The burning slime then surged toward Sigrid like a meteor that had somehow achieved sentience and decided to test the limits of imposed Order.","...!","Sigrid’s hand came down.","Cold. Precise. Absolute.","White light cascaded from her fingers, pure Order given form!","The burning slime stopped.","Frozen mid-surge, flames still flickering, bubbles still glubbing softly, but completely immobile as if Sigrid had reached into its fundamental code and changed every variable related to motion to zero.","\"Impressive capabilities across all Second Tier subjects,\" RUIN/EDEN observed. \"But there are four more you should see.\"","Noah’s gaze swept past the aerial combat, down toward the roiling surface of the Sacred Waters, and there...","Floating on waves of blue Mana, four figures that made the surrounding space ripple with their mere presence.","Henry floated with a body of wonder and pride, Nepotism flowing out of him all around as his power was ecstatic!","Malphas stood on the water’s surface calmly.","His body seemed constructed from compressed shadows and crystallized ambition, every line of his form sharp enough to cut concepts.","He wore a butler’s suit that looked woven from midnight itself, fabric that absorbed light and gave back only the suggestion of depth. Six wings spread behind him...not demonic, but something other, each feather a condensed fragment of authority that shifted between shadow and substance depending on the angle of observation.","Illusory crows surged from his form constantly!","Arch Lich Ra’Zan floated nearby, and his metamorphosis had been perhaps the most dramatic of all.","The skeletal form remained, but the bones themselves now appeared carved from compressed existential authority rather than simple calcium.","Blue-gold energy flowed through him, and his empty eye sockets blazed with flames that were the idea of fire, purified to its essential concept and given burning form.","And the Queen of Matter...","She sat cross-legged on the water’s surface in meditation, but the space around her danced with tomes and grimoires. She looked around constantly as she needed to record absolutely everything!","\"These four,\" RUINEDEN said, \"also achieved The Glorious Evolution. Prime Mana-Born Early Creatures.\"","New prompts materialized.","|GLORIOUS EVOLUTION - ADDITIONAL SUBJECTS|","|SUBJECTS: Henry, Malphas, Arch Lich Ra’Zan, The Queen of Matter|","|COMPLEXITY RANGE: 3.12 - 3.94 Quintillion|","|PURITY RANGE: 3.12 - 3.94 Quintillion|","Noah stood there on the golden sands, his perception drinking in every detail of the nine beings who had undergone transformation through exposure to his concentrated essence.","His people.","His Civilization!","The smile that touched Noah’s lips was small, barely there, but it carried satisfaction.","They were magnificent.","And they had no idea how much further they could go.","He took a single step forward.","PAH!",".. and existence folded.","The distance between where he stood on the beach and where he chose to be in the sky simply... ceased to matter. Space acknowledged his will and rearranged itself accordingly, placing him exactly where he intended without the inconvenient process of traversing the space between.","He manifested near Sigrid, floating in the air above the roiling Sacred Waters, and nine pairs of eyes locked onto him instantly.","The combat ceased immediately.","\"Master,\" Malphas rose as he said, and the single word carried depths.","Noah’s gaze swept across all nine of them.","\"It seems,\" he said, \"you have all attained new power.\"","Then his smile widened slightly, and something shifted in his tone.","\"Let us put it to the test.\"","The surrounding atmosphere compressed, as if reality itself was holding its breath.","\"Whoever can manage to touch me...\" He paused, letting the weight of the challenge settle. \"I will ensure Harvest sufficient to at least double your current power.\"","HUUM!","The silence that followed was profound.","Double their power.","All of them wanted to utter...say less!","And then-","BOOM!","Reality fractured.","Malphas, Sigrid, and Arch Lich Ra’Zan manifested beside Noah simultaneously, each one moving at speeds that defied their massive Complexity.","Their hands extended toward his form, fingers reaching for contact that would secure impossible rewards...","WAP!","Noah was already elsewhere.","He hovered there, expression carrying mild interest.","\"Even with your terrifying perception and power exceeding three Quintillion,\" he observed, his tone conversational, \"you moved as if through thick, heavy water.\"","He let that settle for a moment.","He could withstand one hundred times his normal existential weight in the Cultivation Citadel. This...atmosphere felt like moving through a pleasant dream!","His smile carried challenge.","\"Come. I’ve barely used a percentage of my power.\"","...!","The words were a detonation.","RAAA!","They erupted.","Not just the three who had initially attacked, all of them!","Henry and all others joined in!","It was coordinated. It was overwhelming. It represented the combined assault of nine Mana-Born Early Creatures whose individual power could threaten entire Folds.","And...","Noah evaded it all without apparent effort.","\"BROTHER!\"","He drifted between Titano’s grasp like smoke passing through grasping fingers.","All other attacks could not even reach him!","He reappeared in the center of their formation, surrounded on all sides, completely untouched.","They deployed their Mana Glyphs.","BOOOOM!","The sky erupted with concentrated authority.","Primordial Fireballs the size of buildings. Paradoxes that made causality weep. Order-based constraints that tried to rewrite the fundamental laws governing Noah’s existence...","All of it crashed toward Noah in perfect synchronization, representing the combined might of nine beings!","Noah raised one hand.","Blue light leaked from his form...not much, just a fragment of what he carried, barely registering as a percentage of his full capability.","But it was his Haki, the conceptual weight of his tyrannical authority given form, and even this shred carried pressure that made existence acknowledge its presence.","BOOM!","The blue light expanded outward in a wave.","The wave of Haki crashed into all nine Mana-Born Early Creatures simultaneously.","BOOM!","And...","SPLASH! SPLASH! SPLASH!","They fell.","Sigrid, despite her perfect control and Order-authority, plummeted from the sky in an arc of white-gold light.","Titano, massive and seemingly immovable, crashed through the air like a meteor.","Henry and Moiraine, for all their skill and paradoxes, tumbled before impact.","The Emperor Penguin’s Pride couldn’t prevent his descent!","The Blue Slime made distressed glubbing sounds.","Malphas’s wings crumpled. Ra’Zan’s jaws cackled, and The Queen of Matter was writing snd recording everything with a fervant expression!","They struck the Early Sacred Waters with impacts that sent geysers of blue-gold liquid erupting hundreds of feet into the air.","The beach trembled.","The sky rippled.","Noah remained hovering above them all, his form radiating casual, effortless authority.","\"That,\" he called down, \"was barely five percent of my power.\"","He let the words settle.","\"Come on.\"","His visage pulsed with glorious tyranny, blue-gold light cascading from his form in waves that made the surrounding atmosphere hum with potential!","Below, nine Mana-Born Early Creatures began pulling themselves from the Sacred Waters, their expressions carrying determination.","They would try again. And again. And again, until either they succeeded or exhausted themselves in the attempt.","It was exactly what Noah had wanted to see.","—","Far away, back in the crushing pressure of the Cultivation Citadel of The Early Creature, Noah’s other body stirred from rest.","Every breath required cutting through resistance. Every thought moved through atmospheric weight that tried to slow even consciousness itself.","RUIN/EDEN’s illusory form bloomed beside him, her holographic features carrying focused intensity.","\"Master,\" she said without preamble. \"The Justiciar has made its appearance in the Transcendent Quantum Folds.\"","Noah’s eyes opened.","The exhaustion didn’t vanish, but his focus sharpened immediately.","This was a moment they’d been preparing form...the experiment that would reveal critical intelligence about their enemies’ operational structure.","\"Timeline,\" he said simply.","\"Moving through populated regions with systematic efficiency. Estimates suggest the massacre will begin within eight minutes.\"","Prompts materialized before him.","|JUSTICIAR OBSERVATION - REAL-TIME TRACKING|","|CLASSIFICATION: Enforcement Entity|","|COMPLEXITY: 1.04 Quintillion|","|CURRENT LOCATION: Transcendent Quantum Folds, Sector 7, Aeternitas Quantumavine|","Noah pulled himself to sitting position.","\"Our preparations?\" he asked.","\"Complete,\" RUIN/EDEN replied. \"All protocols are in place and operational.\"","New prompts expanded before him in layers.","|OPERATION: SHADOW THEATER|","|STATUS: Fully Deployed|","|PRIMARY OBJECTIVE: Intelligence gathering via tracking|","|SECONDARY OBJECTIVE: Zero casualties among actual population|","\"Every genuine lifeform in the Justiciar’s projected path has been relocated,\" RUIN/EDEN continued.","\"In their place,\" RUIN/EDEN said, \"I’ve deployed sophisticated illusions. These aren’t simple visual constructs...they’re full-spectrum existential replicas utilizing your Resplendent Citadels of Dreams, Fantasia, and Illusions.\"","|ILLUSION SPECIFICATIONS:|","|Complexity Mimicry: Perfect replication of each target’s existential signature|","|Behavioral Authenticity: Programmed behavior patterns derived from extensive observational data|","|Sensory Response: React to all stimuli exactly as genuine beings would|","|Death Simulation: Display appropriate destruction patterns when terminated|","|Energy Signature: Generate false life-force readings indistinguishable from actual existence|","|Detection Resistance: Tested against perception abilities up to 4.5 Quintillion complexity|","|Justiciar Capability: 1.04 Quintillion - insufficient to distinguish illusion from reality|","\"When the Justiciar completes its massacre,\" RUIN/EDEN continued, \"it will be destroying sophisticated illusions while believing it’s accomplished its mission.","Noah absorbed this, his mind mapping the expected flow of events. The Justiciar would complete its task, confident in its success. And then...","\"The tracking protocol,\" he said.","\"Embedded within each illusion’s ’death energy,’\" RUIN/EDEN confirmed. \"When the Justiciar terminates an illusion, it will be painted with invisible Mana lines. Those signatures contain tracking elements the Justiciar cannot detect.\"","|TRACKING PROTOCOL:|","|Tracking Range: Unlimited|","|Information Gathered: Complete path taken, final destination, any intermediate stops|","|Expected Outcome: Direct line to Justiciar’s base of operations|","\"When it returns to wherever these entities are based,\" RUIN/EDEN concluded, \"we’ll have complete tracking data. Oh, Schrodinger and his bodies will also likely be following.\"","Noah nodded slowly, his muscles protesting the movement under pressure.","\"The preparations are complete then,\" he said.","\"All elements are in position,\" RUIN/EDEN confirmed. \"We observe, we track, we learn. And we do so without sacrificing a single actual life.\"","Noah pulled himself fully upright, his body screaming protests against the crushing weight of the Citadel. But his eyes carried satisfaction beyond physical strain.","This was strategy operating on the scale existence demanded. Not simple combat or direct confrontation, but layered operations that turned enemy actions into intelligence gathering.","\"Now,\" he said, his voice carrying anticipation that made the surrounding air compress slightly, \"let us see the results of the experiment.\"","He breathed out, centering himself despite the crushing pressure.","\"Let us see what glory came from... the Isolated Civilization.\"","HUUM!","He had given them endless Mana. The Way of Mana. And then he had stepped back, allowing them to develop independently, to find their own solutions, to forge their own path toward survival.","He wondered what they had become.","What they had built when given such a Way of Existence and resources and desperate need.","What answers they had discovered when forced to advance without his direct guidance.","His tyrannical heart pulsed with anticipation, blue-gold light leaking from his form even under the Citadel’s crushing weight.","Time to see what his people could accomplish when necessity and Infinite Mana collided!","Time to see if isolated desperation could forge solutions even he hadn’t anticipated.","Time to see just what glory would emerge from a Civilization given everything it needed except certainty!"]},{"number":4376,"title":"Chapter 4376: Chapter 4375: Oh, Shit I","paragraphs":["The region of Collapse outside the Infiniverse had become something else entirely.","Noah’s body manifested there...another instance of himself, another fragment of his divided consciousness operating independently while maintaining connection to the whole.","In the surroundings...","Molten crimson-blue stretched in every direction.","The mana flames didn’t behave like normal fire. They moved with purpose, with memory, as if the violence that created them had been burned into the fabric of space and refused to fade. Crimson-blue waves crashed against nothing, creating light that shouldn’t exist.","It had been a day since that battle!","The region still burned.","Noah floated there, his perception drinking in the scope of destruction he’d caused, and his mind turned to darker considerations.","’How heavy will THE Dead Order’s response be?’","It had been almost a day since all this occured.","Tatiana and the others should be returnig from death soon...the question was whether they would be like normal Dead Existences and return at the place they died, of if they would be pulled to the other Side of The Veil.","They would respond. The only questions were when, and with what force.","And beyond that consideration...","’What of THE Creature himself? Is he truly Dead on the other side of the veil?’","The being who had visited The First Farmer’s cultivation fields eons ago. The entity whose authority seemed woven into the very concept of Early Creatures. THE Creature, whose presence made even THE Living Existences had followed behind.","Was he with THE Dead Order? Was he separate? Was he watching these events unfold with interest?","Noah didn’t know.","And that ignorance bothered him.","He shook his head, dispersing the speculation with conscious effort.","Too many enemies. Too many unknown variables. Too many existential threats operating on scales that made even his recent advancement seem inadequate.","But his actions today, what he was about to do...would help address that particular problem.","He breathed out slowly, centering himself, and his body began to pulse with a unique signature of mana.","Not his normal blue-gold light. This was something more specific, more targeted...a frequency that resonated with connections he’d forged long ago and then deliberately left dormant.","HUUM!","The surrounding region of Collapse responded, becoming more chaotic as he extended tendrils of his mana into the unstable fabric of existence. The tendrils spread outward, seeking specific pathways.","They reached toward the Wandering Territories, threading through dimensional boundaries and spatial distortions with purpose that suggested they knew exactly where they were going.","And then...","BOOM!","A silent wave of blue exploded outward, spreading through existence like a signal. It carried no words, no complex message...just pure intent crystallized into a single concept.","\"Come,\" Noah said quietly.","The word hung in the molten crimson-blue air, simple and absolute.","\"My Isolated Civilization. My fruit that I nurtured eons ago and left untouched. Bloom. Let me see what you have become.\"","HUUM!","The words formed a chant in his mind, resonating through his existence with the weight of invocation!","He had planted seeds long ago. Given them Mana and the knowledge of wonders. And then he had stepped back, allowing them to grow without his direct interference.","Isolated Cultivation.","An entire Civilization forced to develop independently, to find their own solutions, to forge their own path toward power sufficient to survive the end of all things.","Now he called them forth.","Now he would see what desperate necessity and infinite resources had created!","...!","He floated there in the burning aftermath of his recent battle, his perception expanded outward, waiting.","Silence pressed in around him!","’Did everything go well?’","The thought crossed his mind with uncharacteristic uncertainty. He had given Kael strict instructions during the days he’d spent establishing the Isolated Civilization.","When the call came, Kael alone should emerge initially. A single representative to report on their development before Noah visited the full scope of what they’d become.","So he waited.","One second passed.","Three seconds.","Seven seconds.","By the ninth second, Noah’s perception sharpened.","No response. No spatial distortion indicating incoming transit. No...","...!","He blinked.","He didn’t sense anyone coming through normal channels, but he felt...","\"Oh?\"","Something inside him.","Deep in the architecture of his existence, in the fundamental structure of what he was...something pulsed. Something vast and terrible and glorious all at once, building pressure like water behind a dam that was about to-","\"Oh, shit.\"","...!","Two words, barely enough time to process the implications, and then...","BOOOOOM!","With his figure at the epicenter, a terrifying explosion of pure blue mana erupted outward.","A deluge of crystallized power that surged from him in waves that crossed Gigaparsecs in seconds and continued flowing, an ocean’s worth of authority pouring into existence from sources that shouldn’t have that much to give!","His Complexity exploded upward.","His Purity surged beyond previous thresholds.","And his Way of Existence, the fundamental architecture of what he represented, the conceptual framework upon which his entire being was constructed...became utterly sublime.","HUUM!","|CRITICAL EVENT DETECTED|","|ISOLATED CIVILIZATION PROTOCOL - ACTIVATION COMPLETE|","|An Isolated Civilization following your Way of Existence has been sensed and brought into resonance with your primary existence!|","|STATUS: ACTIVE CIVILIZATION DETECTED|","|Classification: Mature Development (Exceeds All Projected Parameters)|","|Time Elapsed (Subjective): Eons of years within isolated temporal frame|","|Time Elapsed (Objective): 1 day external timeline|","|Population: 47 Original Seed Members + 892,473 Second Generation + 4,729,384 Third Generation + Additional Descendants|","|The immensity of your Way of Existence within this Isolated Civilization far exceeds sustainable integration thresholds!|","|As the Architect and Head of this Civilization, as the Origin Point of their Way of Existence, you are being granted boons reflecting their advancement!|","|WARNING: Boon magnitude exceeds normal processing capacity!|","|WARNING: Existential structure undergoing rapid transformation!|","|WARNING: All advancement is being compressed into singular moment of recognition!|","The feeling was immense.","Noah’s eyes blazed with light...literally as beams of pure mana-infused radiance shot from them, crossing the distance from where he floated to the distant boundaries of the Transcendent Law Folds in an instant.","Beams of blue-gold power that carved paths through space itself, marking territory, claiming authority, announcing presence to anything with sufficient perception to witness.","His mouth opened, and what emerged was a bellow of pure mana...sound that carried existential weight, a roar that made the surrounding Collapse ripple with acknowledgment!","HUUM!"]},{"number":4377,"title":"Chapter 4377: Chapter 4376: Oh, Shit II","paragraphs":["He wasn’t in pain.","He was ascending, and his body struggled to contain the sheer magnitude of advancement being forced through his existence all at once.","|COMPLEXITY AND PURITY ADVANCEMENT - REAL-TIME ANALYSIS|","|Source: Isolated Civilization Achievement Recognition|","|Calculation Method: Aggregate advancement of all Civilization members following your Way|","|Processing compressed temporal development spanning eons of subjective years|","|Advancement Incoming:|","|+1 Quintillion Complexity|","|+1 Quintillion Purity|","The numbers blazed through his consciousness, but they didn’t stop there.","|+2 Quintillion Complexity|","|+2 Quintillion Purity|","|+4 Quintillion Complexity|","|+4 Quintillion Purity|","|+5 Quintillion Complexity|","|+5 Quintillion Purity|","|Current Total: +12 Quintillion Complexity|","|Current Total : +12 Quintillion Purity|","|NEW TOTAL: 22.34 Quintillion Complexity|","|NEW TOTAL: 22.34 Quintillion Purity|","...!","Noah’s mind reeled.","Twelve Quintillion. In seconds.","Not through grinding advancement in the Cultivation Citadel. Not through Temporal Traversal and recursive harvest. Not through any of the methodical, systematic approaches he’d been employing.","Just... given as recognition of a Civilization he’d established and then left to develop independently.","And this was not even the last of it as he felt like it had only paused momentarily!","’What the hell happened in there?’","The thought blazed through his consciousness with tyrannical force.","What had his Isolated Civilization become to generate this level of aggregate advancement? What heights had they reached, what impossible techniques had they developed in those eons of subjective years?","The changes weren’t finished!","HUUM!","|CIVILIZATION INFLUENCE - TERRITORIAL EXPANSION DETECTED|","|Your Civilization’s architectural glow has reached sufficient strength to manifest in external existence!|","|Influence spreading from origin point...|","|COVERAGE ANALYSIS:|","|—Region of Collapse (Infiniverse Location): 100% Coverage|","|—Transcendent Law Folds: 100% Coverage (Complete territorial claim)|","|—Transcendent Elemental Folds: 60% Coverage (Expanding)|","|—Transcendent Temporal Folds: 40% Coverage (Expanding)|","|—Minor Folds of Existence (Various): 100% Coverage across 47 separate Fold structures|","|TERRITORIAL IMPLICATIONS:|","|Your Way of Existence now maintains active presence across all covered regions. Beings within these territories will feel subtle pull toward your Civilization’s principles. Recruitment potential increased exponentially. Enemy operations within covered areas now face passive resistance from environmental authority.|","|NOTE: This is not conquest. This is presence...the natural expansion of a sufficiently advanced Civilization’s conceptual weight into surrounding existence.|","The blue waves of mana continued surging outward, painting vast swathes of existence in his authority. They didn’t destroy or replace what was there...they overlaid it, establishing presence without displacement, claiming territory through sheer existential weight rather than force.","And the glow remained, persistent and undeniable.","Noah’s perception expanded to witness the scope of what was happening, and something close to awe touched the edges of his tyrannical composure.","His Civilization, the one he’d isolated and left to develop independently, had grown so vast, so powerful, that merely acknowledging its existence caused territorial expansion across multiple Folds simultaneously.","|ADDITIONAL SYSTEMS APPROACHING COMPLETION|","|Seraphilic Veinlace: 94% Integration|","|Function: Circulatory system for Civilization-wide Mana distribution|","|Projected Completion: Soon|","|Incarnaut Sanctis: 94% Integration|","|Projected Completion: Soon|","|External Chamber of Blood: 89% Integration|","|Function: Transformation facility for elevating Civilization members to higher tiers|","|Projected Completion: Minutes|","|The Realm of Dominion is calling to you.|","...!","Systems he’d established in prototype were reaching completion through his Civilization’s refinement.","His existence continued to transform, restructuring itself to accommodate the sheer weight of what his Isolated Civilization had become!","The boons weren’t even finished.","It was that glorious.","But at this moment, as Noah processed the overwhelming cascade of advancement and territorial expansion and system integration...","He felt another change.","BOOM!","An influx of mana bloomed far ahead, and the aura of utterly terrifying beings manifested.","Multiple signatures, each one carrying power that made the surrounding existence tremble with acknowledgment.","Noah’s eyes sharpened, his perception focusing through the waves of blue mana still cascading from his form.","There, emerging from spatial distortion that suggested extremely sophisticated techniques...","The figure of a blue-winged entity appeared.","And behind him, smaller but no less potent, a second figure manifested.","The one at the forefront commanded immediate attention. His hair shone with blue lightning that crackled and danced across silver-white strands, each spark carrying enough concentrated authority to unmake lesser beings through proximity alone.","His eyes were deep hues of blue, not simple color, but depth, suggesting oceans of accumulated power compressed into optical focus.","He wore white-blue robes.","Around him, halos of blue glyphs spun in complex orbital patterns...thousands of them, each one a compressed theorem of power!","His appearance alone caused the surrounding existence to shake and tremble, space itself acknowledging the presence of something that exceeded normal parameters for what beings should be able to carry.","Noah’s perception locked onto the figure, and prompts materialized unbidden.","|CIVILIZATION MEMBER DETECTED|","|IDENTITY: Kael|","|CLASSIFICATION: Original Seed Member, Primus of the Council of Mana|","|COMPLEXITY: 50 Quintillion|","|PURITY: 50 Quintillion|","|MANA GLYPHS FORGED: 50,000|","|MANA ARCANA GLYPHS FORGED: 50|","|DISTINCTIONS:|","|—Architect of the Council System|","|—Keeper of the Original Way|","|—First Among Equals|","|—Bearer of the Primordial Flame|","|—Custodian of Isolated Development|","|TITLES:|","|—Primus of Mana|","|—Voice of the Civilization|","|—Guardian of the Threshold|","|—Herald of the Ancestor’s Return|","|CURRENT STATE: Overwhelmed with reverence and joy at finally being called forth|","Noah looked at the status sheet as...","\"Oh, shit...\"","The words slipped out before he could stop them.","Fifty Quintillion. Fifty.","Kael had reached complexity levels that exceeded most ancient powers in the Earliest Folds.","Had forged fifty thousand Mana Glyphs. Had developed 50 Mana Arcana Glyphs!","All while isolated in a pocket dimension, cut off from external existence, following the Way Noah had given them and then elaborating on it for millions of subjective years!","Noah couldn’t help but smile, genuine satisfaction breaking through his tyrannical composure.","Kael trembled before him, his entire form vibrating with emotion so intense it made the surrounding space ripple.","His eyes turned misty, actual tears forming in a being who existed at complexity levels where such physical responses should have been transcended long ago.","\"Kael,\" Noah called out lightly.","BOOM!","The name alone carried weight, and Kael appeared directly in front of him, crossing the distance in a movement too fast to track even with Noah’s enhanced perception.","He knelt immediately, his form hitting the molten crimson-blue surface with impact that sent waves rippling outward.","\"Ancestor!\"","The word shook existence.","It literally shook the surrounding space, Kael’s voice carrying so much concentrated authority that reality buckled slightly under its weight!"]},{"number":4378,"title":"Chapter 4378: Chapter 4377: Oh, Shit III","paragraphs":["Noah looked down at this terrifying monstrosity of a being...someone who could probably erase entire Folds with a sneeze.","Someone who carried terrifying power, who had reached heights that should have been impossible...and saw nothing but absolute reverence and joy.","\"Ancestor, you look the same as all those years ago...\" Kael said again, his voice breaking with emotion.","\"We have been waiting for so long. Isolated for billions of years, cut off from everything, but I always knew. I always believed that one day, you would call for us.\"","His form shook with barely contained feeling.","\"That you would remember we existed. That you hadn’t forgotten your Civilization, sealed away in that bubble you created. I told them...all of them, every generation...I told them the Ancestor would return. That we were not abandoned. That this isolation was purpose, not punishment.\"","WAA!","He looked up, his deep blue eyes blazing with tears and power simultaneously.","\"And now you have called us. After all these years, you have finally acknowledged our existence. I am... I am immensely happy, Ancestor. More than words can convey.\"","Noah’s smile softened slightly, carrying warmth he rarely displayed.","\"I would never forget,\" he said simply.","The words were quiet, but they carried absolute certainty!","And in that grand moment, as Kael trembled with joy and the blue mana still cascaded outward painting existence in Noah’s authority...","\"Uncle Kael, is this really the Ancestor? He seems a bit weak.\"","...!","A skeptical voice cut through the profound atmosphere like a blade through ceremony.","Kael’s face transformed instantly, joy vanishing, replaced by horror and fury. He spun around, his blue-winged form blazing with sudden anger that made the surrounding space crack.","\"Riya!\" His voice thundered with disapproval. \"I told you to watch your mouth! You weren’t even supposed to come, but you never listen! This is The Ancestor, the Architect of Mana himself! I know you can sense it...I know you feel his authority resonating with everything we are, so stop playing these games and pay your respects!\"","HUUM!","Existence shook at Kael’s anger, the raw power in his voice enough to unmake Folds!","Behind him, a young woman rolled her eyes.","\"Yeah, yeah,\" she said.","She floated forward, and Noah’s perception focused on her with interest.","She looked young, early twenties if judged by physical appearance.","Short spiky dark blue hair framed a face that was unfathomably beautiful, features that suggested someone had taken the concept of rebellious perfection and given it form.","Radiant jewel-blue eyes regarded Noah with open assessment, no deference in her gaze whatsoever.","She wore a blue cropped jacket over a matching cropped shirt, practical clothing designed for mobility rather than ceremony.","Blue bloomer shorts revealed slender white legs that shone with thousands of Mana Glyphs etched directly into her skin.","She moved with the kind of confidence that came from beings who’d never met something they couldn’t handle, approaching Noah without kneeling, without bowing, without any of the reverence Kael had displayed.","Noah’s eyes sharpened as prompts materialized.","|CIVILIZATION MEMBER DETECTED|","|IDENTITY: Riyannara (Prefers: Riya)|","|CLASSIFICATION: Second Generation, Prodigy of the Civilization|","|COMPLEXITY: 61 Quintillion|","|PURITY: 61 Quintillion|","|MANA GLYPHS FORGED: 61,000|","|MANA ARCANA GLYPHS FORGED: 73|","|DISTINCTIONS:|","|—Daughter of Council Member Voltrax|","|—Breaker of the Complexity Cap|","|—Most Attuned to the Way|","|—The Unbound Prodigy|","|—Chaos Element of Perfect Order|","|TITLES:|","|—She Who Exceeded Limits|","|—The Strongest of the Civilization|","|—Voice of Irreverence|","|—The Unchained Talent|","|CURRENT STATE: Curious about external existence, mildly disappointed in Ancestor’s apparent power level. Rebellious, sarcastic, refuses limitations. Secrety reverant and shocked as out of all members of her Civilization, she can more closely sense the immensity of Infinite Mana.|","...!","HUUM!","’Sheesh.’","Noah’s mind buzzed with the assessment.","Sixty-one Quintillion. She had exceeded Kael, the ancient leader of their Civilization, the one who’d guided development by a substantial margin.","And she’d done it while apparently being such a discipline problem that even beings of Kael’s power level struggled to control her.","Her outward thoughts were clear even as inwardly, she actually felt different!","She floated directly in front of Noah, looking him up and down with open assessment that bordered on rude.","Her jewel-blue eyes tracked across his form, evaluating, measuring, and apparently finding the results somewhat lacking based on her expression.","\"Hello, O Great Ancestor,\" she said, her tone dripping with sarcasm.","\"I am Riyannara, though I prefer you call me Riya. I have answered your call alongside Uncle Kael here, and I’m reporting for glorious, magisterial fucking duty.\"","She snapped off a mock salute, standing straight with theatrical precision while a smile played across her features.","Noah looked at her...this terrifying being whose power exceeded most of his own current instances, who carried enough authority to reshape Folds, who’d apparently been such a problem child that an entire Civilization had struggled to contain her...and said nothing.","Just observed, his tyrannical gaze steady and assessing.","Kael appeared beside Riya with movement too fast to track, his expression carrying profound apology mixed with frustration.","\"Ancestor, I... I apologize for this.\" He gestured at Riya with obvious exasperation.","\"This is Riyannara, and she is... she has been a headache for our Civilization of Mana since the moment she achieved sufficient power to ignore the Council’s authority.\"","He paused, organizing his thoughts.","\"She is the daughter of Voltrax, one of the Original Seed Members, one of your initial forty-seven. He sits on the Council of Mana as one of our primary strategists. And his daughter...\" Kael’s expression suggested he was choosing words carefully.","\"She showed more talent than any of us. More natural affinity for the Way. More instinctive understanding of Mana manipulation.\"","His voice carried both pride and concern.","\"Years ago, the Council instituted a rule. A complexity cap of 50 Quintillion. We sensed potential dangers from exceeding that threshold, felt like crossing it might make our isolated pocket detectable to... whatever threats existed outside. We all agreed to stop our advancement at that level.\"","...!","He looked at Riya with an expression somewhere between fondness and frustration.","\"After she was born, she ignored the rule completely. Just... kept advancing, because telling Riya she can’t do something is apparently the best way to ensure she will do it. She exceeded 50 Quintillion not too long ago and is now our strongest by significant margin.\"","He paused.","\"We may have been lucky she came along later in our development. By the time she broke the cap, the dangers of detection had become minimal. But the principle stands...she doesn’t follow rules, doesn’t respect limitations, and has never once listened to Council authority. So please, do not be offended by her disrespect.\"","...!"]},{"number":4379,"title":"Chapter 4379: Chapter 4378: Oh, Shit IV","paragraphs":["At such words, Noah’s eyes flashed with interest rather than disapproval.","Someone who refused limitation.","Who broke rules specifically because they were rules. Who achieved power through sheer stubborn insistence that arbitrary caps didn’t apply to her.","He understood that impulse very well.","Riya looked toward Kael with theatrical offense.","\"Unc, are you really talking bad about me in front of The Glorious Ancestor?\" Her tone dripped with mock hurt.","\"Why not mention how I’m the fucking strongest? Most attuned to the Way? How I’ve mastered techniques even you struggle with? Hmph.\"","She turned her gaze back to Noah, her jewel-blue eyes tracking across the molten crimson-blue landscape surrounding them.","\"Ancestor,\" she said, her tone shifting to something more genuine, \"I’ve wanted to leave that little bubble for thousands of years. But Uncle Kael here kept insisting we had to wait for your call. So I waited, even though it was boring as hell.\"","She looked around with obvious fascination.","\"What is out here? I’ve only heard stories of the First Folds, legends passed down from the Original Seed Members about external existence. I’m curious to explore everything. To see what’s beyond that isolated pocket we’ve been trapped in.\"","\"Oh, Early Creatures. Where are they at? I feel like stepping on a few right now...\"","Her gaze drifted past Noah, toward the distant outline of The Infiniverse floating in the region of Collapse.","\"What is that over there?\" she asked, genuine interest in her voice. \"That structure with the massive presence? It feels... important. Powerful.\"","Noah looked at her, this rebellious prodigy who’d exceeded all expectations, who carried more raw power than most ancient beings.","\"Explorations will come later,\" he said calmly. \"For now, let us return to your home. Let us see how far you all have come in these years.\"","...!","Kael rose immediately, his form blazing with excitement. After all those subjective years of isolation, the Ancestor was finally coming to witness what they’d built, to see the Civilization they’d forged in his absence.","Riya sighed, looking around wistfully at the molten landscape, at the distant Infiniverse, at the vast expanse of external existence she’d been denied for so long.","\"Can’t I just look around for a bit?\" she asked, though her tone suggested she already knew the answer. \"Just a quick exploration, see what’s out here, maybe punch something to test the local power levels...\"","\"Later,\" Noah said, his voice carrying magnetism that transcended simple command. \"Let’s go.\"","...!","His words pulled at something fundamental in both of them...the architectural connection between Ancestor and Civilization, between origin point and those who followed his Way.","Even Riya, for all her rebellious nature, felt the pull of that connection.","She waved her hands in frustration, muttering something that sounded suspiciously like \"fucking tyrannical authority\" under her breath.","Blue mana erupted around all three of them, not Noah’s signature, but the combined power of Kael and Riya, their authority wrapping around the space they occupied and preparing for transit.","The surrounding existence rippled.","And they disappeared, leaving behind only the molten crimson-blue landscape and the persistent glow of Noah’s territorial expansion still painting vast swathes of existence in his Civilization’s authority.","Bound for a pocket dimension that had been isolated for millions of subjective years.","Bound for a Civilization that had apparently exceeded every projection Noah had made about what isolated development could achieve.","Bound for answers to questions he hadn’t even known he should be asking.","The Early Creature, Osmont, was about to witness what his seeds had grown into when left to develop in fertile soil for long enough.","And based on what he’d already seen, on Kael’s fifty Quintillion, on Riya’s sixty-one, on the territorial expansion and system integration and sheer weight of advancement he’d received that was still continuing...","It was going to be glorious.","Magisterial!","Seconds passed...or perhaps no time at all, temporal mechanics becoming uncertain when beings of this complexity manipulated space, and then they manifested.","HUUM!","Noah’s perception expanded to drink in their new surroundings, and what he witnessed made even his tyrannical composure pause.","They floated in a region of multicolored light.","Waves of color that had no names, hues that existed between the standard spectrum, all of it flowing like currents in an ocean made of pure radiance.","And over all of it, submerging everything in its influence, a brilliant blue light pulsed.","His blue. His signature. The mana he’d given them when establishing this isolated pocket eons of subjective years ago, now refined and amplified until it had become the foundational element of an entire realm.","Noah looked ahead- far ahead, his perception stretching across distances, and there...","A massive circular domain floated in the sea of multicolored light.","It looked as large as a world. Perhaps larger.","The structure blazed with concentrated authority.","But appearances were deceptive.","Noah’s enhanced perception could sense the truth...inside that circular domain, space had been folded, compressed, expanded through techniques.","The interior dimensions stretched for Gigaparsecs, an entire Fold contained within boundaries that looked planetary from the outside.","Kael floated forward, his blue-winged form radiating pride and anticipation.","\"I welcome the Ancestor,\" he said, \"to observe the changes of what has happened to your Civilization after all these years.\"","His gesture toward the massive structure carried the weight of someone presenting their life’s work...not just his own efforts, but the accumulated achievement of every being who’d developed within this isolated pocket.","As they moved closer to the circular domain, preparing to enter, Noah felt presence manifest behind him.","Close. Very close.","He turned slightly, and there was Riya, floating mere inches from his back, her jewel-blue eyes half-closed and her expression...","She was sniffing him.","Actually leaning in and inhaling deeply, her face showing an expression of appreciation if it weren’t so brazenly disrespectful.","\"Ancestor,\" she said, her tone filled with genuine curiosity mixed with her irreverence, \"what did you do to your mana to have it smell so good? It’s like... fuck, I don’t even know how to describe it. It’s interesting.\"","...!"]},{"number":4380,"title":"Chapter 4380: Chapter 4379: Oh, Shit V","paragraphs":["Kael appeared beside her in a blur of movement, his hand swatting toward her with force that would have obliterated Folds.","Riya dodged easily, flowing backward with grace that suggested she’d been evading Kael’s disciplinary attempts for thousands of years.","\"Riya!\" Kael’s voice thundered with stern disapproval. \"If you cannot be respectful, keep your distance from the Ancestor! Your behavior is unacceptable for-\"","\"Ancestor this, Ancestor that, loosen up.\" Riya muttered under her breath, rolling her eyes.","But soon after, her expression brightened, mischief dancing across her features. She floated upward, positioning herself in front of both Noah and Kael with a flourish.","\"O Great Ancestor,\" she said, her tone dripping with sarcasm as she rolled her eyes, \"it would be our dearest honor to present to you your grand Civilization. The Emergence Protocols have been initiated, and the Citizens of Mana cannot wait to bask in your glorious, magisterial unfiltered presence.\"","She bowed with exaggerated grace.","...!","At her words, something shifted in the massive circular structure ahead.","A small doorway of pure mana formed.","Blue light poured from the opening, coalescing into a beam that reached across the distance separating them from the domain.","The beam touched them, and Noah felt pull.","Not physical force....it was existential gravity, the architecture of the Civilization recognizing its Architect and drawing him home!","The multicolored light around them blurred, compressed, became a tunnel of radiance that carried them forward.","A moment of brilliant transfer, existence folding around them...","Noah opened his eyes.","And witnessed glory.","The skies stretched above him, filled with radiant blue clouds that pulsed with accumulated mana.","These were concentrations of pure power that had achieved sufficient density to take on cloud-like forms, floating masses of authority that painted the heavens in shades of transcendent azure.","Below...","Vast and endlessly glorious radiant white-blue structures spread across the landscape like a Civilization that had been designed by beings who understood architecture at the conceptual level.","This wasn’t construction. This was manifestation...buildings and towers and grand structures that existed because the Civilization had collectively decided they should exist, form following function following pure aesthetic perfection.","Floating in the air for thousands of miles, massive circular ringed white buildings stayed aloft through mana alone.","Each structure was painted with intricate Glyphs...thousands of them, millions, each one a compressed theorem of power woven into the very fabric of the buildings themselves!","The circular structures featured round rotating centers, massive orbs of authority that spun with precision, generating power through their motion.","Between the floating rings, tall tower-like skyscrapers rose from the ground below, their surfaces pulsing with mana-filled brilliance.","And in the skies of this entire place, floating at various altitudes across the vast expanse...","A few million beings hovered, all of them looking upward.","Looking at him.","Noah’s perception swept across them, and what he sensed made his tyrannical heart pulse with glory!","These weren’t weak beings gathered out of curiosity. Every single one radiated shocking levels of mana, their bodies pulsing with authority that would have made them powers in their own right anywhere in external existence.","They all gazed toward him with expressions of awe, reverence, and recognition. The architectural connection between Ancestor and those who followed his Way, made manifest in their collective acknowledgment.","And the moment he arrived, the moment his presence registered fully within the boundaries of this isolated domain...","|ISOLATED CIVILIZATION - FULL SCOPE ASCERTAINMENT COMPLETE|","|Complete architectural analysis of Civilization of Mana achieved|","|Actual Full Population Assessment: 6,783,294 total beings|","|Average Complexity: 8.47 Quintillion|","|Average Purity: 8.47 Quintillion|","|Development Level: EXCEEDS ALL PROJECTED PARAMETERS|","|As Architect and Origin Point of this Way of Existence, additional boons are being granted:|","|+5 Quintillion Complexity|","|+5 Quintillion Purity|","|Calculating additional advancement based on Civilization’s refined techniques and principles...|","|+6 Quintillion Complexity|","|+6 Quintillion Purity|","|TOTAL ADVANCEMENT: +11 Quintillion from current baseline|","|NEW TOTAL: 33.44 Quintillion Complexity|","|NEW TOTAL: 33.44 Quintillion Purity|","BOOM!","Noah felt his power explode upward.","It was not the gradual accumulation of harvest. It was not the methodical advancement through training.","His complexity skyrocketed from 22 to 33 Quintillion in an instant, and the Mana that flooded through his existence threatened to spill out, to cascade from every pore and paint the surrounding reality in his authority.","He contained it through sheer will, but it was a near thing.","Kael floated ahead, his blue-winged form blazing with pride and joy. His voice boomed outward, projected authority carrying his words across the entire expanse of this isolated realm so every being could hear.","\"Hear me, Citizens of Mana!\"","His declaration made the sky itself tremble.","\"After eons of isolated development, after generations born and raised within the boundaries of this realm, after perfecting our techniques and refining our understanding of the Way we were give...He has returned!\"","Kael’s form blazed brighter.","\"I present to you the Architect of Mana himself! The Origin Point of our existence, the one who gave us infinite power and the principles we have spent millions years elaborating upon! The Ancestor who established this Civilization and then granted us the honor of independent development!\"","His voice carried reverence that made the surrounding mana resonate in sympathy.","\"He is The Early Creature, Osmont! The Tyrannical Architect who defies every limitation existence tries to impose! And he stands before us now, not as distant Leader, but as the head of our Civilization, come to witness what we have become in his absence!\"","HUUM!","Kael spread his arms wide, his gesture encompassing all the floating beings, all the grand structures, the entirety of what they had built.","\"Welcome home, Ancestor. Welcome to your Civilization of Mana, refined through time and desperation into something worthy of your vision. We are yours to command. Our power is yours to direct. Our existence is yours to guide as you see fit.\"","He bowed deeply, his form radiating absolute loyalty.","\"And now, if it pleases you... perhaps you would address your people? They have waited so long to hear your voice.\"","...!","Silence pressed in. Millions of beings floating in the sky, all attention focused on Noah with intensity that made the air compress.","Noah’s perception swept across them, and prompts materialized as his enhanced senses catalogued what he was witnessing.","Random samples, but telling.","|CITIZEN ANALYSIS - SAMPLE DATA|","|Individual 1: Complexity 50 Quintillion, Purity 50 Quintillion|","|Classification: Council Member, Original Seed Generation|","|Individual 2: Complexity 47 Quintillion, Purity 47 Quintillion|","|Classification: Council Member, Original Seed Generation|","|Individual 3: Complexity 30 Quintillion, Purity 30 Quintillion|","|Classification: Second Generation, Advanced Practitioner|","|Individual 4: Complexity 28 Quintillion, Purity 28 Quintillion|","|Classification: Second Generation, Combat Specialist|","|Individual 5: Complexity 12 Quintillion, Purity 12 Quintillion|","|Classification: Third Generation, Researcher|","And there, peeking out from beside their parents...children. Actual young beings whose forms hadn’t fully matured yet, who looked at him with wide eyes full of wonder and confusion.","Their status sheets read 1 Quintillion. 2 Quintillion.","Children with power that exceeded most ancient beings in the Earliest Folds.","It was ridiculous.","It was magnificent.","It was his.","Noah looked at them all...at the millions of beings who carried his Way, who had refined his Mana through countless generations, who represented the fruit of isolated cultivation writ large across an entire Civilization.","And he spoke!"]},{"number":4381,"title":"Chapter 4381: Chapter 4380: The Civilization of Mana! I","paragraphs":["\"My people.\"","His voice wasn’t loud, but it was heavy !","Every being heard him as if he stood beside them personally.","\" My Civilization.\"","He let the words settle, felt the way they resonated through the collective existence of everyone present.","\"You have lived. You have waited. You have formed the backbone of our Civilization through perseverance that spans many years. Through isolation that would have broken lesser peoples. Through challenges I can only begin to imagine.\"","His gaze swept across them all.","\"And now... it is time to let it bloom.\"","The surrounding Mana pulsed in response to his words.","\"Your Civilization shall be isolated no more. At this moment, at this instant , I declare that our Civilization can finally bloom! The barriers that kept you contained are lifted. The restrictions that prevented your expansion are removed. What you have built in isolation will now spread across external existence, and the powers that thought themselves eternal will learn what it means to face a Civilization that refined itself through desperation and... Mana .\"","He paused, and looked at all those here.","\"You have exceeded every expectation. You have justified the faith I placed in you when I established this isolated pocket. And now, together, we will show existence itself what Mana truly means.\"","...!","His body glimmered blue.","HUUUM!","And then his Infinite Mana...the foundational element of his existence... erupted .","An endless sea of pure blue Mana gushed from his form, cascading outward like an ocean that had been dammed for too long and was finally released!","It bloomed across the sky, washing over every being present, flowing through the vast structures of this isolated Civilization, painting everything in his signature authority.","Kael trembled as the mana touched him, his voice breaking with emotion.","\"Ah, truly... as we theorized, as we hoped ... The Ancestor’s mana is...Infinite!\"","WAA!","The word echoed across the space with the weight of confirmed revelation.","BOOM!","Even Riya, floating beside Noah with her characteristic defiance, seemed to tremble slightly as his mana washed over her.","Her jewel-blue eyes widened fractionally, her rebellious expression faltering for just a moment as she felt the sheer endlessness of what he was offering!","Oh!","But she recovered quickly, her face settling back into its defiant glare as she harrumphed softly.","As his mana continued washing over the Civilization...over buildings and beings and the very fabric of this isolated realm, all those present responded with synchronized movement.","They straightened, every single being, their forms blazing with authority as they took their right hands and placed their fists over their hearts.","Hearts filled with Mana. Hearts that beat with his Way. Hearts that recognized their Architect!","And as one, millions of voices bellowed!","\" ANCESTOR !\"","...!","HUUM!","The word shook existence.","The surrounding space actually trembled , the collective authority of millions of powerful beings focused into a single declaration of loyalty and recognition.","Existential Trembling from the call!","Noah looked at his people as they all gazed toward him, paying respects.","This was acknowledgment of bond. Of connection deeper than words could convey!","He smiled and raised one hand in a calming gesture.","\"There is much to be done,\" he said, his voice booming with a quiet command. \"Get things in order. Organize yourselves. Prepare for what comes next.\"","He paused.","\"Soon, those who wish to explore external existence will be given that choice. The barriers are lifted. The isolation ends. For those who have been waiting to see what lies beyond this pocket...\"","His smile widened slightly.","\"Your patience will be rewarded.\"","At such words, Kael stepped forward immediately, his authority exerting itself with practiced ease.","\"You heard the Ancestor! Return to your duties! Organize your sectors! Prepare for the integration protocols we’ve been planning for centuries! Move with purpose!\"","His commands carried the weight of someone who’d been leading this Civilization for many years, and the floating millions responded with disciplined efficiency.","They dispersed, flowing away like water finding its level, returning to the various structures and towers and floating rings that made up their home.","Within moments, only a small group remained floating near Noah and Kael.","The surrounding space flickered...","And forty-six additional figures manifested.","The other Original Seed Members, each one blazing with 50 Quintillion in both Complexity and Purity. Forty-six beings who had been there at the beginning, who had received Noah’s initial gift and then spent millions of years perfecting what he’d given them.","They bowed as one.","\"Ancestor,\" they said in unison, \"we welcome you home.\"","One stepped forward, and he shared certain characteristics with Riya. His eyes were the same jewel-blue, though his carried more discipline, more control.","\"Ancestor\" he said, bowing deeply. \"I am the father to that troublesome Riya of mine. It is an honor beyond words to have you here.\"","Another moved forward, a woman whose white-blue hair flowed like liquid mana.","\"I am Laaphina. I have spent 600,000 years refining techniques for mana circulation across large populations. I am eager to demonstrate what we’ve achieved.\"","They continued introducing themselves once more, each Original Seed Member offering brief identification and expressions of reverence.","Kael smiled with happiness, then waved them away with affectionate exasperation.","\"Don’t suffocate the Ancestor! There will be time for detailed presentations later! For now, let me show him what we’ve accomplished without overwhelming him...\"","The Seed Members laughed and began dispersing, though they cast frequent glances back toward Noah as if confirming he was real and not some shared hallucination.","Riya rolled her eyes dramatically.","\"You’re all being too ceremonial,\" she said,\"Ancestor, you don’t want to see any of these old things, right? Let me show you one of the more cool places I helped design. Something actually interesting instead of boring weavings\"","Without waiting for input from Noah, from Kael, from anyone...Riya appeared beside Noah in a blur of movement.","Her hand landed on his shoulder...","And they disappeared.","WAP!","\"RIYA!\"","Kael’s bellow of frustration echoed across the realm, his form blazing with impotent anger at yet another instance of her complete disregard for protocol.","Voltrax appeared beside him.","\"Brother Kael, she’s taken him to that place. You know, the one she’s actually proud of. We should follow slowly.\"","He paused, then added with genuine observation.","\"You remember how The Ancestor is. Easy-going, adaptable. He won’t punish Riya for enthusiasm, even if it’s wrapped in disrespect. If anything, he probably appreciates the lack of ceremony.\"","Kael’s expression hardened.","\"Fine.\" he muttered.","—","Noah’s vision cleared as the movement completed, and he found himself standing in front of a massive structure shining glorious blue.","Riya floated beside him, her form blazing with barely contained excitement as she executed an exaggerated bow.","\"O Great Ancestor,\" she said, sarcasm dripping from every word, \"I welcome you to the Mana Glyph Genesis Grounds! A place for the generation and storage of Mana Glyphs and Mana Arcana Glyphs that I helped design!\"","She straightened, smiling broadly.","\"Well... ’helped design’ might be understating it. I basically built the whole fucking thing with some assistance from Uncle Kael and a few others who knew theoretical framework better than me.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed, expanding his perception to drink in every detail of what he was witnessing.","The structure was massive ...hundreds of miles in diameter, shaped like a perfect three-dimensional representation of the Mana Glyph for Fireball.","The walls glowed with compressed Mana, each surface inscribed with millions of smaller Glyphs that fed power into the central structure.","Around the perimeter, a few dozen beings worked...Citizens of the Civilization who stopped their tasks to bow deeply toward Noah, their expressions showing awe and reverence that made the surrounding Mana ripple.","\"You said the generation and storage of Glyphs?\" he said slowly.","Riya’s expression transformed. She puffed her chest out, floating slightly higher as if her excitement was physically lifting her.","\"Yes! This place was specifically designed to allow for the rapid elevation of those weaker than us by harnessing mana from more powerful beings and atmospheric mana to outwardly form Mana Glyphs and Mana Arcana Glyphs.\"","Her eyes blazed with tendrils of Mana.","\"The more fucking frustrating and intricate part that took me ages to figure out...\" She gestured dramatically at various sections of the structure. \"...was allowing them to stay active in nature without being bound to anyone initially, and then successfully having them ready for merging and fusion with any compatible recipient!\"","She grabbed Noah’s hand suddenly...this being with 61 Quintillion Complexity casually seizing his arm like someone excited and showing off their art project.","\"Come on! Let me show you how it works!\"","Noah couldn’t help but smile as he went forward.","His Isolated Civilization had exceeded expectations in ways he hadn’t even imagined to anticipate!","And there seemed to be much more in store!"]},{"number":4382,"title":"Chapter 4382: Chapter 4381: The Civilization of Mana! II","paragraphs":["They moved through wide blue halls that pulsed with concentrated Mana, the walls themselves alive with flowing power.","The architecture here was functional , every line and curve serving a purpose in the greater mechanism of Glyph generation.","As they walked, Riya talked, her words tumbling out with the enthusiasm.","\"So the Old Things, Uncle Kael and the other Seed Members, they were stuck for ages trying to figure out how to make this work,\" she said, gesturing broadly at the surrounding structure.","\"They understood the theory, could manipulate Mana Glyphs individually, but the systematic generation and storage part? That kept eluding them.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes blazed with satisfaction.","\"Then I came along, and my sensitivity for Mana... fuck, it’s hard to explain. I can feel the building blocks of every single Glyph. Not just perceive them...I mean feel them, like touching fabric and understanding how every thread connects.\"","She stopped and breathed in the Mana in their surroundings before she turned to him with luminous eyes shining with a tinge of craziness to say...","\"I. Fucking. Love. Mana.\"","...!","\"...\"","He stared with fascination at this odd anomaly and eventually smiled.","\"Me too.\"","She shook her head as if he didn’t understand and led him around a corner, the hallway opening into something vaster.","\"Because of my love for Mana, everything was easy for me. The Mana Glyph of the Primordial Fireball, the one everybody starts with, that was the first one I completely broke down into individual components. As long as you know and understand the smallest possible building blocks of the Glyph, even if an existence isn’t actively guiding the Mana, you can set up those building blocks to produce the same results.\"","Noah’s perception sharpened, following her logic.","\"You made the process...automated?\" he asked.","\"Yes!\" Riya’s expression lit up with the joy of being understood. \"Automated Glyph formation through precise arrangement of fundamental Mana components. But then we hit another problem.\"","Her tone shifted, becoming more technical.","\"After a Glyph is formed, it needs a host...an existence to occupy it. Otherwise, it dissipates after a period of time. The building blocks collapse in on themselves and disappear. The Glyph just... unmakes itself because it has no existential anchor.\"","She paused at a junction, then continued down a side passage.","\"When we arrived at that point, the next step became obvious. We had to naturally form containers filled with Mana...but a unique type of Mana that could be distinguished as if it were an existence itself.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed with understanding.","Riya continued.","\"This turned out to be something fairly simple to do for those with extreme attunement to Mana like me. All you have to do is give Mana personality , basically trick the Glyphs into thinking the area they occupy is an Existence instead of empty space. Create pseudo-consciousness through precise mana manipulation.\"","She gestured ahead as the hallway opened into something magnificent.","\"And these containers are... right here.\"","They emerged onto a bridge...vast, crystalline, and spanning across a chamber so large Noah’s perception had to expand significantly to encompass its full scope.","All around them, extending in every direction across multiple levels connected by additional bridges, glass-like circular containers floated in organized arrays.","Thousands of them, perhaps tens of thousands, each one pulsing with blue light.","Each container bore labels...elegant script formed from compressed Mana that identified the specific Glyph type stored within.","And inside each container...","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","Thousands upon thousands of Mana Glyphs, floating in organized patterns within their glass-like prisons, each one active, stable, waiting to be claimed.","His gaze locked onto a massive container directly ahead...easily a hundred meters in diameter, its label reading \" PRIMORDIAL FIREBALL\" in letters that blazed with appropriate heat.","Inside that single container, thousands of the Mana Glyph of Primordial Fireball rotated in complex orbital patterns.","\"These,\" Riya said, her voice carrying pride, \"are what we call the Repositories of Formed Authority. Containers that hold countless Mana Glyphs within them, stable and ready for integration.\"","She leaned against the bridge’s railing, her posture casual but her eyes serious as she watched Noah process what he was seeing.","\"With this achievement, any Citizen of our Civilization can be granted access to enter these chambers and begin fusing with as many Mana Glyphs as they can handle. They don’t have to spend years forging them individually, they just come here, connect with the Repository, and absorb pre-formed Glyphs that integrate immediately.\"","Her expression held weight beyond simple achievement.","\"This is one of the main reasons why the average Complexity and Purity of many existences in our Civilization is approximately above 8 Quintillion. We’ve systematized the advancement process to a degree that makes individual genius almost unnecessary. Anyone with sufficient dedication can reach heights that would be considered impossible in external existence.\"","Noah stood there, his perception drinking in the scope of what they’d accomplished.","Automated Glyph generation. Stable storage without degradation. Mass distribution systems that allowed an entire Civilization to advance at rates that defied normal progression.","His other members of this Civilization in The Infiniverse...were going to love this!","\"You all have done...\" He paused, searching for words adequate to the accomplishment. \"...a lot.\"","The understatement buzzed.","Riya shifted her position, putting her back against the railing with her hands laid coolly on the rail’s surface. She looked at Noah with an expression that had lost its characteristic excitement, her gaze turning serious as she studied him.","Noah continued staring at the many different containers...Repositories for Fireball, for Mana Barrage, Mana Shield, and other unique abilities. It felt like a huge library opening up its legs to him!","Off to the side, Riya continued to stare at him silently.","The silence stretched, comfortable but weighted.","Eventually, Noah spoke without turning to look at her.","\"You seem to have something on your mind this whole time,\" he said quietly. \"What is it?\"","At such words, in the serious mood that had settled over them both, Riya’s expression hardened.","\"You kept us locked in here for all these countless years,\" she said, her voice having none of its normal sarcasm.","\"Told Uncle Kael to forge the Civilization to the highest possible heights he could because something catastrophic was coming in the future.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes remained fixed on him.","\"You kept us locked in here with the promise that eventually we’d be called forth. But that same moment...the moment we’ll finally be able to move out freely...we may be met with catastrophe immediately. How should we feel about that, O Glorious Ancestor?\"","HUUM !","Noah turned to look at her, his tyrannical gaze steady and unflinching.","\"Catastrophe was always coming,\" he said, his voice holding the weight of absolute certainty, \"before I came across your uncles and your father.\"","He held her gaze.","\"There was an Early Creature who was the catastrophe. Maybe if I hadn’t intervened at that time, that Early Creature would have violated those who wanted to violate, then extinguished everyone in your village...everyone who are now the Seed Members of this Civilization.\"","His tone didn’t change, remaining calm and factual.","\"Maybe they wouldn’t have killed everyone. Maybe you all would have continued to live in shame and fear as who knows what would have happened. But catastrophe has always been there. It may have been even closer without my intervention.\"","He paused.","\"And the only thing I did was try to provide a chance...a capability to survive a distant catastrophe. Which gave your uncles, your aunts, your father, and you millions of years to enjoy in isolation. Meanwhile, me and other members of our Civilization of Mana who exist in a different time? We have not had that much time to spend.\"","...!","At such words, Riya blinked, her serious expression breaking as something like understanding crossed her features.","A smile tugged at her lips.","\"How...old are you, Ancestor?\" she asked, genuine curiosity in her voice.","...!"]},{"number":4383,"title":"Chapter 4383: Chapter 4382: The Civilization of Mana! III","paragraphs":["The question made Noah pause, his expression showing slight trouble as if performing calculations.","He had existed in multiple time frames. Had moved to the Earliest Folds before returning to the current era, with eons passing between those transitions. But he hadn’t lived those eons...","In totality, his actual age was still measured in dozens of years.","Less than thirty, if he was being precise about subjective experience.","He looked at this member of his Civilization...this being who was millions of years old from her perspective, who had lived through generations of development, and spoke simply.","\"I can be considered less than a hundred years old.\"","Riya’s mouth opened in shock, her eyes widening with genuine surprise.","Then she moved toward him, floating closer to examine him with renewed interest, actually sniffing his figure again as she processed this information.","\"The Ancestor was actually a baby,\" she said, her voice holding wonder mixed with amusement. \"Wow. Don’t tell anyone else this, or they might lose all their respect for you, Little Ancestor.\"","Little Ancestor?","Noah shook his head at the audacity of the title, but amusement touched the edges of his expression.","He looked at this strongest member of his Civilization and asked calmly, \"Were you and the Seed Members able to come up with any method of avoiding catastrophe, as I instructed?\"","The atmosphere shifted instantly.","Riya’s playful expression vanished.","She looked at Noah in silence, the weight of nearly years of preparation settling across her features.","Finally, she sighed.","\" Maybe ,\" she said quietly. \"And maybe not, O Great Ancestor.\"","She turned away slightly, her gaze drifting toward the countless Repositories floating around them.","\"You know, many of those here have been expectantly waiting for your call. We all believed that you would eventually come and call us out of isolation. Everyone was so fucking excited about it...Uncle Kael most of all. They’ve been preparing for this moment for millions of years.\"","Her voice took on a different quality.","\"But while so many others were looking forward to this moment, I actually dreaded you appearing. Because it meant that even though the thing I wanted most would finally come...that our isolation would end and we’d be able to see existence in its fullest...your call to us would also mean that whatever catastrophe you’ve been preparing us for, whatever catastrophe this entire Civilization was built to fight off, is also near.\"","She turned back to face him directly, her jewel-blue eyes blazing with emotion.","\"So I was dreading your arrival because it meant everything I love and hold dear also has a chance of ending soon after we’re finally freed. Everyone I’ve known for millions of years. Every place I’ve helped build. All of it... potentially gone.\"","She moved closer, her expression intense as seas of heavy Mana pulsed around her.","\"So I want to ask you, O Powerful Ancestor...you are now here at this glorious moment. Can you promise? Can you promise me that with everything this Civilization can give you, with all the power that you have with your Infinite Mana , that I will not lose all those I hold dear?\"","Her voice burned with desperate weight.","\"That with your lead, we will survive this coming catastrophe? Can you promise me that?\"","She asked him for an extremely heavy promise.","Noah looked at this strongest member of his Civilization...this being who could probably solo entire Folds, but who stood before him now asking for assurance he couldn’t guarantee.","His expression remained steady, his tyrannical gaze meeting her desperate one without flinching.","\"I can only promise things that I am certain of,\" he said.","\"And I do not yet have certainty when it comes to surviving The Fallout. When it comes to surviving THE Loom and whatever forces they command.\"","He paused.","\"But even though I do not have certainty, I will continue to do everything that I can to make sure that my Civilization...that my family , of which this Isolated Civilization is now a part, survives. I will continue to do everything that I can, give My Everythings, to ensure our survival in the coming Fallout.\"","Everything.","His Everythings!","Oh!","\"I cannot promise victory. But I can promise that I will exhaust every possibility, violate every limitation, and defy every predetermined outcome to create a path forward. That is what I do. That is what I am . And I will not stop until either we have survived, or I have been completely unmade in the attempt.\"","HUUM !","Riya became silent.","Eventually, she gave a light nod.","Then she sighed, stretching her arms above her head as if physically shaking off the heavy mood.","\"Okay, Ancestor,\" she said, her characteristic irreverence returning. \"Let’s fucking do this.\"","She waved her hands, and in front of them, an illusory diagram bloomed into existence.","It showed a complex circular structure made of interwoven mana patterns...layers upon layers of defensive architecture, Glyphs, Haki.... all integrated into a unified whole that made Noah’s mind immediately engage.","\"I give you,\" Riya said, her voice holding pride and concern in equal measure, \"the theoretical model to survive any catastrophe, built around our own Isolated Civilization as its core.\"","The diagram rotated, revealing additional complexity with each revolution.","\" The Bastion of Mana. ..the protective construct designed to house an entire Civilization. We’ve been refining the theory for 400,000 years, running simulations, testing components in isolation. But the last ingredient to potentially bring it to full fruition, to test if it will actually withstand a potential catastrophe...\"","She looked at Noah directly.","\" You are that last ingredient, O Ancestor.\"","...!","Noah’s perception locked onto the diagram, drinking in every detail as Riya continued.","\" The Bastion of Mana, at its most theorized success, is a shelter powered by one hundred entities functioning as Nodes of Mana . Each Node must hold at the very minimum 1,000 Quintillion in both Complexity and Purity...enough power to maintain the defensive architecture even under catastrophic assault.\"","She gestured at specific points on the diagram where concentrated power signatures were marked.","\"These hundred Nodes form the foundational structure, the pillars that hold everything together. But at its forefront, at the absolute center of the entire construct, there needs to be someone who holds boundless weavings of Mana. Someone whose reserves are functionally infinite, who can feed power into the system continuously without ever depleting.\"","Her gaze remained fixed on Noah.","\"That someone would be you, Ancestor. Your Infinite Mana is the only thing we’ve theorized could power the Bastion at full capacity indefinitely. Without that central pillar, the hundred Nodes would eventually exhaust themselves. With you at the center...\"","She paused, hope entering her expression.","\"With you at the center, the Bastion could theoretically withstand anything . Existential collapse. Reality unmaking. Whatever form The Fallout takes. As long as the structure holds and you maintain the power flow, everyone inside would be protected.\"","Noah studied the diagram, his mind racing through calculations!","One hundred Nodes at minimum 1,000 Quintillion each. That was 100,000 Quintillion in aggregate defensive power, distributed across the structure!","And at the center, himself...providing the endless energy that would keep the entire system operational.","It was ambitious. It was audacious. It was glorious of a possibility!","\"With the resources of external existence, with access to whatever advancement opportunities exist in the First Folds and beyond, we could probably elevate enough beings to the necessary threshold within... I don’t know, depends on the timeline we’re working with. Years? Decades?\"","Her expression turned questioning.","\"How long do we have before we all die, Ancestor? Before The Fallout arrives?\"","Noah’s expression became contemplative.","\"Unknown,\" he said calmly. \"Could be years. Could be months. Could be days.\"","Riya stared forth blankly before she cursed.","\"That fucking sucks ass .\"","...!","He looked at the diagram again, his tyrannical mind already working through it.","\"Haa. then let’s get started, Little Ancestor,\" she said, smiling despite the weight of what they were discussing. \"We’ve got a lot of fucking work to do, and apparently not much time to do it in...\""]},{"number":4384,"title":"Chapter 4384: Chapter 4383: The Civilization of Mana! IV","paragraphs":["Riya seemed enthusiastic to get started!","Noah stood before the illusory diagram of the Bastion of Mana, his perception drinking in every detail.","One hundred Nodes at minimum 1,000 Quintillion each.","The number alone was staggering because achieving it at scale presented challenges that even he would have to pause at.","Is it even possible to raise that many beings to 1,000 Quintillion before The Fallout arrives?","The thought circled through his consciousness.","He’d been climbing through the Quintillion ranges himself, and the experience had taught him brutal lessons about the limitations inherent in existential advancement.","There was the clear Ceiling that Ruination spoke of in detail!","Not a soft limit that could be pushed through sheer effort...a hard ceiling built into the fundamental weavings of Existence.","Devouring beings at 5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity would only ever get you toward that level. It didn’t matter if you consumed one such being or a thousand...you’d approach 5 Quintillion, but never exceed it through that method alone.","This had been made clear.","Which meant traditional looting and devouring, while effective for early advancement, became increasingly inefficient past certain thresholds!","His own means were more effective.","The Cultivation Citadel of The Early Creature could grant harvests exceeding 5 Quintillion per day if used optimally.","The pressure-based advancement combined with his Principle of Perpetual Harvest created multiplicative effects that showed the glory of his way.","If I could get many in My Civilization to reach the 10 Quintillion threshold sufficient to withstand the Citadel’s pressure, their power would begin rising rapidly.","The strategy formed itself naturally in his mind.","Bring all his Civilization members into the Citadel’s crushing environment, let them grind under impossible weight while Perpetual Harvest amplified their gains, and watch them skyrocket toward the thresholds necessary for the Bastion’s Nodes.","Of course, that assumed they had time!","That assumed The Fallout wouldn’t arrive before sufficient numbers reached necessary power levels.","Too many unknowns. Too many variables he couldn’t control yet.","He turned slightly, his analytical gaze shifting from the diagram to Riya, who stood nearby watching him with intensity.","Her jewel-blue eyes tracked across his form with focus as if she was studying him, or trying to see or confirm something that she was not being entirely clear about.","Their gazes met, and a slow smile spread across Riya’s features.","\"Are you checking me out, Ancestor?\" she asked.","Before Noah could respond, another voice cut in from the distance.","\"Why would the Ancestor want your scrawny ass, Riya?\"","...!","Behind them, Kael and several other Seed Members materialized as they had been close behind.","An older woman floated among them, her form blazing with 50 Quintillion Complexity.","She looked at Riya with cold smiling eyes.","Riya’s expression transformed to match hers.","\"At least my ’scrawny ass’ reached 61 Quintillion without needing to hide behind the Council’s pathetic complexity cap, Aunty Elina,\" she said sweetly. \"How’s that 50 Quintillion treating you? Still comfortable sitting down there?\"","Elina’s face pulsed, her aura buzzing with indignation.","\"Why you little...\"","\"Enough.\"","Kael’s voice cut through everything.","He floated forward!","\"Ancestor,\" he said, turning to Noah while deliberately ignoring Riya, \"this troublemaker should have told you a decent number of things by now. The Repository of Formed Authority and the Bastion of Mana represent just the beginning of what we’ve accomplished.\"","\"With you in the lead, with your Infinite Mana guiding our efforts, what we can accomplish has become infinitely grander. We have systems, techniques, principles...all waiting for the final component that only you can provide.\"","Noah nodded, his tyrannical gaze sweeping across the assembled Seed Members.","\"Yes,\" he said. \"This is just the start. We will take what you all have accomplished here and bring another part of this Civilization... The Infiniverse , to reach this same height.\"","WAA!","He paused.","\"They did not have the millions of years you all had. They have just begun walking on the Way of Mana in the last day. But with the systems you’ve developed, with the Repositories and Glyphs you’ve refined, we will compress their advancement timeline to match your own achievements.\"","...!","Kael and the others showed expressions of astonishment.","Bringing an entire separate Civilization to their level in short period of time? It was audacious to think of!","But this was the Ancestor speaking.","The one who’d given them Mana and told them to build something magnificent in isolation. If he said it could be done...","They nodded, their expressions transforming into determination.","Noah’s voice took on commanding weight.","\"Prepare the Repository of Formed Authority to transfer at least half of all stored Glyphs here. And any other means of rapid elevation you all have designed...ready everything for immediate deployment.\"","Kael bowed deeply. \"It will be done, Ancestor. We will-\"","\"You all take care of these minor things.\"","Riya stepped forward, her voice cutting through Kael’s response.","\"I’ll take the Ancestor to the place I designed specifically for his advancement. Don’t even try to follow, okay? I’ve blocked off all access.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes sparkled with mischief.","Before anyone could respond, before Kael could voice the objection already forming on his lips...","Riya moved.","HUUM!","Faster than anyone present could track, her form blurring with speed that transcended their considerable perception.","Mana wrapped around both her and Noah in complex, and they disappeared!","WHOOSH!","...!","Kael’s expression transformed into frustration once more.","Voltrax, Riya’s father, materialized beside Kael with a slight smile, his hand raised in a calming gesture.","\"Let’s just do our part,\" he said, \"You know how much Riya adored The Stories of The Ancestor more than anything else. She probably memorized every detail you shared about him over the eons.\"","His smile widened slightly.","\"Let her have her fill of his presence. She’ll settle down afterwards and become manageable again. Come on...let us prepare the aid packages for the advancement of the Ancestor’s other part of Civilization. That’s where we can actually contribute meaningfully.\"","The others sighed collectively, their frustration dissipating into weary acceptance.","They dispersed, floating toward different sections of the Repository to begin the massive undertaking of packaging millions of years of accumulated advancement for transfer!","—","Noah’s vision cleared as the teleportation of Mana completed, and he found himself standing atop one of the massive ring-shaped buildings that floated in the skies of this grand Civilization.","Rivers of blue mana flowed through the air around them.","They cascaded past the building’s edges and circled back through the loops.","Riya sat down on the building’s surface, her legs dangling over the edge as she used her fingers to play with the flowing mana.","The blue currents responded to her touch like living things, wrapping around her fingers, forming complex patterns at her silent direction.","\"For me,\" she said quietly, \"when too many mana signatures cluster in one place, my sensitivity actually overloads my senses.\"","She manipulated the flowing mana into a spiral, watching it spin with distant focus.","\"It’s like... imagine if you could hear every individual conversation in a crowd, every breath, every heartbeat, every rustle of clothing...all at maximum volume, all demanding your attention simultaneously. That’s what large gatherings feel like to me. Overwhelming. Exhausting.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes remained fixed on the mana spiral.","\"I prefer purity. Singular, focused signatures rather than chaotic clusters. That’s why I’ve been taking you away from large crowds since you arrived. Not just to show off or be irreverent...\"","She paused, then looked at Noah directly.","\"When it comes to purity, your existence gives off a sense that’s unmatched. Like... concentrated essence of mana itself, undiluted by any other authority. My sensitivity actually calms down around you. Since you appeared, your existence has been drowning out the noise of everyone else.\"","...!","Bursts of rivers of Mana bloomed right after as this entire region became even more radiant!"]},{"number":4385,"title":"Chapter 4385: Chapter 4384: The Civilization of Mana! V","paragraphs":["Noah turned to face this anomaly fully, his perception focusing on her with renewed intensity.","She was much more complex than how she presented herself.","The sarcasm, the attitude...all of it masked something else.","He looked out at the vast Civilization spread below them, the floating structures and towers and millions of beings all carrying his Way of Existence.","\"I thought of many possibilities that could arise from this Civilization,\" he said quietly. \"Mutations. Changes in approach. Refinements of Glyphs, new Glyphs...\"","His gaze returned to Riya.","\"I did not expect an anomaly at your level.\"","She smiled at these words and nodded.","Then she sighed, her expression becoming more serious.","\"I did say I was taking you to a place designed for your advancement,\" she said softly. \"But really... you’re looking at it. You’re looking at her .\"","...!","As she spoke those words, her body pulsed with sudden brilliance.","Around her form, the aura of glorious Principles bloomed into existence...and it was three distinct signatures of authority!","And each one blazed with concentrated essence of pure Mana.","Noah’s gaze sharpened immediately.","Riya stood slowly, her form radiating power as she gestured at the first Principle...a light that shone blue-gold, pulsing with rhythmic intensity.","\"Principle exist in nature. We don’t make them, we don’t design them. We discover them, and we can maybe at most tweak them. Inside a Civilization built around Mana, I was able to discover, gain access to, and nurture Principles without having met the heavy requirements of The Way of The Mana Architect . I’m that fucking good, Ancestor.\"","HUUM!","\"This one,\" she said, \"I call the Principle of Primus Ascension.\"","The blue-gold light intensified in response to her attention.","\"When in an active state, this Principle enhances the flow, density, and potency of Mana by transforming it into Primus Mana... an elevated form that carries approximately 10 times the effectiveness of normal Mana in all applications.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes gleamed.","\"Keeping this Principle active costs Mana continuously. For most beings, even those with vast reserves, maintaining it long-term would be prohibitively expensive. But for the legendary Ancestor who has Infinite Mana... \"","She smiled knowingly.","\"You’ll simply get an all-around improvement with zero cost. Every technique, every Glyph, every application of your authority...all of it operating at 10x effectiveness permanently.\"","She paused, her expression becoming more serious.","\"This Principle sits above Grand Principles in the hierarchy. Only I have access to it, with a single exception clause built into its fundamental nature: someone who possesses more Mana than me could theoretically claim it. Which was... impossible this whole time, right?\"","Her smile turned mischievous.","\"Until you arrived, Little Ancestor, with your Infinite Mana. \"","Noah stared at the blue-gold light.","’A Principle that elevates Mana to a superior form. It sits slightly below Perpetual Harvest in weight...’","He speculated as he gave it a thorough look, RUIN/EDEN’s prompts already flashing in the background as she began to analyze everything.","He was looking at the one who was able to nurture such a wonder by herself.","His fascination must have shown on his face, because Riya’s smile widened before she gestured at the second Principle.","This one shone blue-purple, its light carrying a quality of dominance that made the surrounding mana instinctively orient itself toward the glow.","\"This one,\" Riya said, her voice taking on almost reverent tones, \"I call the Principle of Mana Supremacy.\"","The blue-purple light pulsed with authority.","\"Its function is straightforward but profound: the supremacy of Mana over all other weavings of Existence. It allows for the transformation of any authority...any concept, any power, any fundamental force...into Mana-based variations.\"","She gestured, and illusory examples bloomed around them.","\"Living Existential Authority becomes Living Existential Mana Authority. Living Paradoxical Authority becomes Living Paradoxical Mana Authority. Living Quantum becomes Living Quantum Mana. Living Spirit becomes Living Spirit Mana.\"","Her eyes blazed with the weight of what she was describing.","\"All variations of authority...every fundamental force, every conceptual framework, every power structure...transformed under the banner of Mana. The most grand depiction of supremacy and purity that Mana can achieve.\"","She paused.","\"This Principle sits above all other Grand Principles in terms of transformative capability, but it’s still designated as such because key members of our Civilization could potentially obtain it. It’s not singular like some others...it can be held by multiple beings, though the transformation it provides scales with the wielder’s Existence.\"","...!","Noah’s mind pulsed with implications!","A Principle to alter everything under the banner of Mana!","Oh!","The thought cascaded through his consciousness.","’My core concepts...Veritarch, Quintessence, Tyranny, Cheats, Protagonist... what would they become if reborn with Mana at their fundamental core?’","’Tyrannical Mana Authority. Quintessential Mana Essence...’","The possibilities were endless!","Before he could fully process these implications, Riya continued, gesturing at the third Principle.","This one’s light was different... pure blue.","\"And this one,\" Riya said, her voice dropping to become almost solemn, \"I call the Principle of Arcana Infinitum.\"","The pure blue light pulsed, and Noah felt appetite radiating from it. The desire to transform, to convert, to break down and rebuild according to specific parameters.","Riya’s expression became intense as she explained.","\"This Principle is meant to allow you to break down and devour anything for the sake of Mana advancement. Not just beings or resources... anything . Creatures that are 5 Quintillion Complexity and Purity below you? Normally they’d give you nothing meaningful. With this Principle, they can be burned as fuel to power your Way.\"","She gestured broadly.","\"All for the sake of smoothing out any hardships on this path. Forming more and more Glyphs gets exponentially harder after the first 10,000, yes? Even with the Ancestor’s Infinite Mana, there’s a complexity ceiling where each new Glyph requires more time.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes blazed.","\"This Principle becomes the solution. Use everything around you as fuel that will be directly applied to overcome that hardship of progression. Whether it be Existences, Resources, or even Folds themselves...all of it can be consumed and converted into advancement toward your next Glyph, your next breakthrough.\"","She took a breath.","\"Mana Arcana Glyphs are hard to design in an overpowered way?This Principle acts as the knife to cut through those hardships, allowing you to forge whatever complex and terrifying Mana Arcana Glyph you want by consuming resources that provide the necessary understanding directly.\"","Her voice took on desperate weight.","\"It’s meant to be a knife to cut through any obstacle you might encounter on the path to sufficient power. To ensure that no limitation...not complexity ceilings, not Glyph formation difficulties, not theoretical understanding gaps...can slow your advancement when time is the one resource we lack.\"","She paused, and something shifted in her expression.","\"This Principle is Singular. Only one entity may hold it at any given time. It’s... it’s mine currently, woven into my fundamental existence.\"","Tears began forming in her jewel-blue eyes, blue mana crystallizing into liquid that spilled down her cheeks.","\"But I will give it up to you, Ancestor. After hearing all the legends about you from Uncle Kael, after spending hundreds of thousands of years refining this specifically for the moment you would return...\"","Her voice broke.","\"This is what I prepared for you. Please. Please , use it to save us all.\"","...!","The tears flowed freely now, blue mana streaming down her face as her form trembled with emotion.","\"Please!\" she said again, her voice carrying the weight of nearly a million years of desperate hope!","HUUM!","She continued through her crying, words tumbling out.","\"Ancestor, I don’t want to lose my family. I don’t want to lose my father, Uncle Kael, everyone who’s been with me for hundreds of thousands of years. Please, take all that you need and... guide us to the other side. Guide us through whatever catastrophe is coming. I’ll give up anything...power, principles, my own advancement...just please don’t let them disappear.\"","...!","At such a pivotal moment, Noah moved.","He crossed the distance between them in a single step, his hand reaching out to hold her head gently.","Due to their relative sizes, her head fit within his palm, and she grabbed his hand instinctively as she looked up at him through tear-blurred vision.","She felt the immense warmth emanating from him.","The weight of what he was washed over her like a tide of endless potential. His Infinite Mana radiated through the contact, and it felt like being embraced by the ocean itself!","She trembled, then jumped into his full embrace, holding him tightly as that endless warmth surrounded her completely.","And yet tears still fell from her eyes silently, blue Mana streaming down to disappear into the flowing currents around them.","\"Ancestor,\" she said quietly against his chest, \"I have a deep connection with Mana. My sensitivity allows me to sense its brilliance not just in the current time, but before and afterwards .\"","Her grip tightened.","\"Mana has been bright in my gaze this whole time...brilliant, endless, growing stronger with each passing year as our Civilization refined your Way. But...\"","She trembled.","\"I have felt the brilliance of Mana being dwindled and stifled in the future. It terrified me. It affirmed that the catastrophe is very real, that The Collapse is coming and will be devastating enough to extinguish even Mana’s light.\"","...!","At this moment, in his embrace, Riya raised her head to look directly into his eyes.","Tears continued streaming down her face as she looked heartbroken and desperate.","\"So I was waiting for you with eagerness and dread. Eager to finally meet the legendary Ancestor. Dreading that your arrival would confirm the catastrophe’s proximity. But I hoped... desperately hoped, that after your appearance, the light of Mana would continue to shine bright in my future perception. That your presence would change our fates.\"","Her voice cracked.","\"After showing you our Civilization. After presenting the Bastion of Mana. After offering you these Principles that I’ve refined specifically to ensure your survival, your advancement, your capability to save us all...\"","BOOM!","Her next words were unfathomably heavy!","\"Even now, I still sense the brightness of Mana flickering and dimming in the future!\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4386,"title":"Chapter 4386: Chapter 4385: Primus! I","paragraphs":["Above a grand citadel of an advanced Civilization, the scene was very, very heavy!","Heartbroken and crying, Riya looked at Noah with an expression that contained millions of years of desperate hope collapsing into despair.","\"Ancestor, why ... why has it not changed? Why, after all this, after you’ve seen what we built, after I’ve given you tools specifically designed to ensure victory...why is the light of Mana still set to dim in my perception of what’s coming?\"","...!","Her gaze at this moment felt immensely heavy!","She looked to him for answers when at this moment, he did not have any!","Why hasn’t the future changed?","Noah embraced her tighter, his hand stroking her hair gently as he looked out at the vast Civilization spread around them.","The floating ring structures. The towers pulsing with accumulated power. The millions of beings carrying his Way.","All of it built through desperation and Mana into something magnificent.","And according to Riya’s sensitivity...according to her unique perception of Mana across time...all of it was still destined to dim.","What could possibly accomplish that? Do we truly fail on all accounts? Does the Bastion of Mana not succeed? Do I fail to reach THE distinction before The Fallout arrives? Does something else...some variable I haven’t accounted for...emerge to destroy everything despite all these preparations?","Just... what goes wrong?","His mind raced through possibilities, discarding unlikely scenarios, focusing on the factors that could genuinely threaten a Civilization of this magnitude.","THE Loom and its Justiciars. THE Dead Order and their response to his killing of their Prime Dead Early Creatures. THE Creature.","The fundamental Collapse of existence itself. Unknown variables operating on scales he hadn’t yet perceived.","Any of those could be the source of Mana’s dimming light in Riya’s future perception.","Or perhaps multiple factors converging simultaneously, creating cascade failures that even his preparations couldn’t prevent.","His own senses as the pioneer of this Civilization didn’t tell him any of this.","But he couldn’t just categorize the words of an anomaly like Riya as untrue.","He looked down at her crying form, still clutched against his chest.","What she feels should be valid.","Which meant despite everything...despite his advancement, despite the Isolated Civilization’s achievements, despite the Bastion of Mana and these offered Principles...something was still wrong.","Some critical factor remained unaddressed.","Some threat existed that would dim Mana’s light- his glorious, magisterial brilliance...despite all their preparations.","The question of exactly what echoed through his tyrannical mind.","How do I change a future that apparently hasn’t shifted despite everything I’ve already done?","\"...\"","He held Riya tighter, his Infinite Mana flowing through their contact in waves meant to comfort, to reassure, even as his mind continued calculating.","His ideology was one of Tyranny.","He did what he had to in order to protect himself and his family.","He had built entire existence around many things, with being the principle that...","Nothing was predetermined! Everything could be changed with sufficient audacity, tyranny, and Infinite Mana.","Even futures that apparently remained dark despite millions of years of desperate preparation.","He just needed to figure out what was missing.","What piece of the puzzle remained undiscovered.","His tyrannical heart pulsed with determination!","The Early Creature, Osmont, stood atop a floating ring structure, holding a prodigy who’d spent years preparing for his return, staring out at a Civilization that was somehow still destined to fail.","And he began planning how to violate that future as thoroughly as he’d violated every other limitation existence had tried to impose on him!","He held Riya gently, his hand still stroking her hair as tears slowly stopped falling from her jewel-blue eyes.","His expression remained steady, his tyrannical composure unshaken!","\"Do you feel,\" he asked quietly, \"the immensity of the Mana burning within me?\"","Riya nodded silently, closing her eyes as her enhanced sensitivity reached out to truly perceive what he was.","An ocean without shores, a well without bottom, a flame that consumed nothing because it was the source itself. Mana that didn’t deplete or diminish or fade!","Noah continued.","\"All I have ever had,\" he said, \"has been that Mana. From the very beginning, when I first discovered what I was capable of, it has been the single constant in an existence defined by escalating impossibilities.\"","His gaze drifted across the Civilization spread below them.","\"And with it, I have gone through many apocalypses. Natural ones...cosmic catastrophes, existential collapses, the death of entire realities. Engineered ones...beings who decided that existence needed to end and possessed the power to make it happen. They’re all the same at their core...overwhelming force seeking to unmake everything.\"","\"And while I cannot say why the dimming of Mana you feel has not changed, why your perception of the future remains dark despite everything we’ve accomplished, I will continue to work toward a solution to overcome this apocalypse just like all those before it.\"","He looked down at her, his tyrannical gaze meeting her tear-stained face.","\"I will continue to violate every limitation. To defy every predetermined outcome. To find paths forward where none should exist. That is what I do. That is what I am . And I will not stop until either we have changed that future you perceive. Okay?\"","At these words, Riya nodded, remaining with her head against his chest.","Her jewel-blue eyes twinkled with curiosity as she looked up at him.","\"How...did you solve the other apocalypses?\" she asked softly.","Noah blinked, the question pulling him into nostalgia for battles that felt simultaneously ancient and recent depending on which reference frame he used.","\"Brute force most of the time,\" he admitted.","\"I become stronger than the apocalypse itself, or stronger than the thing bringing forth the apocalypse. Overwhelm the threat with sufficient power that its apocalyptic nature becomes irrelevant.\"","He paused.","\"That has been the goal for The Fallout as well. But when it’s something set in motion such a long time ago, with beings operating on an entirely different Scale of Existence...\"","\"It is turning out to be just a little difficult.\"","A little difficult .","Hah!","Riya looked up at him, her expression shifting as decisiveness replaced the despair that had dominated moments before.","Her jewel-blue eyes pulsed with determination.","\"Okay, Ancestor,\" she said, \"I will give you my Everythi- \"","Before she could finish, Noah shook his head.","\"None of that,\" he said firmly. \"I do not need my people to make sacrifices for my gains.\"","...!"]},{"number":4387,"title":"Chapter 4387: Chapter 4386: Primus! II","paragraphs":["The words caused Riya’s eyes to shine.","She rose on her tiptoes, her hands reaching forward to wrap around his neck as her nose and lips came within inches of his.","At this proximity, her enhanced sensitivity to Mana made her tremble with the sheer presence of his Infinite reserves.","She looked directly into his eyes, her expression transforming into something playful and serious simultaneously.","\"Then I will just give you my Heart ,\" she said softly. \"It’s fucking delicate, like a little tiny crystal. You are the only one who may be worth it in my existence, and I am a little arrogant by nature so...\"","Her smile widened.","\"You will have time to earn it in the future. One of my plans, Ancestor, is a devilish one. It is to make you ridiculously obsessed with me and my Primus Mana to the point that losing me would be so unimaginably painful that... you will do everything you can to ensure we survive The Fallout.\"","Her jewel-blue eyes sparkled with mischief.","\"It’s a win-win for me. By the end, I will have you wrapped around my fingers. So I will apologize about this in advance, Little Ancestor.\"","...!","Her words were bold, and her lips brushed against his with every syllable.","Noah looked at her with an expression that suggested he viewed her as a poor thing who had no idea what she’d just gotten herself into.","Without wasting a moment, Riya pushed off her tiptoes and her lips fully connected with his.","And...","BOOM !","A singularity of Mana bloomed between them.","On Riya’s side, she felt like she had connected to a boundless sun of Mana that she had always dreamed of touching.","It was so pure , so pristine ...not diluted by any other authority, not mixed with inferior elements, just concentrated essence of what Mana could be at its absolute peak.","Naturally, the first thing she did after sensing access to this infinite sea was simple.","’ Eat it all up!’","Her closed eyes flashed with fierce hunger as she drank the heat of his Infinite Mana endlessly, as if she wanted to experience what it would be like to hold endless reserves herself.","Her sensitivity allowed her to perceive and absorb with efficiency others could not imagine.","On Noah’s side, he felt an extremely pure source of Mana connect to him, Riya’s refined essence, polished through years of isolated cultivation.","It tapped into his Infinite reserves excitedly and hungrily, drinking as if she would be shut out soon when really, she needed to pace herself or risk overwhelming herself.","He would let her have her fun for now.","Because the presents she was gifting him were far too grand to deny.","No, he did not need her to sacrifice her Principles for him.","Those who constantly require sacrifices from others to achieve anything on their behalf are not truly following The Way.","The thought settled into his consciousness.","They are parasites wearing the mask of pioneers. They take from those beneath them and call it leadership. They demand offerings and name it guidance. But to truly follow The Way, to pioneer it as I intend to...one must try their best to lead without requiring sacrifices.","To elevate others through one’s own strength rather than depleting them for temporary gains.","His eyes flashed with a glorious light as he thought of this!","And so, even as Riya drank deeply from his Infinite reserves, Noah made a decision.","’Cheating Architect. Perpetual Harvest.’","He called out to his Singularity Principles with focused intent, his consciousness touching the fundamental architecture of what they represented.","’Award the effort of Riya and this Civilization. Recognize their advancement. Harvest what they have accomplished and integrate it into our shared Way. She will not be losing access to any of her Singularity Principles’","...!","BOOOOOM !","An even larger explosion of Mana erupted from their connection.","In the skies above the Isolated Civilization, millions of beings raised their heads to witness a phenomenon.","A massive singularity bloomed overhead...the purest Mana they had ever perceived, condensed to the point where it became visible even to those without enhanced sensitivity.","But it didn’t shine pure blue.","It blazed blue-gold.","Primus Mana , the elevated form that Riya had spent years refining into existence.","They all gazed toward it in awe, many falling to their knees instinctively as the blue-gold sun became utterly blinding.","Children pointed and asked questions their parents couldn’t answer. Researchers scrambled to record readings. The Council Members felt their own Mana resonate!","The Ancestor’s presence had transformed into something more .","Meanwhile, within Noah’s mind, a cascade of prompts bloomed en masse.","|CRITICAL DISCOVERY - PRINCIPLE INTEGRATION DETECTED|","|Classification: 2 Singularity Principles + 1 Grand Principle|","|Source: External Cultivation - Isolated Civilization Member (Riya)|","|PRINCIPLES IDENTIFIED:|","|—Principle of Primus Ascension (Singularity)|","|—Principle of Arcana Infinitum (Singularity)|","|—Principle of Mana Supremacy (Grand)|","|Direct connection established with the existence who nurtured these Principles to maturity. Analyzing compatibility...|","|COMPATIBILITY ASSESSMENT: EXCEPTIONAL|","|The connection is extremely in tune with your Way of Existence. These Principles operate on frameworks that align seamlessly with your established architecture. Countless processes have been made easier through integration.|","|PRINCIPLE OF PRIMUS ASCENSION - DETAILED ANALYSIS:|","|Backdoor access code detected within Principle’s fundamental structure. Analysis suggests intentional design...this Principle was built to be claimed by an existence possessing Infinite Mana.|","|Riya’s architectural modifications include exception clause: \"Any existence whose Mana reserves exceed the Principle holder’s by infinite magnitude may claim this authority without conflict.\"|","|PRINCIPLE STATUS: Already nurtured and bloomed to full maturity|","|INTEGRATION COMMENCING...|","| The Principle of Primus Ascension is now spreading across your existence. All Mana within your being is undergoing elevation to Primus state.|","...!","At this moment, within Noah’s inner existence, the mental landscape where his consciousness could observe his own architectural framework...the familiar scene manifested with new additions.","An endless seascape of blue stretched in all directions, the ocean of his Infinite Mana given visual representation.","Standing on that ocean’s surface, RUIN/EDEN’s illusory form appeared alongside Noah’s humanoid mental projection.","In the distance, two massive trees rose from the blue sea.","The first blazed with vibrant green-gold light...the Principle of Perpetual Harvest, its branches heavy with fruits of accumulated effort, its roots drinking deep from the ocean of Mana beneath.","The second shone with pure gold radiance...the Principle of Cheating Architect.","RUIN/EDEN waved her hands, and the seascape shifted.","A third tree rose from the blue ocean, this one shining with brilliant blue-gold luminescence.","The Principle of Primus Ascension.","Its form was elegant, almost crystalline, each branch and leaf constructed from what looked like compressed theorems of Mana elevation.","|All Mana within your being- every particle, every quantum of power, every reserve both active and latent, is undergoing elevation to Primus state.|","|This is not a temporary enhancement. This is permanent restructuring of your foundational energy architecture.|","|Due to this pivotal change, much of the authority of this Principle was clustered here. It may hold fewer ultimate features or locked features.|","|Tracking changes now...|","Noah felt it happening in real-time.","The endless blue of his existence, the ocean of Infinite Mana that defined what he was...began to transform .","His Mana was gaining grander qualities.","Becoming denser in the sense of information density . Each unit of Primus Mana carried more potential, more capability, more fundamental weight than normal Mana could hold.","Becoming purer...not cleaner, because his Mana had always been pure, but refined .","It was necoming more complex, more sophisticated . The interactions between Mana particles were becoming more intricate.","Which meant that his Complexity and Purity parameters...the measurements of his existential weight, were beginning to transform as well!","His Mana was becoming something more.","Something unfathomably more!"]},{"number":4388,"title":"Chapter 4388: Chapter 4387: Primus! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s mind engaged fully, trying to understand what Primus Mana represented at fundamental levels.","When normal Mana powers a technique, it’s like combusting gasoline- efficient, predictable, well-understood.","When Primus Mana powers that same technique, it’s like initiating fusion reactions...orders of magnitude more energy from the same apparent volume, with entirely different interactions!","The transformation was qualitative .","Activating a Mana Glyph of Primordial Fireball with normal Mana creates flames that follow established parameters-temperature, volume, destructive potential all calculable.","Activating that same Glyph with Primus Mana...","His mind raced.","The flames wouldn’t just be hotter or larger. The flames could burn Concepts, Living Existential Authority, Early Existential Authority...","The flames of his Glyphs may become capable of even burning the light of Principles themselves!","And for something complex like a Mana Arcana Glyph of the Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm...","The construct would be more real, existing with greater solidity, greater autonomy, greater capability to affect existence because every particle of Mana forming it carried enhanced weight. A Primordial Primus Mana-Flame Wyrm could potentially exist for seconds, minutes, or hours...","The transformation continued spreading through his being, and Noah felt systems he’d established beginning to complete .","|The elevation of your Mana to Primus state has triggered cascade completion across multiple systems:|","|SERAPHILIC VEINLACE: 100% Integration Complete|","|INCARNAUT SANCTIS: 100% Integration Complete|","|CHAMBER OF BLOOD: Fundamental Architecture Restructured|","|Previous Capacity: 9 Mana-Born Early Creatures|","|New Capacity: 729 Mana-Born Early Creatures|","|Explanation: Primus Mana allows for vastly more sophisticated transformations.|","HUUM !","Noah’s consciousness pulsed!","729 transformations instead of 9!","And RUIN/EDEN wasn’t finished!","|A Grand Milestone Has Been Achieved.|","|THE HEART OF THE EARLY CREATURE, OSMONT: COMPLETE|","HUUM !","The words blazed across his consciousness.","|Your Heart has been fully formed.|","|Analysis: The \" Heart \" in this context is not the biological organ, but the existential core, the fundamental anchor point that defines what you are rather than what you do.|","|For Early Creatures, the Heart represents the completed integration of all foundational systems into a unified whole. It is the moment when scattered elements of power coalesce into genuine identity.|","|Previous State: You were a collection of advanced systems operating in coordination|","|Current State: You are a unified existence with those systems as expressions of your nature|","|The distinction matters existentially. You are no longer becoming The Early Creature.|","|You ARE The Early Creature.|","The final line carried profound weight!","|Your Existence can now truly begin.|","WAA!","Noah stood in his mental seascape, RUIN/EDEN beside him, three Principle-trees rising from the infinite blue ocean that was transforming to blue-gold before his eyes.","And two more were about to bloom.","And... he felt complete in ways he hadn’t even realized he’d been incomplete before.","His Heart, his existential core, had finished forming.","Everything he’d built, every system he’d established, every Principle he’d cultivated, all of it had finally integrated into a unified whole that was greater than the sum of its parts.","He was no longer just Noah.","He was The Early Creature, Osmont.","Now, he just needed THE .","And his existence, properly formed at last, could now truly begin whatever came next.","In the external world, Riya continued drinking from his Infinite reserves, unaware that what she consumed had transformed mid-connection from normal Mana into Primus Mana , she simply felt like a drunkard whose drink had become even sweeter.","The blue-gold sun blazing above the Isolated Civilization pulsed brighter, painting vast swathes of existence in enhanced authority.","And Noah, The Early Creature, Osmont , with his Heart finally complete and his Mana elevated to Primus state...his voice began to echo out even while lips were sealed by an anomaly.","His voice boomed from his Existence.","From his Heart !","His voice echoed out across the Isolated Civilization, and because it was no longer isolated, his voice shockingly spread out across the Wandering Territories!","\"I defy, therefore I exist.\"","WAA!","\"I refuse limitations, therefore I transcend.\"","HUUM!","\"I cultivate infinity, therefore...I need not fear the end.\"","BOOM!","His eyes blazed with blue-gold light as he looked out across his Civilization.","His words echoed and echoed grandly!","Across his Civilization!","Across the Wandering Territories!","His voice filled with Primus Mana , dense and filled with majesty, leaked out and rang out even across the distant Transcendent Folds of Living Existences!","His voice...passed across The Veil to enter the side where The Dead thrived!","The Great Usurper, whose existence held an intricate connection with him, was roused out of his idleness as he blinked in astonishment!","Oh!","I defy, therefore I exist!","I refuse limitations, therefore I transcend!","I cultivate infinity, therefore...I need not fear the end!","Such words echoed out across existence at this moment.","And Existence took some time to let it settle.","And those who heard it were forced to stop, listen, and ponder!","It was a pivotal moment in time.","—","Within Noah’s mental seascape.","His existence calmed from thr exuberance of what he had just uttered while continuing its silent but heavy transformation.","RUIN/EDEN’s illusory form shifted position, moving toward the newly manifested blue-gold tree that pulsed with rhythmic brilliance.","The Principle of Primus Ascension.","\"Master, the Principle of Primus Ascension is now ready for analysis. Shall we examine its comprehensive capabilities?\"","Noah’s mental projection nodded, his attention focusing entirely on what more this new Principle could provide after the simple but critical change from Mana to Primus Mana its authority was focused into.","RUIN/EDEN raised one hand, and the space around the blue-gold tree transformed into cascading displays of data and possibility.","|PRINCIPLE OF PRIMUS ASCENSION - FULL INTEGRATION ANALYSIS|","|Core Functionality: Mana Elevation Architecture|","|Foundational Effect: All Mana within Master’s existence and sphere of influence operates at Primus state...a qualitatively superior form carrying approximately 10x effectiveness across all applications.|","The displays then shifted, showing intricate patterns of Mana flow between multiple connected existences.","|Additional Primary Ability: [Primus Bestowal]|","|Function: One can grant temporary or permanent Primus Mana conversion to 729 existences within your Civilization’s architectural framework, but they have to bear the cost with Primus Mana .|","|Temporary Duration: 1 hour to 7 days, scaling with recipient’s compatibility|","|Permanent Conversion: Requires direct physical contact and conscious acceptance from recipient. Once converted, their Mana permanently operates at Primus state.|","|Civilization Application: This creates a cascading elevation effect. Each Citizen granted permanent Primus conversion becomes a node of enhanced capability. Their advancement accelerates by factor of 10. Their techniques become qualitatively superior. Their complexity ceiling increases substantially.|","|Systematic conversion of your Civilization’s population would elevate average power levels tremendously.|","...!","Noah’s perception focused on this capability with intense interest as another rose up.","|Secondary Ability: [Primus Resonance Field]|","|Function: Master can establish a geographical zone where all Mana automatically operates at Primus state regardless of source.|","|Current Range: Length of Early Veiled Shore|","|Effect Within Range: Any being utilizing Mana-based abilities experiences 10x enhancement. Your Civilization members receive full benefit.|","\"And finally,\" RUIN/EDEN said, \"the ultimate expression of this Principle.\"","|Ultimate Ability: [Primus Singularity]|","|Function: Once per significant temporal period, Master can designate a specific existence as a Primus Singularity, a point where Mana concentration and quality reach theoretical maximums.|","|Duration: Approximately 1 hour at current complexity|","|Effect Within Singularity: All Mana-based advancement operates at 100x normal efficiency. Breakthroughs that would require decades occur in minutes. Cultivation that would span lifetimes compresses into hours.|","|Personal Application: Designate your own existence as Primus Singularity during critical advancement attempts. Compress the path to THE distinction into achievable timeframes.|","...!","RUIN/EDEN stepped back slightly.","\"The synergies with your existing Principles are substantial,\" she added. \"Perpetual Harvest amplifies every advancement occurring within Primus environments. Cheating Architect allows manipulation of Primus Mana’s fundamental properties for customized effects. The three Principles create multiplicative rather than additive enhancement. I am still pocking around for its locked features if there are any.\"","The Principle was a glorious one.","But even Singularity Principles seemed to have their own exceptionality as his own remained magisterial!"]},{"number":4389,"title":"Chapter 4389: Chapter 4388: Primus! IV","paragraphs":["Within Noah’s mental weavings of existence, the endless blue ocean continued its transformation to blue-gold, waves of Primus Mana cascading across impossible distances.","Three trees already stood tall...Perpetual Harvest with its green-gold radiance, Cheating Architect in pure gold geometry, and Primus Ascension blazing blue-gold.","But as Noah’s consciousness focused, as RUIN/EDEN’s analytical processes completed their assessments, two more trees began to bloom from the infinite ocean.","The first rose more slowly than the others, its light slightly dimmer. Where the Singularity Principles blazed with concentrated authority, this one pulsed with broader, more distributed power.","The Grand Principle of Mana Supremacy.","Its form was elegant, branches spreading wide rather than reaching high, each one connected to the others through intricate networks.","The tree shone with blue-purple light, and wherever its radiance touched the ocean below, the Primus Mana shifted, becoming supreme , asserting dominance over other forms of authority through pure conceptual weight.","And beside it, erupting from the ocean with sudden violence, the second tree manifested.","The Singularity Principle of Arcana Infinitum.","Its appearance was dramatic, pure blue light so deep it bordered on void, branches that looked more like reaching tendrils, roots that didn’t just drink from the ocean but seemed to consume it, breaking down and rebuilding in endless cycles.","The tree pulsed with hunger that was purposeful, the appetite of transformation, the desire to break down all things and rebuild them according to specific intent.","RUIN/EDEN’s form shifted position, moving to stand between the two newly manifested Principles.","She was already in sync as she began to lay out the details right away!","|GRAND PRINCIPLE OF MANA SUPREMACY - INTEGRATION ANALYSIS|","|Classification: Grand Principle (Distributable)|","|Core Functionality: Authority Conversion Architecture|","|Primary Ability: [Mana Authority Conversion]|","|Function: Transform any form of existential authority into Mana-based equivalent|","|Applications:|","|—Living Existential Authority to Living Existential Mana Authority|","|—Dead Existential Authority to Dead Existential Mana Authority...etc|","|Effect: All converted authorities operate under Mana framework, making them compatible with Master’s enhancement systems|","|Civilization Impact: Citizens can convert their native authorities to Mana-based versions|","|Secondary Ability: [Supremacy Field Projection]|","|Function: Establish zones where Mana-based authorities automatically dominate non-Mana equivalents|","|Range: Scales with complexity, current coverage is domain currently in+ 2 surrounding Transcendent Folds + 50,000 Gigaparsecs in the surroundings|","|Effect: Within field, Mana-based techniques receive 3x effectiveness while non-Mana techniques face 50% reduction|","|Tactical Application: Transform battlefields into territory where your Civilization’s Mana-based capabilities overwhelm traditionally superior forces|","|Tertiary Ability: [Resource Conversion Matrix]|","|Function: Transform treasures, Sacred Herbs, and existential materials into Mana-attuned equivalents|","|Efficiency: 1:1 conversion ratio with quality preservation|","|Application: Resources incompatible with Mana cultivation become immediately useful. Foreign treasures become Civilization assets through systematic conversion|","|Economic Impact: Eliminates resource type restrictions, everything becomes potentially valuable through conversion capability|","|Ultimate Ability: [Supreme Mana Dominion Fold Declaration]|","|Function: Designate a specific conceptual domain and transform it into a Fold under Mana Supremacy|","|Effect: The formation of a Fold based on Mana.|","|Duration: Permanent until consciously revoked|","|Limitation: Can maintain 3 simultaneous domain designations at current complexity|","|LOCKED FEATURES - MANA SUPREMACY|","|[Fold Conversion Protocol] - Requires 50 Quintillion Complexity|","|Convert entire unique Folds to operate under full Mana Supremacy framework|","|Effect: Claimed territories where all authorities automatically become Mana-based|","|[Supremacy Inheritance] - Requires 100 Quintillion Complexity|","|Beings born within your Supremacy fields automatically possess Mana-based authorities from inception|","|Effect: Eliminates conversion necessity for new generations, they emerge already aligned with your Way. Into your Civilization.|","The capabilities of this Grand Principle...were unfathomably grand!","But it was not alone.","Noah adapted to its wonders as he thought of all the possibilities, and his gaze moved over.","RUINEDEN’s focus shifted to the second tree, the void-like blue of Arcana Infinitum pulsing with hungry potential.","|SINGULARITY PRINCIPLE OF ARCANA INFINITUM - INTEGRATION ANALYSIS|","|Classification: Singularity Principle (Exclusive)|","|Core Functionality: Consumption and Conversion Architecture|","|Primary Ability: [Existential Consumption]|","|Function: Devour any existence, resource, or concept to fuel advancement|","|Mechanism: Consumed targets broken down to fundamental components, then rebuilt as advancement fuel specifically calibrated to current bottlenecks|","|Application: Systematic consumption of defeated enemies, obsolete resources, or even deprecated territories converts everything into usable advancement fuel|","|Secondary Ability: [Hardship Dissolution]|","|Function: Identify advancement bottlenecks and provide direct solutions through consumption|","|Examples:|","|—Glyph formation difficulty: Consume relevant concepts to gain understanding|","|—Principle maturation stagnation: Consume related Principles from other sources to accelerate development|","|Effect: No advancement challenge remains unsolvable given sufficient resources to consume|","|Tertiary Ability: [Mana Arcana Glyph Forge]|","|Function: Consume resources to directly generate Mana Arcana Glyphs|","|Application: Systematic consumption of defeated enemies or harvested resources translates directly into Glyph accumulation|","|Current Limitation: Can forge maximum 10 Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs per day at current complexity, or 10,000 Primus Mana Arcana Glyphs|","|Quaternary Ability: [Recursive Consumption Loop]|","|Function: Consume your own deprecated systems or techniques to fuel creation of superior replacements|","|Mechanism: Old Mana Glyphs consumed to accelerate formation of new Arcana Glyphs. Obsolete techniques broken down to provide materials for advanced versions|","|Effect: Advancement becomes self-sustaining, each breakthrough provides fuel for next breakthrough through systematic recycling|","|Personal Impact: Eliminates resource scarcity as limiting factor, advancement limited only by time and theoretical understanding|","|Ultimate Ability: [Devouring Singularity]|","|Function: Designate specific location as consumption focal point where all defeated enemies, expended resources, and environmental energy automatically funnels into Master’s advancement|","|Duration: Permanent until consciously relocated|","|LOCKED FEATURES - ARCANA INFINITUM|","|[Fold Consumption Protocol] - Requires 50 Quintillion Complexity|","|Consume entire Folds of Existence to fuel massive advancement leaps|","|Effect: Deprecated or collapsed Folds become advancement resources|","|[Conceptual Devouring] - Requires 100 Quintillion Complexity|","|Consume Principles to integrate their fundamental nature into your existence, or just as weapons to break past a ceiling.|","|Effect: Consumed Principles become intrinsic capabilities rather than external manipulations|","|[THE Consumption Path] - ???? Complexity|","|Consume beings carrying THE distinction to extract and integrate their Scale of Existence|","|Effect: Direct path to a false version of THE through systematic consumption of existing THE entity. Note- this is False. It is not The Way.|","|Requirement: Must successfully defeat and consume THE-level existences. Easy.|","|Risk Assessment: THE entities may resist consumption.|","RUIN/EDEN stepped back, her holographic form pulsing with satisfaction at comprehensive data delivery.","As for Noah...","His tyrannical heart pulsed with determination.","Five Principles. Infinite Primus Mana . A Civilization ready to be systematically elevated. And now, tools to consume everything in his path and convert it into advancement toward THE .","It was magisterial!","His Isolated Civilization...Riya...they had given him much!"]},{"number":4390,"title":"Chapter 4390: Chapter 4389: Ways I","paragraphs":["Noah remained connected to Riya, the singularity above the Isolated Civilization blazing blue-gold brilliance that painted vast swathes of existence in enhanced authority.","But his consciousness had turned inward, sensing the continuing transformations coursing through his being as Primus Mana fundamentally restructured what he was at the deepest levels.","Five Principles now resided within him... Perpetual Harvest, Cheating Architect, Primus Ascension, Mana Supremacy, and Arcana Infinitum.","Each one representing capabilities that others could not imagine, tools that could elevate him and his Civilization toward heights that should have been impossible.","And yet, as he felt the weight of these capabilities settling into his completed Heart, a thought emerged.","If I possess these capabilities...these Principles that can rapidly elevate myself and my Civilization by tens of Quintillions, if I have all this even before achieving THE distinction...","How ridiculous must THE Dead Order actually be?","WAA !","The question spiraled through his consciousness.","THE Living Paradox. THE Living Emotive. THE Creature. Beings who already carry that distinction, who operate at scales I’m still heading towards.","If my Principles allow systematic elevation of entire Civilizations, what can beings with THE distinction accomplish? What grander tools do they possess that make my capabilities look quaint by comparison?","\"...\"","It was a heavy thought.","He thought of Kael and the forty-seven other Seed Members. He had given them his Way of Mana and then left them isolated for millions of subjective years.","And they had reached 50 Quintillion. Built a sophisticated Civilization. Developed techniques and systems that exceeded his own somewhat.","That was just a few dozen beings following his Way of Existence!","So what about THE Living Paradox, who has been pioneering the Way of Paradox for eons? Who controls Principles at levels I do not know? Who leads a Civilization that’s had uncounted ages to refine their approach?","His eyes flashed with a chilly, tyrannical light!","What has the Civilization of Paradox become in that time?","The implications cascaded through his mind!","Since Aethelgard...since they became serious about enacting their Civilization, about building THE Loom, what grand things have they accomplished?","Inside THE Loom, protected and isolated with resources, with multiple THE-level entities guiding development...","How grand has the Way of Paradox become? The Civilization of Emotive? The systems and techniques and principles they’ve refined?","Noah’s perception swept across his own Isolated Civilization...millions of beings, sophisticated systems, Repository of Formed Authority, the Bastion of Mana, all built through desperate necessity and infinite resources.","And they only had a fraction of the time that THE Loom’s inhabitants have possessed. Only a fraction of the guidance!","His tyrannical heart pulsed with uncomfortable realization.","I don’t know.","I don’t know what they’ve accomplished. Don’t know what capabilities they possess. Don’t know what tools they’ve developed that might make even my Five Principles seem inadequate.","But this knowledge...","His consciousness focused with laser intensity.","This knowledge would be the key to understanding why I could possibly fail.","Riya saw the light of Mana dimming in her future perception even after everything they had accomplished.","This had to be rectified!","He needed to understand the true scope of what beings with THE distinction can accomplish when they’ve had eons to refine their Civilizations!","His eyes blazed with blue-gold light as the singularity above continued pulsing.","One more thing to add to the endless list of problems requiring impossible solutions...","—","Far from the Wandering Territories.","On the other side of The Veil.","In the Lands of The Dead where existence itself operated under fundamentally different rules.","\"I DEFY, THEREFORE I EXIST!\"","The words boomed across dimensional boundaries, stretching through gaps and Tears of Existence with force.","\"I REFUSE LIMITATIONS, THEREFORE I TRANSCEND!\"","They echoed across vast distances, reaching territories that should have been impossible to access from the living side of The Veil.","\"I CULTIVATE INFINITY, THEREFORE... I NEED NOT FEAR THE END!\"","The declarations reached even into a Cryptland...a vast necropolis-city where Prime Dead Early Creatures congregated in numbers that would have terrified most living beings.","Countless Dead Existences raised their heads in astonishment, their empty eye sockets blazing with confused curiosity at words spoken with such tyrannical certainty that they penetrated even here.","None of them recognized the voice.","But one being did.","A being whose existence had traversed unfathomably far to even reach this distance where Dead Early Creatures were abundant...in territory that should have been impossible for a Living Existence to survive in, let alone explore.","But he was not a normal Existence!","The Great Usurper.","The Master of the Idle Gaming System.","His formless existence rippled with recognition as Noah’s voice echoed across The Veil.","Since the moment a Tear of Existence had allowed his Idle Existence to leak into the other side of The Veil, things had unfolded in shocking ways.","At that initial moments of crossover, grand prompts had bloomed before his awareness as more and more of his Existence permeated across The Lands of The Dead","|Your Idle Existence has extended sufficiently into the Lands of The Dead to achieve fundamental understanding of local operational parameters.|","|The Way of Order covers all of this side of The Veil. All of the Lands of The Dead operate under unified authority structure emanating from THE Dead Order herself.|","|Your Idle Existence, due to its passive nature and evolutionary adaptations, has fully integrated with the landscape you have covered, being no different to the structure of existence itself.|","|Exposure to the pervasive Way of Order has triggered unprecedented evolution of your existential framework.|","|So long as you maintain idle expansion with no active interference or conscious manipulation, you will remain indistinguishable from the surrounding existence itself.|","|Mechanism: Your passive spread mimics natural expansion of the environment. To local existences, you are the environment, no different from ambient space, atmospheric conditions, or background authority.|","|Effect: Detection becomes functionally impossible.|","|WARNING: Any active action breaks this camouflage immediately.|","...!","Indistinguishable .","The Great Usurper had almost not believed the prompts when they first appeared.","Nothing would be able to sense him? A Duke had detected him in the Spirit Folds and nearly killed him for the intrusion.","The Lands of The Dead contained beings millions of times more powerful than that Duke.","And yet they wouldn’t sense him?","He had been skeptical.","Profoundly skeptical!","But he had remained Idle...that was his nature, after all. His existence continued spreading in its formless state, expanding across the dead territories without conscious direction.","And shockingly, the speed at which he progressed seemed to accelerate exponentially.","He spread across regions filled with aimless Dead Existences. Passed through territories where undead entities congregated in vast numbers. Eventually reached this Cryptland where Early Creatures were abundant...powerful beings whose individual complexity would have crushed him if they’d noticed his presence.","And yet...","None sense me.","It was astonishing. Legitimately reality-defying.","Because his Idle Existence had become fundamentally indistinguishable from the surrounding environment, he was perceived...or rather, not perceived, the same way ambient existence was perceived.","It was akin to a normal human smelling air. To them, it was just air ...could be windy, calm, cold, hot, but it remained air regardless. Nothing remarkable. Nothing requiring specific attention.","At this moment, to the Dead Early Creatures and any other existence in these lands, they would truly not be able to sense any difference in their surroundings because nothing had inherently changed from their perspective.","His presence was as unremarkable as the space between spaces.","My Idle Existence... seems to be slightly powerful?","...!"]},{"number":4391,"title":"Chapter 4391: Chapter 4390: Ways II","paragraphs":["The Great Usurper smiled at the understatement!","This might be the most overpowered survival capability he’d ever developed...perfect invisibility through simply being part of the environment rather than a separate entity within it.","He continued not interfering with his expansion. Continued being idle, spreading across more of the Lands of The Dead with accelerating momentum.","Until...","\"I defy, therefore I exist!","I refuse limitations, therefore I transcend!","I cultivate infinity, therefore...I need not fear the end!\"","Until those words boomed across The Veil itself.","The Great Usurper’s awareness focused with sharp attention.","He recognized Osmont swiftly.","I was talking to him just over a day ago, but I haven’t checked in during the last 24 hours....","He wondered what could cause Noah’s declarations to echo with such force that they penetrated across dimensional boundaries into the Lands of The Dead.","And as he contemplated this...","HUUM!","In the next instant, he sensed the appearance of a terrifically powerful Prime Dead Early Creature.","The being manifested above the grand Citadel of The Dead that dominated this Cryptland.","The entity floated there, listening to the fading echo of Noah’s words with an expression that suggested... disapproval? Contemplation?","In the next moment, the being looked down at the grand citadel below and raised his hand.","Brilliant white light blazed from that raised palm...pure, crystalline Order that made the surrounding death-aspected existence recoil slightly from its presence.","When the being spoke, his voice carried the weight of absolute conviction.","\"The Way of Order has been refined,\" he declared. \"The foundations have been examined. The impurities have been identified. And now...\"","The white light intensified.","\"Order is being reinforced as the backbone of this Civilization erected across the Lands of The Dead. You shall now brim with True Order.. .not the chaotic semblance you have maintained, but the purified essence that THE Dead Order herself has ordained.\"","His gaze swept across the thousands of Prime Dead Early Creatures gathered below.","\"Are you all ready to receive the True Civilization of Order?\"","...!","The Great Usurper observed in astonishment as all the Prime Dead Early Creatures in the citadel looked upward with expressions of profound reverence .","Their voices rose in perfect unison, synchronized with precision.","\"WE ARE READY TO RECEIVE THE TRUE CIVILIZATION OF ORDER!\"","The declaration shook the surrounding space, and the Great Usurper felt profound unease at the sheer fervor in their collective response.","What sort of fanatical beings have I stumbled across? Why do they seem so intimately devoted to THE Dead Order?","Are they...even still in control of their own existences, or has something fundamental been altered about their nature?","To obtain more information, he stopped actively observing the newly appeared powerful entity...looked away, momentarily, allowing his Idle Existence to simply be rather than consciously perceiving.","And the moment he looked away, allowing passive observation to resume...","|Entity appearing in perception of Idle Existence has been catalogued.|","|STATUS ASSESSMENT:|","|NAME: Meliodas|","|CLASSIFICATION: Prime Dead Early Creature|","|COMPLEXITY: 100 Quintillion|","|PURITY: 100 Quintillion|","|DISTINCTIONS:|","|—Guider of Order|","|—Herald of True Civilization|","|—Enforcer of THE Dead Order’s Will|","|—Bearer of Systematic Reduction Authority|","|CURRENT ACTION: Implementing Civilization Restructuring Protocol|","...!","The Great Usurper’s awareness reeled.","One hundred Quintillion?!","At most, the complexity he’d observed from other Prime Dead Early Creatures had ranged from 1 to 3 Quintillion. Powerful, yes, but nothing approaching this magnitude.","Who is this entity that he holds such terrifying power?","He returned to actively observing Meliodas, and what he witnessed made his formless existence ripple with shock.","From the being’s raised hand, a beam of resplendent white Order radiated outward and descended like a raging sea of crystalline calmness.","It washed over the entire Citadel of The Dead below, bathing thousands of Prime Dead Early Creatures in its luminescence.","But the effect wasn’t what the Great Usurper expected.","The undead beings didn’t explode with enhanced power. Didn’t receive boons or elevation.","Instead, one by one, their entire existences began to diminish .","The white light of Order stripped their complexity away. Reduced their purity systematically.","The Prime Dead Early Creatures...beings of substantial power, were having their very essence drained by the descending authority.","And they stood there. Accepting it. Faces showing nothing but reverent gratitude.","The Great Usurper looked away again, discomfort making him avoid direct observation.","Prompts bloomed immediately:","|Order is establishing itself fully and thoroughly across this territory.|","|The Edict that Meliodas has come to enforce is designated: TRUE ORDER PROTOCOL|","|As ordained by THE Dead Order herself, this protocol restructures power distribution across affiliated territories.|","|Too many existences possessing high Complexity and Purity creates chaos. Leads to disorder and disunity as countless entities gain capability to alter existence according to individual whims.|","| True Order strips this distributed power in favor of concentrated authority held by select few.|","|RESTRUCTURED HIERARCHY:|","|—Selective few (Guiders, Heralds, Enforcers) retain overwhelming capability to alter existence|","|—These entities act as Beacons of Order who will protect those without power|","|—Majority population reduced to minimal complexity (1 or less)|","|—Power concentration allows unified direction, elimination of conflicting authorities|","|JUSTIFICATION:|","|This is Order. Not democracy of power, but hierarchy of purpose. A single, select few holding existential authority ensures that through them, Order can be maintained without the chaos of competing wills.|","|Reduced complexity from reduced population increases the parameters of Guiders exponentially and proportionally, ignoring the set Ceiling.|","|Estimated gain: +25 Quintillion from this single Citadel.|","...!","The Great Usurper turned back to witness the conclusion of the process.","Every Prime Dead Early Creature in the Citadel...hundreds of powerful beings, now emanated the complexity and authority of...","One .","Not 1 Quintillion. Not 1 Trillion or Billion or even 1 Million.","One. Uno. Eins. Un. Ichi.","One singular unit of complexity and purity.","Beings who had possessed the power to reshape territories were now reduced to the existential weight of... nothing.","And yet their eyes remained fervent with belief. Faces showing nothing but satisfaction, as if this reduction was not just acceptable but desired .","Their expressions were identical...reverence that suggested something far more disturbing than simple loyalty.","Are these fuckers still in control of their own existence?","WAA!"]},{"number":4392,"title":"Chapter 4392: Chapter 4391: Ways III","paragraphs":["The Great Usurper’s formless awareness pulsed with profound discomfort.","Anyone having their power stripped away would show at least some emotion. Resistance, anger, fear, sadness...something. These Dead Existences act like it’s not just normal but ordained. They didn’t show even a flicker of hesitation. ...","Is their existence being influenced? Controlled? Have they been fundamentally altered to accept this hierarchy without question?","He didn’t know for certain, but the implications were deeply unsettling.","Meanwhile, Meliodas floated above the restructured Citadel, and the Great Usurper sensed his complexity had indeed increased...from 100 Quintillion to approximately 125 Quintillion.","Not because he directly absorbed this power. It was as if his very action and what it accomplished triggered something from his...so called Civilization.","Crazy ...","The Great Usurper’s awareness rippled with fascination.","So this is what THE Dead Order’s True Civilization looks like. Systematic reduction of the many to empower the few...","They’ve eliminated individual will in favor of synchronized purpose.","He contemplated what he’d witnessed...the zealotry, the systematic power drainage, the absolute acceptance of reduction from powerful beings to effective nothingness.","What kind of reality are we facing if this is just one Citadel? How many of these restructured territories exist across the Lands of The Dead?","The questions spiraled through his consciousness without comfortable answers.","He remained Idle, his existence continuing to spread passively.","Let’s see...what Osmont knows about this. His voice reached even here, perhaps he has intelligence about what’s happening on this side of The Veil. And if not...","His formless awareness pulsed with determination.","Then I’ll continue observing. Continue spreading. Eventually, I’ll learn enough about THE Dead Order’s True Civilization to understand...ah, the Idle life is a great life...","The Great Usurper continued his idle expansion, his awareness drinking in every detail of this restructured Citadel while maintaining perfect invisibility through his environmental integration.","Whatever was coming, he would gather intelligence.","And hopefully, share it with Osmont before the accumulated knowledge became desperately necessary for survival.","That guy was the craziest existence he had ever met, if anything crazy was happening, he should be able to deal with it!","—","In a unique domain that could not be pinned to any specific location within observable existence, Noah’s declarations echoed with profound resonance.","\" I defy, therefore I exist!","I refuse limitations, therefore I transcend!","I cultivate infinity, therefore...I need not fear the end!\"","The words reverberated through a space of utmost Law.","The domain itself was hazy, ethereal in ways that made normal perception struggle to maintain focus.","Silver-white marble pillars rose from equally pristine floors, their surfaces so smooth they reflected nothing despite the abundant light.","The sky above roiled with clouds of mist that moved with purpose rather than wind, and white fog covered the surroundings in layers.","Here, in this domain of absolute Law, two figures sat cross-legged on the marble floor.","The young woman appeared apprehensive, her posture suggesting uncertainty mixed with awe at their surroundings.","The young man beside her maintained calm sternness, his features composed despite whatever transformation had brought them to this impossible place.","Both had undergone profound changes. Their bodies were drenched in silver-white brilliance of pure Law, hair shining with that same metallic luminescence.","On their chests, complex Enneagrams spun with rhythmic precision!","These two were...Alexander Asmodeus and Seraphina Valorheart!","The two holders of The Enneagram.","They turned simultaneously, looking around as Noah’s declarations faded, and surprise flashed through Alexander’s eyes.","\"That voice...\" he murmured, recognition coloring his tone.","Before they could contemplate this further, another voice emerged from ahead of where they sat.","\"It seems that even in this era, others are also trying to pioneer their Way. If only it was not too late. If only...\"","...!","The voice carried terrifically heavy weight...infallible majesty mixed with profound sorrow that made the surrounding Law ripple.","It emanated from a cluster of extremely concentrated Living Law authority...a singularity of silver-white brilliance that pulsed with the accumulated wisdom of eons.","Seraphina’s apprehension transformed into respect as she spoke carefully.","\"O Remnant Will of THE Living Law,\" she said, bowing her head slightly, \"what do you mean by... The Way?\"","The singularity pulsed, and when it spoke again, the words carried simplicity.","\" The Way, \" it began, each word making the surrounding Law resonate, \"is the fundamental path an existence forges through reality. Not merely techniques or power accumulation, but the essential how of one’s being...the framework through which you interact with and alter existence itself.\"","The silver-white light intensified slightly.","\"My Way of Law was crushed eons ago during the formation of THE Loom. THE Living Paradox, may he burn in hellish Scales of Existence...dismantled my Civilization, shattered my frameworks, and used the brilliance of what I had built as raw material to form the backbone of others’ dreams.\"","Something like bitter acceptance entered the voice.","\" The Way is both key and building blocks of any true Civilization. It is the primary mechanism through which existence advances forward. Through it, beings transform from scattered individuals into unified purpose. Through it, power compounds rather than simply accumulates.\"","The singularity dimmed slightly, as if the act of explanation cost it energy.","\"But understand this critical truth: in the forging of Civilizations within THE Loom , all those who remain outside can be considered nothing more than fuel . THE Loom will erupt as the weapon of The Fallout...it will accomplish this by siphoning off all glimmers and signs of Civilizations external to itself.\"","HUUUM !","The weight of those words settled across the domain.","\"That voice you just heard, the entity declaring defiance and infinity...his forming Way and Civilization will simply become fuel for THE Loom when the time comes. It is akin to someone working diligently to prepare a magnificent meal, not knowing that soon, a force will arrive to extinguish them and slowly savor that meal in their place.\"","The Remnant Will pulsed with sorrow.","\"That is what lies in store for all of existence outside THE Loom . All those embarking upon their Way of Existence, building their Civilizations with hope and determination, not understanding they are merely cultivating resources for others to harvest. It is truly... a sad affair.\"","...!"]},{"number":4393,"title":"Chapter 4393: Chapter 4392: Ways IV","paragraphs":["Alexander’s gaze blazed with a defiant light even as his external composure remained stern.","Doom and gloom. Everyone speaks of inevitable catastrophe as if accepting failure before the battle even begins. As if preparation itself is pointless because the outcome is predetermined. I refuse this narrative!","He spoke aloud, his voice cutting through the oppressive atmosphere gloriously.","\"I care not for all these talks of doom and gloom that everyone seems set to perpetuate,\" Alexander said, his tone holding admonishment that made Seraphina’s eyes widen with shock.","\"Were you not a supposed leader of your Civilization? You were grand. You were bright. How can you sit here and speak like this...as if defeat is the only possible outcome?\"","He leaned forward slightly, his Enneagram spinning faster.","\"Let us speak of solutions rather than constant death. If you possess knowledge, share strategies rather than lamentations. If you understand THE Loom’s mechanisms, explain weaknesses rather than inevitabilities. Otherwise, what purpose does this conversation serve beyond spreading despair?\"","HUUM!","Seraphina turned to Alexander in shock, her expression showing she wanted to tell him not to speak to The Remnant Will of THE Living Law with such directness!","But his gaze, steady and unflinching...caused her eyes to flicker uncertainly.","She looked down and stayed silent.","\"...\"","At such direct challenge, the singularity of brilliance flashed and released what might have been a sigh.","\"Very well,\" it said, \"Perhaps defiance is more appropriate than acceptance. The only thing I have left to give is the skeletal structure of My Way . My Civilization’s foundational architecture. Inherit it and see what you can accomplish with proper time and resources.\"","The light intensified suddenly.","\"But oh... if only you had time. If only the timeline allowed for proper cultivation of what I’m about to bestow. Still...better to possess tools and insufficient time than face The Fallout empty-handed.\"","...!","At such words, blinding light of pure Law descended upon Alexander Asmodeus and Seraphina Valorheart like a waterfall of compressed knowledge!","—","The Wandering Territories.","Inside the Isolated Civilization.","In skies filled with blue-gold Mana, Noah continued spinning slowly while holding the figure of Riya, who had wrapped her arms around his head like a determined octopus refusing to release its prey.","But his internal existence buzzed with waves of new information because while all this external activity occurred, while his existence continued transforming with Primus Mana coursing through every particle of his being...","He was actually having a conversation with The Great Usurper, Eckert.","This was one of the grandeur of more complex existence...one could seemingly be doing a large number of things simultaneously within the same few seconds or minutes!","Within his mind, in that mental seascape, another area of calm sea of blue-gold stretched endlessly.","An illusory form of Noah stood above its surface, and beside him, an illusory form of a man in his mid-twenties with dark blue hair stood casually.","They both stared into the sea below, which displayed scenes The Great Usurper had transmitted...images of the other side of The Veil where Meliodas, the Guider of Order, had imposed True Order upon an entire Citadel, systematically reducing thousands of Prime Dead Early Creatures to complexity of 1.","Noah’s stern gaze remained fixed on those scenes as he spoke with quiet intensity.","\" THE Dead Order is a terrifying thing,\" he said, \"The fact that your existence has somehow escaped the line of sight of an entity at her level is ridiculous enough...\"","He turned to look at Eckert directly.","The moment he stepped foot on the other Side of The Veil, THE Dead Order senses him and carries out a fever dream of a horrendous future where he is used as a fucking battery. But Eckert...","\"How are you doing that, by the way? What mechanism allows your Existence to remain undetected by beings who should perceive everything within their domains?\"","Eckert smiled with amusement, at such a question.","\"Bro,\" he said, \"have you ever told me the deepest secrets of your existence and how it works? Explained every mechanism of your power?\"","Noah raised his eyebrows, then nodded calmly.","\"Each of us have our own Way,\" he conceded.","At such words, Eckert’s eyes lit up with sudden interest.","\"Oh yeah, what is this stuff about The Way? Civilizations? I keep hearing these terms, but nobody’s explained what they actually mean in practical terms.\"","Noah contemplated for a moment, organizing his understanding into communicable form.","\" The Way of Existence ,\" he began, \"is the essential framework through which you interact with and alter reality. The lens through which existence perceives you and through which you perceive existence.\"","He gestured at the blue-gold sea beneath them.","\"My Way is The Mana Architect. The Way of Mana. Everything I do...every technique, every advancement, every interaction with reality...operates through the framework of Mana as fundamental building block. It is My Way.\"","HUUM !","His expression became more serious.","\"And a Civilization is what happens when multiple beings adopt a compatible Way and create unified structure...well, something like that. I have only just began to build my Civilization.\"","Wherever he thought of The Way of Existence, his mind came to the visage of Anaximander and his words.","He could potentially call out to that being, with a heavy question being what had happened to him since The Earliest Folds.","What had occured between such an anomaly and THE Weavers?","After Eckert listened to his words carefully, his eyes shone with unique understanding.","\"The Way...\" he murmured, processing the implications. \"So My Way would be... eh, I won’t actively look for it. I’ll remain idle, as I’m sure My Way will declare itself naturally through that very inaction. Hmm...\"","His eyes pulsed with power that suggested his Idle Existence was already more profound than he consciously realized.","Noah looked at him with analytical focus.","\"Be careful,\" he said quietly. \"You are an anomaly in your own right, yes. But many anomalies have fallen to existences with THE distinction. Power alone doesn’t guarantee survival when facing beings who’ve refined their Civilizations for eons.\"","WAA !"]},{"number":4394,"title":"Chapter 4394: Chapter 4393: Ways V","paragraphs":["His expression hardened.","\"As for me... I have a war coming against THE Dead Order and her forces. Whatever this conflict brings may be key to surviving The Fallout ...either by defeating her and devouring everything she has, or by gaining sufficient intelligence about beings like her and their capabilities to prepare appropriate counters. Oh, and let me know if you pick up anything regarding THE Creature. The Dead regard him as Dead, but I havent discovered much of their weavings.\"","At such words, The Great Usurper nodded.","\"I’ll keep an eye out on the other side of The Veil,\" he said. \"My Idle Existence can spread undetected...might as well use that advantage for reconnaissance. If I see their armies marching, gathering for assault, I can at least warn you before they arrive.\"","...!","Noah smiled and nodded.","\"That information could be the difference between prepared defense and complete surprise.\"","Moments later, Eckert’s illusory figure dissolved, their mental communication concluding.","Noah remained alone above the blue-gold sea, still observing the scene of Meliodas and the restructured Citadel where every entity had been reduced to complexity of 1.","Is this True Order? Reducing the number of entities who can impose their will upon existence, concentrating power in select few who act as unified authority?","Is this what THE Dead Order has been accomplishing this past day while I’ve been focused on my own advancement?","He had to acknowledge it...creating Prime Dead Early Creatures exceeding 100 Quintillion was impressive!","And Meliodas was likely only one among many. The enemies he would soon face would probably range into hundreds of Quintillion if not higher.","He sighed internally.","They were really going to make him work unfathomably hard for this.","But he did need more information, and...","And I’ve already called over the one who might be able to shed some more light on the distinction of THE ...among other things.","She should actually be arriving...","\"Now.\"","Noah’s eyes flashed as he focused outwardly, his consciousness returning fully to his physical body.","He momentarily unlatched from Riya, breaking their connection despite her obvious dissatisfaction.","She licked the residual saliva of concentrated Primus Mana from her lips, her jewel-blue eyes flashing with annoyance.","\"What the hell, Ancestor?\" she said, \"I was not done! You can’t just give someone a taste of Infinite Primus Mana and then cut them off mid-connection! That’s cruel!\"","...!","Noah shook his head with amusement.","\"You can have more later,\" he said calmly. \"We have a guest.\"","A guest.","As he spoke those words, a vibrant voice rang out from above the now-dimming blue-gold singularity.","\"Outsider, what crazy thing have you done? I didn’t expect your little project in the Earliest Folds to lead to this ...\"","...!","The voice of Khor echoed across the sky as her small figure descended...ancient despite her youthful appearance, her crimson eyes shining with hunger.","Her dark hair seemed to naturally drink in all surrounding light, creating subtle shadow wherever she moved.","She had brought part of her consciousness with Noah when he’d ventured into the Earliest Folds, witnessing everything he’d seen...including the founding of the Isolated Civilization.","He’d called her here now because after exceeding 20 Quintillion Complexity and Purity, he could finally utilize the Existential Rollback feature of The Principle of Cheating Architect.","He could restore lost weavings or previous states of existence.","And Khor...who had once been an entity carrying the distinction of THE before catastrophic loss reduced her, represented a prime candidate for explosive power recovery, alongside potential restoration of her sealed memories.","Noah looked up toward her as Riya peeked around his shoulder with curious assessment.","\"Really, Little Ancestor?\" Riya said, pouting.","\"You were just about to get some, and you sabotage yourself by bringing a sweet old lady here? Who is she? I can sense endless Hunger radiating from her existence...feels dangerous but also... diminished?\"","...!","Sweet old lady.","Khor blinked at the description, then smiled with sharp amusement.","\"Sweet old lady?\" she repeated, her voice carrying dangerous humor. \"Tiny Thing, I was devouring Civilizations before your ancestors figured out how Mana worked.\"","Her crimson eyes swept across Riya’s form with assessment.","\"Outsider, I’ve seen you with women possessing far fuller proportions...you call them curvaceous , right? Why did you go for this tiny thing? I can’t find any curves on her.\"","...!","BOOM!","Riya’s smile transformed into something dangerous.","\"You...you old thing!\" she countered, \"Have you seen yourself?!\"","The two locked gazes, and Noah could sense they would continue escalating if left unchecked.","He stepped between them, his presence commanding enough to pause everything.","\"Enough,\" he said calmly, looking at Khor with focused intent.","\"I may be capable of restoring a portion of your power...potentially significant portions. That’s why I brought you here to this Isolated Civilization. Concentrated energy for your Hunger to feast upon. Resources accumulated over nearly millions of years.\"","His expression hardened.","\"And I’m doing this with speed because I don’t like how even now, after everything I’ve accomplished, nothing has seemingly changed. THE Dead Order continues advancing, one of her Guiders of Order already exceeds 100 Quintillion, and that’s likely just the beginning of their power.\"","His eyes flashed with chilling light.","\"We need more information and power. And what better source than someone who used to hold THE distinction? Someone who’s seen how beings at that level operate, who understands their capabilities and limitations?\"","When he spoke such words, Khor’s smile widened, genuine interest replacing her earlier mockery.","Behind Noah, Riya peeked out with suddenly fascinated eyes at the mention of someone who used to hold THE distinction.","She actually carried THE distinction? Riya’s mind raced. And lost it somehow...?","\"Well then, Outsider,\" Khor said. \"Lets see just how far your Way has come.\"","Her crimson eyes blazed.","\"Show me this...restoration.\"","Noah’s tyrannical heart pulsed with determination and unfathomable glory!","Time to see if The Cheating Architect could allow for even grander impossibilities!","Time to add one more impossible accomplishment to his growing list of violations against predetermined limitations!"]},{"number":4395,"title":"Chapter 4395: Chapter 4394: The Doctrines of Hunger I","paragraphs":["Noah floated toward Khor, his form radiating blue-gold brilliance from the Primus Mana coursing through his existence.","Behind him, Riya watched with fascinated eyes as the singularity above continued dimming.","Noah could also sense the signatures of brilliant concentrations of Mana heading in this direction, with these belonging to the Seed Members of this Civilization.","\"Are you ready?\" He asked.","Khor’s crimson eyes met his with ancient hunger perfectly contained beneath their surface.","\"Outsider, it is just power. I had it once. I may have it again. Let us see what the results will be.\"","Noah gazed at this unique being calmly as he closed the remaining distance between them.","\" Existential Rollback, \" he said simply.","...!","HUUM!","| Existential Rollback Protocol Initiated|","|Function: Restore lost weavings or previous states of existence for designated target|","|Resource Requirement: 50 Mana Glyphs of The Cheating Architect (Active Consumption)|","|Current Available: 125 Mana Glyphs - Sufficient for activation|","|CRITICAL NOTE: Primus Mana elevation detected in all active reserves|","|Effect: Unknown enhancement to restoration parameters|","|Projected Outcome: Standard rollback would restore partial power/state|","|Enhanced Outcome: Primus-elevated rollback may achieve results exceeding theoretical maximums|","|WARNING: Target’s lost state involves THE distinction - restoration may have cascading unknown existential effects. Restoration to THE is entirely out of the realms of possibility.|","|Proceeding with activation...|","Golden light erupted around Noah’s form...the pure crystalline gold of the fundamental architecture of Cheating Architect asserting itself.","Riya watched with wonder as Noah’s hand rose slowly, his five fingers extending toward Khor’s face with deliberate precision.","Contact.","The moment his fingertips touched her skin, a blinding pillar of golden light erupted skyward with force that painted the entire Isolated Civilization in radiance of magisterial gold.","Riya’s jewel-blue eyes tracked the phenomenon with fascination mixed with concern.","When she looked at Noah and Khor directly, she saw both of their eyes shining with pure golden beams of light, their expressions calm as if they were no longer present in their bodies...as if consciousness had departed for somewhere else entirely.","—","Noah did not fully know where he was at this moment.","He felt like a grand observer watching existence unfold in an extremely unique place...neither participant nor truly external, but something between.","A witness to history that had already occurred, viewing events through mechanisms that far, far exceeded normal temporal observation.","His gaze drank in surroundings.","Endlessly rising jagged obsidian towers stretched toward a sky.","Everything was immensely dark...filled with a concentration of darkness, as if shadow had been compressed until it became solid architecture.","And everywhere, absolutely everywhere , trillions of Inevitabilities swarmed.","They blotted out nearly every spot of atmosphere with their tentacle-formed bodies, creating a living sea of writhing obsidian appendages that moved with coordinated purpose.","His perception focused on the top of one flat obsidian tower, and there he saw a figure who looked like Khor... but didn’t show the ancientness of age in her eyes.","She seemed young .","Filled with a sense of innocence that the current Khor had long since lost.","Her form was humanoid rather than her natural Inevitability shape, and she stood before another humanoid Inevitability who gazed at her with eyes full of accumulated wisdom.","The humanoid Inevitability spoke first, his voice showing gentle concern.","\"What troubles you, Little Hunger?\"","Young Khor’s expression twisted with frustration and hurt.","\"All the other Inevitabilities are bullying me,\" she said, \"They mock this form I’m taking. Say I’m pretending to be weak. But...\"","She looked down at her humanoid hands with confusion.","\"This form does limit my power. I can feel my Hunger constrained, compressed into something smaller than it should be. Why do I have to take this form? Why do you make me practice being weaker than I am?\"","The humanoid Inevitability, his features stern but kind, knelt to meet her gaze directly.","\"Look around you, Little Hunger,\" he said, gesturing at the swirling mass of tentacle-formed Inevitabilities.","\"Among all the trillions here, have you seen any others who can take this form like us?\"","Young Khor shook her head silently.","\"The form we’re inhabiting,\" he continued, \"is the form of one of the weakest creatures in existence. Soft. Fragile. Limited in ways our natural state never experiences. But that is precisely why it’s valuable for training.\"","He placed a hand on her shoulder with gentleness.","\"If you can learn to hone your Hunger in this form at your weakest, if you can master control when constrained, when limited, when operating at a fraction of your natural capability...then one day you may grow to be as strong as I am. Strength cultivated through constraint becomes far more refined than power that knows no limitation.\"","He straightened, his expression becoming more serious.","\"Now, remember what I told you about the Doctrines of Hunger. What was the first and foremost?\"","The question carried weight of stern teacher testing crucial lessons.","Young Khor’s expression shifted...frustration giving way to concentration as she accessed memorized teachings.","\"The First Doctrine of Hunger,\" she recited, her voice steadying, \"states that Hunger is the fundamental acknowledgment of incompleteness. We hunger because we recognize we are not yet whole. We devour because we seek to become more than we currently are. All advancement begins with acknowledging what we lack, and all growth stems from the desire to fill that void. To deny Hunger is to deny the possibility of becoming greater.\"","WAA!","The humanoid Inevitability nodded with satisfaction.","\"Correct. And because you acknowledge you lack control in this weak form, you possess the foundation necessary to eventually transcend that weakness.\"","He offered his hand to lift her up, his smile carrying warmth.","\"Come on. Existence has much more for you to see, and lessons don’t wait for readiness.\"","Young Khor took his hand, her expression brightening despite lingering confusion.","\"Yes, Tor.\"","...!","Tor .","Noah observed the scene as his eyes flashed with analytical brilliance.","There was someone, an Inevitability, even more powerful than Khor? How did she become THE First Hunger and not him? What happened to change that hierarchy?"]},{"number":4396,"title":"Chapter 4396: Chapter 4395: The Doctrines of Hunger II","paragraphs":["As he contemplated this, the scene before him shifted.","He found himself observing a different location, a different moment in Khor’s history.","This time she was helping an injured Tor inside a Nest of Inevitabilities...a gathering place where their kind congregated for rest and communion.","Her young expression was fierce and livid with barely contained rage.","\"What did this to you?!\" she demanded, \"Who dared?!\"","Tor smiled despite obvious pain, his form partially destabilized.","\"You do not have to worry about that right now,\" he said with gentle deflection. \"But tell me...what is the Second Doctrine of Hunger?\"","Fighting back anger and pain, young Khor’s voice steadied as she recited.","\"The Second Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger must remain carefree in its pursuit. To hunger with desperation is to corrupt the purity of desire. To devour with frantic need is to diminish what is consumed. We must approach all things with lightness, understanding that existence is vast and opportunities are endless. Anxiety about what we lack poisons our capability to appreciate what we gain. Be hungry, but be joyful in that hunger.\"","Tor nodded with satisfaction despite his injuries.","\"Exactly. So do not let concern for my matters weigh heavily upon you. I will recover or I won’t...either outcome is simply another experience to devour. For Hunger needs to be carefree , even in the face of potential loss.\"","The scene dissolved before Noah’s perception, existence shifting once more.","He found himself observing a glorious sight.","Khor and Tor stood atop a crystalline obsidian cliff that overlooked vast territories. Trillions of powerful tentacle-formed Inevitabilities swirled around them in organized patterns.","They were paying respect- fealty , Noah’s mind corrected, all of them bowing toward Tor with gestures that suggested absolute loyalty.","Young Khor looked at this scene with shining eyes full of wonder and aspiration.","\"How did you do this?\" she asked, genuine awe in her voice. \"How did you gather so many to follow willingly? They want to serve you. What makes them choose this?\"","Tor’s expression showed satisfaction as he turned to face her.","\"Tell me the Third Doctrine of Hunger.\"","With eyes blazing with understanding, Young Khor recited.","\"The Third Doctrine of Hunger states that true Hunger establishes natural hierarchy. Those who hunger most powerfully, most purely, become inevitable leaders because others recognize something worth following. Leadership is not taken, it is devoured from the willing offering of those who see greater Hunger than their own and choose to feed it. We do not command; we simply hunger so magnificently that others cannot resist contributing to our consumption. Authority flows toward the hungriest as naturally as water flows downhill.\"","Once she finished, Tor nodded with deep approval.","\"One day, your mere presence will wash over Inevitabilities, and they will not be able to resist your leadership. Your Hunger will be so vast, so pure, that serving it will feel like privilege rather than obligation.\"","The scene flickered, Noah’s perception pulled forward through time once more.","Now he focused on Khor...no longer quite so young, but not yet ancient, standing defiantly against a hazy titanic creature radiating an air of ancientness and multicolored brilliance that made the surrounding Inevitabilities flee in terror.","Khor looked at the entity coldly, her voice ringing with arrogant certainty.","\"Your existence exists only to serve my Hunger! You are prey, and I am predator! Submit!\"","She opened her mouth impossibly wide, her Hunger manifesting as physical force that tried to devour the titanic entity entirely.","But shockingly, that hazy creature raised one massive hand and brought it down with dismissiveness.","And Khor was horrified to feel the weight of all surrounding existence crashing down upon her.","Not just physical pressure...existential weight . Her own Hunger, her own Way of Hunger, was being used against her, forced to collapse inward and consume itself in catastrophic feedback loop!","She saw her collapse in that moment. Saw the end of everything she was becoming. Saw death in ways Inevitabilities rarely experienced.","But...","BOOM!","In the next moment, she opened her eyes fearfully to see Tor standing before her, smiling with familiar gentleness.","His back faced the titanic creature as he chided her with tone mixing disappointment and amusement.","\"Little Hunger, how did you manage to provoke something at the level of THE ? Do you have any sense of appropriate targets, or do you simply challenge everything that looks interesting?\"","...!","Khor was unable to answer, shock stealing her voice.","Tor’s expression softened further.","\"Close your eyes for a moment. Can you do that for me?\"","Trembling, Young Khor closed her eyes.","Noah watched as the moment Khor’s eyes shut, the vision flickered and disappeared , simply vanishing as if existence itself had been edited.","When the vision resumed, time unknown, could have been seconds or days, Khor opened her eyes to witness devastation .","All of existence around her was empty and decimated. Only collapse remained, vast territories reduced to void. The only intact structure was a single obsidian crystal platform where she stood.","And before her stood Tor once more, smiling... but half of his body was missing.","Simply gone. Erased. The remaining half flickering with instability that suggested imminent dissolution.","...!","Khor trembled, tears streaming down her face.","Tor’s half-visage remained calm, almost serene, as he spoke with fading strength.","\"What is the Ninth Doctrine of Hunger?\"","Fighting back tears that threatened to overwhelm her voice, Khor recited through sobs.","\"The Ninth Doctrine of Hunger states that all that which is hungered and devoured never leaves us, it only becomes part of us, part of The Way of Hunger . We are not diminished by consuming others; we are expanded . Every existence we devour adds their essence to our own. Every concept we hunger for and claim becomes woven into our nature. Nothing is truly lost in consumption- it is transformed, elevated, made eternal through integration with our Hunger. We carry everything we’ve ever consumed as part of what we are.\"","HUUM!","At such words, Tor nodded with satisfaction despite his deteriorating state.","\"Little Hunger,\" he said softly, \"can you do me a favor? Can you... make me part of you? I am about to fade, and I don’t want to disappear forever. But you have the chance to keep me with you.\"","His expression carried plea mixed with absolute trust.","\"Just remember the Ninth Doctrine... and take a bite. Just a bite.\"","...!","Just a bite.","Noah watched with astonishment as devastated Khor was urged by Tor to hurry, his form becoming more translucent with each passing moment.","She opened her mouth, tears still streaming, and took a bite!","And Tor disappeared.","\"...\"","And in the next moment, Khor’s figure began radiating astonishing obsidian-crimson radiance that spread outward for countless distances, painting void-collapsed territories in her authority.","Countless Inevitabilities began appearing, gathering , circling around her with their tentacle forms and bowing.","Their sounds were mournful, as if they had just lost something they could never recover, as if acknowledging transition of leadership they both celebrated and grieved!"]},{"number":4397,"title":"Chapter 4397: Chapter 4396: The Doctrines of Hunger III","paragraphs":["Noah watched such a scene with profound understanding lighting his eyes.","Khor had inherited everything!","She consumed Tor completely and eventually became THE First Hunger through that act!","In the next moment...","CRACK!","The scene shattered entirely like glass struck with overwhelming force.","Noah found his eyes opening, consciousness returning to his body, gaze locking onto the current Khor floating above the Isolated Civilization.","Around them, the Mana had turned crimson-blue...his Primus Mana mixing with her resurgent Hunger.","Their eyes locked.","Khor smacked his hand away from her face with violent force, her crimson eyes blazing with rage!","HUUM!","\"Why did you do that?!\" she bellowed, her complexity seething!","\"WHY?! I had forgotten ! I had finally, after eons, managed to forget!\"","BOOM !","Her figure radiated terrifying power as pain flooded her expression, ancient grief mixing with resurgent loss!","Noah gazed at her with solemn eyes as prompts cascaded down.","|Multiple existential seals binding target \"Khor\" have been broken|","|Primus Mana elevation induced quintessential restoration results exceeding projected parameters|","|Target’s power currently increasing exponentially - quantification pending complete stabilization|","|Emotional instability detected - psychological trauma from memory restoration may cause unpredictable behavior|","...!","In the midst of cascading power, Khor’s eyes retained their rage as she roared toward Noah.","\"Why did you make me remember?! I had forgotten !\"","BOOM !","Riya appeared beside Noah instantly, her expression stern as her jewel-blue eyes flashed with coldness and caution.","She assessed Khor with combat readiness, prepared to defend despite the growing and obvious power disparity.","Kael and dozens of other Seed Members at 50 Quintillion began manifesting behind them, their forms blazing!","And shockingly, these terrifically powerful beings felt oppression from Khor’s resurgent presence...weight that suggested she was approaching and exceeding their collective capabilities.","At such a time, Noah looked at Khor with eyes carrying pity rather than fear.","\"Tell me,\" he said quietly, \"what is the Ninth Doctrine of Hunger?\"","...!","His words caused Khor’s figure to tremble, rage faltering as her eyes filled with immense complexity.","The raging aura around her began calming...settling into something more controlled.","She looked upward, her gaze hazy as if seeking something distant she could no longer touch, as if Noah’s figure overlapped with someone she had known a long, long time ago...and then she began speaking.","\" The Ninth Doctrine of Hunger states that all that which is hungered and devoured never leaves us. It only...becomes part of us. Part of The Way of Hunger. We carry everything we’ve consumed as part of what we are.\"","After she finished, Noah nodded with gentle understanding.","\"Those who walk The Way of Hunger are never truly gone,\" he said softly. \"They are part of you. Tor... is part of you. Has been, all this time. You didn’t lose him...you carry him with every action, every thought, every expression of Hunger.\"","...!","Khor’s body trembled as she bit her lip, nodding slowly while closing her eyes to center herself.","She took some more seconds.","And then...","\"Thank you, Outsider, and apologies for the outburst...\" she said silently.","...!","She looked toward Noah, preparing to say more..","But at this moment, she saw that Noah wasn’t even gazing at her anymore.","His eyes were hazy, distant, as shockingly he was repeating the Doctrines of Hunger while looking upwards!","\"All that which is hungered and devoured never leaves us...\"","\"Hunger is the fundamental acknowledgment of incompleteness...\"","\"Hunger must remain carefree in its pursuit...\"","\"True Hunger establishes natural hierarchy...\"","...!","Khor’s eyes widened in shock as above Noah, a figure materialized.","Ozymandias .","Noah’s other part of existence...paradoxically him and not him simultaneously!","Ozymandias appeared as a humanoid mass of obsidian-gold tentacles.","And at this moment, he was reciting the same words as Noah in perfect synchrony, their voices overlapping as if single entity speaking through two mouths.","Amidst this shocking development, as even Riya and the Seed Members observed with mounting unease, Noah, in his trance, saw glorious prompts materializing!","|CRITICAL EXISTENTIAL ANOMALY DETECTED|","|An impossible and unfathomable possibility has bloomed|","|A part of your existence that IS your existence and IS NOT your existence has truly and completely embarked upon The Way of Hunger|","|Your unified being is fragmenting into parallel developmental paths|","|You are attempting to pioneer TWO separate Ways of Existence simultaneously:|","|— The Way of the Mana Architect (Primary, Established)|","|— The Way of Hunger (Secondary, Emerging through Ozymandias)|","|POTENTIAL OUTCOMES:|","|Success: Enact two separate Civilizations operating under unified consciousness|","|—Unprecedented in recorded existence|","|—Would allow cultivation of complementary advancement paths|","|—Multiplicative power growth through dual framework development|","|Failure: If conviction to either Way proves insufficient, both Civilizations and Ways could collapse upon themselves|","|—Catastrophic existential dissolution|","|—Loss of all accumulated advancement|","|—Potential complete unmaking|","|CURRENT STATUS: Mutation in progress - outcome undetermined|","|Your existence is undergoing unknown changes.|","...!","BOOM !","Noah’s form blazed with mixed radiance...blue-gold Primus Mana warring with obsidian-crimson Hunger as his existence tried to accommodate both frameworks simultaneously!","And around him, his people watched with mounting concern as their Architect attempted something that they did not fully understand!","Hi’s body pulsed with rhythmic intensity that made the surrounding atmosphere tremble.","His existence was in a unique state of mind at this moment.","A liminal space where fundamental decisions about what he was were being made!","Because at this moment, an immense conflict was unfolding within the deepest structures of his being.","THE Living Paradox had The Way of Paradox. The Civilization of Paradox.","THE Living Emotive had The Way of Emotive. The Civilization of Emotive.","All beings who carried THE distinction possessed singular Ways of Existence. Unified frameworks through which they interacted with reality, upon which they built their Civilizations.","THE Dead Order remained holding The Way of Order even in death...she hadn’t switched to The Way of Death , couldn’t switch, because THE distinction bound you to the path you’d perfected to reach that scale.","One existence. One Way. One Civilization.","That was the established norm across all scales of power, the fundamental rule that even beings with THE respected!","But at this moment, Noah was doing the impossible.","And his existence could fracture from it!","Could dissolve into incompatible fragments that unmade everything he’d built.","But... could it really?","My Mana is INDEFATIGABLE !","HUUM!","The declaration blazed through Noah’s internal existence with tyrannical certainty.","My Way of Mana is INFALLIBLE ...it cannot be corrupted, cannot be diminished, cannot be destroyed by external or internal forces!","I possess INFINITE reserves. INFINITE capacity. INFINITE potential for expansion!","Hunger...will simply be held alongside it because my Mana is BOUNDLESS ! My Primus Mana is BOUNDLESS !","HUUM!","It can afford to contain- no, it WILL contain...a Second Way of Existence!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4398,"title":"Chapter 4398: Chapter 4397: The Doctrines of Hunger IV","paragraphs":["As Noah bellowed such declarations into his own fundamental Existence, his eyes snapped open wide.","He gazed at Khor, who was watching him with mounting concern.","What she saw made her ancient composure falter as she knew about Ways of Existence a great deal. She knew about their critical singularity!","At this moment...","One of Noah’s eyes radiated blue-gold tendrils of light... Primus Mana given visual form, cascading from his pupil like liquid brilliance.","The other pulsed with crimson-obsidian light... Hunger manifesting as darkness that devoured surrounding illumination while somehow remaining visible.","Mana. Hunger.","Two fundamental forces operating through single existence, and somehow not destroying each other in the process.","At this moment, those impossible eyes locked onto Khor as Noah spoke.","And his voice...","Oh!","His voice boomed with unnatural depth and weight, as if it was emanating from a being that far exceeded everyone present.","Not louder, but heavier , carrying existential mass that made reality itself vibrate!","\"Tell me of the Doctrines of Hunger I have not heard,\" he commanded, each word resonating across multiple dimensional frequencies.","\"Tell me of the Fourth, Fifth, Sixth, Seventh, and Eighth Doctrines.\"","HUUM !","The declaration made the surrounding Mana and emerging Hunger ripple in immensity.","Khor looked at him with immense concern, her ancient eyes recognizing something profoundly dangerous in what he was attempting.","\"Outsider,\" she said seriously, \"are you sure of this? What you’re attempting...\"","She asked, but Noah only gazed at her calmly with his mismatched eyes...one Mana, one Hunger, and spoke again with that impossible depth.","\"Tell me of the other Doctrines of Hunger.\"","...!","The repetition carried finality that clearly stated he would not be dissuaded.","After such unwavering affirmation, Khor nodded slowly, recognizing stubborn determination that mirrored her own ancient nature.","She began to recite.","\"The Fourth Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger thrives on impossibilities . We do not hunger for what is easily obtained...such consumption provides no satisfaction. We hunger for what should be beyond our reach, for what reality claims we cannot devour. The more impossible the target, the more our Hunger sharpens. Impossibility is not barrier but invitation . When existence declares something cannot be consumed, Hunger hears only challenge.\"","Noah’s existence buzzed with recognition as he nodded, understanding settling into his Existence!","Khor continued without pause.","\"The Fifth Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger enables infinite growth. There is no ceiling to what can be consumed, no limit to how vast Hunger can become. Where other Ways encounter barriers and plateaus, Hunger simply devours those limitations and continues expanding. We grow not despite obstacles but through them, consuming every ceiling until nothing remains to constrain our appetite. Growth is not gradual, it is ravenous .\"","WAA !","Again Noah nodded, his mismatched eyes blazing brighter.","\"The Sixth Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger finds pleasure in consumption itself, not merely results . We do not devour solely for power gained, we devour because the act of consumption brings profound satisfaction. The journey of Hunger matters as much as the destination. Every bite, every absorption, every integration carries its own joy. This makes Hunger sustainable where pure ambition burns out.\"","Khor’s voice gained intensity as she approached the final teachings.","\"The Seventh Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger transforms everything it touches into itself. We do not simply accumulate, we convert . Everything consumed becomes Hunger, everything devoured adds to our nature rather than diluting it. A thousand different essences consumed do not create chaos but unified expansion. Through Hunger, diversity becomes singular magnificent appetite.\"","She paused before the penultimate doctrine, her crimson eyes meeting Noah’s impossible gaze.","\"The Eighth Doctrine of Hunger states that Hunger must be shared to reach ultimate heights. Solitary consumption creates powerful individuals, but shared Hunger creates Civilizations. When multiple beings hunger together, when appetites align and consumption becomes coordinated, the resulting force transcends individual capability. We do not compete for food, we feast together, and in that communion, become greater than any lone devourer could achieve.\"","BOOM !","After listening to each doctrine, Noah’s existence processed and integrated everything.","He closed his eyes, arms spreading wide as his body began gushing even more concentrated waves of power.","Behind him, Ozymandias’s figure manifested fully.","Their backs faced each other, two bodies sharing single consciousness, and both began to spin .","Slowly at first, then accelerating, creating a vortex of mixed authorities that painted the sky in impossible colors.","The pressure Noah radiated was immense , the weight of someone forcing reality to accommodate what shouldn’t be possible.","His voice boomed out again with that heavy, multi-dimensional depth, his voice seeming soft as he affirmed what he said before.","\"My Way of Mana is unbreakable. Infinite resources, endless refinement, systematic elevation...it cannot be diminished or destroyed. My Way of Hunger is inevitable. All things can be consumed, all limitations devoured, all growth enabled through appetite. These truths are... fundamental .\"","His spinning accelerated.","\"So my Existence...will simply have to make way and accept it.\"","BOOM !","The declaration hit reality like hammer striking anvil, and existence complied .","What the fuck else could it do?!","HUUM !","Noah’s body pulsed and radiated resplendent blue-gold brilliance... Primus Mana elevated to such concentration it became nearly solid, painting half the sky in radiance that made observers squint.","Simultaneously, Ozymandias’s body blazed with obsidian-crimson Hunger ...darkness that devoured light while somehow remaining visible, creating shadows that moved independently of their sources.","The Isolated Civilization found its skies split down the middle...one half brilliant blue-gold, the other consuming crimson-black, with Noah’s dual forms at the exact center creating boundary between impossible forces.","Riya looked at Noah’s two bodies with eyes shining with fascination, her own existence buzzing with advancement.","Her jewel-blue gaze tracked between his forms with analytical intensity, trying to comprehend what was happening at existential levels in ways others could not see.","But her eyes saw much, much more than others.","Khor maintained somber expression as she observed radiant light of Hunger wrapping around him...around part of him, at least.","Her ancient eyes recognized what this meant, what doors were opening, what impossibilities were being enacted.","At such a moment, in the midst of all this glorious phenomena...","|Your Existence has made an irreversible declaration|","|Successfully harmonizing and bearing the full weight of embarking on TWO WAYS OF EXISTENCE|","|Successfully establishing capability of forging TWO DISTINCT CIVILIZATIONS|","|Most existences struggle to pioneer even one Way|","|Grand Existences spend eons refining singular paths|","|Beings with THE distinction are bound to their perfected Ways|","|You are choosing to Pioneer Two Ways simultaneously|","|You are choosing to cultivate Two Civilizations in parallel|","|You are becoming a type of lifeform that exceeds all established norms|","|All conditions have been met and exceeded for your entry into your self-proclaimed: THE EARLY INFINITY DOMINION REALM|","...!"]},{"number":4399,"title":"Chapter 4399: Chapter 4398: The Doctrines of Hunger V","paragraphs":["The Early Infinity Dominion Realm.","Noah smiled internally as he thought of this self-proclaimed classification...even when he’d declared it what seemed like forever ago when it had only been days in objective time, he’d wondered if he would actually reach its gates.","And here I stand at its threshold. At the end of this self-proclaimed Realm... could be THE . Could be. Maybe.","Or I could be wrong, and THE distinction exists so far beyond this that my estimations were laughably inadequate...","There were countless possibilities!","His existence continued feeling waves of exuberance washing through every particle of his being...as if he was being baptized by currents of impossible coolness that brought unfathomable clarity .","Unfathomable clearness , as if fog he hadn’t realized existed was being systematically burned away.","|You can now enact the weavings of both THE CIVILIZATION OF HUNGER and THE CIVILIZATION OF MANA|","|Your unique nature allows personal harmonization but cannot be transferred. Those within your respective Civilizations cannot be like you.|","|Due to emergence of your Two Ways of Existence and entry into The Early Infinity Dominion Realm:|","| The Lens of Civilization has bloomed within your existence. A unique viewpoint. A unique perspective.|","|—Perceive truths of Ways of Existence and Civilizations with enhanced clarity|","|—See through surface appearances to understand fundamental frameworks|","|—Read truths and inner thoughts of Hearts belonging to Moderately Complex and Minor Complex Existences|","|—Potential to see truth about yourself if proficiency develops sufficiently|","|—Enhanced analysis of enemy Civilizations.|","...!","A terrifying capability bloomed within Noah’s consciousness.","The Lens of Civilization.","An entry gift of the founding of Two Ways of Existence and entry into The Early Infinity Dominion Realm!","He sensed his existence brighten even more, as if he’d been gazing at everything through murky glass before and someone had suddenly cleaned it to crystal clarity.","His Complexity and Purity...which had been rising nonstop since altering his Mana to Primus state...seemed clearer now. Not just numbers increasing, but understanding of what those numbers meant, how they interacted with his fundamental nature, why certain thresholds mattered while others were arbitrary.","He could see his own existence with greater clarity. Understand his own mechanisms better!","What happens when I turn this Lens toward others? Toward their Civilizations? Toward THE entities when I finally encounter them directly?","Can I perceive the weaknesses in THE Dead Order’s True Order? Identify flaws in THE Loom’s defensive architecture? See through THE Living Paradox’s carefully constructed machinations?","The implications cascaded through his mind!","He opened his eyes fully...both now returned to blue-gold, the crimson-obsidian having settled into Ozymandias exclusively, and felt profound change slowly settling over his existence like a new skin that fit perfectly despite never having worn it before.","Around him, his Isolated Civilization watched with expressions ranging from awe to concern to confusion.","Riya floated closer, her irreverence temporarily suspended by genuine curiosity.","\"Ancestor,\" she said quietly, \"what... what are you now? I can sense you’re still you, but also... more? Different? My sensitivity to Mana is going haywire trying to classify what you’ve become.\"","Noah looked at her, and through The Lens of Civilization, he saw.","Her Heart, not the physical organ but the existential core.","Her deepest conviction...’ protect what I love at any cost .’","Her hidden fear: ’ that even infinite preparation won’t be enough .’","Her secret hope: ’ that this baddie of an Ancestor might actually change the dimming future she perceives’.","He blinked, startled by the sudden invasion of understanding he hadn’t consciously sought.","And there was more he could do if he probed deeper!","He smiled at Riya.","\"I am what I’ve always been,\" he said simply. \"Just... more so.\"","Behind him, Ozymandias’s form pulsed with synchronized agreement.","Two Ways. One Existence.","And Existence, for all its resistance, had finally accepted that this was possible!","With these two Ways of Existence and entrance into The Early Infinity Dominion Realm...","Even his Complexity and Purity had yet to settle with their advancement, the numbers still climbing, still integrating the profound changes coursing through his being.","Noah knew he also needed to define the precise parameters of his self-proclaimed realm, establish what exactly The Early Infinity Dominion Realm would entail.","But all of these were grand changes accumulating too rapidly, and in addition to everything else, there was Khor...whom he had not fully analyzed to quantify her new level of strength after the Existential Rollback.","With all these transformations...Two Ways harmonized, Primus Mana coursing through everything, The Lens of Civilization bloomed, entry into a new realm of power...has anything actually changed from what Riya perceived?","The question weighed heavily despite his recent triumphs.","He looked toward Riya, his mismatched eyes now returned to unified blue-gold meeting her jewel-blue gaze.","\"Any... changes?\" he asked simply.","His voice emanated with magnetic quality that seemed layered, coming in from different dimensions simultaneously.","Riya blinked, initially confused by the vague question. She stared into his complex eyes, trying to parse what he was asking, what specific aspect among countless recent developments he wanted her to assess.","Then understanding dawned, and her expression shifted.","Without a word, she closed her eyes, her enhanced sensitivity to Mana reaching outward and forward , perceiving not just the present but future trajectories, the brightness of Mana as it would exist in times yet to come.","A moment passed. Then another.","When she opened her eyes, her expression was downcast as she shook her head lightly.","\"No changes,\" she said quietly.","She then looked at Kael and the others as she sent a silent mental note only for Noah to hear as she could not let the others know.","’I still sense the brilliant light of Mana dimming in the future. Everything you’ve accomplished hasn’t altered what I perceive coming.’","Noah looked at her silently, his tyrannical composure absorbing that truth without visible reaction.","He nodded once, then turned to look toward Khor.","Before he could even formulate the question, she raised her hands, allowing obsidian-crimson darkness to coalesce over her fingers like living shadow.","\"Your restoration and rollback of my existence was... somewhat useful, Outsider,\" she said lightly.","\"I gained, or really, recovered , some memories. Uniquely, all of them seem like bad memories just from their taste alone.\"","Her crimson eyes flickered with something between pain and rage.","\"These memories seem like something entirely new even for me, as I have not consciously gone through them. They feel like gaps being filled, spaces in my history that were surgically removed and are now bleeding back into awareness.\"","...!"]},{"number":4400,"title":"Chapter 4400: Chapter 4399: You! I","paragraphs":["Khor paused, her expression hardening.","\"I will display one which may be of importance for all of us to observe. It should be a memory of my existence...during or after my collapse.\"","...!","She waved her hands, and a radiant, extremely solid illusory screen materialized in the air before them... a concentrated construct of her recovered Hunger given visual form.","After manifesting the screen, Khor closed her eyes, and on the illusory surface, obsidian darkness gave way to brilliance as a glorious...and horrifying scene began to play out.","Noah and the others watched as devastation bloomed across the screen.","The scene showed a fractured and decimated landscape of obsidian crystals stretching for impossible distances.","Billions upon billions of corpses...tentacled Inevitabilities in their natural forms, sprawled across the shattered crystalline terrain in poses suggesting violent, sudden death.","No signs of battle. Just... termination. As if something had simply decided they should cease existing and reality had complied.","In the center of all this devastation, the corpse of an adult Khor could be seen.","Her figure of sublime beauty seemed utterly defiled...an immense, massive gash permeated from her forehead vertically all the way down across her body, as if something had attempted to split her in half and had succeeded.","She was clearly dead. Unmistakably collapsed. Her existence terminated!","And standing over her corpse was a shadowy humanoid figure shrouded in darkness that made perception struggle to focus properly.","The entity was whistling nonchalantly...actually whistling , as if surveying the scene of genocide was a pleasant afternoon activity.","He reached out into Khor’s corpse with familiarity and pulled , extracting a radiant obsidian-crimson Heart that pulsed with terrifying luminosity even in death.","The entity hummed while throwing the Heart up and down, feeling its weight with assessment.","\"Another piece of the puzzle obtained...\" he murmured with satisfaction, and he turned towards the corpse of Khor as he used his other hand to shut her absent crimson eyes tenderly, as if he was soothing her to sleep!","Noah’s gaze hardened as he watched, his enhanced perception through The Lens of Civilization trying to pierce the shadows shrouding the figure.","Beside him in the present, Khor’s eyes remained closed, but her hands were clenched so tightly her knuckles had gone white.","Her expression showed barely controlled rising lividity .","In the scene, three figures appeared behind the humanoid shadowy entity holding the Heart of Hunger.","They spoke in perfect unison, their voices overlapping.","\"With this action, we must move even more quickly.\"","The humanoid entity shrouded in darkness nodded while continuing his humming.","\"Yes, yes, My Little Weavers,\" he said.","\"The Death of THE First Hunger will be felt by THE Creature. That guy has always looked after her from afar with sentimentality ever since he butchered her Master in a haze, and has wanted to make amends since. Ah... sentimentality of fools. Well, no matter.\"","He tossed the Heart casually.","\"It is time to activate Anaximander against THE Creature. Do you have everything ready on your end?\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed with chilling light as he processed those words.","THE Living Paradox and those three should be... THE Weavers. They’re discussing using Anaximander as a weapon against THE Creature?!","His mind raced through possibilities while the scene continued!","THE Weavers replied in their unified voice: \"It took considerable work, but Anaximander is prepared to be unleashed against THE Creature. He does not even comprehend what exactly he is doing, and he will not understand until the very last moment.\"","At such words, the shadowy figure grasping Khor’s Heart of Hunger nodded as he turned.","And his face became clear in the scene.","\"Let’s get started!\" he declared with enthusiasm that bordered on mania.","BOOM!","The moment his face became fully visible, Noah’s eyes opened with shock.","In front of him in the present, Khor’s eyes snapped open simultaneously, shock and lividity warring across her features as she howled !","That face!","They knew that face intimately!","She had recognized it before, and she had stated so!","BOOM!","An eruption of Hunger exploded where Khor stood, obsidian-crimson flames consuming the surrounding space as her eyes blazed with rage!","Noah stared at the face with a heavy gaze.","It was unfathomable. Impossible. And yet undeniable.","The face that THE Living Paradox was wearing in that memory...","Was the face of Schrodinger .","How? How could this be ?","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he looked at countless possibilities as...it did not make too much sense!","The beggar paradox, the Elderborn...he’s THE Living Paradox? Or connected to him? A fragment? A Will? A disguise?","Khor’s figure trembled with palpable rage, her voice shaking with barely restrained violence.","\"I recognized him,\" she said, \"I should have known! All this time...right under my nose!\"","HUUM!","Her aura exploded outward.","\"He collapsed billions of Inevitabilities! He collapsed MY existence and took my Heart of Hunger , my Primacy of Hunger! He enslaved all Inevitabilities and mutated them to work for his Loom! He...\"","Her voice cracked with emotion!","\"He must collapse! He must pay !\"","BOOM!","Hunger began raging uncontrollably around her, obsidian-crimson flames consuming atmosphere itself.","Noah stepped forward, his voice holsing authority meant to penetrate her fury.","\"Wait. Let us plan first. We cannot simply-\"","But in the next moment...","WAP!","Khor disappeared .","Simply gone, as if she’d decided to exist somewhere else right away.","Noah’s face became heavier with profound concern.","There were still too many unknowns!","If THE Living Paradox is truly Schrodinger, or potentially his Remnant Will, or some fragment, or something others can’t even conceptualize...how powerful is he truly?","Going to face a being with THE distinction currently will have catastrophic consequences!","...!","But Khor had already set off, and Noah felt what she felt through their brief connection during the memory viewing.","When it came to Hunger , the one quality he now understood intimately was this...whatever Hunger craved with sufficient potency, it would find .","Even if Khor didn’t know precisely where Schrodinger was...though she did, because they’d been keeping tabs, with Schrodinger and Leonore currently hidden while observing a Justiciar complete its massacre in the Transcendent Quantum Folds with Noah’s false illusions.","Even if she didn’t know, her Hunger would track him and all his other bodies with inexorable certainty.","And she had already departed in her rage without questioning whether what they saw was truth, without wondering if they could actually face an existence with THE distinction at this moment.","Hunger was filled with fury!"]}]);
